#. type: anchor{#1}
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:167
msgid "Using Texinfo"
msgstr "Usando Texinfo"

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:172
msgid ""
"@dfn{Texinfo} is a documentation system that uses a single source file to "
"produce both online information and printed output.  This means that instead "
"of writing several different documents, one for each output format, you need "
"only write one document."
msgstr ""
"@dfn{Texinfo} é um sistema de documentação que usa um arquivo fonte "
"único para produzir informações online e saída impressa. Isso significa "
"que, em vez de escrever vários documentos, um para cada formato de saída, "
"você precisa escrever somente um documento."

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:179
msgid ""
"Using Texinfo, you can create a printed document (via the @TeX{} typesetting "
"system) in PDF format, including chapters, sections, cross-references, and "
"indices.  From the same Texinfo source file, you can create HTML output "
"suitable for use with a web browser, you can create an Info file for use in "
"GNU Emacs or other Info-reading programs, and also create DocBook, EPUB 3, "
"or @LaTeX{} files."
msgstr ""
"Usando Texinfo, você consegue criar um documento impresso (via sistema "
"tipográfico @TeX{}) em formato PDF, incluindo capítulos, seções, "
"referências cruzadas e índices. A partir do mesmo arquivo fonte do "
"Texinfo, você consegue criar saída HTML adequada para uso com um navegador "
"web; você consegue criar um arquivo do Info para uso no GNU Emacs ou outros "
"programas de leitura do Info; e também criar arquivos Docbook, EPUB 3 ou "
"@LaTeX{}."

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:180
#, no-wrap
msgid "Source file format"
msgstr "Formato do arquivo fonte"

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:181
#, no-wrap
msgid "Semantic markup"
msgstr "Marcação semântica"

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:187
msgid ""
"A Texinfo source file is a plain text file containing text interspersed with "
"@dfn{@@-commands} (words preceded by an @samp{@@}) that tell the Texinfo "
"processors what to do.  Texinfo's markup commands are almost entirely "
"@dfn{semantic}; that is, they specify the intended meaning of text in the "
"document, rather than physical formatting instructions."
msgstr ""
"Um arquivo fonte do Texinfo é um arquivo de texto simples contendo texto "
"intercalado com @dfn{comandos @@} (palavras precedidas por um @samp{@@}) que "
"informam aos processadores Texinfo o que fazer. Os comandos de marcação do "
"Texinfo são quase inteiramente @dfn{semânticos}; isto é, eles especificam "
"o significado pretendido do texto no documento, em vez de instruções de "
"formatação física."

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:190
msgid ""
"GNU Emacs has a special mode, called Texinfo mode, that provides various "
"Texinfo-related features. (@xref{Texinfo Mode}.)"
msgstr ""
"O GNU Emacs tem um modo especial, chamado modo Texinfo, que fornece vários "
"recursos relacionados ao Texinfo. (@xref{Modo Texinfo}.)"

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:191
#, no-wrap
msgid "Limited scope of Texinfo"
msgstr "Escopo limitado do Texinfo"

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:200
msgid ""
"Texinfo was devised specifically for the purpose of writing software "
"documentation and manuals.  If you want to write a good manual for your "
"program, Texinfo has many features which we hope will make your job easier.  "
"However, Texinfo is not intended to be a general-purpose formatting "
"program.  It provides almost no commands for controlling the final "
"formatting, so may be inappropriate for your needs if you want to lay out a "
"newspaper, devise a glossy magazine ad, or follow the exact formatting "
"requirements of a publishing house."
msgstr ""
"Texinfo foi concebido especificamente para o propósito de escrever "
"documentação e manuais de software. Se você quer escrever um bom manual "
"para teu programa, Texinfo tem muitos recursos que nós esperamos que "
"tornarão teu trabalho mais fácil. No entanto, Texinfo não é destinado "
"para ser um programa de formatação de propósito geral. Ele quase não "
"fornece comandos para controlar a formatação final, de forma que pode ser "
"inapropriado para tuas necessidades se você quiser esquematizar um jornal, "
"conceber um anúncio brilhante de revista ou seguir as exigências exatas de "
"formatação de uma editora."

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:201
#, no-wrap
msgid "Spelling of Texinfo"
msgstr "Escrita de Texinfo"

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:202
#, no-wrap
msgid "Pronunciation of Texinfo"
msgstr "Pronúncia de Texinfo"

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:210
msgid ""
"Spell ``Texinfo'' with a capital ``T'' and the other letters in lowercase.  "
"The first syllable of ``Texinfo'' is pronounced like ``speck'', not "
"``hex''.  This odd pronunciation is derived from the pronunciation of "
"@TeX{}.  Pronounce @TeX{} as if the @samp{X} were the last sound in the name "
"`Bach'.  In the word @TeX{}, the @samp{X} is, rather than the English letter "
"``ex'', actually the Greek letter ``chi''."
msgstr ""
"Escreva-se ``Texinfo'' com um ``T'' maiúsculo e as outras letras em "
"minúsculas. A primeira silaba de ``Texinfo'' é pronunciada como ``speck'', "
"e não ``hex''. Essa pronúncia estranha é derivada da pronúncia de "
"@TeX{}. Pronuncie-se @TeX{} como se o @samp{X} fosse o último som no nome "
"`Bach'. Na palavra @TeX{}, o @samp{X} é, em vez da letra do Inglês ``ex'', "
"na verdade a letra Grega ``chi''."

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:214
msgid ""
"Texinfo is the official documentation format of the GNU project.  More "
"information, including manuals for GNU packages, is available at the "
"@uref{http://www.gnu.org/doc/, GNU documentation web page}."
msgstr ""
"Texinfo é o formato oficial de documentação do projeto GNU. Mais "
"informações, incluindo manuais para pacotes GNU, estão disponíveis na "
"@uref{http://www.gnu.org/doc/, página web da documentação GNU}."

#. type: section
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:216 texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:218
#, no-wrap
msgid "Reporting Bugs"
msgstr "Informando Defeitos"

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:218
msgid "@nodedescription Submitting effective bug reports."
msgstr "@nodedescription Submetendo informes eficazes de defeitos."

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:220
#, no-wrap
msgid "Bugs, reporting"
msgstr "Defeitos, informando"

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:221
#, no-wrap
msgid "Suggestions for Texinfo, making"
msgstr "Sugestões para Texinfo, fazendo"

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:222
#, no-wrap
msgid "Reporting bugs"
msgstr "Informando Defeitos"

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:227
msgid ""
"We welcome bug reports and suggestions for any aspect of the Texinfo system: "
"programs, documentation, installation, etc.  Please email them to "
"@email{bug-texinfo@@gnu.org}.  You can get the latest version of Texinfo via "
"its home page, @uref{http://www.gnu.org/software/texinfo}."
msgstr ""
"Nós apreciamos informes de defeitos e sugestões para qualquer aspecto do "
"sistema Texinfo: programas, documentação, instalação, etc. Por favor, "
"envie-os para @email{bug-texinfo@@gnu.org}. Você consegue obter a versão "
"mais recente do Texinfo por meio da página inicial dele, "
"@uref{http://www.gnu.org/software/texinfo}."

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:228
#, no-wrap
msgid "Checklist for bug reports"
msgstr "Lista de verificação para informes de defeitos"

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:231
msgid ""
"For bug reports, please include enough information for the maintainers to "
"reproduce the problem.  Generally speaking, that means:"
msgstr ""
"Para informes de defeitos, por favor, inclua informações suficientes para "
"os(as) mantenedores(as) reproduzirem o problema. Falando genericamente, isso "
"significa:"

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:233
#, no-wrap
msgid "The version number of Texinfo and the program(s) or manual(s) involved."
msgstr ""
"O número da versão do Texinfo e o(s) programa(s) ou manual(is) "
"envolvido(s)."

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:234
#, no-wrap
msgid "The contents of any input files necessary to reproduce the bug."
msgstr ""
"O conteúdo de quaisquer arquivos de entrada necessários para reproduzir o "
"defeito."

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:235
#, no-wrap
msgid "Precisely how you ran any program(s) involved."
msgstr "Precisamente como você executou quaisquer programa(s) envolvido(s)."

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:236
#, no-wrap
msgid "A description of the problem and samples of any erroneous output."
msgstr "Uma descrição do problema e amostras de quaisquer saídas errôneas."

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:237
#, no-wrap
msgid "Hardware and operating system names and versions."
msgstr "Nomes e versões do hardware e do sistema operacional."

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:238
#, no-wrap
msgid "Anything else that you think would be helpful."
msgstr "Qualquer outra coisa que você pense que pudesse ajudar."

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:243
msgid ""
"When in doubt whether something is needed or not, include it.  It's better "
"to include too much than to leave out something important."
msgstr ""
"Quando em dúvida se alguma coisa é necessária ou não, inclua-a. É "
"melhor incluir muito mais que deixar de fora algo importante."

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:246
msgid ""
"It is critical to send an actual input file that reproduces the problem."
msgstr ""
"É crítico enviar um arquivo de entrada atual que reproduza o problema."

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:249
msgid ""
"Any problems with the Info reader in Emacs should be reported to the Emacs "
"developers: see @ref{Bugs,,, emacs, The GNU Emacs Manual}."
msgstr ""
"Quaisquer problemas com o leitor do Info no Emacs deveriam ser informados "
"para os(as) desenvolvedores(as) do Emacs: veja-se @ref{Bugs,,, emacs, O "
"Manual do GNU Emacs}."

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:250
#, no-wrap
msgid "Patches, contributing"
msgstr "Remendos, contribuindo"

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:255
msgid ""
"Patches are welcome; if possible, please make them with @samp{@w{diff -c}}, "
"@samp{@w{diff -u}} (@pxref{,,, diffutils, Comparing and Merging Files}), or "
"@samp{git diff} and include @file{ChangeLog} entries (@pxref{Change Log,,, "
"standards, GNU Coding Standards}), and follow the existing coding style."
msgstr ""
"Remendos são bem-vindos; se possível, por favor, faça-os com "
"@samp{@w{diff -c}}, @samp{@w{diff -u}} (@pxref{,,, diffutils, Comparando e "
"Mesclando Arquivos}), ou @samp{git diff} e inclua entradas de "
"@file{ChangeLog} (@pxref{Change Log,,, standards, Padrões GNU de "
"Codificação}), e siga o estilo existente de codificação."

#. type: section
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:257 texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:259
#, no-wrap
msgid "Output Formats"
msgstr "Formatos de Saída"

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:259
msgid "@nodedescription Overview of the supported output formats."
msgstr "@nodedescription Visão geral dos formatos suportados de saída."

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:260
#, no-wrap
msgid "Output formats"
msgstr "Formatos de saída"

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:261
#, no-wrap
msgid "Back-end output formats"
msgstr "Estrutura de retaguarda, formatos de saída"

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:264
msgid ""
"Here is an overview of the output formats currently supported by Texinfo."
msgstr ""
"Aqui está uma visão geral dos formatos de saída atualmente suportados por "
"Texinfo."

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:266
#, no-wrap
msgid "Info output, overview"
msgstr "Saída do Info, visão geral"

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:267 texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:824
#, no-wrap
msgid "Info"
msgstr "Info"

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:275
msgid ""
"(Generated via @command{texi2any}.)  Info format is mostly a plain text "
"transliteration of the Texinfo source.  It adds a few control characters to "
"provide navigational information for cross-references, indices, and so on.  "
"The Emacs Info subsystem (@pxref{Top,,, info, Info}), and the standalone "
"@command{info} program (@pxref{Top,,, info-stnd, GNU Info}), among others, "
"can read these files.  @xref{Info Files}, and @ref{Creating and Installing "
"Info Files}."
msgstr ""
"(Gerado via @command{texi2any}.)   O formato Info é em sua maior parte "
"transliteração de texto plano do fonte Texinfo.   Ele adiciona uns poucos "
"caracteres de controle para fornecer informação de navegação para "
"referências cruzadas, índices, e assim por diante.   O subsistema Emacs "
"Info (veja-se @ref{Top,,, info, Info}), e o programa autônomo "
"@command{info} (@pxref{Top,,, info-stnd, GNU Info}), entre outros, conseguem "
"ler esses arquivos. Veja-se @ref{Arquivos do Info}, e @ref{Criando e "
"Instalando Arquivos Info}."

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:276
#, no-wrap
msgid "Plain text output, overview"
msgstr "Saída gerada de texto simples, visão geral"

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:277
#, no-wrap
msgid "Plain text"
msgstr "Texto simples"

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:281
msgid ""
"(Generated via @command{texi2any --plaintext}.)  This is almost the same as "
"Info output with the navigational control characters are omitted."
msgstr ""
"(Gerado via @command{texi2any --plaintext}.)   Essa é quase a mesma que a "
"saída Info com os caracteres de controle de navegação omitidos."

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:282
#, no-wrap
msgid "HTML output, overview"
msgstr "Saída gerada de HTML, visão geral"

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:283 texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:830
#, no-wrap
msgid "HTML"
msgstr "HTML"

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:298
msgid ""
"(Generated via @command{texi2any --html}.)  HTML, standing for Hyper Text "
"Markup Language, is the language for writing documents on the World Wide "
"Web.  Web browsers can render this language online.  There are many versions "
"of HTML, both different standards and browser-specific variations.  "
"@command{texi2any} uses a subset of the language that can be interpreted by "
"any common browser, intentionally not using many newer or less "
"widely-supported tags.  Although the native output is thus rather plain, it "
"can be customized at various levels, if desired.  @xref{Generating HTML}."
msgstr ""
"(Gerado via @command{texi2any --html}.) HTML, que significa Hyper Text "
"Markup Language, é a linguagem para escrever documentos na World Wide Web. "
"Os navegadores da Web conseguem renderizar essa linguagem online. Existem "
"muitas versões de HTML, tanto diferentes usos mais comuns quanto "
"variações específicas de navegador. @command{texi2any} usa um subconjunto "
"da linguagem que consegue ser interpretado por qualquer navegador comum, "
"intencionalmente não usando muitas etiquetas mais novas ou menos amplamente "
"suportadas. Embora a saída nativa seja, portanto, bastante simples, ela "
"pode ser personalizada em vários níveis, se desejado. @xref{Gerando HTML}."

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:299
#, no-wrap
msgid "EPUB 3 output, overview"
msgstr "Saída EPUB 3, visão geral"

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:300
#, no-wrap
msgid "EPUB 3"
msgstr "EPUB 3"

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:307
msgid ""
"(Generated via @command{texi2any --epub3}.)  EPUB is a format designed for "
"reading electronic books on portable devices.  It is a derivative of HTML@.  "
"The format was developed by the International Digital Publishing Forum "
"(IDPF), which is now part of the World Wide Web Consortium (W3C)@.  The "
"latest major revision, EPUB 3, dates from 2011."
msgstr ""
"(Gerada via @command{texi2any --epub3}.) EPUB é um formato projetado para "
"leitura de livros eletrônicos em dispositivos portáteis. É um derivado do "
"HTML@. O formato foi desenvolvido pelo International Digital Publishing "
"Forum (IDPF), que agora faz parte do World Wide Web Consortium (W3C)@. A "
"mais recente grande revisão, EPUB 3, data de 2011."

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:309
#, no-wrap
msgid "DVI output, overview"
msgstr "Saída DVI, visão geral"

#. type: pindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:310
#, no-wrap
msgid "dvips @r{(program)}"
msgstr "dvips @r{(programa)}"

#. type: pindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:311
#, no-wrap
msgid "xdvi"
msgstr "xdvi"

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:312
#, no-wrap
msgid "DVI"
msgstr "DVI"

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:323
msgid ""
"(Generated via @command{texi2dvi}.)  The DeVIce Independent binary format is "
"output by the @TeX{} typesetting program (@uref{http://tug.org}).  This is "
"then read by a DVI `driver', which knows the actual device-specific commands "
"that can be viewed or printed, notably Dvips for translation to PostScript "
"(@pxref{Top,,, dvips, Dvips}) and Xdvi for viewing on an X display "
"(@uref{http://sourceforge.net/projects/xdvi/}).  @xref{Hardcopy with "
"@TeX{}}.  (Be aware that the Texinfo language is very different from "
"@TeX{}'s usual languages: plain @TeX{}, @LaTeX{}, Con@TeX{}t, etc.)"
msgstr ""
"(Gerada via @command{texi2dvi}.)   O formato binário DeVIce Independent é "
"liberado pelo programa tipográfico @TeX{} (@uref{http://tug.org}). Essa é "
"então lida por um `controlador' DVI, o qual conhece os atuais comandos "
"específicos de dispositivo que podem ser visualizados ou impressos, "
"notadamente Dvips para tradução para PostScript (veja-se @ref{Top,,, "
"dvips, Dvips}) e Xdvi para visualização em uma tela do X "
"(@uref{http://sourceforge.net/projects/xdvi/}). Veja-se @ref{Impresso com "
"@TeX{}}. (Esteja ciente de que a linguagem do Texinfo é muito diferente das "
"linguagens usuais do @TeX{}: @TeX{} simples, @LaTeX{}, Con@TeX{}t, etc.)"

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:324
#, no-wrap
msgid "PostScript output, overview"
msgstr "Saída gerada PostScript, visão geral"

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:325
#, no-wrap
msgid "PostScript"
msgstr "PostScript"

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:332
msgid ""
"(Generated via @command{texi2dvi --ps}.)  PostScript is a page description "
"language that became widely used around 1985 and is still used today.  "
"@uref{https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/PostScript} gives a basic description "
"and more preferences.  By default, Texinfo uses the @command{dvips} program "
"to convert @TeX{}'s DVI output to PostScript.  @xref{Top,,, dvips, Dvips}."
msgstr ""
"(Gerada via @command{texi2dvi --ps}.)   PostScript é uma linguagem de "
"descrição de página que se tornou amplamente usada por volta de 1985 e "
"ainda é usada hoje em dia. @uref{https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/PostScript} "
"dá uma descrição básica e mais preferências.   Por padrão, Texinfo usa "
"o programa @command{dvips} para converter a saída DVI do @TeX{} para "
"PostScript.  Veja-se @ref{Top,,, dvips, Dvips}."

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:333
#, no-wrap
msgid "PDF output, overview"
msgstr "Saída gerada PDF, visão geral"

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:334
#, no-wrap
msgid "Beebe, Nelson"
msgstr "Beebe, Nelson"

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:335
#, no-wrap
msgid "PDF"
msgstr "PDF"

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:347
msgid ""
"(Generated via @command{texi2dvi --pdf} or @command{texi2pdf}.)  This format "
"was developed by Adobe Systems for portable document interchange, based on "
"their previous PostScript language.  It can represent the exact appearance "
"of a document, including fonts and graphics, and supporting arbitrary "
"scaling.  It is intended to be platform-independent and easily viewable, "
"among other design goals; "
"@uref{https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Portable_Document_Format} and "
"@uref{http://tug.org/TUGboat/tb22-3/tb72beebe-pdf.pdf} have some "
"background.  By default, Texinfo uses the @command{pdftex} program, an "
"extension of @TeX{}, to output PDF; see "
"@uref{http://tug.org/applications/pdftex}.  @xref{PDF Output}."
msgstr ""
"(Gerada via @command{texi2dvi --pdf} ou @command{texi2pdf}.)   Esse formato "
"foi desenvolvido pela Adobe Systems para intercâmbio de documento "
"portável, baseado na linguagem PostScript prévia deles.   Ele consegue "
"representar a exata aparência de um documento, incluindo fontes e "
"gráficos, e suportar escalonamento arbitrário.   Ele é entendido como "
"sendo independente de plataforma e facilmente visualizável, entre outros "
"objetivos de projeto; "
"@uref{https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Portable_Document_Format} e "
"@uref{http://tug.org/TUGboat/tb22-3/tb72beebe-pdf.pdf} tem algum "
"conhecimento.   Por padrão, Texinfo usa o programa @command{pdftex}, uma "
"extensão de @TeX{}, para gerar PDF; veja-se "
"@uref{http://tug.org/applications/pdftex}. Veja-se @ref{Saída PDF}."

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:348
#, no-wrap
msgid "LaTeX output, overview"
msgstr "Saída LaTeX, visão geral"

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:349
#, no-wrap
msgid "@LaTeX{}"
msgstr "@LaTeX{}"

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:357
msgid ""
"(Generated via @command{texi2any --latex}.)  This is a typesetting system "
"built on top of @TeX{}.  It was originally released by Leslie Lamport in "
"1984.  @LaTeX{} adds more definitions to those of @TeX{} and has a wide "
"range of packages built on it. @LaTeX{} is ubiquitous in academic "
"literature. The current version of @LaTeX{} is under active development; "
"more information is available online at "
"@uref{https://www.latex-project.org/}."
msgstr ""
"(Gerada via @command{texi2any --latex}.) Esse é um sistema de tipografia "
"construído sobre o @TeX{}. Foi lançado originalmente por Leslie Lamport em "
"1984. O @LaTeX{} adiciona mais definições para aquelas do @TeX{} e tem uma "
"ampla gama de pacotes construídos sobre ele. O @LaTeX{} é onipresente na "
"literatura acadêmica. A versão atual do @LaTeX{} está sob desenvolvimento "
"ativo; mais informações estão disponíveis online em "
"@uref{https://www.latex-project.org/}."

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:362
msgid ""
"The @LaTeX{} output can be further processed into DVI, PostScript, or PDF@.  "
"In theory, the @LaTeX{} output should allow for much more customizability of "
"the output than would be possible with the plain @TeX{} implementation of "
"Texinfo."
msgstr ""
"A saída do @LaTeX{} pode ser processada posteriormente em DVI, PostScript "
"ou PDF@. Em teoria, a saída do @LaTeX{} deveria permitir muito mais "
"personalização da saída do que seria possível com a implementação "
"@TeX{} simples do Texinfo."

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:364
#, no-wrap
msgid "DocBook output, overview"
msgstr "Saída Docbook, visão geral"

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:365
#, no-wrap
msgid "XML DocBook output, overview"
msgstr "Saída XML Docbook, visão geral"

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:366 texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:839
#, no-wrap
msgid "DocBook"
msgstr "Docbook"

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:373
msgid ""
"(Generated via @command{texi2any --docbook}.)  This is an XML-based format, "
"primarily for technical documentation.  It therefore bears some resemblance, "
"in broad outline, to Texinfo.  See @uref{http://www.docbook.org}.  Various "
"converters from DocBook @emph{to} Texinfo have also been developed; see the "
"Texinfo web pages."
msgstr ""
"(Gerada via @command{texi2any --docbook}.)   Esse é um formato baseado em "
"XML, primariamente para documentação técnica.   Ele, por conseguinte, "
"assume alguma semelhança, em linhas gerais, com Texinfo.   Veja-se "
"@uref{http://www.docbook.org}. Vários conversores de Docbook @emph{para} "
"Texinfo também foram desenvolvidos; vejam-se as páginas web do Texinfo."

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:374
#, no-wrap
msgid "XML Texinfo output, overview"
msgstr "Saída XML Texinfo, visão geral"

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:375
#, no-wrap
msgid "Texinfo XML output, overview"
msgstr "Saída Texinfo XML, visão geral"

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:376
#, no-wrap
msgid "DTD, for Texinfo XML"
msgstr "DTD, para Texinfo XML"

#. type: pindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:377
#, no-wrap
msgid "texinfo.dtd"
msgstr "texinfo.dtd"

#. type: pindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:378
#, no-wrap
msgid "txixml2texi"
msgstr "txixml2texi"

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:379 texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:835
#, no-wrap
msgid "XML"
msgstr "XML"

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:385
msgid ""
"(Generated via @command{texi2any --xml}.)  The @command{texi2any} XML "
"output, unlike all the other output formats, is a transliteration of the "
"Texinfo source, rather than finished output.  Texinfo XML files cannot be "
"viewed in web browsers or other programs."
msgstr ""
"(Gerada via @command{texi2any --xml}.) A saída XML do @command{texi2any}, "
"diferente de todos os outros formatos de saída, é uma transliteração do "
"fonte do Texinfo, em vez de uma saída finalizada. Os arquivos XML do "
"Texinfo não podem ser visualizados em navegadores da web ou outros "
"programas."

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:392
msgid ""
"XML is a generic syntax specification usable for any sort of content.  (A "
"reference is at @uref{http://www.w3.org/XML}.)  The purpose of the Texinfo "
"XML output is to allow further processing by XML tools.  The output syntax "
"is defined in an XML DTD, which is contained in a file @file{texinfo.dtd} "
"included in the Texinfo source distribution."
msgstr ""
"XML é uma especificação genérica de sintaxe usável para qualquer tipo "
"de conteúdo. (Uma referência está em @uref{http://www.w3.org/XML}.) O "
"propósito da saída XML do Texinfo é o de permitir processamento posterior "
"por ferramentas XML. A sintaxe de saída é definida em um DTD de XML, que "
"está contido em um arquivo @file{texinfo.dtd} incluído na distribuição "
"do fonte do Texinfo."

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:397
msgid ""
"The Texinfo source distribution includes a utility script @file{txixml2texi} "
"to do a backward transformation to recreate the original Texinfo content "
"(except for Texinfo macros and conditionals)."
msgstr ""
"A distribuição do fonte do Texinfo inclui um script utilitário "
"@file{txixml2texi} para fazer uma transformação reversa para recriar o "
"conteúdo Texinfo original (exceto para macros e condicionais do Texinfo)."

#. type: section
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:401 texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:403
#, no-wrap
msgid "Info Files"
msgstr "Arquivos do Info"

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:403
msgid "@nodedescription What is an Info file?"
msgstr "@nodedescription O que é um arquivo do Info?"

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:404
#, no-wrap
msgid "Info files"
msgstr "Arquivos Info"

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:410
msgid ""
"As mentioned above, Info format is mostly a plain text transliteration of "
"the Texinfo source, with the addition of a few control characters to "
"separate nodes and provide navigational information, so that Info-reading "
"programs can operate on it."
msgstr ""
"Conforme mencionado acima, o formato Info é em sua maioria uma "
"transliteração de texto plano do fonte Texinfo, com a adição de uns "
"poucos caracteres de controle para separar nós e fornecer informação de "
"navegação, de forma que os programas de leitura Info consigam operar sobre "
"ele."

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:415
msgid ""
"Info files are nearly always created by processing a Texinfo source "
"document.  @command{texi2any}, also known as @command{makeinfo}, is the "
"principal command that converts a Texinfo file into an Info file; "
"@pxref{Generic Translator @command{texi2any}}."
msgstr ""
"Os arquivos Info são quase sempre criados pelo processamento de um "
"documento fonte do Texinfo.  @command{texi2any}, também conhecido como "
"@command{makeinfo}, é o comando principal que converte um arquivo Texinfo "
"em um arquivo Info; veja-se @ref{Tradutor Genérico @command{texi2any}}."

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:425
msgid ""
"Generally, you enter an Info file through a node that by convention is named "
"`Top'.  This node normally contains just a brief summary of the file's "
"purpose, and a large menu through which the rest of the file is reached.  "
"From this node, you can either traverse the file systematically by going "
"from node to node, or you can go to a specific node listed in the main menu, "
"or you can search the index menus and then go directly to the node that has "
"the information you want.  Alternatively, with the standalone Info program, "
"you can specify specific menu items on the command line (@pxref{Top,,, info, "
"Info})."
msgstr ""
"Geralmente, você adentra um arquivo Info via um nó que, por convenção, "
"é chamado `Top'.   Esse nó normalmente contém somente um sumário curto "
"do propósito do arquivo, e um menu amplo por meio do qual o restante do "
"arquivo é alcançado.   A partir desse nó, você ou pode atravessar o "
"arquivo sistematicamente, indo de nó a nó; ou você pode ir até um nó "
"específico listado no menu principal; ou você pode pesquisar no menu de "
"índice e então ir diretamente ao nó que tenha a informação que você "
"deseja.   Alternativamente, com programa autônomo Info, você consegue "
"especificar itens específicos de menu na linha de comando (veja-se "
"@ref{Top,,, info, Info})."

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:430
msgid ""
"If you want to read through an Info file in sequence, as if it were a "
"printed manual, you can hit @key{SPC} repeatedly, or you get the whole file "
"with the advanced Info command @kbd{g *}.  (@xref{Advanced,, Advanced Info "
"commands, info, Info}.)"
msgstr ""
"Se você desejar ler ao longo de um arquivo Info em sequência, como se ele "
"fosse um manual impresso, você pode teclar @key{ESPAÇO} repetidamente, ou "
"você percorre o arquivo inteiro com o comando Info avançado @kbd{g *}. "
"(Veja-se @ref{Advanced,, Advanced Info commands, info, Info}.)"

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:434
msgid ""
"The @file{dir} file in the @file{info} directory serves as the departure "
"point for the whole Info system.  From it, you can reach the `Top' nodes of "
"each of the documents in a complete Info system."
msgstr ""
"O arquivo @file{dir} no diretório @file{info} serve como o ponto de chegada "
"para o sistema Info inteiro.   A partir dele, você consegue alcançar os "
"nós `Top' de cada um dos documentos em um sistema Info completo."

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:435
#, no-wrap
msgid "URI syntax for Info"
msgstr "Sintaxe URI para Info"

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:439
msgid ""
"If you wish to refer to an Info file via a URI, you can use the (unofficial) "
"syntax exemplified by the following.  This works with Emacs/W3, for example:"
msgstr ""
"Se você desejar se referir a um arquivo Info via URI, você pode usar a "
"sintaxe (não oficial) exemplificada pelo seguinte.   Isto funciona com "
"Emacs/W3, por exemplo:"

#. type: example
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:443
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"info:emacs#Dissociated%20Press\n"
"info:///usr/info/emacs#Dissociated%20Press\n"
"info://localhost/usr/info/emacs#Dissociated%20Press\n"
msgstr ""
"info:emacs#Dissociated%20Press\n"
"info:///usr/info/emacs#Dissociated%20Press\n"
"info://localhost/usr/info/emacs#Dissociated%20Press\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:446
msgid "The @command{info} program itself does not follow URIs of any kind."
msgstr "O próprio programa @command{info} não segue URIs de qualquer tipo."

#. type: section
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:448 texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:450
#, no-wrap
msgid "Printed Books"
msgstr "Livros Impressos"

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:450
msgid "@nodedescription Characteristics of a printed book or manual."
msgstr "@nodedescription Características de um livro ou manual impresso."

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:451
#, no-wrap
msgid "Printed book and manual characteristics"
msgstr "Manual e livro impresso, características"

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:452
#, no-wrap
msgid "Manual characteristics, printed"
msgstr "Características de manual, impresso"

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:453
#, no-wrap
msgid "Book characteristics, printed"
msgstr "Características de livro, impresso"

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:454
#, no-wrap
msgid "Texinfo printed book characteristics"
msgstr "Características de livro impresso Texinfo"

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:455
#, no-wrap
msgid "Characteristics, printed books or manuals"
msgstr "Características, manuais ou livros impressos"

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:457
#, no-wrap
msgid "Knuth, Donald"
msgstr "Knuth, Donald"

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:462
msgid ""
"A Texinfo file can be formatted and typeset as a printed book or manual.  To "
"do this, you need @TeX{}, a sophisticated typesetting program written by "
"Donald Knuth of Stanford University.  It is not part of the Texinfo "
"distribution."
msgstr ""
"Um arquivo Texinfo pode ser formatado e tipografado como um livro ou um "
"manual impresso.   Para fazer isso, você precisa do @TeX{}, um sofisticado "
"programa de tipografia escrito por Donald Knuth da Universidade Stanford. "
"Ele não é parte da distribuição do Texinfo."

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:467
msgid ""
"Texinfo provides a file @file{texinfo.tex} that contains the definitions "
"that @TeX{} uses when it typesets a Texinfo file.  You can get the latest "
"version of @file{texinfo.tex} from the Texinfo home page, "
"@uref{http://www.gnu.org/software/texinfo/}."
msgstr ""
"O Texinfo fornece um arquivo @file{texinfo.tex} que contém as definições "
"que o @TeX{} usa quando tipografa um arquivo do Texinfo. Você consegue "
"obter a versão mais recente do @file{texinfo.tex} a partir da página "
"inicial do Texinfo, @uref{http://www.gnu.org/software/texinfo/}."

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:472
msgid ""
"A Texinfo-based book is similar to any other typeset, printed work: it can "
"have a title page, copyright page, table of contents, and preface, as well "
"as chapters, numbered or unnumbered sections and subsections, page headers, "
"cross-references, footnotes, and indices."
msgstr ""
"Um livro baseado em Texinfo é similar a qualquer outro trabalho "
"tipografado, impresso: ele pode ter uma página de título, página de "
"direitos autorais, sumário, e prefácio, bem como capítulos, seções e "
"subseções numeradas ou não numeradas, cabeçalhos de páginas, "
"referências cruzadas, notas de rodapé, e índices."

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:477
msgid ""
"@TeX{} is very powerful and has a great many features.  However, because a "
"Texinfo file must be able to present information both on a character-only "
"terminal in Info form and in a typeset book, the formatting commands that "
"Texinfo supports are necessarily limited."
msgstr ""
"@TeX{} é muito poderoso e tem muitos recursos ótimos. No entanto, como um "
"arquivo do Texinfo precisa ser capaz de apresentar informações tanto em um "
"terminal somente de caracteres no formato do Info quanto em um livro "
"tipografado, os comandos de formatação que o Texinfo suporta são "
"necessariamente limitados."

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:480
msgid ""
"@xref{Hardcopy with @TeX{}}, for more information on processing a manual "
"with @TeX{}."
msgstr ""
"@xref{Impresso com @TeX{}}, para mais informações acerca do processamento "
"de um manual com @TeX{}."

#. type: section
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:482 texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:484
#, no-wrap
msgid "Adding Output Formats"
msgstr "Adicionando Formatos de Saída"

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:484
msgid "@nodedescription Man pages and implementing new formats."
msgstr "@nodedescription Páginas de manual e implementando novos formatos."

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:485
#, no-wrap
msgid "Additional output formats"
msgstr "Formatos adicionais de saída"

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:489
msgid ""
"The output formats in the previous sections handle a wide variety of usage, "
"but of course there is always room for more."
msgstr ""
"Os formatos de saída nas seções anteriores lidam com uma variedade ampla "
"de usos, porém, certamente, sempre existe espaço para mais."

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:490
#, no-wrap
msgid "Output formats, supporting more"
msgstr "Formatos de saída, suportando mais"

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:491
#, no-wrap
msgid "SGML-tools output format"
msgstr "Ferramentas SGML, formatos de saída"

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:502
msgid ""
"If you are a programmer and would like to contribute to the GNU project by "
"implementing additional output formats for Texinfo, that would be "
"excellent.  The way to do this that would be most useful is to write a new "
"back-end for @command{texi2any}, our reference implementation of a Texinfo "
"parser; it creates a tree representation of the Texinfo input that you can "
"use for the conversion.  The documentation in the source file "
"@file{tp/Texinfo/Convert/Converter.pm} is a good place to start "
"(@pxref{Texinfo::Convert::Converter,,,texi2any_internals,Texinfo modules "
"documentation}).  @xref{Generic Translator @command{texi2any}}."
msgstr ""
"Se você for um(a) programador(a) e gostaria de contribuir para com o "
"projeto GNU implementando formatos adicionais de saída para o Texinfo, isso "
"seria excelente.   A maneira de fazer isso que seria mais útil é a de "
"escrever uma estrutura de retaguarda nova para @command{texi2any}, nossa "
"implementação de referência de um analisador Texinfo; ela cria uma "
"representação de árvore da entrada de Texinfo que você consegue usar "
"para a conversão. A documentação no arquivo fonte "
"@file{tp/Texinfo/Convert/Converter.pm} é um bom lugar para começar "
"(@pxref{Texinfo::Convert::Converter,,,texi2any_internals,documentação dos "
"módulos do Texinfo}). @ref{Tradutor Genérico @command{texi2any}}."

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:507
msgid ""
"Another viable approach is use the Texinfo XML output from "
"@command{texi2any} as your input.  This XML is an essentially complete "
"representation of the input, but without the Texinfo syntax and option "
"peculiarities, as described above."
msgstr ""
"Outra abordagem viável é a de usar a saída XML do Texinfo oriunda do "
"@command{texi2any} como tua entrada.   Esse XML é uma representação "
"essencialmente completa da entrada, porém sem as peculiaridades da sintaxe "
"e de opção do Texinfo, conforme descrito acima."

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:508
#, no-wrap
msgid "Texinfo parsers, discouraging more"
msgstr "Analisadores Texinfo, desencorajando mais"

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:516
msgid ""
"If you still cannot resist the temptation of writing a new program that "
"reads Texinfo source directly, let us give some more caveats: please do not "
"underestimate the amount of work required.  Texinfo is by no means a simple "
"language to parse correctly, and remains under development, so you would be "
"committing to an ongoing task.  You are advised to check that the tests of "
"the language that come with @command{texi2any} give correct results with "
"your new program."
msgstr ""
"Se você ainda não conseguir resistir à tentação de escrever um programa "
"novo que leia diretamente o fonte do Texinfo, permita-nos te dar mais "
"algumas advertências: por favor, não subestime a quantidade de trabalho "
"exigida.   Texinfo não é de forma alguma uma linguagem simples de se "
"analisar corretamente, e permanece sob desenvolvimento, de maneira que você "
"estaria se comprometendo com uma tarefa em andamento.   Você está "
"aconselhado(a) a verificar se os testes da linguagem que vem com "
"@command{texi2any} dão resultados corretos com o teu programa novo."

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:517
#, no-wrap
msgid "Man page output, not supported"
msgstr "Saída de página de manual, não suportada"

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:527
msgid ""
"From time to time, proposals are made to generate traditional Unix man pages "
"from Texinfo source.  However, because man pages have a strict conventional "
"format, creating a good man page requires a completely different source from "
"that needed for the typical Texinfo applications of writing a good user "
"tutorial and/or a good reference manual.  This makes generating man pages "
"incompatible with the Texinfo design goal of not having to document the same "
"information in different ways for different output formats.  You might as "
"well write the man page directly."
msgstr ""
"De tempos em tempos, propostas são feitas para gerar páginas de manual "
"Unix tradicionais a partir do fonte do Texinfo.   Entretanto, pelo motivo de "
"que as páginas de manual tem um formato convencional estrito, criar uma "
"página de manual boa exige um fonte completamente diferente daquele "
"necessário para as aplicações Texinfo típicas de escrita de um tutorial "
"de usuário(a) bom e (ou) um bom manual de referência.   Isso torna a "
"geração de páginas de manual incompatível com o objetivo do projeto do "
"Texinfo de não ter de documentar a mesma informação de maneiras "
"diferentes para diferentes formatos de saída.   Você poderia também "
"escrever a página de manual diretamente."

#. type: pindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:528
#, no-wrap
msgid "help2man"
msgstr "help2man"

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:529
#, no-wrap
msgid "O'Dea, Brendan"
msgstr "O'Dea, Brendan"

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:536
msgid ""
"As an alternative way to support man pages, you may find the program "
"@command{help2man} to be useful.  It generates a traditional man page from "
"the @samp{--help} output of a program.  In fact, the man pages for the "
"programs in the Texinfo distribution are generated with this.  It is GNU "
"software written by Brendan O'Dea, available from "
"@uref{http://www.gnu.org/software/help2man}."
msgstr ""
"Como um meio alternativo para suportar páginas de manual, você "
"possivelmente ache que o programa @command{help2man} seja útil.   Ele gera "
"uma página de manual tradicional a partir da saída @samp{--help} de um "
"programa. De fato, as páginas de manual para os programas na distribuição "
"do Texinfo são geradas com isso. Ele é software GNU escrito por Brendan "
"O'Dea, disponível a partir de @uref{http://www.gnu.org/software/help2man}."

#. type: section
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:538 texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:540
#, no-wrap
msgid "History"
msgstr "Histórico"

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:540
msgid "@nodedescription Acknowledgements, contributors and genesis."
msgstr "@nodedescription Agradecimentos, colaboradores(as) e gênese."

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:542
#, no-wrap
msgid "Stallman, Richard M."
msgstr "Stallman, Richard M."

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:543
#, no-wrap
msgid "Chassell, Robert J."
msgstr "Chassell, Robert J."

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:544
#, no-wrap
msgid "Fox, Brian"
msgstr "Fox, Brian"

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:545
#, no-wrap
msgid "Berry, Karl"
msgstr "Berry, Karl"

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:546
#, no-wrap
msgid "Smith, Gavin"
msgstr "Smith, Gavin"

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:554
msgid ""
"Richard M. Stallman invented the Texinfo format, wrote the initial "
"processors, and created Edition 1.0 of this manual.  Robert@tie{}J.  "
"Chassell greatly revised and extended the manual, starting with Edition "
"1.1.  Brian Fox was responsible for the standalone Texinfo distribution "
"until version 3.8.  Karl Berry continued maintenance from Texinfo 3.8 "
"(manual edition 2.22), and Gavin Smith has continued maintenance since "
"Texinfo 6.0."
msgstr ""
"Richard M. Stallman inventou o formato Texinfo, escreveu os processadores "
"iniciais e criou a Edição 1.0 deste manual. Robert@tie{}J. Chassell "
"revisou e estendeu muito o manual, começando com a Edição 1.1. Brian Fox "
"foi responsável pela distribuição autônoma do Texinfo até a versão "
"3.8. Karl Berry continuou a manutenção a partir do Texinfo 3.8 (edição "
"do manual 2.22), e Gavin Smith continuou a manutenção desde o Texinfo 6.0."

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:555
#, no-wrap
msgid "History of Texinfo"
msgstr "Histórico do Texinfo"

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:556
#, no-wrap
msgid "Texinfo history"
msgstr "Texinfo, estória"

#. type: subheading
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:557
#, no-wrap
msgid "Beginnings"
msgstr "Começo"

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:559
#, no-wrap
msgid "NLS"
msgstr "NLS"

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:564
msgid ""
"Richard Stallman included an on-line, hypertext help system called Info in "
"the original implementation of Emacs (in 1975/6).  Stallman had been "
"inspired after seeing a presentation a couple of years earlier on the "
"``NLS'' hypertext system of Douglas Engelbart."
msgstr ""
"Richard Stallman incluiu um sistema de ajuda de hipertexto online chamado "
"Info na implementação original do Emacs (em 1975/6). Stallman foi "
"inspirado depois de ver uma apresentação alguns anos antes acerca do "
"sistema de hipertexto ``NLS'' de Douglas Engelbart."

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:588
#, no-wrap
msgid "Scribe"
msgstr "Scribe"

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:589
#, no-wrap
msgid "Reid, Brian"
msgstr "Reid, Brian"

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:595
msgid ""
"In another development, in the 1970's at CMU, Brian Reid developed a program "
"and format named Scribe to mark up documents for printing.  It used the "
"@code{@@} character to introduce commands, as Texinfo does.  Much more "
"consequentially, it strove to describe document contents rather than "
"formatting, an idea wholeheartedly adopted by Texinfo."
msgstr ""
"Em outro desenvolvimento, na década de 1970 na CMU, Brian Reid desenvolveu "
"um programa e formato chamado Scribe para marcar documentos para impressão. "
"Ele usava o caractere @code{@@} para introduzir comandos, como o Texinfo "
"faz. Muito mais consequentemente, ele se esforçou para descrever o "
"conteúdo do documento em vez da formatação, uma ideia adotada de todo o "
"coração pelo Texinfo."

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:596
#, no-wrap
msgid "Bolio"
msgstr "Bolio"

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:597
#, no-wrap
msgid "Bo@TeX{}"
msgstr "Bo@TeX{}"

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:602
msgid ""
"Meanwhile, people at MIT developed another format called Bolio.  Richard "
"Stallman (RMS) worked on converting Bolio to use @TeX{} as its typesetting "
"language, resulting in Bo@TeX{}.  The earliest Bo@TeX{} version seems to "
"have been 0.02 on October 31, 1984."
msgstr ""
"Enquanto isso, pessoas no MIT desenvolveram outro formato chamado Bolio. "
"Richard Stallman (RMS) trabalhou na conversão do Bolio para usar @TeX{} "
"como a linguagem dele de tipografia, resultando no Bo@TeX{}. A versão mais "
"antiga do Bo@TeX{} parece ter sido 0.02 em 31 de outubro de 1984."

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:607
msgid ""
"Bo@TeX{} could only be used as a markup language for documents to be "
"printed, not for online documents.  RMS combined Bo@TeX{} and Info to create "
"Texinfo, a mark-up language for text that is intended to be read both online "
"and as printed hard copy."
msgstr ""
"O Bo@TeX{} só podia ser usado como uma linguagem de marcação para "
"documentos a serem impressos, não para documentos online. RMS combinou o "
"Bo@TeX{} e o Info para criar o Texinfo, uma linguagem de marcação para "
"texto que se destina a ser lido online e como cópia impressa."

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:613
msgid ""
"The original translator to create Info was written (primarily by RMS and Bob "
"Chassell) in Emacs Lisp, namely the @code{texinfo-format-buffer} and other "
"functions.  In the early 1990s, Brian Fox reimplemented the conversion "
"program in C, now called @command{makeinfo}, as well as the standalone "
"@command{info} program."
msgstr ""
"O tradutor original para criar o Info foi escrito (principalmente por RMS e "
"Bob Chassell) em Emacs Lisp, ou seja, o @code{texinfo-format-buffer} e "
"outras funções. No início da década de 1990, Brian Fox reimplementou o "
"programa de conversão em C, agora chamado @command{makeinfo}, bem como o "
"programa autônomo @command{info}."

#. type: subheading
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:614
#, no-wrap
msgid "Reimplementing in Perl"
msgstr "Reimplementando em Perl"

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:616
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:16722
#, no-wrap
msgid "Cons, Lionel"
msgstr "Cons, Lionel"

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:617
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:17912
#, no-wrap
msgid "Dumas, Patrice"
msgstr "Dumas, Patrice"

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:627
msgid ""
"In 2012, the C @command{makeinfo} was itself replaced by a Perl "
"implementation generically called @command{texi2any}.  This version supports "
"the same level of output customization as @command{texi2html}, an "
"independent program originally written by Lionel Cons, later with "
"substantial work by many others.  The many additional features needed to "
"make @command{texi2html} a replacement for @command{makeinfo} were "
"implemented by Patrice Dumas.  The first, never-released version of "
"@command{texi2any} was based on the @command{texi2html} code."
msgstr ""
"Em 2012, o @command{makeinfo} do C foi substituído por uma implementação "
"Perl genericamente chamada @command{texi2any}. Essa versão suporta o mesmo "
"nível de personalização de saída que @command{texi2html}, um programa "
"independente escrito originalmente por Lionel Cons, mais tarde com trabalho "
"substancial de muitos(as) outros(as). Os muitos recursos adicionais "
"necessários para tornar @command{texi2html} um substituto para "
"@command{makeinfo} foram implementados por Patrice Dumas. A primeira "
"versão, nunca lançada, do @command{texi2any} foi baseada no código do "
"@command{texi2html}."

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:628
#, no-wrap
msgid "Tree representation of documents"
msgstr "Representação de documentos em árvore"

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:629
#, no-wrap
msgid "Syntax tree representation of documents"
msgstr "Sintaxe, Representação de documentos em árvore"

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:630
#, no-wrap
msgid "Abstract syntax tree representation of documents"
msgstr "Sintaxe abstrata, Representação de documentos em árvore"

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:639
msgid ""
"That implementation, however, was abandoned in favor of the current program "
"(also written by Patrice Dumas), which parses the Texinfo input into a tree "
"for processing.  It inherited the design of customization and other features "
"from @command{texi2html} (for more on @command{texi2html} compatibility, "
"@pxref{@command{texi2html}}).  However, @command{texi2any} is a full "
"reimplementation: it constructs a tree-based representation of the input "
"document for all back-ends to work from."
msgstr ""
"Essa implementação, no entanto, foi abandonada em favor do programa atual "
"(também escrito por Patrice Dumas), que analisa a entrada do Texinfo em uma "
"árvore para processamento. Ele herdou o projeto de personalização e "
"outros recursos do @command{texi2html} (para mais informações acerca da "
"compatibilidade do @command{texi2html}, @pxref{@command{texi2html}}). No "
"entanto, o @command{texi2any} é uma reimplementação completa: ele "
"constrói uma representação baseada em árvore do documento de entrada "
"para todas as estruturas de retaguarda trabalharem."

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:647
msgid ""
"The new Perl program is much slower than the old C program.  The speed gap "
"has partially closed since first release, but it may not ever be entirely "
"comparable.  So why did we switch? In short, we intend and hope that the "
"present program will be much easier than the previous C implementation of "
"@command{makeinfo} to extend to different output styles, back-end output "
"formats, and all other customizations.  In more detail:"
msgstr ""
"O novo programa Perl é muito mais lento que o antigo programa C. A lacuna "
"de velocidade foi parcialmente fechada desde o primeiro lançamento, mas "
"pode nunca ser totalmente comparável. Então, por que nós comutamos? Em "
"resumo, nós pretendemos e esperamos que o programa atual seja muito mais "
"fácil que a implementação C anterior do @command{makeinfo} para estender "
"a diferentes estilos de saída, formatos de saída de estrutura de "
"retaguarda e todas as outras personalizações. Em mais detalhes:"

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:649
#, no-wrap
msgid "HTML customization.  Many GNU and other free software packages"
msgstr ""
"Personalização de HTML.  Muitos pacotes de software livre GNU e outros"

#. type: itemize
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:656
msgid ""
"had been happily using the HTML customization features in "
"@command{texi2html} for years.  Thus, in effect two independent "
"implementations of the Texinfo language had developed, and keeping them in "
"sync was not simple.  Adding the HTML customization possible in "
"@command{texi2html} to a C program would have been an enormous effort."
msgstr ""
"tem sido felizes no uso das características de personalização de HTML no "
"@command{texi2html} por anos.  Assim, na verdade, duas implementações "
"independentes da linguagem Texinfo foram desenvolvidas, e mantê-las em "
"sincronia não era simples.  Adicionar a possibilidade de personalização "
"de HTML no @command{texi2html} a um programa C teria sido um esforço enorme."

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:657
#, no-wrap
msgid "Unicode, and multilingual support generally, especially of east"
msgstr ""
"Unicode, e suporte multilíngue em geral, especialmente de idiomas do leste"

#. type: itemize
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:663
msgid ""
"Asian languages.  At that time, doing it in C would have been tantamount to "
"rewriting the entire program.  Since then, the parser and bits of converter "
"back-ends have been rewritten in C, but the converter back-ends are still "
"mostly in Perl which has good multilingual support built in."
msgstr ""
"asiático. Naquela época, fazer isso em C teria sido equivalente a "
"reescrever o programa inteiro. Desde então, o analisador e os bits das "
"estruturas de retaguarda do conversor foram reescritos em C, mas as "
"estruturas de retaguarda do conversor ainda estão principalmente em Perl, "
"que tem um bom suporte multilíngue integrado."

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:664
#, no-wrap
msgid "Additional back-ends.  The @command{makeinfo} code had become"
msgstr "Estruturas adicionais de retaguarda. O código do @command{makeinfo}"

#. type: itemize
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:671
msgid ""
"convoluted to the point where adding a new back-end was quite complex, "
"requiring complex interactions with existing back-ends.  In contrast, the "
"new implementation provides a clean tree-based representation for all "
"back-ends to work from.  People have requested numerous different back-ends "
"(@LaTeX{}, the latest (X)HTML, @dots{}); this change made them much more "
"feasible to implement.  Which leads to the last item:"
msgstr ""
"complicou-se até o ponto onde adicionar-se uma nova estrutura de retaguarda "
"era bastante complexo, exigindo interações complexas com estruturas de "
"retaguarda existentes. Em contraste, a nova implementação fornece uma "
"representação limpa baseada em árvore para todas as estruturas de "
"retaguarda trabalharem. Pessoas tem solicitado numerosas estruturas de "
"retaguarda (@LaTeX{}, o mais recente (X)HTML, @dots{}); essa mudança os "
"tornou muito mais viáveis de implementar. O que nos leva ao último item:"

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:672
#, no-wrap
msgid "Making contributions easier.  In general, due to the cleaner"
msgstr ""
"Facilitando as contribuições. Em geral, devido à estrutura mais limpa, a"

#. type: itemize
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:679
msgid ""
"structure, the separate parser/back-ends implementation should be "
"considerably easier than the former C @command{makeinfo} implementation for "
"anyone to read and contribute to, with the resulting obvious benefits.  "
"After ten years, contributed back-ends were yet to happen, but it is still "
"believed that this structure could in theory lend better to contributions."
msgstr ""
"implementação separada do analisador/estruturas de retaguarda deveria ser "
"consideravelmente mais fácil que a implementação C anterior do "
"@command{makeinfo} para qualquer um(a) ler e contribuir, com os benefícios "
"óbvios resultantes. Depois de dez anos, as estruturas de retaguarda "
"contribuídas ainda estavam para acontecer, mas ainda se acredita que essa "
"estrutura poderia, em teoria, se prestar melhor às contribuições."

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:682
#, no-wrap
msgid "@command{texi2any}, as reference implementation"
msgstr "@command{texi2any}, como implementação de referência"

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:683
#, no-wrap
msgid "Reference implementation"
msgstr "Implementação de referência"

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:684
#, no-wrap
msgid "Implementation, @command{texi2any} as reference"
msgstr "Implementação, @command{texi2any} como referência"

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:685
#, no-wrap
msgid "Texinfo language tests"
msgstr "Testes da linguagem do Texinfo"

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:686
#, no-wrap
msgid "Tests, of Texinfo language"
msgstr "Testes, da linguagem do Texinfo"

#. type: anchor{#1}
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:698
msgid "Reference Implementation"
msgstr "Implementação de referência"

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:698
msgid ""
"@command{texi2any} is intended to be a reference implementation that defines "
"parts of the language not fully specified by the manual.  Without such a "
"reference, alternative implementations would be very likely to have subtle, "
"or not-so-subtle, differences in behavior, and thus Texinfo documents would "
"become dependent on the processor.  It is also important to have consistent "
"command-line options for all processors.  Extensive tests of the language "
"and processor were developed at the same time as @command{texi2any}; we "
"encourage anyone thinking of writing a program to parse Texinfo input to "
"make use of these tests."
msgstr ""
"@command{texi2any} é destinado a ser uma implementação de referência que "
"define partes da linguagem não totalmente especificadas pelo manual. Sem "
"tal referência, implementações alternativas muito provavelmente teriam "
"diferenças sutis, ou não tão sutis, no comportamento, e assim os "
"documentos do Texinfo se tornariam dependentes do processador. Também é "
"importante ter opções de linha de comando consistentes para todos os "
"processadores. Testes extensivos da linguagem e do processador foram "
"desenvolvidos ao mesmo tempo que @command{texi2any}; nós encorajamos "
"qualquer um(a) pensando em escrever um programa para analisar a entrada do "
"Texinfo a fazer uso desses testes."

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:699
#, no-wrap
msgid "Future of Texinfo implementations"
msgstr "Futuro das implementações do Texinfo"

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:705
msgid ""
"With the release of @command{texi2any} as the reference implementation, "
"development of both the C implementation of @command{makeinfo} and "
"@command{texi2html} has been halted.  Going forward, we ask authors of "
"Texinfo documents to use only @command{texi2any}."
msgstr ""
"Com o lançamento do @command{texi2any} como implementação de referência, "
"o desenvolvimento tanto da implementação C do @command{makeinfo} quanto do "
"@command{texi2html} foi interrompido. Daqui para frente, nós pedimos para "
"os(as) autores(as) de documentos do Texinfo que usem somente o "
"@command{texi2any}."

#. type: chapter
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:707 texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:710
#, no-wrap
msgid "Writing a Texinfo File"
msgstr "Escrevendo um Arquivo do Texinfo"

#.  old name
#. type: anchor{#1}
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:710
msgid "Beginning and Ending a File"
msgstr "Iniciando e Terminando um Arquivo"

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:710
msgid "@nodedescription Format of a Texinfo source file."
msgstr "@nodedescription Formato de um arquivo fonte do Texinfo."

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:714
msgid ""
"This chapter describes Texinfo syntax and what is required in a Texinfo "
"file, and gives a short sample file."
msgstr ""
"Este capítulo descreve a sintaxe do Texinfo e o que é exigido em um "
"arquivo do Texinfo, e dá um arquivo curto de amostra."

#. type: node
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:716
#, no-wrap
msgid "Conventions"
msgstr "Convenções"

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:718
msgid "@nodedescription General rules for writing a Texinfo file."
msgstr "@nodedescription Regras gerais para escrever um arquivo do Texinfo."

#. type: section
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:718
#, no-wrap
msgid "General Syntactic Conventions"
msgstr "Convenções Sintáticas Gerais"

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:719
#, no-wrap
msgid "General syntactic conventions"
msgstr "Convenções sintáticas gerais"

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:720
#, no-wrap
msgid "Syntactic conventions"
msgstr "Sintáticas, convenções"

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:721
#, no-wrap
msgid "Conventions, syntactic"
msgstr "Convenções, sintáticas"

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:722
#, no-wrap
msgid "Characters, basic input"
msgstr "Caracteres, entrada básica"

#.  old name
#. type: anchor{#1}
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:724
msgid "Formatting Commands"
msgstr "Comandos de Formatação"

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:726
msgid ""
"This section describes the general conventions used in all Texinfo documents."
msgstr ""
"Esta seção descreve as convenções gerais usadas em todos os documentos "
"do Texinfo."

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:729
#, no-wrap
msgid "Source files, characters used"
msgstr "Arquivos fonte, caracteres usados"

#. type: itemize
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:737
msgid ""
"All printable ASCII characters except @samp{@@}, @samp{@{} and @samp{@}} can "
"appear in a Texinfo file and stand for themselves.  @samp{@@} is the escape "
"character which introduces commands, while @samp{@{} and @samp{@}} are used "
"to surround arguments to certain commands.  To put one of these special "
"characters into the document, put an @samp{@@} character in front of it, "
"like this: @samp{@@@@}, @samp{@@@{}, and @samp{@@@}}."
msgstr ""
"Todos os caracteres ASCII imprimíveis, exceto @samp{@@}, @samp{@{} e "
"@samp{@}}, podem aparecer em um arquivo do Texinfo e representam eles "
"mesmos. @samp{@@} é o caractere de encapsulamento que introduz comandos, "
"enquanto @samp{@{} e @samp{@}} são usados para envolver argumentos a certos "
"comandos.   Para colocar um desses caracteres especiais no documento, "
"coloque um caractere @samp{@@} em frente a ele, como isto: @samp{@@@@}, "
"@samp{@@@{}, e @samp{@@@}}."

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:739
#, no-wrap
msgid "@sortas{at} @@-commands"
msgstr "@sortas{at} Comandos @@"

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:740
#, no-wrap
msgid "Formatting commands"
msgstr "Formatando, comandos"

#. type: itemize
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:745
msgid ""
"In a Texinfo file, the commands you write to describe the contents of the "
"manual are preceded by an @samp{@@} character; they are called "
"@dfn{@@-commands}.  (The @samp{@@} in Texinfo has the same meaning that "
"@samp{\\} has in plain @TeX{}.)"
msgstr ""
"Em um arquivo do Texinfo, os comandos que você escreve para descrever o "
"conteúdo do manual são precedidos por um caractere @samp{@@}; eles são "
"chamados de @dfn{comandos @@}. (O @samp{@@} no Texinfo tem o mesmo "
"significado que o @samp{\\} tem no @TeX{} simples.)"

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:746
#, no-wrap
msgid "Braces, when to use"
msgstr "Chaves, quando usar"

#. type: itemize
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:753
msgid ""
"Depending on what they do or what arguments they take, you need to write "
"@@-commands on lines of their own, or as part of sentences.  As a general "
"rule, a command requires braces if it mingles among other text; but it does "
"not need braces if it is on a line of its own.  For more details of Texinfo "
"command syntax, see @ref{Command Syntax}."
msgstr ""
"Dependendo do que eles fazem ou de quais argumentos recebam, você precisa "
"escrever comandos @@ em linhas próprias, ou como parte de frases. Como "
"regra geral, um comando exige chaves se ele se misturar com outro texto; mas "
"não precisa de chaves se estiver em uma linha própria. Para mais detalhes "
"da sintaxe de comandos do Texinfo, veja-se @ref{Sintaxe do Comando}."

#. type: itemize
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:759
msgid ""
"Whitespace following an @@-command name is optional and (usually)  ignored "
"if present.  The exceptions are contexts when whitespace is significant, "
"e.g., an @code{@@example} environment."
msgstr ""
"Espaço em branco seguindo um nome de comando @@ é opcional e (normalmente) "
"ignorado se presente.  As exceções são contextos quando o espaço em "
"branco é significativo, por exemplo, um ambiente de @code{@@example}."

#. type: itemize
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:764
msgid ""
"Texinfo supports the usual quotation marks used in English and in other "
"languages; see @ref{Inserting Quotation Marks}."
msgstr ""
"Texinfo suporta as aspas normais usadas em Inglês e em outros idiomas; "
"veja-se @ref{Inserindo Aspas}."

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:766
#, no-wrap
msgid "Multiple dashes in source"
msgstr "Vários traços no fonte"

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:767
#, no-wrap
msgid "Dashes in source"
msgstr "Traços no fonte"

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:768
#, no-wrap
msgid "Hyphens in source, two or three in a row"
msgstr "Hifens no fonte, dois ou três em uma linha"

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:769
#, no-wrap
msgid "Em dash, producing"
msgstr "Travessão, produzindo"

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:770
#, no-wrap
msgid "En dash, producing"
msgstr "Traço de ligação, produzindo"

#. type: itemize
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:780
msgid ""
"Use three hyphens in a row, @samp{---}, to produce a long dash---like this "
"(called an @dfn{em dash}), used for punctuation in sentences.  Use two "
"hyphens, @samp{--}, to produce a medium dash (called an @dfn{en dash}), used "
"primarily for numeric ranges, as in ``June 25--26''.  Use a single hyphen, "
"@samp{-}, to produce a standard hyphen used in compound words.  For display "
"on the screen, Info reduces three hyphens to two and two hyphens to one (not "
"transitively!).  Of course, any number of hyphens in the source remain as "
"they are in literal contexts, such as @code{@@code} and @code{@@example}."
msgstr ""
"Use três hifens em uma linha, @samp{---}, para produzir um traço "
"longo---como esse (chamado um @dfn{travessão}), usado para pontuação em "
"frases.  Use dois hifens, @samp{--}, para produzir um traço médio (chamado "
"um @dfn{traço de ligação}), usado primariamente para intervalos "
"numéricos, como em ``Junho 25--26''.  Use um hífen simples, @samp{-}, para "
"produzir um hífen padrão usado em palavras compostas.  Para exibir na "
"tela, Info reduz três hifens para dois e dois hifens para um (não "
"transitivamente!).  Certamente, qualquer número de hifens no fonte "
"permanece como estiverem em contextos literais, tais como @code{@@code} e "
"@code{@@example}."

#. type: itemize
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:788
msgid ""
"@emph{Whitespace}.  Texinfo files are plain text files composed of lines "
"terminated by the usual newline character (line feed).  Texinfo processors "
"read input one line at a time.  Paragraphs are terminated by an empty line "
"or a line containing only spaces. A sequence of several spaces in text is "
"usually treated the same as a single space (except in verbatim modes)."
msgstr ""
"@emph{Espaço em branco}. Arquivos do Texinfo são arquivos de texto simples "
"compostos de linhas terminadas pelo usual caractere de nova linha (avanço "
"de linha). Processadores do Texinfo leem a entrada uma linha por vez. "
"Parágrafos são terminados por uma linha vazia ou uma linha contendo "
"somente espaços. Uma sequência de vários espaços no texto geralmente é "
"tratada da mesma forma que um espaço (exceto em modos literais)."

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:789
#, no-wrap
msgid "Form feed character"
msgstr "Caractere de avanço de formulário"

#. type: kbd{#1}
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:790
#, no-wrap
msgid "CTRL-l"
msgstr "CTRL-l"

#. type: itemize
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:798
msgid ""
"Form feed (@kbd{CTRL-l}) characters in normal text end any open paragraph.  "
"Other ASCII whitespace (tab, carriage return) may be treated the same as "
"space characters, although the results may differ depending on output "
"format.  Hence, there is not much point in using these in documents.  "
"Non-ASCII spaces, such as Unicode ``em space'', are not recognized as "
"whitespace at all and will be treated as regular, non-whitespace characters."
msgstr ""
"Caracteres de avanço de formulário (@kbd{CTRL-l}) em texto normal encerram "
"qualquer parágrafo aberto. Outros espaços em branco ASCII (tabulação, "
"retorno de carro) podem ser tratados da mesma forma que caracteres de "
"espaço, embora os resultados possam diferir dependendo do formato de "
"saída. Portanto, não existe muito sentido em usá-los em documentos. "
"Espaços não ASCII, como Unicode ``em space'', não são reconhecidos como "
"espaços em branco e serão tratados como caracteres regulares, não "
"espaços em branco."

#. type: itemize
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:801
msgid ""
"However, in verbatim modes, for example in code samples, tab characters may "
"produce the correct formatting in the output."
msgstr ""
"No entanto, em modos literais, por exemplo, em amostras de código, "
"caracteres de tabulação podem produzir a formatação correta na saída "
"gerada."

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:815
#, no-wrap
msgid "PDF/DVI"
msgstr "PDF/DVI"

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:817
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Ignored between paragraphs.\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
"Ignorado entre parágrafos.\n"
"\n"

#. type: findex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:818 texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:9566
#, no-wrap
msgid "LaTeX"
msgstr "LaTeX"

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:823
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Ignored in contexts where spaces are ignored except after specific\n"
"commands closing braces (@code{@@caption} for example).  Left as is\n"
"in the output otherwise.\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
"Ignorado em contextos onde espaços são ignorados, exceto depois de "
"comandos\n"
"específicos fechando chaves (@code{@@caption} por exemplo). Deixado como\n"
"está na saída gerada, caso contrário.\n"
"\n"

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:829
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Output as-is between paragraphs (their most common use); ignored in "
"contexts\n"
"where spaces are ignored except after specific commands closing braces\n"
"(@code{@@caption} for example).  In other contexts, they may be treated as\n"
"regular spaces (and thus consolidated with surrounding whitespace).\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
"Saída gerada como está entre parágrafos (uso mais comum dela); ignorada "
"em contextos\n"
"onde espaços são ignorados, exceto depois de comandos específicos "
"fechando chaves\n"
"(@code{@@caption} por exemplo). Em outros contextos, eles podem ser tratados "
"como\n"
"espaços regulares (e, portanto, consolidados com espaços em branco ao "
"redor).\n"
"\n"

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:834
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Written as a numeric entity except contexts where spaces are ignored;\n"
"for example, in @samp{@@footnote@{ ^L foo@}}, the form feed is\n"
"ignored.\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
"Escrito como uma entidade numérica, exceto contextos onde espaços são "
"ignorados;\n"
"por exemplo, em @samp{@@footnote@{ ^L foo@}}, a alimentação de formulário "
"é\n"
"ignorada.\n"
"\n"

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:838
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Keep them everywhere; in attributes, escaped as @samp{\\f}; also,\n"
"@samp{\\} is escaped as @samp{\\\\} and newline as @samp{\\n"
"}.\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
"Mantenha-os em qualquer lugar; em atributos, encapsulados como @samp{\\f}; "
"também,\n"
"@samp{\\} é encapsulado como @samp{\\\\} e nova linha como @samp{\\n"
"}.\n"
"\n"

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:841
#, no-wrap
msgid "Completely removed, as they are not allowed.\n"
msgstr "Completamente removidos, dado que não são permitidos.\n"

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:850 texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:852
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:854
#, no-wrap
msgid "Comments"
msgstr "Comentários"

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:852
msgid "@nodedescription Writing comments and ignored text in general."
msgstr "@nodedescription Escrevendo comentários e texto ignorado em geral."

#. type: findex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:855
#, no-wrap
msgid "comment"
msgstr "comentário"

#. type: findex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:856
#, no-wrap
msgid "c"
msgstr "c"

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:866
msgid ""
"You can write comments in a Texinfo file by using the @code{@@comment} "
"command, which may be abbreviated to @code{@@c}.  Such comments are for a "
"person looking at the Texinfo source file.  All the text on a line that "
"follows either @code{@@comment} or @code{@@c} is a comment; the rest of the "
"line does not appear in the visible output.  (To be precise, the character "
"after the @code{@@c} or @code{@@comment} must be something other than a dash "
"or alphanumeric, or it will be taken as part of the command.)"
msgstr ""
"Você pode escrever comentários em um arquivo do Texinfo usando o comando "
"@code{@@comment}, o qual pode ser abreviado para @code{@@c}. Tais "
"comentários são para uma pessoa examinando o arquivo fonte do Texinfo. "
"Todo o texto em uma linha que se seguir ou a @code{@@comment} ou a "
"@code{@@c} é um comentário; o restante da linha não aparece na saída "
"gerada visível.  (Para ser preciso(a), o caractere depois do @code{@@c} ou "
"do @code{@@comment} deve necessariamente ser algo que não um traço ou "
"alfanumérico, ou será tomado como sendo parte do comando.)"

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:872
msgid ""
"Often, you can write the @code{@@comment} or @code{@@c} in the middle of a "
"line, and only the text that follows after the @code{@@comment} or "
"@code{@@c} command does not appear; but some commands, such as "
"@code{@@settitle}, work on a whole line.  You cannot use @code{@@comment} or "
"@code{@@c} within a line beginning with such a command."
msgstr ""
"Frequentemente, você pode escrever o @code{@@comment} ou o @code{@@c} no "
"meio de uma linha, e somente o texto que se seguir depois do comando "
"@code{@@comment} ou @code{@@c} não aparece; porém alguns comandos, tais "
"como @code{@@settitle}, funcionam sobre uma linha inteira.  Você não pode "
"usar @code{@@comment} ou @code{@@c} dentro de uma linha que se inicie com um "
"tal comando."

#. type: findex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:873
#, no-wrap
msgid "DEL @r{(comment character)}"
msgstr "DEL @r{(caractere de comentário)}"

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:874
#, no-wrap
msgid "Catcode for comments in @TeX{}"
msgstr "Código de categoria para comentários no @TeX{}"

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:882
msgid ""
"In cases of nested command invocations, complicated macro definitions, etc., "
"@code{@@c} and @code{@@comment} may provoke an error when processing with "
"@TeX{}.  Therefore, you can also use the @kbd{DEL} character (ASCII 127 "
"decimal, 0x7f hex, 0177 octal) as a true @TeX{} comment character (catcode "
"14, in @TeX{} internals).  Everything on the line after the @kbd{DEL} will "
"be ignored and the next line will be merged."
msgstr ""
"Em casos de invocações aninhadas de comando, definições complicadas de "
"macro, etc., @code{@@c} e @code{@@comment} podem provocar um erro quando do "
"processamento com @TeX{}.  Por conseguinte, você também pode usar o "
"caractere @kbd{DEL} (decimal 127 ASCII, hexadecimal 0x7f, octal 0177) como "
"um verdadeiro caractere de comentário do @TeX{} (código de categoria 14, "
"nos internos do @TeX{}). Tudo na linha depois de @kbd{DEL} será ignorado e "
"a próxima linha será mesclada."

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:883
#, no-wrap
msgid "Ignored text"
msgstr "Texto ignorado"

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:884
#, no-wrap
msgid "Unprocessed text"
msgstr "Texto não processado"

#. type: findex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:885
#, no-wrap
msgid "ignore"
msgstr "ignore"

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:893
msgid ""
"You can also have long stretches of text ignored by the Texinfo processors "
"with the @code{@@ignore} and @code{@@end ignore} commands.  Write each of "
"these commands on a line of its own, starting each command at the beginning "
"of the line.  Text between these two commands does not appear in the "
"processed output.  You can use @code{@@ignore} and @code{@@end ignore} for "
"writing comments.  (For some caveats regarding nesting of such commands, "
"@pxref{Conditional Nesting}.)"
msgstr ""
"Você também pode ter trechos longos de texto ignorados pelos processadores "
"Texinfo com os comandos @code{@@ignore} e @code{@@end ignore}. Escreva cada "
"um desses comandos em uma linha própria, iniciando cada comando no começo "
"da linha.  O texto entre esses dois comandos não aparece na saída gerada "
"processada.  Você pode usar @code{@@ignore} e @code{@@end ignore} para "
"escrever comentários.  (Para algumas advertências relativamente ao "
"aninhamento de tais comandos, veja-se @ref{Aninhamento de Condicional}.)"

#. type: node
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:895
#, no-wrap
msgid "Minimum"
msgstr "Mínimo"

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:897
msgid "@nodedescription What a Texinfo file must have."
msgstr "@nodedescription O que um arquivo do Texinfo precisa ter."

#. type: section
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:897
#, no-wrap
msgid "What a Texinfo File Must Have"
msgstr "O Que um Arquivo do Texinfo Precisa Ter"

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:898
#, no-wrap
msgid "Minimal Texinfo file (requirements)"
msgstr "Arquivo mínimo do Texinfo (exigências)"

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:899
#, no-wrap
msgid "Required in Texinfo file"
msgstr "Exigido no arquivo do Texinfo"

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:900
#, no-wrap
msgid "Texinfo file minimum"
msgstr "Mínimo do arquivo do Texinfo"

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:908
msgid ""
"By convention, the name of a Texinfo file ends with one of the extensions "
"@file{.texi}, @file{.texinfo}, @file{.txi}, or @file{.tex}.  Using "
"@file{.tex} is discouraged as this extension is already used by @TeX{} and "
"@LaTeX{} input files.  The most common and recommended extension is "
"@file{.texi}.  The name of a Texinfo file should only contain ASCII "
"characters."
msgstr ""
"Por convenção, o nome de um arquivo do Texinfo termina com uma das "
"extensões @file{.texi}, @file{.texinfo}, @file{.txi} ou @file{.tex}. Usar "
"@file{.tex} é desencorajado, pois essa extensão já é usada pelos "
"arquivos de entrada do @TeX{} e do @LaTeX{}. A extensão mais comum e "
"recomendada é @file{.texi}. O nome de um arquivo do Texinfo deveria conter "
"somente caracteres ASCII."

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:918
msgid ""
"The output name is based on the input file name, in the default case.  "
"First, any of the extensions @file{.texi}, @file{.tex}, @file{.txi}, or "
"@file{.texinfo} is removed from the input file name; then, the output format "
"specific extension is added---@file{.html} when generating HTML, "
"@file{.info} when generating Info, etc.  The output name should only contain "
"ASCII characters@footnote{@command{texi2any} can handle non ASCII characters "
"in input file names, but non ASCII characters in output name will create "
"problems for some output formats, especially for cross-references.}."
msgstr ""
"O nome da saída gerada é baseado no nome do arquivo de entrada, no caso "
"padrão. Primeiro, quaisquer das extensões @file{.texi}, @file{.tex}, "
"@file{.txi} ou @file{.texinfo} são removidas do nome do arquivo de entrada; "
"a seguir, a extensão específica do formato da saída gerada é "
"adicionada---@file{.html} ao gerar HTML, @file{.info} ao gerar Info, etc. O "
"nome da saída gerada deveria conter somente caracteres "
"ASCII@footnote{@command{texi2any} consegue manusear caracteres não ASCII em "
"nomes de arquivo de entrada, mas caracteres não ASCII no nome da saída "
"gerada criarão problemas para alguns formatos de saída, especialmente para "
"referências cruzadas.}."

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:919
#, no-wrap
msgid "Requirements for formatting"
msgstr "Exigências para formatação"

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:920
#, no-wrap
msgid "Minimal requirements for formatting"
msgstr "Exigências mínimas para formatação"

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:921
#, no-wrap
msgid "Formatting requirements"
msgstr "Exigências de formatação"

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:924
msgid ""
"In order to be made into a printed manual, a Texinfo file must begin with a "
"line like this:"
msgstr ""
"Para a finalidade de ser transformado em um manual impresso, um arquivo do "
"Texinfo precisa iniciar com uma linha como esta:"

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:934
msgid ""
"The contents of the file follow this beginning, and then you must end the "
"Texinfo source with a line like this:"
msgstr ""
"O conteúdo do arquivo segue esse início, e então você precisa finalizar "
"o fonte do Texinfo com uma linha como esta:"

#. type: example
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:937 texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:1036
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:2169
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@bye\n"
msgstr "@@bye\n"

#. type: findex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:939
#, no-wrap
msgid "\\input @r{(raw @TeX{} startup)}"
msgstr "\\input @r{(iniciação do @TeX{} bruto)}"

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:945
msgid ""
"The @code{@@bye} line at the end of the file on a line of its own tells "
"@TeX{} that the file is ended and to stop formatting.  If you leave this "
"out, you'll be dumped at @TeX{}'s prompt at the end of the run."
msgstr ""
"A linha @code{@@bye} no final do arquivo em uma linha própria informa ao "
"@TeX{} que o arquivo está terminado e para parar a formatação. Se deixar "
"isso de fora, você será despejado(a) no prompt do @TeX{} no final da "
"execução."

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:951
msgid ""
"Furthermore, you will usually provide a Texinfo file with a title, a title "
"page, indices, and the like, all of which are explained in this manual.  But "
"the minimum, which can be useful for short documents, is just the one line "
"at the beginning and the one line at the end."
msgstr ""
"Além disso, você normalmente fornecerá um arquivo do Texinfo com um "
"título, uma página de título, índices e similares, todos os quais estão "
"explicados neste manual. Mas o mínimo, que pode ser útil para documentos "
"curtos, é apenas a linha no início e a linha no final."

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:955
msgid ""
"Without additional information, the input and output encodings are assumed "
"to be UTF-8, an universal codeset compatible with 7-bit ASCII."
msgstr ""
"Sem informações adicionais, as codificações de entrada e saída são "
"assumidas como UTF-8, um conjunto universal de códigos compatível com "
"ASCII de 7 bits."

#. type: node
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:957
#, no-wrap
msgid "Short Sample Texinfo File"
msgstr "Arquivo Curto do Texinfo de Amostra"

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:961
msgid "@nodedescription A short sample Texinfo file."
msgstr "@nodedescription Um arquivo curto do Texinfo de amostra."

#. type: section
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:961
#, no-wrap
msgid "Short Sample"
msgstr "Amostra Curta"

#. type: anchor{#1}
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:961
msgid "Sample Beginning"
msgstr "Amostra de Início"

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:962
#, no-wrap
msgid "Sample Texinfo file, no comments"
msgstr "Arquivo do Texinfo de amostra, sem comentários"

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:965
msgid "Here is a short sample Texinfo file."
msgstr "Aqui está um arquivo curto de amostra do Texinfo."

#. type: example
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:969
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"@@settitle Sample Manual 1.0\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
"@@settitle Manual do Sample 1.0\n"
"\n"

#. type: example
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:972
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"@@copying\n"
"This is a short example of a complete Texinfo file.\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
"@@copying\n"
"Este é um exemplo curto de um arquivo completo do Texinfo.\n"
"\n"

#. type: example
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:975
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Copyright @@copyright@{@} 2016 Free Software Foundation, Inc.\n"
"@@end copying\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
"Copyright @@copyright@{@} 2016 Free Software Foundation, Inc.\n"
"@@end copying\n"
"\n"

#. type: example
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:982
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"@@titlepage\n"
"@@title Sample Title\n"
"@@page\n"
"@@vskip 0pt plus 1filll\n"
"@@insertcopying\n"
"@@end titlepage\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
"@@titlepage\n"
"@@title Título do Sample\n"
"@@page\n"
"@@vskip 0pt plus 1filll\n"
"@@insertcopying\n"
"@@end titlepage\n"
"\n"

#. type: example
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:984
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"@@contents\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
"@@contents\n"
"\n"

#. type: example
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:987
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"@@node Top\n"
"@@top GNU Sample\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
"@@node Top\n"
"@@top GNU Sample\n"
"\n"

#. type: example
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:990
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This manual is for GNU Sample\n"
"(version @@value@{VERSION@}, @@value@{UPDATED@}).\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
"Este manual é para GNU Sample\n"
"(versão @@value@{VERSION@}, @@value@{UPDATED@}).\n"
"\n"

#. type: example
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:996
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"@@menu\n"
"* First Chapter::    The first chapter is the\n"
"                      only chapter in this sample.\n"
"* Index::            Complete index.\n"
"@@end menu\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
"@@menu\n"
"* Primeiro Capítulo:: O primeiro capítulo é o\n"
"                      único capítulo nesta amostra.\n"
"* Índice::            Índice completo.\n"
"@@end menu\n"
"\n"

#. type: group
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:1000
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:2085
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"@@node First Chapter\n"
"@@chapter First Chapter\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
"@@node Primeiro Capítulo\n"
"@@chapter Primeiro Capítulo\n"
"\n"

#. type: group
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:1004
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:2089
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"@@cindex chapter, first\n"
"This is the first chapter.\n"
"@@cindex index entry, another\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
"@@cindex capítulo, primeiro\n"
"Este é o primeiro capítulo.\n"
"@@cindex entrada de índice, outra\n"
"\n"

#. type: group
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:1007
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:2091
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Here is a numbered list.\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
"Aqui está uma lista numerada.\n"
"\n"

#. type: group
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:1011
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:2095
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"@@enumerate\n"
"@@item\n"
"This is the first item.\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
"@@enumerate\n"
"@@item\n"
"Este é o primeiro item.\n"
"\n"

#. type: group
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:1015
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"@@item\n"
"This is the second item.\n"
"@@end enumerate\n"
msgstr ""
"@@item\n"
"Este é o segundo item.\n"
"@@end enumerate\n"

#. type: group
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:1020
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:2103
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"@@node First Section\n"
"@@section First Section\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
"@@node Primeira Seção\n"
"@@section Primeira Seção\n"
"\n"

#. type: group
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:1022
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:2105
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"First section of first chapter.\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
"Primeira seção do primeiro capítulo.\n"
"\n"

#. type: group
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:1026
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:2109
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"@@node Second Section\n"
"@@section Second Section\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
"@@node Segunda Seção\n"
"@@section Segunda Seção\n"
"\n"

#. type: example
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:1028
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Second section of first chapter.\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
"Segunda seção do primeiro capítulo.\n"
"\n"

#. type: example
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:1032
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:2165
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"@@node Index\n"
"@@unnumbered Index\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
"@@node Índice\n"
"@@unnumbered Índice\n"
"\n"

#. type: example
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:1034
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:2167
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"@@printindex cp\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
"@@printindex cp\n"
"\n"

#. type: section
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:1039
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:1041
#, no-wrap
msgid "Texinfo File Header"
msgstr "Cabeçalho do Arquivo do Texinfo"

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:1041
msgid "@nodedescription The first lines."
msgstr "@nodedescription As primeiras linhas."

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:1042
#, no-wrap
msgid "Header for Texinfo files"
msgstr "Cabeçalho para arquivos do Texinfo"

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:1043
#, no-wrap
msgid "Texinfo file header"
msgstr "Cabeçalho do arquivo do Texinfo"

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:1046
msgid "Texinfo files start with the line:"
msgstr "Arquivos do Texinfo iniciam com a linha:"

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:1055
msgid ""
"The @samp{\\input texinfo} line tells @TeX{} to use the @file{texinfo.tex} "
"file, which tells @TeX{} how to translate the Texinfo @@-commands into "
"@TeX{} typesetting commands.  (Note the use of the backslash, @samp{\\}; "
"this is correct for @TeX{}.)"
msgstr ""
"A linha @samp{\\input texinfo} diz ao @TeX{} para usar o arquivo "
"@file{texinfo.tex}, que diz ao @TeX{} como traduzir os comandos @@ do "
"Texinfo para comandos de tipografia do @TeX{}. (Observe o uso da barra "
"invertida, @samp{\\}; isso é correto para o @TeX{}.)"

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:1059
msgid ""
"It makes sense to include any command that affects document formatting as a "
"whole in the header.  The @code{@@settitle} line is usually present at the "
"beginning of the header:"
msgstr ""
"Faz sentido incluir qualquer comando que afete a formatação do documento "
"como um todo no cabeçalho. A linha @code{@@settitle} geralmente está "
"presente no começo do cabeçalho:"

#. type: example
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:1062
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@settitle Sample Manual 1.0\n"
msgstr "@@settitle Manual do Sample 1.0\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:1069
msgid ""
"The @code{@@settitle} line specifies a title for the page headers (or "
"footers) of the printed manual, and the default title and document "
"description for the @samp{<head>} in HTML@.  @code{@@synindex} "
"(@pxref{@code{@@synindex}}), for instance, is another command often included "
"in the header."
msgstr ""
"A linha @code{@@settitle} especifica um título para os cabeçalhos de "
"página (ou rodapés) do manual impresso, e o título padrão e a "
"descrição do documento para @samp{<head>} em HTML@. @code{@@synindex} "
"(@pxref{@code{@@synindex}}), por exemplo, é outro comando frequentemente "
"incluído no cabeçalho."

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:1078
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The start of the Texinfo file up to the first content that is output as part "
"of the main body of the document is the @dfn{preamble}.  It includes the "
"header, @ref{Document Permissions} and @ref{Titlepage & Copyright Page} "
"specification.  It is important for the @LaTeX{} output format as the end of "
"preamble is where the @code{\\begin@{document@}} line is output.  In other "
"output formats it may be used to determine how some special output is "
"formatted, for example @ref{@code{@@copying}} output as a comment at the "
"beginning of output files, or the language used in file headers."
msgstr ""
"O início do arquivo do Texinfo até o primeiro conteúdo que é gerado como "
"parte do corpo principal do documento é o @dfn{preâmbulo}. Ele inclui o "
"cabeçalho, @ref{Permissões do Documento} e a especificação @ref{Página "
"de Título e Página de Copyright}. É importante para o formato de saída "
"do @LaTeX{}, pois o fim do preâmbulo é onde a linha "
"@code{\begin@{document@}} é gerada. Em outros formatos de saída, ele pode "
"ser usado para determinar como alguma saída especial é formatada, por "
"exemplo, a saída @ref{@code{@@copying}} como um comentário no início dos "
"arquivos de saída ou o idioma usado nos cabeçalhos de arquivo."

#. type: node
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:1081
#, no-wrap
msgid "First Line"
msgstr "Primeira Linha"

#. type: subsection
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:1082
#, no-wrap
msgid "The First Line of a Texinfo File"
msgstr "A Primeira Linha de um Arquivo do Texinfo"

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:1084
#, no-wrap
msgid "@nodedescription The first line of a Texinfo file."
msgstr "@nodedescription A primeira linha de um arquivo do Texinfo."

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:1084
#, no-wrap
msgid "First line of a Texinfo file"
msgstr "Primeira linha de um arquivo do Texinfo"

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:1085
#, no-wrap
msgid "Beginning line of a Texinfo file"
msgstr "Linha inicial de um arquivo do Texinfo"

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:1086
#, no-wrap
msgid "Header of a Texinfo file"
msgstr "Cabeçalho de um arquivo do Texinfo"

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:1090
msgid ""
"Every Texinfo file that is to be the top-level input to @TeX{} must begin "
"with a line that looks like this:"
msgstr ""
"Cada arquivo do Texinfo que deva ser a entrada de nível superior para "
"@TeX{} precisa começar com uma linha semelhante a esta:"

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:1104
msgid ""
"When the file is processed by @TeX{}, the @samp{\\input texinfo} command "
"tells @TeX{} to load the macros needed for processing a Texinfo file.  These "
"are in a file called @file{texinfo.tex}, which should have been installed on "
"your system along with either the @TeX{} or Texinfo software.  @TeX{} uses "
"the backslash, @samp{\\}, to mark the beginning of a command, exactly as "
"Texinfo uses @samp{@@}.  The @file{texinfo.tex} file causes the switch from "
"@samp{\\} to @samp{@@}; before the switch occurs, @TeX{} requires @samp{\\}, "
"which is why it appears at the beginning of the file."
msgstr ""
"Quando o arquivo for processado pelo @TeX{}, o comando @samp{\\input "
"texinfo} diz ao @TeX{} para carregar as macros necessárias para processar "
"um arquivo do Texinfo. Elas estão em um arquivo chamado @file{texinfo.tex}, "
"que deveria ter sido instalado no teu sistema ou junto com o software @TeX{} "
"ou com o Texinfo. O @TeX{} usa a barra invertida, @samp{\\}, para marcar o "
"início de um comando, exatamente como o Texinfo usa @samp{@@}. O arquivo "
"@file{texinfo.tex} causa a comutação de @samp{\\} para @samp{@@}; antes "
"que a comutação ocorra, o @TeX{} exige @samp{\\}, e é por isso que ela "
"aparece no início do arquivo."

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:1107
msgid ""
"You may optionally follow this line with a comment to tell GNU Emacs to use "
"Texinfo mode when the file is edited:"
msgstr ""
"Opcionalmente, você pode seguir essa linha com um comentário para informar "
"ao GNU Emacs para usar o modo Texinfo quando o arquivo for editado:"

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:1114
msgid "from the file extension automatically."
msgstr ""

#. type: node
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:1116
#, no-wrap
msgid "@code{@@setfilename}"
msgstr "@code{@@setfilename}"

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:1118
msgid "@nodedescription Give the name of the output file."
msgstr "@nodedescription Forneça o nome do arquivo da saída gerada."

#. type: subsection
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:1118
#, no-wrap
msgid "@code{@@setfilename}: Set the Output File Name"
msgstr "@code{@@setfilename}: Configure o Nome do Arquivo da Saída Gerada"

#. type: findex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:1125
#, no-wrap
msgid "setfilename"
msgstr "setfilename"

#. type: anchor{#1}
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:1125
msgid "Setting the Output File Name"
msgstr "Configurando o Nome do Arquivo da Saída Gerada"

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:1126
#, no-wrap
msgid "output file name"
msgstr "Nome do arquivo da saída gerada"

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:1134
msgid ""
"The @code{@@setfilename} line specifies the name of the output file to be "
"generated by @command{texi2any}.  This command is ignored for @TeX{} "
"formatting.  When present, it should be the first Texinfo command (that is, "
"after @samp{\\input texinfo}).  Write the @code{@@setfilename} command at "
"the beginning of a line and follow it on the same line by the Info file name."
msgstr ""
"A linha @code{@@setfilename} especifica o nome do arquivo de saída a ser "
"gerado por @command{texi2any}. Esse comando é ignorado para formatação "
"@TeX{}. Quando presente, deveria ser o primeiro comando do Texinfo (isto é, "
"depois de @samp{\\input texinfo}). Escreva o comando @code{@@setfilename} no "
"início de uma linha e siga-o na mesma linha pelo nome do arquivo do Info."

#. type: example
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:1137
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@setfilename @var{info-file-name}\n"
msgstr "@@setfilename @var{nome-arquivo-info}\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:1145
msgid ""
"The name must be different from the name of the Texinfo file.  There are two "
"conventions for choosing the name: you can either remove the extension (such "
"as @samp{.texi}) entirely from the input file name, or (recommended) replace "
"it with the @samp{.info} extension.  It is not advised to base the "
"@code{@@setfilename} name on a entirely different name than the input file "
"name."
msgstr ""
"O nome precisa ser diferente do nome do arquivo do Texinfo. Existem duas "
"convenções para escolher o nome: você pode ou remover a extensão (como "
"@samp{.texi}) inteiramente do nome do arquivo de entrada ou (recomendado) "
"substituí-la pela extensão @samp{.info}. Não é aconselhável basear o "
"nome de @code{@@setfilename} em um nome totalmente diferente do nome do "
"arquivo de entrada."

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:1146
#, no-wrap
msgid "Ignored before @code{@@setfilename}"
msgstr "Ignorado antes de @code{@@setfilename}"

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:1147
#, no-wrap
msgid "@samp{\\input} source line ignored"
msgstr "linha @samp{\\input} do fonte ignorada"

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:1152
msgid ""
"When a @code{@@setfilename} line is present, the Texinfo processors ignore "
"everything written before the @code{@@setfilename} line.  This is why the "
"very first line of the file (the @code{\\input} line) does not show up in "
"the output."
msgstr ""
"Quando uma linha @code{@@setfilename} está presente, os processadores do "
"Texinfo ignoram tudo escrito antes da linha @code{@@setfilename}. É por "
"isso que a primeiríssima linha do arquivo (a linha @code{\input}) não "
"aparece na saída gerada."

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:1157
msgid ""
"If there is no @code{@@setfilename} line, @command{texi2any} uses the input "
"file name to determine the output name (@pxref{Minimum}).  The "
"@code{\\input} line is still ignored in this processing, as well as leading "
"blank lines."
msgstr ""
"Se não existir nenhuma linha @code{@@setfilename}, @command{texi2any} "
"usará o nome do arquivo de entrada para determinar o nome da saída "
"(@pxref{Mínimo}). A linha @code{\\input} ainda será ignorada nesse "
"processamento, assim como as linhas em branco iniciais."

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:1162
msgid ""
"When producing another output format, @command{texi2any} will replace any "
"final extension with the output format-specific extension (@samp{html} when "
"generating HTML, for example), or add a dot followed by the extension "
"(@samp{.html} for HTML) if the given name has no extension."
msgstr ""
"Ao produzir outro formato de saída, @command{texi2any} substituirá "
"qualquer extensão final pela extensão específica do formato de saída "
"(@samp{html} ao gerar HTML, por exemplo) ou adicionará um ponto seguido "
"pela extensão (@samp{.html} para HTML) se o nome fornecido não tiver "
"extensão."

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:1166
msgid ""
"@@-commands are not allowed in @code{@@setfilename}, except for @code{@@@@}, "
"@code{@@@{}, @code{@@@}} and associated @@-commands such as "
"@code{@@atchar@{@}}."
msgstr ""
"Comandos @@ não são permitidos em @code{@@setfilename}, exceto para "
"@code{@@@@}, @code{@@@{}, @code{@@@}} e comandos @@ associados, como "
"@code{@@atchar@{@}}."

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:1175
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"@code{@@setfilename} used to be required by the Texinfo processors and some "
"other programs.  This should not be the case any more; @code{@@setfilename} "
"can be omitted.  If the Texinfo input is processed from standard input, "
"without an input file name to deduce the base file name from, "
"@code{@@setfilename} could still be relevant.  This is not the only way, "
"however: @option{--output} option specifies the output file name on the "
"@command{texi2any} command-line (@pxref{Invoking @command{texi2any}})."
msgstr ""
"@code{@@setfilename} costumava ser exigido pelos processadores do Texinfo e "
"por alguns outros programas. Isso não mais deveria ser o caso; "
"@code{@@setfilename} pode ser omitido. Se a entrada do Texinfo for "
"processada a partir da entrada padrão, sem um nome de arquivo de entrada "
"para deduzir o nome base do arquivo, @code{@@setfilename} ainda poderia ser "
"relevante. No entanto, essa não é a única maneira: a opção "
"@option{--output} especifica o nome do arquivo de saída na linha de comando "
"do @command{texi2any} (@pxref{Invocando @command{texi2any}})."

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:1176
#, no-wrap
msgid "Length of file names"
msgstr "Comprimento dos nomes dos arquivos"

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:1177
#, no-wrap
msgid "File name collision"
msgstr "Colisão de nome de arquivo"

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:1178
#, no-wrap
msgid "Info file name, choosing"
msgstr "Nome do arquivo do Info, escolhendo"

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:1191
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Although an explicit @samp{.info} extension is preferable, some operating "
"systems cannot handle long file names.  You can run into a problem even when "
"the file name you specify is itself short enough.  This occurs because the "
"Info formatters split a long Info file into short indirect subfiles, and "
"name them by appending @samp{-1}, @samp{-2}, @dots{}, @samp{-10}, "
"@samp{-11}, and so on, to the original file name.  (@xref{Tag and Split "
"Files}.)  The subfile name @file{texinfo.info-10}, for example, is too long "
"for old systems with a 14-character limit on filenames; so the Info file "
"name for this document could be @file{texinfo} rather than "
"@file{texinfo.info} on such a system.  @code{@@setfilename} is a way to "
"specify an alternative name."
msgstr ""
"Embora uma extensão @samp{.info} explícita seja preferível, alguns "
"sistemas operacionais não conseguem lidar com nomes longos de arquivo. "
"Você pode ter um problema mesmo quando o nome do arquivo que especificar "
"for curto o suficiente. Isso ocorre porque os formatadores do Info dividem "
"um arquivo longo do Info em subarquivos curtos indiretos e os nomeiam "
"pospondo @samp{-1}, @samp{-2}, @dots{}, @samp{-10}, @samp{-11} e assim por "
"diante ao nome original do arquivo. (@xref{Arquivos de Etiqueta e de "
"Divisão}.) O nome do subarquivo @file{texinfo.info-10}, por exemplo, é "
"muito longo para sistemas antigos com um limite de 14 caracteres sobre nomes "
"de arquivo; portanto, o nome do arquivo do Info para esse documento poderia "
"ser @file{texinfo} em vez de @file{texinfo.info} em tal sistema. "
"@code{@@setfilename} é uma maneira de especificar um nome alternativo."

#. type: node
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:1193
#, no-wrap
msgid "@code{@@settitle}"
msgstr "@code{@@settitle}"

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:1195
msgid "@nodedescription Create a title for the printed work."
msgstr "@nodedescription Crie um título para o trabalho impresso."

#. type: subsection
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:1195
#, no-wrap
msgid "@code{@@settitle}: Set the Document Title"
msgstr "@code{@@settitle}: Configura o Título do Documento"

#. type: findex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:1198
#, no-wrap
msgid "settitle"
msgstr "settitle"

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:1199
#, no-wrap
msgid "Document title, specifying"
msgstr "Título de documento, especificando"

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:1202
msgid "A Texinfo file should contain a line that looks like this:"
msgstr "Um arquivo Texinfo deveria conter uma linha que se pareça com isto:"

#. type: example
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:1205
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@settitle @var{title}\n"
msgstr "@@settitle @var{título}\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:1213
msgid ""
"Write the @code{@@settitle} command at the beginning of a line and follow it "
"on the same line by the title.  Do not write anything else on the line.  The "
"@code{@@settitle} command should precede everything that generates actual "
"output.  The best place for it is right after the @code{@@setfilename} "
"command, if present (described in the previous section)."
msgstr ""
"Escreva o comando @code{@@settitle} no início de uma linha e siga-o na "
"mesma pelo título.  Não escreva nada mais na linha.  O comando "
"@code{@@settitle} deveria preceder tudo o que gera saída atual.  O melhor "
"lugar para ele é logo depois do comando @code{@@setfilename}, se presente "
"(descrito na seção anterior)."

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:1217
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This command gives the title to use in a header or footer for double-sided "
"printed output, in case such headings are output.  For more on headings for "
"printed output, see @ref{Heading Generation}."
msgstr ""
"Esse comando fornece o título para se usar em um cabeçalho ou rodapé para "
"saída impressa frente e verso, caso tais títulos sejam produzidos. Para "
"mais acerca de títulos para saída impressa, veja-se @ref{Geração de "
"Títulos}."

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:1218
#, no-wrap
msgid "@code{<title>} HTML tag"
msgstr "Etiqueta @code{<title>} do HTML"

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:1221
msgid ""
"In HTML, @var{title} serves as the document @samp{<title>} and it becomes "
"the default document description in the @samp{<head>} part."
msgstr ""
"Em HTML, @var{title} serve como o @samp{<title>} do documento e se torna a "
"descrição padrão do documento na parte @samp{<head>}."

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:1229
msgid ""
"When the title page is used in the output, as is generally the case for "
"printed output, the title in the @code{@@settitle} command does not affect "
"the title as it appears on the title page.  Thus, the two do not need not to "
"match exactly.  A practice we recommend is to include the version or edition "
"number of the manual in the @code{@@settitle} title; on the title page, the "
"version number generally appears as a @code{@@subtitle} so it would be "
"omitted from the @code{@@title}.  @xref{@code{@@titlepage}}."
msgstr ""
"Quando a página de título for usada na saída gerada, como geralmente é o "
"caso para saída impressa, o título no comando @code{@@settitle} não afeta "
"o título conforme ele aparece na página de título. Assim, os dois não "
"precisam não corresponder exatamente. Uma prática que nós recomendamos é "
"a de incluir o número da versão ou o da edição do manual no título "
"@code{@@settitle}; na página de título, o número da versão geralmente "
"aparece como um @code{@@subtitle}, de forma que ele seria omitido do "
"@code{@@title}. @xref{@code{@@titlepage}}."

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:1231
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:1233
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:1234
#, no-wrap
msgid "Preamble"
msgstr "Preâmbulo"

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:1233
msgid "@nodedescription Start of the Texinfo file up to first content."
msgstr ""
"@nodedescription Início do arquivo do Texinfo até o primeiro conteúdo."

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:1235
#, no-wrap
msgid "Texinfo Preamble"
msgstr "Preâmbulo do Texinfo"

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:1242
msgid ""
"The @dfn{preamble} starts at the beginning of the Texinfo file and continues "
"until the first directly output material.  It typically includes the file "
"header (@pxref{Texinfo File Header}), the @code{@@copying} block specifying "
"the document permissions (@pxref{@code{@@copying}}) and the "
"@code{@@titlepage} specification (@pxref{Titlepage & Copyright Page})."
msgstr ""
"O @dfn{preâmbulo} começa no início do arquivo do Texinfo e continua até "
"o primeiro material diretamente produzido. Ele tipicamente inclui o "
"cabeçalho do arquivo (@pxref{Cabeçalho do Arquivo do Texinfo}), o bloco "
"@code{@@copying} especificando as permissões do documento "
"(@pxref{@code{@@copying}}) e a especificação @code{@@titlepage} "
"(@pxref{Página de Título e Página de Direitos Autorais})."

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:1249
msgid ""
"The preamble may contain commands that affect document formatting as a whole "
"but which do not produce output, or do not produce output straight away, "
"such as @code{@@settitle} (@pxref{@code{@@settitle}}), "
"@code{@@documentlanguage}, (@pxref{@code{@@documentlanguage}}), commands "
"setting the headings, controlling indentation or hyphenation, or the table "
"of contents (@pxref{Contents})."
msgstr ""
"O preâmbulo pode conter comandos que afetam a formatação do documento "
"como um todo, mas que não produzem saída, ou não produzem saída "
"imediatamente, como @code{@@settitle} (@pxref{@code{@@settitle}}), "
"@code{@@documentlanguage}, (@pxref{@code{@@documentlanguage}}), comandos que "
"definem os títulos, controlam o recuo ou a hifenização, ou o sumário "
"(@pxref{Conteúdo})."

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:1261
msgid ""
"Any text that starts a paragraph, @@-commands that are formatted as "
"quotations, tables, lists and so on, and @code{@@node} (@pxref{Nodes})  and "
"chapter structuring commands (@pxref{Chapter Structuring}) end the preamble."
msgstr ""
"Qualquer texto que inicia um parágrafo, comandos @@ que são formatados "
"como citações, tabelas, listas e assim por diante, e @code{@@node} "
"(@pxref{Nós}) e comandos de estruturação de capítulos "
"(@pxref{Estruturação de Capítulos}) encerram o preâmbulo."

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:1264
msgid ""
"The concept of the preamble is significant for @LaTeX{} output, as the "
"@code{\\begin@{document@}} line is output at the end of the preamble."
msgstr ""
"O conceito de preâmbulo é significativo para a saída do @LaTeX{}, pois a "
"linha @code{\\begin@{document@}} é gerada no final do preâmbulo."

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:1268
msgid ""
"In plaintext, the preamble is simply output as usual at the beginning of the "
"document; for example, a @code{@@contents} in the preamble is output as the "
"table of contents (@pxref{Contents})."
msgstr ""
"Em texto simples, o preâmbulo é simplesmente gerado como de costume no "
"início do documento; por exemplo, um @code{@@contents} no preâmbulo é "
"gerado como o sumário (@pxref{Conteúdo})."

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:1274
msgid ""
"There is not much special treatment of the preamble for HTML and Info output "
"either.  However, some settings current at the very end of the preamble may "
"be used for the document as a whole, regardless of what follows.  This may "
"apply to commands specifying the indentation, or the language "
"(@pxref{@code{@@documentlanguage}})."
msgstr ""
"Também não existe muito tratamento especial do preâmbulo para saída HTML "
"e Info. No entanto, algumas configurações atuais no finalzinho do "
"preâmbulo podem ser usadas para o documento como um todo, independentemente "
"do que se segue. Isso pode se aplicar a comandos que especificam o recuo ou "
"o idioma (@pxref{@code{@@documentlanguage}})."

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:1279
msgid ""
"For example, for the following document, the HTML and Info copying comments "
"are formatted with @code{@@documentlanguage} set to @samp{pt}, as it is the "
"last @code{@@documentlanguage} before the end of the preamble."
msgstr ""
"Por exemplo, para o documento a seguir, os comentários de cópia de HTML e "
"de Info são formatados com @code{@@documentlanguage} configurado como "
"@samp{pt}, pois é o último @code{@@documentlanguage} antes do final do "
"preâmbulo."

#. type: group
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:1284
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"@@documentlanguage fr\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
"@@documentlanguage fr\n"
"\n"

#. type: group
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:1288
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"@@copying\n"
"The copying information @@error@{@} some text\n"
"@@end copying\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
"@@copying\n"
"A informação de cópia @@error@{@} algum texto\n"
"@@end copying\n"
"\n"

#. type: group
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:1290
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"@@documentlanguage pt\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
"@@documentlanguage pt\n"
"\n"

#. type: group
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:1292
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Text ending the preamble\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
"Texto finalizando o preâmbulo\n"
"\n"

#. type: group
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:1294
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"@@documentlanguage de\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
"@@documentlanguage de\n"
"\n"

#. type: group
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:1296
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"@@node Top\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
"@@node Top\n"
"\n"

#. type: node
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:1301
#, no-wrap
msgid "Start and End of Header"
msgstr "Início e Fim do Cabeçalho"

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:1303
msgid "@nodedescription Formatting a region in Emacs requires this."
msgstr "@nodedescription Formatar uma região no Emacs exige isto."

#. type: subsection
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:1303
#, no-wrap
msgid "Start and End of Header for Emacs"
msgstr "Início e Fim do Cabeçalho para Emacs"

#.  nome antigo
#. type: anchor{#1}
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:1305
msgid "Start of Header"
msgstr "Início do Cabeçalho"

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:1305
#, no-wrap
msgid "Start of header line"
msgstr "Início da linha de cabeçalho"

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:1311
msgid ""
"In Emacs, start- and end-of-header lines can be used to enclose commands "
"that globally affect the document in the Texinfo preambule.  This allows you "
"to format only part of a Texinfo file for Info or printing.  "
"@xref{@code{texinfo-format} commands}."
msgstr ""
"No Emacs, as linhas de início e de fim de cabeçalho podem ser usadas para "
"cercar comandos que afetam globalmente o documento no preâmbulo do Texinfo. "
"Isso permite que você formate somente parte de um arquivo do Texinfo para "
"Info ou impressão. @xref{Comandos @code{texinfo-format}}."

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:1313
msgid "A start-of-header line is a Texinfo comment that looks like this:"
msgstr ""
"Uma linha de início de cabeçalho é um comentário do Texinfo que se "
"parece com isto:"

#. type: example
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:1316
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@c %**start of header\n"
msgstr "@@c %**start of header\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:1322
msgid ""
"Write the start-of-header line on the second line of a Texinfo file.  Follow "
"the start-of-header commands that globally affect the document formatting, "
"such as @code{@@settitle}, @code{@@synindex} or @code{@@footnotestyle}; and "
"then by an @w{end-of-header} line."
msgstr ""
"Escreva a linha de início de cabeçalho na segunda linha de um arquivo do "
"Texinfo. Siga os comandos de início de cabeçalho que afetam globalmente a "
"formatação do documento, como @code{@@settitle}, @code{@@synindex} ou "
"@code{@@footnotestyle}; e então por uma linha @w{end-of-header}."

#.  nome antigo
#. type: anchor{#1}
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:1324
msgid "End of Header"
msgstr "Fim do Cabeçalho"

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:1324
#, no-wrap
msgid "End of header line"
msgstr "Linha de fim do cabeçalho"

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:1327
msgid "A end-of-header line is a Texinfo comment that looks like this:"
msgstr ""
"Uma linha de fim de cabeçalho é um comentário do Texinfo que se parece "
"com isto:"

#. type: example
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:1330
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@c %**end of header\n"
msgstr "@@c %**end of header\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:1336
msgid ""
"The odd string of characters, @samp{%**}, is to ensure that no other comment "
"is accidentally taken for a start-of-header line.  You can change it if you "
"wish by setting the @code{tex-start-of-header} and/or "
"@code{tex-end-of-header} Emacs variables.  @xref{Texinfo Mode Printing}."
msgstr ""
"A estranha sequência de caracteres, @samp{%**}, é para garantir que nenhum "
"outro comentário seja acidentalmente tomado como uma linha de início de "
"cabeçalho. Você pode mudá-la se desejar, configurando as variáveis do "
"Emacs @code{tex-start-of-header} e (ou) @code{tex-end-of-header}. "
"@xref{Impressão no Modo Texinfo}."

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:1339
msgid ""
"The start- and end-of-header lines are not part of the Texinfo format "
"specification, which is why they are implemented with comments."
msgstr ""
"As linhas de início e fim do cabeçalho não são parte da especificação "
"do formato do Texinfo, e é por isso que são implementadas com comentários."

#. type: section
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:1341
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:1343
#, no-wrap
msgid "Directory Category"
msgstr "Categoria de Diretório"

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:1343
msgid "@nodedescription A category for a manual."
msgstr "@nodedescription Uma categoria para um manual."

#. type: findex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:1345
#, no-wrap
msgid "dircategory"
msgstr "dircategory"

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:1346
#, no-wrap
msgid "Dir categories, choosing"
msgstr "Categorias de diretório, escolhendo"

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:1347
#, no-wrap
msgid "Categories, choosing"
msgstr "Categorias, escolhendo"

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:1353
msgid ""
"Use the @code{@@dircategory} command to specify a category for the manual.  "
"Here are a few examples of category names:"
msgstr ""
"Use o comando @code{@@dircategory} para especificar uma categoria para o "
"manual. Aqui estão alguns exemplos de nomes de categorias:"

#. type: display
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:1371
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Basics\n"
"Text creation and manipulation\n"
"Archiving\n"
"Compression\n"
"Database\n"
"Editors\n"
"Emacs\n"
"Email\n"
"Graphics\n"
"Localization\n"
"Network applications\n"
"Printing\n"
"Science\n"
"Software development\n"
"Software libraries\n"
"Version control\n"
msgstr ""
"Fundamentos\n"
"Criação e manipulação de texto\n"
"Arquivamento\n"
"Compressão\n"
"Base de dados\n"
"Editores\n"
"Emacs\n"
"Mensagens eletrônicas\n"
"Gráficos\n"
"Localização\n"
"Aplicativos de rede de intercomunicação\n"
"Impressão\n"
"Ciência\n"
"Desenvolvimento de software\n"
"Bibliotecas de software\n"
"Controle de versão\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:1376
msgid ""
"@code{@@dircategory} commands are usually followed by a @code{@@direntry} "
"blocks, which are used by @command{install-info}.  @xref{Installing Dir "
"Entries}, for details."
msgstr ""
"Comandos @code{@@dircategory} geralmente são seguidos por uns blocos "
"@code{@@direntry}, que são usados pelo @command{install-info}. "
"@xref{Instalando Entradas de Diretório}, para detalhes."

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:1380
msgid ""
"The first @code{@@dircategory} command in a manual is the category for the "
"entire manual.  Subsequent uses of @code{@@dircategory} set the category for "
"following @code{@@direntry} blocks only."
msgstr ""
"O primeiro comando @code{@@dircategory} em um manual é a categoria para o "
"manual inteiro. Usos subsequentes de @code{@@dircategory} configuram a "
"categoria somente para blocos @code{@@direntry} seguintes."

#. type: section
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:1382
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:1385
#, no-wrap
msgid "Document Permissions"
msgstr "Permissões de Documentos"

#.  nome antigo de nó
#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:1385
msgid "@nodedescription Ensuring your manual is free."
msgstr "@nodedescription Garantindo que teu manual seja livre."

#. type: anchor{#1}
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:1385
msgid "Software Copying Permissions"
msgstr "Permissões de Cópia de Software"

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:1386
#, no-wrap
msgid "Document permissions"
msgstr "Permissões de documentos"

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:1387
#, no-wrap
msgid "Copying permissions"
msgstr "Permissões de cópia"

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:1393
msgid ""
"This segment describes the document and contains the copyright notice and "
"copying permissions.  This is done with the @code{@@copying} command.  A "
"real manual includes more text here, according to the license under which it "
"is distributed."
msgstr ""
"Este segmento descreve o documento e contém o aviso de direitos autorais e "
"permissões de cópia. Isso é feito com o comando @code{@@copying}. Um "
"manual real inclui mais texto aqui, de acordo com a licença sob a qual ele "
"é distribuído."

#. type: group
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:1398
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"@@copying\n"
"This is a short example of a complete Texinfo file, version 1.0.\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
"@@copying\n"
"Este é um exemplo curto de um arquivo completo do Texinfo, versão 1.0.\n"
"\n"

#. type: group
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:1401
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Copyright @@copyright@{@} 2016 Free Software Foundation, Inc.\n"
"@@end copying\n"
msgstr ""
"Copyright @@copyright@{@} 2016 Free Software Foundation, Inc.\n"
"@@end copying\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:1409
msgid ""
"The copyright notice and copying permissions for a document need to appear "
"in several places in the various Texinfo output formats.  Therefore, Texinfo "
"provides a command (@code{@@copying}) to declare this text once, and another "
"command (@code{@@insertcopying}) to insert the text at appropriate points."
msgstr ""
"O aviso de direitos autorais e as permissões de cópia para um documento "
"precisam aparecer em vários lugares nos vários formatos da saída gerada "
"do Texinfo. Portanto, o Texinfo fornece um comando (@code{@@copying}) para "
"declarar esse texto uma vez, e outro comando (@code{@@insertcopying}) para "
"inserir o texto nos pontos apropriados."

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:1416
msgid ""
"If the document is a software manual, the software is typically under a "
"different license---for GNU and many other free software packages, software "
"is usually released under the GNU GPL, and manuals are released under the "
"GNU FDL@.  It is helpful to state the license of the software of the manual, "
"but giving the complete text of the software license is not necessarily "
"required."
msgstr ""
"Se o documento for um manual de software, o software tipicamente está sob "
"uma licença diferente---para GNU e muitos outros pacotes de software livre, "
"o software geralmente é lançado sob a GNU GPL, e os manuais são lançados "
"sob a GNU FDL@. É útil declarar a licença do software do manual, mas "
"fornecer o texto completo da licença do software não é necessariamente "
"exigido."

#. type: node
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:1418
#, no-wrap
msgid "@code{@@copying}"
msgstr "@code{@@copying}"

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:1420
msgid "@nodedescription Declare the document's copying permissions."
msgstr "@nodedescription Declare as permissões de cópia do documento."

#. type: subsection
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:1420
#, no-wrap
msgid "@code{@@copying}: Declare Copying Permissions"
msgstr "@code{@@copying}: Declarar Permissões de Cópia"

#. type: findex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:1423
#, no-wrap
msgid "copying"
msgstr "copying"

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:1431
msgid ""
"The @code{@@copying} command should be given very early in the document; the "
"recommended location is right after the header material (@pxref{Texinfo File "
"Header}).  It conventionally consists of a sentence or two about what the "
"program is, identification of the documentation itself, the legal copyright "
"line, and the copying permissions.  Here is a skeletal example:"
msgstr ""
"O comando @code{@@copying} deveria ser fornecido bem no início do "
"documento; o local recomendado é logo depois do material do cabeçalho "
"(@pxref{Cabeçalho do Arquivo do Texinfo}). Ele consiste convencionalmente "
"em uma ou duas frases acerca do que é o programa, identificação da "
"documentação em si, a linha jurídica de direitos autorais e as "
"permissões de cópia. Aqui está um exemplo esquelético:"

#. type: example
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:1436
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"@@copying\n"
"This manual is for @var{program} (version @var{version}, updated\n"
"@var{date}), which @dots{}\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
"@@copying\n"
"Este manual é para @var{programa} (versão @var{versão}, atualizado "
"@var{data}), que @dots{}\n"

#. type: example
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:1438
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Copyright @@copyright@{@} @var{years} @var{copyright-owner}.\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""
"Copyright @@copyright@{@} @var{anos} @var{titular-copyright}.\n"
"\n"

#. type: example
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:1443
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"@@quotation\n"
"Permission is granted to @dots{}\n"
"@@end quotation\n"
"@@end copying\n"
msgstr ""
"@@quotation\n"
"Permissão é concedida para @dots{}\n"
"@@end quotation\n"
"@@end copying\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:1447
msgid ""
"The @code{@@quotation} has no legal significance; it's there to improve "
"readability in some contexts."
msgstr ""
"O @code{@@quotation} não tem significado jurídico; ele está lá para "
"melhorar a legibilidade em alguns contextos."

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:1454
msgid ""
"The text of @code{@@copying} appears as a comment at the beginning of Info "
"and HTML output files.  This information is also output at the beginning of "
"the DocBook output files using appropriate markup.  It is @emph{not} output "
"implicitly in plain text or printed output; it's up to you to use "
"@code{@@insertcopying} to emit the copying information.  See the next "
"section for details."
msgstr ""
"O texto de @code{@@copying} aparece como um comentário no início dos "
"arquivos da saída gerada do Info e de HTML. Essas informações também "
"são geradas no início dos arquivos da saída gerada do DocBook usando-se "
"marcação apropriada. Elas @emph{não} são geradas implicitamente em texto "
"simples ou em saída impressa; cabe inteiramente a você usar "
"@code{@@insertcopying} para emitir as informações de cópia. Veja-se a "
"próxima seção para detalhes."

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:1459
msgid ""
"The @code{@@copyright@{@}} command generates a @samp{c} inside a circle when "
"the output format supports this glyph (print and HTML always do, for "
"instance).  When the glyph is not supported in the output, it generates the "
"three-character sequence @samp{(C)}."
msgstr ""
"O comando @code{@@copyright@{@}} gera um @samp{c} dentro de um círculo "
"quando o formato da saída gerada suportar esse glifo (impressa e HTML "
"sempre suportam, por exemplo). Quando o glifo não for suportado na saída "
"gerada, ele gera a sequência de três caracteres @samp{(C)}."

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:1462
msgid "The copyright notice itself has the following legally-prescribed form:"
msgstr ""
"O aviso de direitos autorais em si tem o seguinte formato juridicamente "
"prescrito:"

#. type: example
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:1465
#, no-wrap
msgid "Copyright @copyright{} @var{years} @var{copyright-owner}.\n"
msgstr "Copyright @copyright{} @var{anos} @var{titular-copyright}.\n"

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:1467
#, no-wrap
msgid "Copyright word, always in English"
msgstr "Palavra Copyright, sempre em inglês"

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:1471
msgid ""
"The word `Copyright' must always be written in English, even if the document "
"is otherwise written in another language.  This is due to international law."
msgstr ""
"A palavra `Copyright' precisa sempre estar escrita em inglês, mesmo que o "
"documento esteja escrito em outro idioma. Isso é devido ao direito "
"internacional."

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:1472
#, no-wrap
msgid "Years, in copyright line"
msgstr "Anos, na linha de direitos autorais"

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:1477
msgid ""
"The list of years should include all years in which a version was completed "
"(even if it was released in a subsequent year).  It is simplest for each "
"year to be written out individually and in full, separated by commas."
msgstr ""
"A lista de anos deveria incluir todos os anos nos quais uma versão foi "
"concluída (mesmo se ela foi lançada em um ano subsequente). É mais "
"simples que cada ano esteja escrito individualmente e por completo, separado "
"por vírgulas."

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:1478
#, no-wrap
msgid "Copyright holder for FSF works"
msgstr "Titular dos direitos autorais para obras da FSF"

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:1479
#, no-wrap
msgid "Holder of copyright for FSF works"
msgstr "Obras da FSF, Titular dos direitos autorais das"

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:1480
#, no-wrap
msgid "Owner of copyright for FSF works"
msgstr "Proprietário(a) dos direitos autorais das obras da FSF"

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:1484
msgid ""
"The copyright owner (or owners) is whoever holds legal copyright on the "
"work.  In the case of works assigned to the FSF, the owner is `Free Software "
"Foundation, Inc.'."
msgstr ""
"O(A) proprietário(a) (ou proprietários(as)) dos direitos autorais é quem "
"titularizar os direitos autorais sobre a obra. No caso de obras atribuídas "
"à FSF, o(a) proprietário(a) é `Free Software Foundation, Inc.'."

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:1490
msgid ""
"The copyright `line' may actually be split across multiple lines, both in "
"the source document and in the output.  This often happens for documents "
"with a long history, having many different years of publication.  If you do "
"use several lines, do not indent any of them (or anything else in the "
"@code{@@copying} block) in the source file."
msgstr ""
"A `linha' de direitos autorais pode, na verdade, ser dividida em várias "
"linhas, tanto no documento fonte quanto na saída gerada. Isso geralmente "
"acontece para documentos com um longo histórico, tendo muitos anos de "
"publicação. Se você usar várias linhas, não recue nenhuma delas (ou "
"qualquer outra coisa no bloco @code{@@copying}) no arquivo fonte."

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:1496
msgid ""
"@xref{Copyright Notices,,, maintain, GNU Maintainer Information}, for "
"additional information.  @xref{GNU Sample Texts}, for the full text to be "
"used in GNU manuals.  @xref{GNU Free Documentation License}, for the license "
"itself under which GNU and other free manuals are distributed."
msgstr ""
"@xref{Copyright Notices,,, maintain, Informações do(a) Mantenedor(a) GNU}, "
"para informações adicionais. @xref{Textos GNU de Amostra}, para o texto "
"completo a ser usado nos manuais GNU. @xref{Licença GNU de Documentação "
"Livre}, para a licença em si sob a qual o GNU e outros manuais livres são "
"distribuídos."

#. type: node
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:1498
#, no-wrap
msgid "@code{@@insertcopying}"
msgstr "@code{@@insertcopying}"

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:1500
msgid "@nodedescription Where to insert the permissions."
msgstr "@nodedescription Onde inserir as permissões."

#. type: subsection
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:1500
#, no-wrap
msgid "@code{@@insertcopying}: Include Permissions Text"
msgstr "@code{@@insertcopying}: Incluir Texto de Permissões"

#. type: findex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:1503
#, no-wrap
msgid "insertcopying"
msgstr "insertcopying"

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:1504
#, no-wrap
msgid "Copying text, including"
msgstr "Texto de reprodução, incluindo"

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:1505
#, no-wrap
msgid "Permissions text, including"
msgstr "Texto das permissões, incluindo"

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:1506
#, no-wrap
msgid "Including permissions text"
msgstr "Incluindo texto das permissões"

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:1510
msgid ""
"The @code{@@insertcopying} command is simply written on a line by itself, "
"like this:"
msgstr ""
"O comando @code{@@insertcopying} simplesmente é escrito em uma linha "
"própria, como esta:"

#. type: example
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:1513
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:1829
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@insertcopying\n"
msgstr "@@insertcopying\n"

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:1518
msgid ""
"This inserts the text previously defined by @code{@@copying}.  To meet legal "
"requirements, it must be used on the copyright page in the printed manual "
"(@pxref{Copyright})."
msgstr ""
"Isso insere o texto previamente definido por @code{@@copying}.  Para atender "
"às exigências jurídicas, ele precisa ser usado na página de direitos "
"autorais no manual impresso (veja-se @ref{Direitos Autorais})."

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:1527
msgid ""
"The @code{@@copying} command itself causes the permissions text to appear in "
"an Info file @emph{before} the first node.  The text is also copied into the "
"beginning of each split Info output file, as is legally necessary.  This "
"location implies a human reading the manual using Info does @emph{not} see "
"this text (except when using the advanced Info command @kbd{g *}). This does "
"not matter for legal purposes, because the text is present.  But to get a "
"visible text in the output, @code{@@insertcopying} should be used."
msgstr ""
"O próprio comando @code{@@copying} faz com que o texto das permissões "
"apareça em um arquivo Info @emph{antes} do primeiro nó.  O texto também "
"é copiado no início de cada arquivo dividido de saída Info, como é "
"juridicamente necessário. Esse local implica que um humano lendo o manual "
"usando Info @emph{não} vê esse texto (exceto quando usar o comando "
"avançado @kbd{g *} do Info). Isso não importa para propósitos jurídicos, "
"pois o texto está presente. Mas, para obter um texto visível na saída "
"gerada, @code{@@insertcopying} deveria ser usado."

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:1532
msgid ""
"Similarly, the @code{@@copying} text is automatically included at the "
"beginning of each HTML output file, as an HTML comment.  Again, this text is "
"not visible without @code{@@insertcopying} (unless the reader views the HTML "
"source)."
msgstr ""
"Similarmente, o texto @code{@@copying} é automaticamente incluído no "
"início de cada arquivo de saída HTML, como um comentário HTML.  De novo, "
"esse texto não é visível sem @code{@@insertcopying} (a menos que o(a) "
"leitor(a) visualize o fonte HTML)."

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:1537
msgid ""
"The permissions text defined by @code{@@copying} also appears automatically "
"at the beginning of the DocBook output files using appropriate markup.  "
"@code{@@insertcopying} can be used to output the permission text within "
"normal text."
msgstr ""
"O texto de permissões definido por @code{@@copying} também aparece "
"automaticamente no início dos arquivos de saída Docbook usando-se "
"marcação apropriada. @code{@@insertcopying} pode ser usado para gerar o "
"texto de permissão dentro do texto normal."

#. type: node
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:1539
#, no-wrap
msgid "Titlepage & Copyright Page"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:1541
msgid "@nodedescription Creating the title and copyright pages."
msgstr ""

#. type: section
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:1541
#, no-wrap
msgid "Title and Copyright Pages"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:1547
msgid ""
"In hard copy output, the manual's name and author are usually printed on a "
"title page.  Copyright information is usually printed on the back (verso) of "
"the title page.  This segment must be enclosed between @code{@@titlepage} "
"and @code{@@end titlepage} commands:"
msgstr ""

#. type: group
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:1552
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"@@titlepage\n"
"@@title Sample Title\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: group
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:1560
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"@@c The following two commands start the copyright page.\n"
"@@page\n"
"@@vskip 0pt plus 1filll\n"
"@@insertcopying\n"
"@@end titlepage\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:1567
msgid ""
"We use the @code{@@insertcopying} command to include the permission text "
"from the previous section, instead of writing it out again."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:1572
msgid ""
"The title and copyright pages appear in printed manuals, but not in most "
"other output formats.  In HTML, the best way to get a title page similar to "
"printed manuals is to set the @code{NO_TOP_NODE_OUTPUT} customization "
"variable (@pxref{@code{NO_TOP_NODE_OUTPUT}})."
msgstr ""

#. type: node
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:1574
#, no-wrap
msgid "@code{@@titlepage}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:1576
msgid "@nodedescription Create a title for the printed document."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:1576
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19706
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@titlepage"
msgstr ""

#. type: findex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:1579
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:1580
#, no-wrap
msgid "titlepage"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:1579
#, no-wrap
msgid "Title page"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:1585
msgid ""
"Start the material for the title page and following copyright page with "
"@code{@@titlepage} on a line by itself and end it with @code{@@end "
"titlepage} on a line by itself."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:1590
msgid ""
"The @code{@@end titlepage} command starts a new page and turns on page "
"numbering (@pxref{Heading Generation}).  All the material that you want to "
"appear on unnumbered pages should be put between the @code{@@titlepage} and "
"@code{@@end titlepage} commands."
msgstr ""

#. type: findex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:1591
#, no-wrap
msgid "page@r{, within @code{@@titlepage}}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:1598
msgid ""
"By using the @code{@@page} command, you can force a page break within the "
"region delineated by the @code{@@titlepage} and @code{@@end titlepage} "
"commands and thereby create more than one unnumbered page.  This is how the "
"copyright page is produced.  (The @code{@@titlepage} command might perhaps "
"have been better named the @code{@@titleandadditionalpages} command, but "
"that would have been rather long!)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:1610
msgid ""
"When you write a manual about a computer program, you should write the "
"version of the program to which the manual applies on the title page.  If "
"the manual changes more frequently than the program or is independent of it, "
"you should also include an edition number@footnote{We have found that it is "
"helpful to refer to versions of independent manuals as `editions' and "
"versions of programs as `versions'; otherwise, we find we are liable to "
"confuse each other in conversation by referring to both the documentation "
"and the software with the same words.} for the manual.  This helps readers "
"keep track of which manual is for which version of the program.  (The `Top' "
"node should also contain this information; see @ref{The Top Node}.)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:1618
msgid ""
"One method uses the @code{@@title}, @code{@@subtitle}, and @code{@@author} "
"commands to create a title page.  With this method, you do not specify any "
"of the actual formatting of the title page.  You specify the text you want, "
"and Texinfo does the formatting.  The usual formatting consist of black "
"rules under the title and author lines and the subtitle text set flush to "
"the right-hand side of the page."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:1624
msgid ""
"Texinfo also provides a second method for creating a title page.  using "
"typesetting commands that are not to be used in the main text.  This method "
"uses uses the @code{@@titlefont}, @code{@@sp}, and @code{@@center} commands "
"to generate a title page in which the words on the page are centered."
msgstr ""

#. type: findex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:1625
#, no-wrap
msgid "shorttitlepage"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:1626
#, no-wrap
msgid "Bastard title page"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:1627
#, no-wrap
msgid "Title page @subentry bastard"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:1634
msgid ""
"For sufficiently simple documents, and for the bastard title page in "
"traditional book frontmatter, Texinfo also provides a command "
"@code{@@shorttitlepage} which takes the rest of the line as the title.  The "
"argument is typeset on a page by itself and followed by a blank page.  In "
"HTML, @code{@@shorttitlepage} can play the same role as @code{@@settitle}, "
"if @code{@@settitle} is not set.  @xref{@code{@@settitle}}."
msgstr ""

#. type: node
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:1636
#, no-wrap
msgid "@code{@@title @@subtitle @@author}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:1639
msgid ""
"@nodedescriptionblock The @code{@@title}, @code{@@subtitle}, and "
"@code{@@author} commands."
msgstr ""

#. type: subsection
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:1640
#, no-wrap
msgid "@code{@@title}, @code{@@subtitle}, and @code{@@author}"
msgstr ""

#.  old name
#. type: anchor{#1}
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:1643
msgid "title subtitle author"
msgstr ""

#. type: findex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:1643
#, no-wrap
msgid "title"
msgstr ""

#. type: findex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:1644
#, no-wrap
msgid "subtitle"
msgstr ""

#. type: findex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:1645
#, no-wrap
msgid "author"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:1650
msgid ""
"You can use the @code{@@title}, @code{@@subtitle}, and @code{@@author} "
"commands to create a title page in which the vertical and horizontal spacing "
"is done for you automatically."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:1657
msgid ""
"Write the @code{@@title}, @code{@@subtitle}, or @code{@@author} commands at "
"the beginning of a line followed by the title, subtitle, or author.  The "
"@code{@@author} command may be used for a quotation in an @code{@@quotation} "
"block (@pxref{@code{@@quotation}}); except for that, it is an error to use "
"any of these commands outside of @code{@@titlepage}."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:1663
msgid ""
"The @code{@@title} command normally produces a line in which the title is "
"set flush to the left-hand side of the page in a larger than normal font.  "
"The title is underlined with a black rule.  The title must be given on a "
"single line in the source file; it will be broken into multiple lines of "
"output is needed."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:1669
msgid ""
"For long titles, the @code{@@*} command may be used to specify the line "
"breaks in long titles if the automatic breaks do not suit.  Such explicit "
"line breaks are generally reflected in all output formats; if you only want "
"to specify them for the printed output, use a conditional "
"(@pxref{Conditionals}).  For example:"
msgstr ""

#. type: example
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:1672
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@title This Long Title@@inlinefmt@{tex,@@*@} Is Broken in @@TeX@{@}\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:1676
msgid ""
"The @code{@@subtitle} command normally sets subtitles in a normal-sized font "
"flush to the right-hand side of the page."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:1682
msgid ""
"The @code{@@author} command normally sets the names of the author or authors "
"in a middle-sized font flush to the left-hand side of the page on a line "
"near the bottom of the title page.  The names are followed by a black rule "
"that is thinner than the rule that normally underlines the title."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:1686
msgid ""
"There are two ways to use the @code{@@author} command: you can write the "
"name or names on the remaining part of the line that starts with an "
"@code{@@author} command:"
msgstr ""

#. type: example
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:1689
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@author by Jane Smith and John Doe\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:1694
msgid ""
"or you can write the names one above each other by using multiple "
"@code{@@author} commands:"
msgstr ""

#. type: group
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:1699
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"@@author Jane Smith\n"
"@@author John Doe\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:1704
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:1772
msgid "A template for this method looks like this:"
msgstr ""

#. type: group
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:1715
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"@@titlepage\n"
"@@title @var{name-of-manual-when-printed}\n"
"@@subtitle @var{subtitle-if-any}\n"
"@@subtitle @var{second-subtitle}\n"
"@@author @var{author}\n"
"@@page\n"
"@dots{}\n"
"@@end titlepage\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: node
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:1719
#, no-wrap
msgid "@code{@@titlefont @@center @@sp}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:1722
msgid ""
"@nodedescriptionblock The @code{@@titlefont}, @code{@@center}, and "
"@code{@@sp} commands."
msgstr ""

#. type: subsection
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:1723
#, no-wrap
msgid "@code{@@titlefont}, @code{@@center}, and @code{@@sp}"
msgstr ""

#.  old name
#. type: anchor{#1}
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:1726
msgid "titlefont center sp"
msgstr ""

#. type: findex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:1726
#, no-wrap
msgid "titlefont"
msgstr ""

#. type: findex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:1727
#, no-wrap
msgid "center"
msgstr ""

#. type: findex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:1728
#, no-wrap
msgid "sp @r{(titlepage line spacing)}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:1732
msgid ""
"You can also use the @code{@@titlefont}, @code{@@sp}, and @code{@@center} "
"commands to create a title page for a printed document."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:1736
msgid ""
"Use the @code{@@titlefont} command to select a large font suitable for the "
"title itself.  You can use @code{@@titlefont} more than once if you have an "
"especially long title."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:1741
msgid ""
"For HTML output, each @code{@@titlefont} command produces an @code{<h1>} "
"heading, but the HTML document @code{<title>} is not affected.  For that, "
"you could put a @code{@@settitle} command before the @code{@@titlefont} "
"command (@pxref{@code{@@settitle}})."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:1744
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:6150
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:8279
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:8923
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:11170
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:11223
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:11489
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:13462
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:18073
msgid "For example:"
msgstr ""

#. type: example
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:1747
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@titlefont@{Texinfo@}\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:1751
msgid ""
"Use the @code{@@center} command at the beginning of a line to center the "
"remaining text on that line.  Thus,"
msgstr ""

#. type: example
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:1754
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@center @@titlefont@{Texinfo@}\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:1759
msgid ""
"centers the title, which in this example is ``Texinfo'' printed in the title "
"font."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:1761
msgid "Use the @code{@@sp} command to insert vertical space.  For example:"
msgstr ""

#. type: example
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:1764
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:10474
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@sp 2\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:1770
msgid ""
"This inserts two blank lines on the printed page.  (@xref{@code{@@sp}}, for "
"more information about the @code{@@sp} command.)"
msgstr ""

#. type: group
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:1784
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"@@titlepage\n"
"@@sp 10\n"
"@@center @@titlefont@{@var{name-of-manual-when-printed}@}\n"
"@@sp 2\n"
"@@center @var{subtitle-if-any}\n"
"@@sp 2\n"
"@@center @var{author}\n"
"@dots{}\n"
"@@end titlepage\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:1788
msgid "The spacing of the example fits an 8.5 by 11 inch manual."
msgstr ""

#. type: node
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:1790
#, no-wrap
msgid "Copyright"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:1793
msgid ""
"@nodedescriptionblock How to write the copyright notice and include copying "
"permissions."
msgstr ""

#. type: subsection
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:1794
#, no-wrap
msgid "Copyright Page"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:1795
#, no-wrap
msgid "Copyright page"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:1796
#, no-wrap
msgid "Printed permissions"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:1797
#, no-wrap
msgid "Permissions, printed"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:1805
msgid ""
"By international treaty, the copyright notice for a book must be either on "
"the title page or on the back of the title page.  When the copyright notice "
"is on the back of the title page, that page is customarily not numbered.  "
"Therefore, in Texinfo, the information on the copyright page should be "
"within @code{@@titlepage} and @code{@@end titlepage} commands."
msgstr ""

#. type: findex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:1806
#, no-wrap
msgid "vskip @r{@TeX{} vertical skip}"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:1807
#, no-wrap
msgid "filll @r{@TeX{} dimension}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:1811
msgid ""
"Use the @code{@@page} command to cause a page break.  To push the copyright "
"notice and the other text on the copyright page towards the bottom of the "
"page, use the following incantation after @code{@@page}:"
msgstr ""

#. type: example
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:1814
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@vskip 0pt plus 1filll\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:1823
msgid ""
"The @code{@@vskip} command inserts whitespace in the @TeX{} output; it is "
"ignored in all other output formats.  The @samp{0pt plus 1filll} means to "
"put in zero points of mandatory whitespace, and as much optional whitespace "
"as needed to push the following text to the bottom of the page.  Note the "
"use of three @samp{l}s in the word @samp{filll}; this is correct."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:1826
msgid ""
"To insert the copyright text itself, write @code{@@insertcopying} next "
"(@pxref{Document Permissions}):"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:1833
msgid ""
"Follow the copying text by the publisher, ISBN numbers, cover art credits, "
"and other such information."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:1835
msgid "Here is an example putting all this together:"
msgstr ""

#. type: example
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:1842
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"@@titlepage\n"
"@dots{}\n"
"@@page\n"
"@@vskip 0pt plus 1filll\n"
"@@insertcopying\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: example
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:1844
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Published by @dots{}\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: example
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:1847
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Cover art by @dots{}\n"
"@@end titlepage\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:1853
msgid ""
"We have one more special case to consider: for plain text output, you must "
"insert the copyright information explicitly if you want it to appear.  For "
"instance, you could have the following after the copyright page:"
msgstr ""

#. type: example
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:1858
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"@@ifplaintext\n"
"@@insertcopying\n"
"@@end ifplaintext\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:1862
msgid ""
"You could include other title-like information for the plain text output in "
"the same place."
msgstr ""

#. type: subsection
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:1864
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:1866
#, no-wrap
msgid "Heading Generation"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:1866
msgid ""
"@nodedescription Turn on page headings after the title and copyright pages."
msgstr ""

#.  old name
#. type: anchor{#1}
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:1869
msgid "end titlepage"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:1869
#, no-wrap
msgid "Generating page headings"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:1875
msgid ""
"Texinfo has two standard page heading formats, one for documents printed on "
"one side of each sheet of paper (single-sided printing), and the other for "
"documents printed on both sides of each sheet (double-sided printing)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:1877
msgid "In full generality, you can control the headings in different ways:"
msgstr ""

#. type: itemize
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:1882
msgid ""
"The conventional way is to write a @code{@@setchapternewpage} command before "
"the title page commands."
msgstr ""

#. type: itemize
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:1888
msgid ""
"Most documents are formatted with the standard single-sided or double-sided "
"headings, (sometimes) using @code{@@setchapternewpage odd} for double-sided "
"printing and (almost always) no @code{@@setchapternewpage} command for "
"single-sided printing (@pxref{@code{@@setchapternewpage}})."
msgstr ""

#. type: itemize
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:1894
msgid ""
"Alternatively, you can use the @code{@@headings} command to prevent page "
"headings from being generated or to start them for either single or "
"double-sided printing. To turn off headings, write @code{@@headings off}.  "
"@xref{@code{@@headings}}."
msgstr ""

#. type: itemize
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:1898
msgid ""
"Or, you may specify your own page heading and footing format.  "
"@xref{Headings}."
msgstr ""

#. type: node
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:1901
#, no-wrap
msgid "Contents"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:1903
msgid "@nodedescription How to create a table of contents."
msgstr ""

#. type: section
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:1903
#, no-wrap
msgid "Generating a Table of Contents"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:1904
#, no-wrap
msgid "Table of contents"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:1905
#, no-wrap
msgid "Contents, table of"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:1906
#, no-wrap
msgid "Short table of contents"
msgstr ""

#. type: findex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:1907
#, no-wrap
msgid "contents"
msgstr ""

#. type: findex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:1908
#, no-wrap
msgid "summarycontents"
msgstr ""

#. type: findex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:1909
#, no-wrap
msgid "shortcontents"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:1916
msgid ""
"The @code{@@chapter}, @code{@@section}, and other structuring commands "
"(@pxref{Chapter Structuring}) supply the information to make up a table of "
"contents, but they do not cause an actual table to appear in the manual.  To "
"do this, you must use the @code{@@contents} and/or @code{@@summarycontents} "
"command(s)."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:1918
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:18740
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@contents"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:1925
msgid ""
"Generates a table of contents in a printed manual, including all chapters, "
"sections, subsections, etc., as well as appendices and unnumbered chapters.  "
"Headings generated by @code{@@majorheading}, @code{@@chapheading}, and the "
"other @code{@@@dots{}heading} commands do not appear in the table of "
"contents (@pxref{Structuring Command Types})."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:1926
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19535
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@shortcontents"
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:1927
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19623
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@summarycontents"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:1929
msgid "(@code{@@summarycontents} is a synonym for @code{@@shortcontents}.)"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:1934
msgid ""
"Generates a short or summary table of contents that lists only the chapters, "
"appendices, and unnumbered chapters.  Sections, subsections and "
"subsubsections are omitted.  Only a long manual needs a short table of "
"contents in addition to the full table of contents."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:1943
msgid ""
"Both contents commands should be written on a line by themselves, and placed "
"near the beginning of the file, after the @code{@@end titlepage} "
"(@pxref{@code{@@titlepage}}), before any sectioning command.  The contents "
"commands automatically generate a chapter-like heading at the top of the "
"first table of contents page, so don't include any sectioning command such "
"as @code{@@unnumbered} before them."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:1948
msgid ""
"Since an Info file uses menus instead of tables of contents, the Info "
"formatting commands ignore the contents commands.  But the contents are "
"included in plain text output and in other output formats, such as HTML."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:1953
msgid ""
"In HTML output, the links in the short table of contents point to "
"corresponding entries in the full table of contents rather than the text of "
"the document. The links in the full table of contents point to the main text "
"of the document."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:1955
msgid "@code{@@shortcontents} is not implemented for @LaTeX{} output."
msgstr ""

#. type: node
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:1957
#, no-wrap
msgid "The Top Node"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:1959
msgid "@nodedescription Creating the `Top' node and master menu."
msgstr ""

#. type: section
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:1959
#, no-wrap
msgid "The `Top' Node and Master Menu"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:1960
#, no-wrap
msgid "Top node"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:1961
#, no-wrap
msgid "Node, @samp{Top}"
msgstr ""

#. type: anchor{#1}
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:1963
msgid "Top Node Example"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:1968
msgid ""
"The `Top' node is the node in which a reader enters an Info manual.  As "
"such, it should contain a very brief description of the manual (including "
"the version number).  The contents of the `Top' node do not appear in "
"printed output nor in DocBook output."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:1972
msgid ""
"It is conventional to write a @code{@@top} sectioning command line "
"containing the title of the document immediately after the @code{@@node Top} "
"line (@pxref{@code{@@top} Command})."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:1976
msgid ""
"We repeat the short description from the beginning of the @samp{@@copying} "
"text, but there's no need to repeat the copyright information, so we don't "
"use @samp{@@insertcopying} here."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:1980
msgid ""
"The `Top' node contains a top-level @dfn{menu} listing the chapters, and "
"possibly a @dfn{detailed menu} listing all the nodes in the entire document."
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:1981
#, no-wrap
msgid "Top node example"
msgstr ""

#. type: example
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:1985
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"@@node Top\n"
"@@top Short Sample\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: example
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:1987
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This is a short sample Texinfo file.\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: group
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:1994
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"@@menu\n"
"* First Chapter::    The first chapter is the\n"
"                       only chapter in this sample.\n"
"* Index::            Complete index.\n"
"@@end menu\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: node
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:1999
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:2002
#, no-wrap
msgid "Master Menu Parts"
msgstr ""

#. type: subsection
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:2003
#, no-wrap
msgid "Parts of a Master Menu"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:2004
#, no-wrap
msgid "Master menu"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:2005
#, no-wrap
msgid "Menu, master"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:2006
#, no-wrap
msgid "Parts of a master menu"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:2013
msgid ""
"A @dfn{master menu} is the main menu.  It is customary to include a detailed "
"menu listing all the nodes in the document in this menu.  Like any other "
"menu, a master menu is enclosed in @code{@@menu} and @code{@@end menu} and "
"does not appear in the printed output nor in DocBook output."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:2017
msgid ""
"The master menu contains entries for the major nodes in the Texinfo file: "
"the nodes for the chapters, chapter-like sections, and the appendices, "
"followed by nodes for the indices."
msgstr ""

#. type: findex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:2018
#, no-wrap
msgid "detailmenu"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:2019
#, no-wrap
msgid "Detailed menu"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:2028
msgid ""
"You may choose to follow these entries with a @dfn{detailed menu}.  This "
"lists other, lower-level nodes, often ordered by chapter.  These items may "
"be a convenience for an inquirer who can go directly to a particular node "
"when searching for specific information, rather than going through an "
"intermediate menu.  If you use a detailed menu in your master menu, mark it "
"with the @code{@@detailmenu @dots{} @@end detailmenu} environment."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:2033
msgid ""
"Each section in the menu can be introduced by a descriptive line.  So long "
"as the line does not begin with an asterisk, it will not be treated as a "
"menu entry.  (@xref{Writing a Menu}, for more information.)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:2036
msgid ""
"For example, the master menu for this manual looks like the following (but "
"has many more entries):"
msgstr ""

#. type: group
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:2043
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"@@menu\n"
"* Copying Conditions::  Your rights.\n"
"* Overview::            Texinfo in brief.\n"
"@dots{}\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: group
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:2047
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"* Command and Variable Index::\n"
"* General Index::\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: group
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:2052
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"@@detailmenu\n"
"--- The Detailed Node Listing ---\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: group
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:2054
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Overview of Texinfo\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: group
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:2057
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"* Reporting Bugs:: @dots{}\n"
"@dots{}\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: group
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:2061
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Beginning a Texinfo File\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: group
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:2066
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"* Sample Beginning:: @dots{}\n"
"@dots{}\n"
"@@end detailmenu\n"
"@@end menu\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: section
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:2070
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:2072
#, no-wrap
msgid "The Body of the Document"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:2072
msgid "@nodedescription The rest of the nodes."
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:2074
#, no-wrap
msgid "Frontmatter, text in"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:2080
msgid ""
"The body segment contains all the text of the document.  A manual is divided "
"into one or more @dfn{nodes} (@pxref{Nodes}).  The example illustrates a "
"chapter made of three nodes, one for introductory material in the chapter, "
"and two sections.  The introductory material contains an enumerated list."
msgstr ""

#. type: group
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:2099
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"@@item\n"
"This is the second item.\n"
"@@end enumerate\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: group
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:2111
#, no-wrap
msgid "Second section of first chapter.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:2118
msgid ""
"In the Info output, the @samp{First Chapter} node will contain a menu "
"listing the two sections in the chapter.  Similarly, when this node is "
"output in its own HTML file, it will contain a table of contents for the "
"chapter."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:2120
msgid "Here is what the contents of this chapter will look like:"
msgstr ""

#. type: chapheading
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:2124
#, no-wrap
msgid "1. First Chapter"
msgstr ""

#. type: quotation
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:2127
msgid "This is the first chapter."
msgstr ""

#. type: quotation
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:2129
msgid "Here is a numbered list."
msgstr ""

#. type: enumerate
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:2133
msgid "This is the first item."
msgstr ""

#. type: enumerate
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:2136
msgid "This is the second item."
msgstr ""

#. type: heading
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:2138
#, no-wrap
msgid "1.1 First Section"
msgstr ""

#. type: quotation
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:2141
msgid "First section of first chapter."
msgstr ""

#. type: heading
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:2142
#, no-wrap
msgid "1.2 Second Section"
msgstr ""

#. type: quotation
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:2145
msgid "Second section of first chapter."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:2149
msgid "into nodes.)"
msgstr ""

#. type: node
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:2151
#, no-wrap
msgid "Ending a File"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:2153
msgid "@nodedescription What is at the end of a Texinfo file?"
msgstr ""

#. type: section
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:2153
#, no-wrap
msgid "Ending a Texinfo File"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:2154
#, no-wrap
msgid "Ending a Texinfo file"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:2155
#, no-wrap
msgid "Texinfo file ending"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:2156
#, no-wrap
msgid "File ending"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:2161
msgid ""
"The end of a Texinfo file should include commands to create indices "
"(@pxref{Printing Indices & Menus}), and the @code{@@bye} command to mark the "
"last line to be processed.  For example:"
msgstr ""

#. type: findex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:2171
#, no-wrap
msgid "bye"
msgstr ""

#. type: anchor{#1}
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:2176
msgid "File End"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:2176
msgid ""
"A @code{@@bye} command terminates Texinfo processing.  It should be on a "
"line by itself.  Anything following @code{@@bye} is completely ignored."
msgstr ""

#. type: chapter
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:2178
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:2180
#, no-wrap
msgid "Nodes"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:2180
msgid "@nodedescription Writing nodes, the basic unit of Texinfo."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:2182
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:2216
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:15146
#, no-wrap
msgid "node"
msgstr ""

#. type: anchor{#1}
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:2182
msgid "@@node"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:2183
#, no-wrap
msgid "Node, defined"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:2190
msgid ""
"A @dfn{node} is a region of text that begins at a @code{@@node} command, and "
"continues until the next @code{@@node} command.  To specify a node, write a "
"@code{@@node} command at the beginning of a line, and follow it with the "
"name of the node.  Info readers display one node at a time, and provide "
"commands for the user to move to related nodes.  The HTML output can be "
"similarly navigated."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:2196
msgid ""
"Nodes are used as the targets of cross-references.  Cross-references, such "
"as the one at the end of this sentence, are made with @code{@@xref} and "
"related commands; see @ref{Cross References}.  Cross-references can be "
"sprinkled throughout the text.  Other @@-commands may also be the target of "
"cross-references (@pxref{@code{@@anchor}}, @pxref{Floats})."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:2207
msgid ""
"Normally, you put a node command immediately before each chapter structuring "
"command---for example, an @code{@@section} or @code{@@subsection} line.  "
"(@xref{Chapter Structuring}.)  You should do this even if you do not intend "
"to format the file for Info.  This is because printed output uses both "
"@code{@@node} names and chapter-structuring names in the output for "
"cross-references.  The only time you are likely to use the chapter "
"structuring commands without also using nodes is if you are writing a "
"document that contains no cross references and will only be printed, not "
"transformed into Info, HTML, or other formats."
msgstr ""

#. type: node
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:2209
#, no-wrap
msgid "Writing a Node"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:2211
msgid "@nodedescription How to write a @code{@@node} line."
msgstr ""

#. type: section
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:2211
#, no-wrap
msgid "Writing a @code{@@node} Line"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:2212
#, no-wrap
msgid "Writing a @code{@@node} line"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:2213
#, no-wrap
msgid "@code{@@node} line writing"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:2214
#, no-wrap
msgid "Node line writing"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:2219
msgid ""
"Write @code{@@node} at the beginning of a line followed by the name of the "
"node, like this:"
msgstr ""

#. type: example
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:2222
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@node @var{node-name}\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:2227
msgid ""
"After you have inserted a @code{@@node} line, you should immediately write "
"the @@-command for the associated chapter or section (if any)  and insert "
"its name."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:2234
msgid ""
"You may optionally follow the node name argument to @code{@@node} with up to "
"three optional arguments on the rest of the same line, separating the "
"arguments with commas.  These are the names of the `Next', `Previous', and "
"`Up' pointers, in that order.  Hence, the template for a fully-written-out "
"node line with `Next', `Previous', and `Up' pointers looks like this:"
msgstr ""

#. type: example
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:2237
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@node @var{node-name}, @var{next}, @var{previous}, @var{up}\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:2246
msgid ""
"The @var{node-name} argument must be present, but the others are optional.  "
"If you wish to specify some but not others, just insert commas as needed, as "
"in: @samp{@@node mynode,,,uppernode}.  Any spaces before or after each name "
"on the @code{@@node} line are ignored.  However, if your Texinfo document is "
"hierarchically organized, as virtually all are, we recommend leaving off all "
"the pointers and letting @code{texi2any} determine them."
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:2247
#, no-wrap
msgid "Creating pointers with @code{texi2any}"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:2248
#, no-wrap
msgid "Pointer creation with @code{texi2any}"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:2249
#, no-wrap
msgid "Automatic pointer creation with @code{texi2any}"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:2250
#, no-wrap
msgid "Implicit pointer creation with @code{texi2any}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:2258
msgid ""
"The @code{texi2any} program automatically determines node pointers for a "
"hierarchically organized document.  For it to do this, each @code{@@node} "
"command should be followed immediately by a sectioning command such as "
"@code{@@chapter} or @code{@@section} (except that comment lines may "
"intervene).  Finally, you must follow the `Top' @code{@@node} line with a "
"line beginning with @code{@@top} to mark the top-level node in the file.  "
"@xref{@code{@@top} Command}."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:2264
msgid ""
"Even when you explicitly specify all pointers, you cannot write the nodes in "
"the Texinfo source file in an arbitrary order.  You must write the nodes in "
"the order you wish them to appear in the output.  For Info format one can "
"imagine that the order may not matter, but it matters for the other formats."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:2272
msgid ""
"In most cases, you will want to take advantage of the pointer creation "
"feature, and not redundantly specify node pointers that the programs can "
"determine.  However, Texinfo documents are not required to be organized "
"hierarchically or in fact to contain sectioning commands at all (for "
"example, if you never intend the document to be printed), so node pointers "
"may still be specified explicitly, in full generality."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:2276
msgid ""
"If you are using GNU Emacs, and want explicit pointers, you can use the "
"update node commands provided by Texinfo mode to insert the names of the "
"pointers.  (@xref{Updating Nodes and Menus}.)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:2283
msgid ""
"Alternatively, you can insert the `Next', `Previous', and `Up' pointers "
"yourself.  If you do this in Emacs, you may find it helpful to use the "
"Texinfo mode keyboard command @kbd{C-c C-c n}.  This command inserts "
"@samp{@@node} and a comment line listing the names of the pointers in their "
"proper order.  The comment line helps you keep track of which arguments are "
"for which pointers."
msgstr ""

#. type: node
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:2285
#, no-wrap
msgid "Node Names"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:2287
msgid "@nodedescription How to choose node names."
msgstr ""

#. type: section
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:2287
#, no-wrap
msgid "Choosing Node Names"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:2289
#, no-wrap
msgid "Node names, choosing"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:2292
msgid ""
"The name of a node identifies the node.  For all the details of node names, "
"@pxref{Node Line Requirements})."
msgstr ""

#.  previous node name
#. type: anchor{#1}
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:2295
msgid "Node Line Tips"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:2295
msgid "Here are some suggestions for node names:"
msgstr ""

#. type: itemize
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:2299
msgid "Try to pick node names that are informative but short."
msgstr ""

#. type: itemize
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:2303
msgid ""
"In the Info file, the file name, node name, and pointer names are all "
"inserted on one line, which may run into the right edge of the window.  "
"(This does not cause a problem with Info, but is ugly.)"
msgstr ""

#. type: itemize
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:2308
msgid ""
"Try to pick node names that differ from each other near the beginnings of "
"their names.  This way, it is easy to use automatic name completion in Info."
msgstr ""

#. type: itemize
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:2315
msgid ""
"Conventionally, node names are capitalized in the same way as section and "
"chapter titles.  In this manual, initial and significant words are "
"capitalized; others are not.  In other manuals, just initial words and "
"proper nouns are capitalized.  Either way is fine; we recommend just being "
"consistent."
msgstr ""

#. type: itemize
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:2323
msgid ""
"In HTML output, any characters in the node name other than plain ASCII "
"letters, numbers or spaces will be changed in the file name.  (@xref{HTML "
"Xref Node Name Expansion}.)  This can make the URLs for the pages in your "
"manual less user-friendly; for example, in this manual the @samp{@@dots} "
"node is output as @file{__0040dots.html}."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:2330
msgid ""
"Because node names are used in cross-references, it is not desirable to "
"casually change them once published.  When you delete or rename a node, it "
"is usually a good idea to define an @code{@@anchor} with the old name.  That "
"way, references from other manuals, from mail archives, and so on are not "
"invalidated.  @xref{@code{@@anchor}}."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:2333
msgid ""
"The pointers from a given node enable you to reach other nodes and consist "
"simply of the names of those nodes."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:2340
msgid ""
"Normally, a node's `Up' pointer contains the name of the node whose menu "
"mentions that node.  The node's `Next' pointer contains the name of the node "
"that follows the present node in that menu and its `Previous' pointer "
"contains the name of the node that precedes it in that menu.  When a node's "
"`Previous' node is the same as its `Up' node, both pointers name the same "
"node."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:2344
msgid ""
"Usually, the first node of a Texinfo file is the `Top' node, and its `Up' "
"pointer points to the @file{dir} file, which contains the main menu for all "
"of Info."
msgstr ""

#. type: node
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:2346
#, no-wrap
msgid "Node Line Requirements"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:2348
msgid "@nodedescription Keep names unique."
msgstr ""

#. type: section
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:2348
#, no-wrap
msgid "@code{@@node} Line Requirements"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:2350
#, no-wrap
msgid "Node line requirements"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:2351
#, no-wrap
msgid "Restrictions on node names"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:2354
msgid "Names used with @code{@@node} have several requirements:"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:2357
#, no-wrap
msgid "Unique node names requirement"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:2358
#, no-wrap
msgid "Node names must be unique"
msgstr ""

#. type: itemize
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:2360
msgid "All the node names in a single Texinfo file must be unique."
msgstr ""

#. type: itemize
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:2367
msgid ""
"This means, for example, that if you end every chapter with a summary, you "
"must name each summary node differently.  You cannot just call them all "
"``Summary''.  You may, however, duplicate the titles of chapters, sections, "
"and the like.  Thus you can end each chapter with a section called "
"``Summary'', so long as the node names for those sections are all different."
msgstr ""

#. type: itemize
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:2370
msgid ""
"Node names, anchor names (@pxref{@code{@@anchor}}), and float labels "
"(@pxref{@code{@@float}}) must all be unique."
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:2372
#, no-wrap
msgid "Commands in node names"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:2373
#, no-wrap
msgid "@sortas{at} @@-commands @subentry in node names"
msgstr ""

#. type: itemize
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:2381
msgid ""
"Node names can contain @@-commands@footnote{Prior to the Texinfo 5 release "
"in 2013, this feature was supported in an ad hoc way (the "
"@option{--commands-in-node-names} option to @command{makeinfo}).  Now it is "
"part of the language.  }.  For example, using @code{@@TeX@{@}} in a node "
"name results in the @TeX{} logo being output, as it would be in normal "
"text.  Cross-references should use @code{@@TeX@{@}} just as the node name "
"does."
msgstr ""

#. type: itemize
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:2388
msgid ""
"Some commands do not make sense in node names; for instance, environments "
"(e.g., @code{@@quotation}), commands that read a whole line as their "
"argument (e.g., @code{@@sp}), and plenty of others.  For the complete list "
"of commands that are allowed, and their expansion for HTML identifiers and "
"file names, @pxref{HTML Xref Command Expansion}."
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:2390
#, no-wrap
msgid "Parentheses in node name"
msgstr ""

#. type: itemize
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:2394
msgid ""
"A node name may not start with a left parenthesis preceding a right "
"parenthesis, as in @code{(not)allowed}, since this syntax is used to specify "
"an external manual."
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:2396
#, no-wrap
msgid "Colon in node name"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:2397
#, no-wrap
msgid "Comma in node name"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:2398
#, no-wrap
msgid "Period in node name"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:2399
#, no-wrap
msgid "Characters, invalid in node name"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:2400
#, no-wrap
msgid "Invalid characters in node names"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:2401
#, no-wrap
msgid "Node names, invalid characters in"
msgstr ""

#. type: anchor{#1}
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:2412
msgid "Info Node Names Constraints"
msgstr ""

#. type: itemize
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:2412
msgid ""
"Unfortunately, you cannot reliably use periods, commas, or colons within a "
"node name; these can confuse some Info readers.  @command{texi2any} quotes "
"problematic node names and labels by default, but some Info readers do not "
"recognize this syntax.  Node name and label quoting causes @code{DEL} "
"characters (@samp{CTRL-?}, character number 127, often rendered as "
"@samp{^?}) to appear around the name.  To remove node names and labels "
"quoting, you can set the customization variable "
"@code{INFO_SPECIAL_CHARS_QUOTE} to @samp{0} (@pxref{Other Customization "
"Variables})."
msgstr ""

#. type: itemize
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:2418
msgid ""
"@command{texi2any} warns about such problematic usage in node names, menu "
"items, and cross-references.  If you don't want to see the warnings, you can "
"set the customization variable @code{INFO_SPECIAL_CHARS_WARNING} to @samp{0} "
"(@pxref{Other Customization Variables})."
msgstr ""

#. type: itemize
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:2423
msgid ""
"If you insist on using these characters in node names, in order not to "
"confuse the Texinfo processors you must still escape those characters, by "
"using either special insertions (@pxref{Inserting a Comma}) or @code{@@asis} "
"(@pxref{@code{@@asis}}).  For example:"
msgstr ""

#. type: example
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:2426
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@node foo@@asis@{::@}bar@@comma@{@} baz\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: itemize
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:2430
msgid ""
"As an example of avoiding the special characters, the following is a section "
"title in this manual:"
msgstr ""

#. type: example
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:2433
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"@@section @@code@{@@@@unnumbered@}, @@code@{@@@@appendix@}: Chapters "
"with@enddots{}\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: itemize
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:2437
msgid "But the corresponding node name lacks the commas and the subtitle:"
msgstr ""

#. type: example
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:2440
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@node @@code@{@@@@unnumbered @@@@appendix@}\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:2442
#, no-wrap
msgid "Case in node name"
msgstr ""

#. type: itemize
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:2445
msgid "Case is significant in node names."
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:2446
#, no-wrap
msgid "White space in node name"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:2447
#, no-wrap
msgid "Spaces in node name"
msgstr ""

#. type: itemize
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:2452
msgid ""
"Spaces before and after names on the @samp{@@node} line are ignored.  "
"Multiple whitespace characters ``inside'' a name are collapsed to a single "
"space.  For example:"
msgstr ""

#. type: example
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:2459
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"@@node foo bar\n"
"@@node  foo bar,\n"
"@@node foo bar ,\n"
"@@node foo  bar,\n"
"@@node  foo  bar ,\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: itemize
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:2472
msgid ""
"In menu entries, a single internal space should be used in node names or "
"some versions of some Info readers will not find the node."
msgstr ""

#. type: node
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:2475
#, no-wrap
msgid "First Node"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:2477
msgid "@nodedescription How to write a `Top' node."
msgstr ""

#. type: section
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:2477
#, no-wrap
msgid "The First Node"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:2478
#, no-wrap
msgid "Top node is first"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:2479
#, no-wrap
msgid "First node"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:2487
msgid ""
"The first node of a Texinfo file is the @dfn{Top} node, except in an "
"included file (@pxref{Include Files}).  The Top node should contain a short "
"summary and a master menu.  @xref{The Top Node} for more information on the "
"Top node contents and examples.  Straight text before the Top node outside "
"of any node should be avoided.  Such text, if present, is not output for "
"DocBook."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:2490
msgid "Here is a description of the node pointers to be used in the Top node:"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:2493
#, no-wrap
msgid "Up node of Top node"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:2494
#, no-wrap
msgid "(dir) as Up node of Top node"
msgstr ""

#. type: itemize
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:2498
msgid ""
"The Top node (which must be named @samp{top} or @samp{Top}) should have as "
"its `Up' node the name of a node in another file, where there is a menu that "
"leads to this file.  Specify the file name in parentheses."
msgstr ""

#. type: itemize
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:2505
msgid ""
"Usually, all Info files are available through a single virtual Info tree, "
"constructed from multiple directories.  In this case, use @samp{(dir)} as "
"the parent of the Top node; this specifies the top-level node in the "
"@file{dir} file, which contains the main menu for the Info system as a "
"whole.  (Each directory with Info files is intended to contain a file named "
"@file{dir}.)"
msgstr ""

#. type: itemize
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:2514
msgid ""
"That's fine for Info, but for HTML output, one might well want the Up link "
"from the Top node to go to some specific place.  For example, for GNU the "
"natural place would be @url{http://www.gnu.org/manual/} (a web page "
"collecting links to most GNU manuals), better specified as just "
"@code{/manual/} if the manual will be installed on @code{www.gnu.org}.  This "
"can be specified with the @code{TOP_NODE_UP_URL} customization variable "
"(@pxref{HTML Customization Variables}), as in"
msgstr ""

#. type: example
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:2517
#, no-wrap
msgid "$ @kbd{texi2any --html -c TOP_NODE_UP_URL=/manual/} ...\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:2523
#, no-wrap
msgid "Prev node of Top node"
msgstr ""

#. type: itemize
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:2525
msgid "The `Prev' node of the Top node is usually omitted."
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:2527
#, no-wrap
msgid "Next node of Top node"
msgstr ""

#. type: itemize
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:2530
msgid ""
"The `Next' node of the Top node should be the first chapter in your document."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:2535
msgid ""
"@xref{Installing an Info File}, for more information about installing an "
"Info file in the @file{info} directory."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:2538
msgid ""
"It is usually best to leave the pointers off entirely and let the tools "
"implicitly define them, with this simple result:"
msgstr ""

#. type: example
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:2541
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@node Top\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: node
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:2544
#, no-wrap
msgid "@code{@@top} Command"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:2546
msgid "@nodedescription How to use the @code{@@top} command."
msgstr ""

#. type: section
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:2546
#, no-wrap
msgid "The @code{@@top} Sectioning Command"
msgstr ""

#.  old name
#.  another old name
#.  yet another name
#. type: anchor{#1}
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:2551
msgid "top command"
msgstr ""

#. type: anchor{#1}
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:2551
msgid "makeinfo top"
msgstr ""

#. type: anchor{#1}
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:2551
msgid "makeinfo top command"
msgstr ""

#. type: findex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:2551
#, no-wrap
msgid "top"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:2556
msgid ""
"The @code{@@top} command is a special sectioning command that you should "
"only use after a @samp{@@node Top} line at the beginning of a Texinfo file."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:2559
msgid ""
"It produces the same sort of output as @code{@@unnumbered} "
"(@pxref{@code{@@unnumbered @@appendix}}).  In @LaTeX{} @code{\\part*} is "
"used."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:2563
msgid ""
"@code{@@top} is ignored when raising or lowering sections.  That is, it is "
"never lowered and nothing can be raised to it (@pxref{Raise/lower sections})."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:2568
msgid ""
"It used to be conventional to wrap the @samp{Top} node in an "
"@code{@@ifnottex} conditional so that it would not appear in printed output "
"(@pxref{Conditionals}).  Thus, a Top node often looked like this:"
msgstr ""

#. type: example
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:2573
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"@@ifnottex\n"
"@@node Top\n"
"@@top @var{your-manual-title}\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: example
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:2576
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"@var{very-high-level-summary}\n"
"@@end ifnottex\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:2580
msgid ""
"This is no longer necessary, as the @samp{Top} node is now never output for "
"printed output.  The @samp{Top} node is not output for DocBook either."
msgstr ""

#. type: section
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:2582
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:2584
#, no-wrap
msgid "Texinfo Document Structure"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:2584
msgid "@nodedescription Double structure of documents."
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:2585
#, no-wrap
msgid "Texinfo document structure"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:2586
#, no-wrap
msgid "Document structure, of Texinfo"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:2587
#, no-wrap
msgid "Structure, of Texinfo documents"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:2588
#, no-wrap
msgid "Double structure, of Texinfo documents"
msgstr ""

#.  old node name
#. type: anchor{#1}
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:2591
msgid "Two Paths"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:2596
msgid ""
"Nodes can contain @dfn{menus}, which contain the names of @dfn{child nodes} "
"within the parent node; for example, a node corresponding to a chapter would "
"have a menu of the sections in that chapter.  The menus allow the user to "
"move to the child nodes in the Info output."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:2611
msgid ""
"In addition, nodes contain @dfn{node pointers} that name other nodes.  The "
"`Next' and `Previous' pointers link nodes at the same sectioning level into "
"a chain.  As you might imagine, the `Next' pointer links to the next node, "
"and the `Previous' pointer links to the previous node.  In general, `Next' "
"and `Previous' refer to nodes at the @emph{same hierarchical level} in the "
"manual, not necessarily to the next node within the Texinfo file.  In the "
"Texinfo file, the subsequent node may be at a lower level---a section-level "
"node most often follows a chapter-level node, for example.  Thus, for "
"example, all the nodes that are at the level of sections within a chapter "
"are linked together, and the order in this chain is the same as the order of "
"the children in the menu of the parent chapter.  Each child node records the "
"parent node name as its `Up' pointer."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:2616
msgid ""
"Since the `Top' node is the only node at that level, `Next' refers to the "
"first following node, which is almost always a chapter or chapter-level "
"node.  This is an exception to the rule of `Next' being at the same "
"hierarchical level."
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:2617
#, no-wrap
msgid "@code{accesskey} @subentry in HTML output of nodes"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:2630
msgid ""
"The Info and HTML output for each node includes links to the `Next', "
"`Previous', and `Up' nodes.  The HTML also uses the @code{accesskey} "
"attribute with the values @samp{n}, @samp{p}, and @samp{u} respectively.  "
"This allows people using web browsers to follow the navigation using "
"(typically) @kbd{M-@var{letter}}, e.g., @kbd{M-n} for the `Next' node, from "
"anywhere within the node.  Node pointers and menus provide structure for "
"Info files just as chapters, sections, subsections, and the like provide "
"structure for printed books.  The two structures are theoretically distinct; "
"in practice, however, the tree structure of printed books is essentially "
"always used for the node and menu structure also, as this leads to a "
"document which is easy to follow."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:2637
msgid ""
"Typically, the sectioning structure and the node structure are completely "
"parallel, with one node for each chapter, section, etc., and with the nodes "
"following the same hierarchical arrangement as the sectioning.  Thus, if a "
"node is at the logical level of a chapter, its child nodes are at the level "
"of sections; similarly, the child nodes of sections are at the level of "
"subsections."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:2644
msgid ""
"It is technically possible to create Texinfo documents with only one "
"structure or the other, or for the two structures not to be parallel, or for "
"either the sectioning or node structure to be different from the "
"conventional structure.  To the best of our knowledge, however, all the "
"Texinfo manuals currently in general use do follow the conventional parallel "
"structure."
msgstr ""

#. type: node
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:2646
#, no-wrap
msgid "Node Menu Illustration"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:2648
msgid "@nodedescription A diagram, and sample nodes and menus."
msgstr ""

#. type: section
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:2648
#, no-wrap
msgid "Node and Menu Illustration"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:2652
msgid ""
"Here is a diagram that illustrates a Texinfo file with three chapters, each "
"of which contains two sections."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:2658
msgid ""
"The ``root'' is at the top of the diagram and the ``leaves'' are at the "
"bottom.  This is how such a diagram is drawn conventionally; it illustrates "
"an upside-down tree.  For this reason, the root node is called the `Top' "
"node, and `Up' node pointers carry you closer to the root."
msgstr ""

#. type: group
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:2671
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"                         Top\n"
"                          |\n"
"        -------------------------------------\n"
"       |                  |                  |\n"
"    Chapter 1          Chapter 2          Chapter 3\n"
"       |                  |                  |\n"
"    --------           --------           --------\n"
"   |        |         |        |         |        |\n"
"Section  Section   Section  Section   Section  Section\n"
"  1.1      1.2       2.1      2.2       3.1      3.2\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:2677
msgid ""
"Using explicit pointers (not recommended, but shown for purposes of the "
"example), the fully-written command to start Chapter@tie{}2 would be this:"
msgstr ""

#. type: group
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:2682
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"@@node     Chapter 2,  Chapter 3, Chapter 1, Top\n"
"@@comment  node-name,  next,      previous,  up\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:2692
msgid ""
"This @code{@@node} line says that the name of this node is "
"``Chapter@tie{}2'', the name of the `Next' node is ``Chapter 3'', the name "
"of the `Previous' node is ``Chapter@tie{}1'', and the name of the `Up' node "
"is ``Top''.  You can (and should) omit writing out these node names if your "
"document is hierarchically organized, but the pointer relationships still "
"obtain."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:2696
msgid ""
"To go to Sections 2.1 and 2.2 using Info, you need a menu inside Chapter 2.  "
"(@xref{Menus}.)  You would write the menu just before the beginning of "
"Section 2.1, like this:"
msgstr ""

#. type: group
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:2703
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   @@menu\n"
"   * Sect. 2.1::    Description of this section.\n"
"   * Sect. 2.2::    Description.\n"
"   @@end menu\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:2707
msgid "The automatic pointers for the node for Sect.@: 2.1 correspond to:"
msgstr ""

#. type: group
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:2712
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"@@node     Sect. 2.1, Sect. 2.2, ,         Chapter 2\n"
"@@comment  node-name, next,      previous, up\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:2717
msgid ""
"Note that no `Prev' pointer is generated, since there is no other node at "
"the same hierarchical level before Sect.@: 2.1."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:2719
msgid ""
"Using explicit pointers, the node for Sect.@: 2.1 could be written like this:"
msgstr ""

#. type: group
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:2724
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"@@node     Sect. 2.1, Sect. 2.2, Chapter 2, Chapter 2\n"
"@@comment  node-name, next,      previous,  up\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:2736
msgid ""
"With automatic pointers, the `Next' and `Previous' pointers of a node lead "
"to other nodes at the same level---from chapter to chapter or from section "
"to section.  As shown, when using explicit pointers, the pointers can also "
"lead somewhere else, here, for example, the `Previous' pointer points up.  "
"An `Up' pointer usually leads to a node at the level above (closer to the "
"`Top' node; and a `Menu' leads to nodes at a level below (closer to "
"`leaves').  (A cross-reference can point to a node at any level; see "
"@ref{Cross References}.)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:2742
msgid ""
"Technically, explicit node pointers can carry you to any node, regardless of "
"the structure of the document; even to nodes in a different Info file.  "
"However, it would be very confusing for readers to have the `Next', "
"`Previous' and `Up' pointers lead to nodes that do not correspond, even "
"loosely, to the next, previous and up node."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:2750
msgid ""
"A @code{@@node} command and a chapter structuring command are conventionally "
"used together, in that order, often followed by indexing commands.  (As "
"shown in the example above, you may follow the @code{@@node} line with a "
"comment line, e.g., to show which pointer is which if explicit pointers are "
"used.)  The Texinfo processors use this construct to determine the "
"relationships between nodes and sectioning commands."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:2754
msgid ""
"Here is the beginning of the chapter in this manual called ``Ending a "
"Texinfo File''.  This shows a @code{@@node} line followed by a "
"@code{@@chapter} line, and then by indexing lines."
msgstr ""

#. type: group
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:2762
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"@@node Ending a File\n"
"@@chapter Ending a Texinfo File\n"
"@@cindex Ending a Texinfo file\n"
"@@cindex Texinfo file ending\n"
"@@cindex File ending\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: section
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:2766
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:2770
#, no-wrap
msgid "Node Descriptions"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:2769
msgid ""
"@nodedescriptionblock @code{@@nodedescription} and "
"@code{@@nodedescriptionblock}."
msgstr ""

#. type: findex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:2772
#, no-wrap
msgid "nodedescription"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:2777
msgid ""
"You can provide a short description of the purpose of a node by using the "
"@code{@@nodedescription} command following the @code{@@node} line.  Such a "
"description might elaborate on or extend the information in the node name "
"itself."
msgstr ""

#. type: findex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:2778
#, no-wrap
msgid "nodedescriptionblock"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:2781
msgid ""
"You can also use a @code{@@nodedescriptionblock} environment to provide a "
"node description. This may be useful for longer descriptions."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:2788
msgid ""
"@command{texi2any} uses the content you provide with these commands when "
"outputing menus for Info output format (and, optionally, for HTML).  "
"@command{texi2any} uses the description after a menu entry for the node if "
"it is generating the menu automatically, or if no description for the menu "
"entry was provided in an explicit @code{@@menu} block. (@xref{Menus})."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:2790
msgid "Here is an example of using these commands:"
msgstr ""

#. type: example
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:2794
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"@@node Tools\n"
"@@chapter Tools\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: example
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:2796
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This chapter is on different tools you can use.\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: example
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:2800
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"@@node Screwdrivers\n"
"@@nodedescription Flathead and Phillips.\n"
"@@section Screwdrivers\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: example
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:2802
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This section is about screwdrivers.\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: example
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:2809
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"@@node Drills\n"
"@@nodedescriptionblock\n"
"Making holes in things with power screwdrivers, drill drivers, combi\n"
"drills, impact drivers, hammer drills, breakers and demolition drills.\n"
"@@end nodedescriptionblock\n"
"@@section Drills\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: example
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:2811
#, no-wrap
msgid "This section is about drills.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:2815
msgid ""
"In Info output, @command{texi2any} would output the @samp{Tools} node with a "
"menu as follows:"
msgstr ""

#. type: group
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:2818
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:2932
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"* Menu:\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: example
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:2824
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"* Screwdrivers::          Flathead and Phillips.\n"
"* Drills::                Making holes in things with power\n"
"                          screwdrivers, drill drivers, combi\n"
"                          drills, impact drivers, hammer drills,\n"
"                          breakers and demolition drills.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:2827
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:2829
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:2830
#, no-wrap
msgid "Menus"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:2829
msgid "@nodedescription Listing subordinate nodes."
msgstr ""

#. type: findex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:2831
#, no-wrap
msgid "menu"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:2838
msgid ""
"@dfn{Menus} contain pointers to subordinate nodes.  In Info output, you use "
"menus to go to such nodes.  @command{texi2any} can output menus in HTML "
"output, but does not do so by default (@pxref{Other Customization "
"Variables}, under @code{FORMAT_MENU}).  Menus have no role in printed "
"manuals or other output formats."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:2842
msgid ""
"Menus are automatically generated by @command{texi2any} when outputting Info "
"for nodes followed by a sectioning command, without an explicit "
"@code{@@menu} block, and with automatic pointers."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:2850
msgid ""
"It is often more convenient to let @command{texi2any} generate menus for "
"you, as you do not then have the burden of updating menu blocks in your "
"Texinfo source when you add, remove, or relocate nodes.  In the usual case "
"of a hierarchically organized manual with sectioning commands associated "
"with nodes, and with node pointers left out, you should only write menus if "
"you want exact control over the contents and formatting of menus in Info."
msgstr ""

#. type: subsection
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:2852
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:2854
#, no-wrap
msgid "Writing a Menu"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:2854
msgid "@nodedescription What is a menu?"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:2855
#, no-wrap
msgid "Writing a menu"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:2856
#, no-wrap
msgid "Menu writing"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:2861
msgid ""
"A menu consists of a @code{@@menu} command on a line by itself, followed by "
"menu entry lines or menu comment lines, and then followed by an @code{@@end "
"menu} command on a line by itself."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:2863
msgid "A menu looks like this:"
msgstr ""

#. type: group
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:2868
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:2945
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"@@menu\n"
"Larger Units of Text\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: group
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:2873
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:2950
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"* Files::                       All about handling files.\n"
"* Multiples: Buffers.           Multiple buffers; editing\n"
"                                 several files at once.\n"
"@@end menu\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:2876
#, no-wrap
msgid "Spaces, in menus"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:2879
msgid ""
"In a menu, every line that begins with an @w{@samp{* }} is a @dfn{menu "
"entry}.  (Note the space after the asterisk.)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:2885
msgid ""
"A line that does not start with an @w{@samp{* }} may also appear in a menu.  "
"Such a line is not a menu entry but rather a @dfn{menu comment} line that "
"appears in the Info file.  In the example above, the line @samp{Larger Units "
"of Text} is such a menu comment line; the two lines starting with @w{@samp{* "
"}} are menu entries."
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:2886
#, no-wrap
msgid "Hierarchical documents, and menus"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:2894
msgid ""
"Technically, menus can carry you to any node, regardless of the structure of "
"the document; even to nodes in a different Info file.  However, the "
"@command{texi2any} implicit pointer creation feature (@pxref{Writing a "
"Node}) and GNU Emacs Texinfo mode updating commands work only to create "
"menus of subordinate nodes in a hierarchically structured document.  In a "
"hierarchically structured document, it is much better to use "
"cross-references to refer to arbitrary nodes."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:2898
msgid ""
"In Info, a user selects a node with the @kbd{m} (@code{Info-menu})  "
"command.  The menu entry name is what the user types after the @kbd{m} "
"command."
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:2898
#, no-wrap
msgid "@code{accesskey} @subentry in HTML output of menus"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:2904
msgid ""
"In the HTML output, the @code{accesskey} attribute is used with the values "
"@samp{1}@dots{}@samp{9} for the first nine entries.  This allows people "
"using web browsers to follow the first menu entries using (typically) "
"@kbd{M-@var{digit}}, e.g., @kbd{M-1} for the first entry."
msgstr ""

#. type: node
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:2906
#, no-wrap
msgid "Menu Example"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:2908
msgid "@nodedescription Two and three part menu entries."
msgstr ""

#. type: subsection
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:2908
#, no-wrap
msgid "A Menu Example"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:2909
#, no-wrap
msgid "Menu example"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:2910
#, no-wrap
msgid "Example menu"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:2915
msgid "A menu looks like this in Texinfo:"
msgstr ""

#. type: group
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:2922
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"@@menu\n"
"* menu entry name: Node name.   A short description.\n"
"* Node name::                   This form is preferred.\n"
"@@end menu\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:2928
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:2956
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:5007
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:5137
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:5256
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:5684
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:6804
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:6841
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:6907
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:6935
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:7067
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:7153
msgid "This produces:"
msgstr ""

#. type: group
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:2935
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"* menu entry name: Node name.   A short description.\n"
"* Node name::                   This form is preferred.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:2940
msgid "Here is an example as you might see it in a Texinfo file:"
msgstr ""

#. type: group
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:2961
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"* Menu:\n"
"Larger Units of Text\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: group
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:2965
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"* Files::                       All about handling files.\n"
"* Multiples: Buffers.           Multiple buffers; editing\n"
"                                 several files at once.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:2973
msgid ""
"In this example, the menu has two entries.  @samp{Files} is both a menu "
"entry name and the name of the node referred to by that name.  "
"@samp{Multiples} is the menu entry name; it refers to the node named "
"@samp{Buffers}. The line @samp{Larger Units of Text} is a comment; it "
"appears in the menu, but is not an entry."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:2977
msgid ""
"Since no file name is specified with either @samp{Files} or @samp{Buffers}, "
"they must be the names of nodes in the same Info file (@pxref{Other Info "
"Files, , Referring to Other Info Files})."
msgstr ""

#. type: subsection
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:2979
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:2981
#, no-wrap
msgid "Menu Location"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:2981
msgid "@nodedescription Menus go at the ends of nodes."
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:2982
#, no-wrap
msgid "Menu location"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:2983
#, no-wrap
msgid "Location of menus"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:2989
msgid ""
"There may be at most one menu in a node.  A menu is conventionally located "
"at the end of a node, without any regular text or additional commands "
"between the @code{@@end menu} and the beginning of the next node."
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:2990
#, no-wrap
msgid "Info format, and menus"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:2996
msgid ""
"This convention is useful, since a reader who uses the menu could easily "
"miss any such text.  Also, any such post-menu text will be considered part "
"of the menu in Info output (which has no marker for the end of a menu).  "
"Thus, a line beginning with @samp{* } will likely be incorrectly handled."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:3001
msgid ""
"It's usually best if a node with a menu does not contain much text.  If you "
"find yourself with a lot of text before a menu, we generally recommend "
"moving all but a couple of paragraphs into a new subnode.  Otherwise, it is "
"easy for readers to miss the menu."
msgstr ""

#. type: node
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:3003
#, no-wrap
msgid "Menu Parts"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:3005
msgid "@nodedescription A menu entry has three parts."
msgstr ""

#. type: subsection
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:3005
#, no-wrap
msgid "The Parts of a Menu"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:3006
#, no-wrap
msgid "Parts of a menu"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:3007
#, no-wrap
msgid "Menu parts"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:3008
#, no-wrap
msgid "@code{@@menu} parts"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:3011
msgid "A menu entry has three parts, only the second of which is required:"
msgstr ""

#. type: enumerate
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:3015
msgid "The menu entry name (optional)."
msgstr ""

#. type: enumerate
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:3018
msgid "The name of the node (required)."
msgstr ""

#. type: enumerate
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:3021
msgid "A description of the item (optional)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:3025
msgid ""
"The template for a generic menu entry looks like this (but see the next "
"section for one more possibility):"
msgstr ""

#. type: example
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:3028
#, no-wrap
msgid "* @var{menu-entry-name}: @var{node-name}.   @var{description}\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:3033
msgid ""
"Follow the menu entry name with a single colon, and follow the node name "
"with tab, comma, newline, or the two characters period and space (@samp{. })."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:3042
msgid ""
"The third part of a menu entry is a descriptive phrase or sentence.  Menu "
"entry names and node names are often short; the description explains to the "
"reader what the node is about.  A useful description complements the node "
"name rather than repeats it.  The description, which is optional, can spread "
"over multiple lines; if it does, some authors prefer to indent the second "
"line while others prefer to align it with the first (and all others).  It's "
"up to you.  An empty line, or the next menu entry, ends a description."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:3049
msgid ""
"Space characters in a menu are preserved as-is in the Info output; this "
"allows you to format the menu as you wish.  Unfortunately you must type node "
"names without any extra spaces or some versions of some Info readers will "
"not find the node (@pxref{Node Line Requirements})."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:3053
msgid ""
"@command{texi2any} warns and protect names when the text of a menu item (and "
"node names and cross-references) contains a problematic construct that could "
"interfere with its parsing in Info.  @xref{Info Node Names Constraints}."
msgstr ""

#. type: subsection
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:3055
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:3057
#, no-wrap
msgid "Less Cluttered Menu Entry"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:3057
msgid "@nodedescription Two part menu entry."
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:3058
#, no-wrap
msgid "Two part menu entry"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:3059
#, no-wrap
msgid "Double-colon menu entries"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:3060
#, no-wrap
msgid "Menu entries with two colons"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:3061
#, no-wrap
msgid "Less cluttered menu entry"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:3062
#, no-wrap
msgid "Uncluttered menu entry"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:3067
msgid ""
"When the menu entry name and node name are the same, you can write the name "
"immediately after the asterisk and space at the beginning of the line and "
"follow the name with two colons."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:3070
msgid "For example, write"
msgstr ""

#. type: example
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:3074
#, no-wrap
msgid "* Name::                        @var{description}\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:3079
msgid "instead of"
msgstr ""

#. type: example
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:3082
#, no-wrap
msgid "* Name: Name.                   @var{description}\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:3086
msgid ""
"We recommend using the node name for the menu entry name whenever possible, "
"since it reduces visual clutter in the menu."
msgstr ""

#. type: node
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:3088
#, no-wrap
msgid "Other Info Files"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:3090
msgid "@nodedescription How to refer to a different Info file."
msgstr ""

#. type: subsection
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:3090
#, no-wrap
msgid "Referring to Other Info Files"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:3091
#, no-wrap
msgid "Referring to other Info files"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:3092
#, no-wrap
msgid "Nodes in other Info files"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:3093
#, no-wrap
msgid "Other Info files' nodes"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:3094
#, no-wrap
msgid "Going to other Info files' nodes"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:3095
#, no-wrap
msgid "Info; other files' nodes"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:3100
msgid ""
"You can create a menu entry that enables a reader in Info to go to a node in "
"another Info file by writing the file name in parentheses just before the "
"node name.  Some examples:"
msgstr ""

#. type: group
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:3107
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"@@menu\n"
"* @var{first-entry-name}:(@var{filename})@var{nodename}.     "
"@var{description}\n"
"* (@var{filename})@var{second-node}::                  @var{description}\n"
"@@end menu\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:3114
msgid ""
"For example, to refer directly to the @samp{Outlining} and @samp{Rebinding} "
"nodes in the @cite{Emacs Manual}, you could write a menu like this:"
msgstr ""

#. type: group
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:3123
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"@@menu\n"
"* Outlining: (emacs)Outline Mode. The major mode for\n"
"                                   editing outlines.\n"
"* (emacs)Rebinding::              How to redefine the\n"
"                                   meaning of a key.\n"
"@@end menu\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:3128
msgid ""
"If you do not list the node name, but only name the file, then Info presumes "
"that you are referring to the `Top' node.  Examples:"
msgstr ""

#. type: group
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:3134
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"* Info: (info).         Documentation browsing system.\n"
"* (emacs)::             The extensible, self-documenting\n"
"                         text editor.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:3141
msgid ""
"The GNU Emacs Texinfo mode menu updating commands only work with nodes "
"within the current buffer, so you cannot use them to create menus that refer "
"to other files.  You must write such menus by hand.  @xref{Updating Nodes "
"and Menus}."
msgstr ""

#. type: chapter
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:3143
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:3145
#, no-wrap
msgid "Chapter Structuring"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:3145
msgid "@nodedescription Creating chapters, sections, appendices, etc."
msgstr ""

#.  old name
#. type: anchor{#1}
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:3147
msgid "Structuring"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:3147
#, no-wrap
msgid "Chapter structuring"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:3148
#, no-wrap
msgid "Structuring of chapters"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:3149
#, no-wrap
msgid "Sectioning"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:3156
msgid ""
"Texinfo's @dfn{chapter structuring} commands divide a document into a "
"hierarchy of chapters, sections, subsections, and subsubsections.  These "
"commands generate large headings in the text, like the one above.  They also "
"provide information for generating the table of contents (@pxref{Contents,, "
"Generating a Table of Contents})."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:3159
msgid ""
"Normally you put a @code{@@node} command immediately before each chapter "
"structuring command.  @xref{Nodes}."
msgstr ""

#. type: node
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:3161
#, no-wrap
msgid "Tree Structuring"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:3163
msgid "@nodedescription A manual is like an upside down tree @dots{}"
msgstr ""

#. type: section
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:3163
#, no-wrap
msgid "Tree Structure of Sections"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:3164
#, no-wrap
msgid "Tree structuring"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:3171
msgid ""
"A Texinfo file is usually structured like a book with chapters, sections, "
"subsections, and the like.  This structure can be visualized as a tree (or "
"rather as an upside-down tree) with the root at the top and the levels "
"corresponding to chapters, sections, subsection, and subsubsections."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:3174
msgid ""
"Here is a diagram that shows a Texinfo file with three chapters, each with "
"two sections."
msgstr ""

#. type: group
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:3187
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"                         Top\n"
"                          |\n"
"        -------------------------------------\n"
"       |                  |                  |\n"
"    Chapter 1          Chapter 2          Chapter 3\n"
"       |                  |                  |\n"
"    --------           --------           --------\n"
"   |        |         |        |         |        |\n"
"Section  Section   Section  Section   Section  Section\n"
"  1.1      1.2       2.1      2.2       3.1      3.2\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:3193
msgid ""
"In a Texinfo file that has this structure, the beginning of Chapter 2 would "
"be written like this:"
msgstr ""

#. type: group
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:3198
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"@@node    Chapter 2\n"
"@@chapter Chapter 2\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:3204
msgid ""
"For purposes of example, here is how it would be written with explicit node "
"pointers:"
msgstr ""

#. type: group
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:3209
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"@@node    Chapter 2,  Chapter 3, Chapter 1, Top\n"
"@@chapter Chapter 2\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:3215
msgid ""
"The chapter structuring commands are described in the sections that follow; "
"the @code{@@node} command is described in the previous chapter "
"(@pxref{Nodes})."
msgstr ""

#. type: section
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:3217
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:3218
#, no-wrap
msgid "Structuring Command Types"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:3223
msgid ""
"The chapter structuring commands fall into four groups, each of which "
"contains structuring commands at the levels of chapters, sections, "
"subsections, and subsubsections:"
msgstr ""

#. type: itemize
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:3229
msgid ""
"The @code{@@chapter}-like commands and @code{@@appendix}-like commands "
"produce numbered or lettered entries both in the body of a document and in "
"its table of contents."
msgstr ""

#. type: itemize
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:3236
msgid ""
"The @code{@@unnumbered}-like commands produce unnumbered entries both in the "
"body of a document and in its table of contents.  The @code{@@top} command, "
"which has a special use, is a member of this group (@pxref{@code{@@top} "
"Command}).  An @code{@@unnumbered} section is a normal part of the document "
"structure."
msgstr ""

#. type: itemize
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:3242
msgid ""
"The @code{@@heading}-like commands produce simple unnumbered headings that "
"do not appear in a table of contents, are not associated with nodes, and "
"cannot be cross-referenced.  These heading commands never start a new page."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:3249
msgid ""
"In printed output, the chapter structuring commands produce headings in the "
"document.  When a @code{@@setchapternewpage} command says to do so, the "
"@code{@@chapter}, @code{@@unnumbered}, and @code{@@appendix} commands start "
"new pages in the printed manual; the @code{@@heading} commands do not.  "
"@xref{@code{@@setchapternewpage}}."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:3254
msgid ""
"In Info and plain text output, the command causes the title to appear on a "
"line by itself, with a line of an ASCII character (@samp{*}, @samp{=}, "
"@dots{}) inserted underneath.  For example, the ``Chapter Structuring'' "
"heading could be:"
msgstr ""

#. type: group
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:3259
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"5 Chapter Structuring\n"
"*********************\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:3266
msgid ""
"same level.  For instance, it is the same for the chapter-level commands "
"@code{@@chapter}, @code{@@apppendix}, @code{@@unnumbered} and "
"@code{@@chapheading}."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:3271
msgid ""
"In HTML, the chapter-level commands produce an @code{<h2>}-level header by "
"default (controlled by the @code{CHAPTER_HEADER_LEVEL} customization "
"variable, @pxref{Other Customization Variables}).  The heading element level "
"is adjusted for the other commands."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:3277
msgid ""
"In the DocBook output, the appropriate level of element is used.  The "
"produced element includes all following sections up to the next command at "
"the same or higher level.  For example, a @code{<chapter>} element is "
"produced for @code{@@chapter}, and contains any sections or subsections in "
"the chapter."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:3279
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:6948
msgid "Here is a summary:"
msgstr ""

#. type: tex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:3282
#, no-wrap
msgid "{\\globaldefs=1 \\smallfonts \\rm}\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:3285
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"@tab                              @tab                       @tab No new page"
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:3286
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"@i{Numbered}           @tab @i{Unnumbered}               @tab "
"@i{Lettered/numbered} @tab @i{Unnumbered}"
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:3287
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In contents            @tab In contents                  @tab In "
"contents           @tab Not in contents"
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:3288
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"@tab @code{@@top}                 @tab                       @tab "
"@code{@@majorheading}"
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:3289
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"@code{@@chapter}       @tab @code{@@unnumbered}          @tab "
"@code{@@appendix} @tab @code{@@chapheading}"
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:3290
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"@code{@@section}       @tab @code{@@unnumberedsec}       @tab "
"@code{@@appendixsec} @tab @code{@@heading}"
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:3291
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"@code{@@subsection}    @tab @code{@@unnumberedsubsec}    @tab "
"@code{@@appendixsubsec} @tab @code{@@subheading}"
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:3292
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"@code{@@subsubsection} @tab @code{@@unnumberedsubsubsec} @tab "
"@code{@@appendixsubsubsec} @tab @code{@@subsubheading}"
msgstr ""

#. type: tex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:3296
#, no-wrap
msgid "{\\globaldefs=1 \\textfonts \\rm}\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: node
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:3299
#, no-wrap
msgid "@code{@@chapter}"
msgstr ""

#. type: section
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:3300
#, no-wrap
msgid "@code{@@chapter}: Chapter Structuring"
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:3303
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:15139
#, no-wrap
msgid "chapter"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:3310
msgid ""
"@code{@@chapter} identifies a chapter in the document--the highest level of "
"the normal document structuring hierarchy.  Write the command at the "
"beginning of a line and follow it on the same line by the title of the "
"chapter.  The chapter is numbered automatically, starting from@tie{}1."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:3314
msgid ""
"For example, the present chapter in this manual is entitled ``Chapter "
"Structuring''; the @code{@@chapter} line looks like this:"
msgstr ""

#. type: example
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:3317
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@chapter Chapter Structuring\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: node
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:3321
#, no-wrap
msgid "@code{@@unnumbered @@appendix}"
msgstr ""

#. type: section
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:3322
#, no-wrap
msgid "@code{@@unnumbered}, @code{@@appendix}: Chapters with Other Labeling"
msgstr ""

#.  old name
#. type: anchor{#1}
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:3325
msgid "unnumbered & appendix"
msgstr ""

#. type: findex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:3325
#, no-wrap
msgid "unnumbered"
msgstr ""

#. type: findex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:3326
#, no-wrap
msgid "appendix"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:3333
msgid ""
"Use the @code{@@unnumbered} command to start a chapter-level element that "
"appears without chapter numbers of any kind.  Use the @code{@@appendix} "
"command to start an appendix that is labeled by letter (`A', `B', @dots{}) "
"instead of by number; appendices are also at the chapter level of "
"structuring."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:3337
msgid ""
"Write an @code{@@appendix} or @code{@@unnumbered} command at the beginning "
"of a line and follow it on the same line by the title, just as with "
"@code{@@chapter}."
msgstr ""

#. type: findex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:3338
#, no-wrap
msgid "centerchap"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:3346
msgid ""
"Texinfo also provides a command @code{@@centerchap}, which is analogous to "
"@code{@@unnumbered}, but centers its argument in the printed and HTML "
"outputs.  This kind of stylistic choice is not usually offered by Texinfo.  "
"You are recommended not to use this command, as it may be removed in future "
"releases of Texinfo."
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:3347
#, no-wrap
msgid "DocBook and prefatory sections"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:3348
#, no-wrap
msgid "Preface, etc., and DocBook"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:3351
msgid ""
"With @code{@@unnumbered}, if the name of the associated node is one of these "
"English words (case-insensitive):"
msgstr ""

#. type: example
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:3354
#, no-wrap
msgid "Acknowledgements  Colophon  Dedication  Preface\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:3356
#, no-wrap
msgid "@code{<acknowledgements>} DocBook tag"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:3357
#, no-wrap
msgid "@code{<colophon>} DocBook tag"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:3358
#, no-wrap
msgid "@code{<dedication>} DocBook tag"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:3359
#, no-wrap
msgid "@code{<preface>} DocBook tag"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:3360
#, no-wrap
msgid "@code{<chapter>} DocBook tag"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:3365
msgid ""
"(@code{<preface>}, etc.)@: instead of the default @code{<chapter>}.  The "
"argument to @code{@@unnumbered} itself can be anything, and is output as the "
"element title as usual."
msgstr ""

#. type: node
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:3367
#, no-wrap
msgid "@code{@@majorheading @@chapheading}"
msgstr ""

#. type: section
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:3368
#, no-wrap
msgid "@code{@@majorheading}, @code{@@chapheading}: Chapter-level Headings"
msgstr ""

#.  old name
#. type: anchor{#1}
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:3371
msgid "majorheading & chapheading"
msgstr ""

#. type: findex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:3371
#, no-wrap
msgid "majorheading"
msgstr ""

#. type: findex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:3372
#, no-wrap
msgid "chapheading"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:3376
msgid ""
"The @code{@@majorheading} and @code{@@chapheading} commands produce "
"chapter-like headings in the body of a document."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:3380
msgid ""
"However, neither command produces an entry in the table of contents, and "
"neither command causes @TeX{} to start a new page in a printed manual."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:3384
msgid ""
"In @TeX{}, a @code{@@majorheading} command generates a larger vertical "
"whitespace before the heading than a @code{@@chapheading} command but is "
"otherwise the same."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:3389
msgid ""
"In other output formats, the @code{@@majorheading} and @code{@@chapheading} "
"commands produce a similar output to @code{@@chapter}.  The difference is "
"the lack of numbering and the lack of any association with nodes.  "
"@xref{@code{@@chapter}}."
msgstr ""

#. type: node
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:3391
#, no-wrap
msgid "@code{@@section}"
msgstr ""

#. type: section
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:3392
#, no-wrap
msgid "@code{@@section}: Sections Below Chapters"
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:3395
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:15143
#, no-wrap
msgid "section"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:3404
msgid ""
"An @code{@@section} command identifies a section within a chapter unit, "
"whether created with @code{@@chapter}, @code{@@unnumbered}, or "
"@code{@@appendix}, following the numbering scheme of the chapter-level "
"command.  Thus, within a @code{@@chapter} chapter numbered `1', the sections "
"are numbered `1.1', `1.2', etc.; within an @code{@@appendix} ``chapter'' "
"labeled `A', the sections are numbered `A.1', `A.2', etc.; within an "
"@code{@@unnumbered} chapter, the section gets no number."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:3408
msgid ""
"To make a section, write the @code{@@section} command at the beginning of a "
"line and follow it on the same line by the section title.  For example:"
msgstr ""

#. type: example
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:3411
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@section This is a section\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:3414
msgid "Section titles are listed in the table of contents."
msgstr ""

#. type: node
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:3416
#, no-wrap
msgid "@code{@@unnumberedsec @@appendixsec @@heading}"
msgstr ""

#. type: section
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:3417
#, no-wrap
msgid "@code{@@unnumberedsec}, @code{@@appendixsec}, @code{@@heading}"
msgstr ""

#.  old name
#. type: anchor{#1}
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:3420
msgid "unnumberedsec appendixsec heading"
msgstr ""

#. type: findex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:3420
#, no-wrap
msgid "unnumberedsec"
msgstr ""

#. type: findex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:3421
#, no-wrap
msgid "appendixsec"
msgstr ""

#. type: findex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:3422
#, no-wrap
msgid "heading"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:3428
msgid ""
"The @code{@@unnumberedsec}, @code{@@appendixsec}, and @code{@@heading} "
"commands are, respectively, the unnumbered, appendix-like, and heading-like "
"equivalents of the @code{@@section} command (see the previous section)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:3433
msgid ""
"@code{@@unnumberedsec} and @code{@@appendixsec} do not need to be used in "
"ordinary circumstances, because @code{@@section} may also be used within "
"@code{@@unnumbered} and @code{@@appendix} chapters; again, see the previous "
"section."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:3435
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@unnumberedsec"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:3439
msgid ""
"The @code{@@unnumberedsec} command may be used within an unnumbered chapter "
"or within a regular chapter or appendix to produce an unnumbered section."
msgstr ""

#. type: findex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:3440
#, no-wrap
msgid "appendixsection"
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:3441
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@appendixsec"
msgstr ""

#. type: itemx
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:3442
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@appendixsection"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:3445
msgid ""
"@code{@@appendixsection} is a longer spelling of the @code{@@appendixsec} "
"command; the two are synonymous."
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:3448
msgid ""
"Conventionally, the @code{@@appendixsec} or @code{@@appendixsection} command "
"is used only within appendices."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:3449
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@heading"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:3455
msgid ""
"You may use the @code{@@heading} command (almost) anywhere for a "
"section-style heading that will not appear in the table of contents.  The "
"@code{@@heading}-series commands can appear inside most environments, for "
"example, though pathological and useless locations such as an argument to "
"another command, etc., are not allowed."
msgstr ""

#. type: node
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:3459
#, no-wrap
msgid "@code{@@subsection}"
msgstr ""

#. type: section
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:3460
#, no-wrap
msgid "@code{@@subsection}: Subsections Below Sections"
msgstr ""

#. type: findex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:3463
#, no-wrap
msgid "subsection"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:3467
msgid ""
"Subsections are to sections as sections are to chapters; "
"@pxref{@code{@@section}}.  For example:"
msgstr ""

#. type: example
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:3470
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@subsection This is a subsection\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:3473
msgid "Subsection titles are listed in the table of contents."
msgstr ""

#. type: node
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:3475
#, no-wrap
msgid "@code{@@unnumberedsubsec @@appendixsubsec @@subheading}"
msgstr ""

#. type: section
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:3476
#, no-wrap
msgid "The @code{@@subsection}-like Commands"
msgstr ""

#.  old name
#. type: anchor{#1}
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:3479
msgid "unnumberedsubsec appendixsubsec subheading"
msgstr ""

#. type: findex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:3479
#, no-wrap
msgid "unnumberedsubsec"
msgstr ""

#. type: findex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:3480
#, no-wrap
msgid "appendixsubsec"
msgstr ""

#. type: findex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:3481
#, no-wrap
msgid "subheading"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:3482
#, no-wrap
msgid "Subsection-like commands"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:3488
msgid ""
"The @code{@@unnumberedsubsec}, @code{@@appendixsubsec}, and "
"@code{@@subheading} commands are, respectively, the unnumbered, "
"appendix-like, and heading-like equivalents of the @code{@@subsection} "
"command.  (@xref{@code{@@subsection}}.)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:3493
msgid ""
"@code{@@unnumberedsubsec} and @code{@@appendixsubsec} do not need to be used "
"in ordinary circumstances, because @code{@@subsection} may also be used "
"within sections of @code{@@unnumbered} and @code{@@appendix} chapters "
"(@pxref{@code{@@section}})."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:3501
msgid ""
"An @code{@@subheading} command produces a heading like that of a subsection "
"except that it is not numbered and does not appear in the table of "
"contents.  Similarly, an @code{@@unnumberedsubsec} command produces an "
"unnumbered heading like that of a subsection and an @code{@@appendixsubsec} "
"command produces a subsection-like heading labeled with a letter and "
"numbers; both of these commands produce headings that appear in the table of "
"contents."
msgstr ""

#. type: node
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:3503
#, no-wrap
msgid "@code{@@subsubsection}"
msgstr ""

#. type: section
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:3504
#, no-wrap
msgid "@code{@@subsubsection} and Other Subsub Commands"
msgstr ""

#. type: findex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:3507
#, no-wrap
msgid "subsubsection"
msgstr ""

#. type: findex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:3508
#, no-wrap
msgid "unnumberedsubsubsec"
msgstr ""

#. type: findex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:3509
#, no-wrap
msgid "appendixsubsubsec"
msgstr ""

#. type: findex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:3510
#, no-wrap
msgid "subsubheading"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:3511
#, no-wrap
msgid "Subsub sectioning commands"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:3515
msgid ""
"The fourth and lowest level sectioning commands in Texinfo are the `subsub' "
"commands.  They are:"
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:3517
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@subsubsection"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:3521
msgid ""
"Subsubsections are to subsections as subsections are to sections.  "
"(@xref{@code{@@subsection}}.)  Subsubsection titles appear in the table of "
"contents."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:3522
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@unnumberedsubsubsec"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:3526
msgid ""
"Unnumbered subsubsection titles appear in the table of contents, but lack "
"numbers.  Otherwise, unnumbered subsubsections are the same as "
"subsubsections."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:3527
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@appendixsubsubsec"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:3531
msgid ""
"Conventionally, appendix commands are used only for appendices and are "
"lettered and numbered appropriately.  They also appear in the table of "
"contents."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:3532
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@subsubheading"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:3535
msgid ""
"The @code{@@subsubheading} command may be used anywhere that you want a "
"small heading that will not appear in the table of contents."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:3542
msgid ""
"As with subsections, @code{@@unnumberedsubsubsec} and "
"@code{@@appendixsubsubsec} do not need to be used in ordinary circumstances, "
"because @code{@@subsubsection} may also be used within subsections of "
"@code{@@unnumbered} and @code{@@appendix} chapters "
"(@pxref{@code{@@section}})."
msgstr ""

#. type: node
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:3544
#, no-wrap
msgid "@code{@@part}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:3546
msgid "@nodedescription Collections of chapters."
msgstr ""

#. type: section
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:3546
#, no-wrap
msgid "@code{@@part}: Groups of Chapters"
msgstr ""

#. type: findex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:3547
#, no-wrap
msgid "part"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:3548
#, no-wrap
msgid "Part pages"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:3554
msgid ""
"The final sectioning command is @code{@@part}, to mark a @dfn{part} of a "
"manual, that is, a group of chapters or (rarely) appendices.  This behaves "
"quite differently from the other sectioning commands, to fit with the way "
"such ``parts'' are conventionally used in books."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:3559
msgid ""
"No @code{@@node} command is associated with @code{@@part}.  Just write the "
"command on a line by itself, including the part title, at the place in the "
"document you want to mark off as starting that part.  For example:"
msgstr ""

#. type: example
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:3562
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@part Part I:@@* The beginning\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:3566
msgid ""
"As can be inferred from this example, no automatic numbering or labeling of "
"the @code{@@part} text is done.  The text is taken as-is."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:3571
msgid ""
"Because parts are not associated with nodes, no general text can follow the "
"@code{@@part} line.  To produce the intended output, it must be followed by "
"a chapter-level command (including its node).  Thus, to continue the example:"
msgstr ""

#. type: example
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:3574
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"@@part Part I:@@* The beginning\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: example
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:3578
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"@@node Introduction\n"
"@@chapter Introduction\n"
"...\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:3590
msgid ""
"In the @TeX{} output, the @code{@@part} text is included in both the normal "
"and short tables of contents (@pxref{Contents}), without a page number "
"(since that is the normal convention).  In addition, a ``part page'' is "
"output in the body of the document, with just the @code{@@part} text.  In "
"the example above, the @code{@@*} causes a line break on the part page (but "
"is replaced with a space in the tables of contents).  This part page is "
"always forced to be on an odd (right-hand) page, regardless of the chapter "
"pagination (@pxref{@code{@@setchapternewpage}}).  In the @LaTeX{} output, "
"the @code{@@part} is output as @code{\\part}."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:3594
msgid ""
"In the HTML output, the @code{@@part} text is similarly included in the "
"tables of contents, and a heading is included in the main document text, as "
"part of the following chapter or appendix node."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:3598
msgid ""
"In the DocBook output, the @code{<part>} element includes all the following "
"chapters, up to the next @code{<part>}.  A @code{<part>} containing chapters "
"is also closed at an appendix."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:3600
msgid "In the Info and plain text output, @code{@@part} has no effect."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:3603
msgid ""
"@code{@@part} is ignored when raising or lowering sections (see next "
"section).  That is, it is never lowered and nothing can be raised to it."
msgstr ""

#. type: node
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:3605
#, no-wrap
msgid "Raise/lower sections"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:3607
msgid "@nodedescription How to change commands' hierarchical level."
msgstr ""

#. type: section
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:3607
#, no-wrap
msgid "Raise/lower Sections: @code{@@raisesections} and @code{@@lowersections}"
msgstr ""

#. type: findex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:3608
#, no-wrap
msgid "raisesections"
msgstr ""

#. type: findex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:3609
#, no-wrap
msgid "lowersections"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:3610
#, no-wrap
msgid "Raising and lowering sections"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:3611
#, no-wrap
msgid "Lowering and raising sections"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:3612
#, no-wrap
msgid "Sections, raising and lowering"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:3617
msgid ""
"The @code{@@raisesections} and @code{@@lowersections} commands implicitly "
"raise and lower the hierarchical level of following chapters, sections and "
"the other sectioning commands (excluding parts)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:3623
msgid ""
"That is, the @code{@@raisesections} command changes sections to chapters, "
"subsections to sections, and so on.  Conversely, the @code{@@lowersections} "
"command changes chapters to sections, sections to subsections, and so on.  "
"Thus, a @code{@@lowersections} command cancels a @code{@@raisesections} "
"command, and vice versa."
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:3624
#, no-wrap
msgid "Include files, and section levels"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:3630
msgid ""
"As a practical matter, you generally only want to raise or lower large "
"chunks, usually in external files.  You can use @code{@@lowersections} to "
"include text written as an outer or standalone Texinfo file in another "
"Texinfo file as an inner, included file (@pxref{Include Files}).  Typical "
"usage looks like this:"
msgstr ""

#. type: example
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:3635
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"@@lowersections\n"
"@@include somefile.texi\n"
"@@raisesections\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:3639
msgid "sections in the main file would also be lowered.)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:3643
msgid ""
"If the included file being lowered has a @code{@@top} node, you'll need to "
"conditionalize its inclusion with a flag (@pxref{@code{@@set @@value}})."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:3649
msgid ""
"Any menus in the final result have to take the raising and lowering into "
"account, so arbitrarily sprinkling @code{@@raisesections} and "
"@code{@@lowersections} commands throughout the document will likely lead to "
"errors (unless the menus in your document are all generated automatically)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:3657
msgid ""
"Repeated use of the commands continues to raise or lower the hierarchical "
"level a step at a time.  An attempt to raise above `chapter' reproduces "
"chapter commands; an attempt to lower below `subsubsection' reproduces "
"subsubsection commands.  Also, lowered subsubsections and raised chapters "
"will not work with @command{texi2any}'s feature of implicitly determining "
"node pointers, since the menu structure cannot be represented correctly."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:3660
msgid ""
"Write each @code{@@raisesections} and @code{@@lowersections} command on a "
"line of its own."
msgstr ""

#. type: node
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:3662
#, no-wrap
msgid "Cross References"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:3664
msgid "@nodedescription Writing cross-references."
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:3664
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:3666
#, no-wrap
msgid "Cross-references"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:3665
#, no-wrap
msgid "Making cross-references"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:3667
#, no-wrap
msgid "References"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:3671
msgid ""
"@dfn{Cross-references} are used to refer the reader to other parts of the "
"same or different Texinfo files."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:3679
msgid ""
"Use cross-references to provide access to information that is too detailed "
"for the current context, or incidental to it.  An online help system or a "
"reference manual is not like a novel; few read such documents in sequence "
"from beginning to end.  Instead, people look up what they need.  For this "
"reason, such creations should contain many cross-references to help readers "
"find other information that they may not have read."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:3688
msgid ""
"In a printed manual, a cross-reference results in a page reference, unless "
"it is to another manual altogether, in which case the cross-reference names "
"that manual.  In Info, a cross-reference results in an entry that you can "
"follow using the Info @samp{f} command.  (@xref{Help-Xref,, Following "
"cross-references, info, Info}.)  In HTML, a cross-reference results in an "
"hyperlink.  In DocBook, the @code{<link>} element is used for "
"cross-references unless it is to another manual, in which case the "
"cross-reference names that manual."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:3697
msgid ""
"The various cross-reference commands use nodes, anchors "
"(@pxref{@code{@@anchor}}) or float labels (@pxref{@code{@@float}}) to define "
"cross-reference locations.  When @TeX{} generates a DVI file, it records "
"each cross-reference location page number and uses the page numbers in "
"making references.  Thus, even if you are writing a manual that will only be "
"printed, and not used online, you must nonetheless write @code{@@node} lines "
"(or @code{@@anchor} anchors) in order to name the places to which you make "
"cross-references."
msgstr ""

#. type: node
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:3701
#, no-wrap
msgid "Cross Reference Commands"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:3703
msgid "@nodedescription A summary of the different commands."
msgstr ""

#. type: section
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:3703
#, no-wrap
msgid "Different Cross-reference Commands"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:3704
#, no-wrap
msgid "Different cross-reference commands"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:3707
msgid "There are three different cross-reference commands:"
msgstr ""

#. type: code{#1}
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:3709
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:4223
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@xref"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:3713
msgid ""
"Used to start a sentence with an Info cross-reference saying @samp{*Note "
"@var{name}: @var{node}.} or with @w{`See @dots{}'} in other output formats."
msgstr ""

#. type: code{#1}
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:3714
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:4237
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@ref"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:3719
msgid ""
"Used within or, more often, at the end of a sentence; produces an Info "
"cross-reference saying @samp{*note @var{name}: @var{node}.}, and just the "
"reference in other output formats, without the preceding `See'."
msgstr ""

#. type: code{#1}
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:3720
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:4297
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@pxref"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:3725
msgid ""
"Used within parentheses, at the end of a sentence, or otherwise before "
"punctuation, to make a reference.  Its output starts with a lowercase "
"@samp{*note} in Info, and with a lowercase `see' in the other output "
"formats.  (@samp{p} is for `parenthesis'.)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:3732
msgid ""
"Additionally, there are commands to produce references to documents outside "
"the Texinfo system.  The @code{@@cite} command is used to make references to "
"books and manuals.  @code{@@url} produces a @acronym{URL}, for example a "
"reference to a page on the World Wide Web."
msgstr ""

#. type: node
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:3734
#, no-wrap
msgid "Cross Reference Parts"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:3736
msgid "@nodedescription A cross-reference has several parts."
msgstr ""

#. type: section
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:3736
#, no-wrap
msgid "Parts of a Cross-reference"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:3737
#, no-wrap
msgid "Cross-reference parts"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:3738
#, no-wrap
msgid "Parts of a cross-reference"
msgstr ""

#.  merged node
#. type: anchor{#1}
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:3740
msgid "Reference Syntax"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:3746
msgid ""
"A cross-reference command requires only one argument, which is the name of "
"the node to which it refers.  A cross-reference command may contain up to "
"four additional arguments.  The template for a full five argument "
"cross-reference looks like this:"
msgstr ""

#. type: group
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:3751
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"@@xref@{@var{node-name}, @var{online-label}, @var{printed-label},\n"
"@var{manual-name}, @var{printed-manual-title}@}\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:3755
msgid "The five possible arguments for a cross-reference are:"
msgstr ""

#. type: enumerate
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:3765
msgid ""
"The node or anchor name.  This is the location to which the cross-reference "
"takes you.  In a printed document, the location of the node provides the "
"page reference only for references within the same document.  Use "
"@code{@@node} to define the node (@pxref{Writing a Node}), @code{@@anchor} "
"(@pxref{@code{@@anchor}}), or @code{@@float} (@pxref{@code{@@float}}) with a "
"label.  This argument is required (except for reference to whole manuals)."
msgstr ""

#. type: enumerate
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:3769
msgid ""
"Write a node name in a cross-reference in exactly the same way as in the "
"@code{@@node} line, including the same capitalization; otherwise, the "
"processors may not find the reference."
msgstr ""

#. type: enumerate
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:3774
msgid ""
"A label for online output.  It is usually omitted; then the topic "
"description (third argument) is used if it was specified; if that was "
"omitted as well, the node name is used."
msgstr ""

#. type: enumerate
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:3779
msgid ""
"A label for printed output.  Often, this is the title or topic of the "
"section.  This is used as the name of the reference in the printed manual.  "
"If omitted, the node name is used."
msgstr ""

#. type: enumerate
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:3783
msgid ""
"The name of the manual to which the reference refers, if it is outside the "
"current manual, in a different Texinfo file."
msgstr ""

#. type: enumerate
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:3787
msgid ""
"The title of the printed manual to which the reference refers, from a "
"different Texinfo file."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:3792
msgid ""
"Whitespace before and after the commas separating these arguments is "
"ignored.  To include a comma in one of the arguments, use @code{@@comma@{@}} "
"(@pxref{Inserting a Comma})."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:3795
msgid ""
"Cross-references with one, two, three, four, and five arguments are "
"described separately in following sections."
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:3796
#, no-wrap
msgid "Comma after cross-reference"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:3802
msgid ""
"When processing with TeX, a comma is automatically inserted after the page "
"number for cross-references to within the same manual, unless the closing "
"brace of the argument is followed by non-whitespace (such as a comma or "
"period).  This gives you the choice of whether to have a comma there in "
"other output formats.  For example,"
msgstr ""

#. type: example
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:3805
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@xref@{Another Section@} for more info\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:3811
msgid ""
"with TeX produces @w{`See Another Section, page @var{ppp}, for more info'}, "
"and in the Info output produces @w{@samp{*Note Another Section:: for more "
"info}}."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:3816
msgid ""
"If an unwanted comma is added, follow the argument with a command such as "
"@samp{@@:}.  For example, @w{@samp{@@xref@{Hurricanes@}@@: --- for the "
"details}} produces"
msgstr ""

#. type: quotation
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:3819
msgid "See Hurricanes, page @var{ppp} --- for the details"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:3823
msgid "@w{`See Hurricanes, page @var{ppp}, --- for the details'}."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:3827
msgid ""
"@command{texi2any} warns and protect names when the text of a "
"cross-reference (and node names and menu items) contains a problematic "
"construct that could interfere with its parsing in Info.  @xref{Info Node "
"Names Constraints}."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:3830
msgid "@raisesections"
msgstr ""

#. type: node
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:3830
#, no-wrap
msgid "One Argument"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:3832
msgid "@nodedescription @code{@@xref} with one argument."
msgstr ""

#. type: subsection
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:3832
#, no-wrap
msgid "@code{@@xref} with One Argument"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:3833
#, no-wrap
msgid "One-argument form of cross-references"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:3837
msgid ""
"The simplest form of @code{@@xref} takes one argument, the name of another "
"node in the same Texinfo file."
msgstr ""

#. type: itemize
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:3841
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:3882
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:3931
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:4034
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:5225
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:5639
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:5804
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:6346
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:7138
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:7929
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:8873
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:10629
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:10826
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:10980
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:12326
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:13329
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:20014
msgid "For example,"
msgstr ""

#. type: example
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:3844
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@xref@{Tropical Storms@}.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:3848
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:3941
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:3969
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:4078
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:4107
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:5107
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:5168
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:5233
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:5327
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:5409
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:5815
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:5979
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:6017
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:6082
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:6269
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:6309
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:6358
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:6383
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:6429
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:9097
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:9866
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:9960
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:10002
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:10641
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:10838
msgid "produces"
msgstr ""

#. type: example
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:3851
#, no-wrap
msgid "*Note Tropical Storms::.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:3855
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:3896
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:3948
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:3976
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:4087
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:4116
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:4205
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:4330
msgid "in Info and"
msgstr ""

#. type: quotation
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:3858
msgid "See Section 3.1 [Tropical Storms], page 24."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:3862
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:3955
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:3983
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:4095
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:4124
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:4212
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:4337
msgid "in a printed manual."
msgstr ""

#. type: node
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:3864
#, no-wrap
msgid "Two Arguments"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:3866
msgid "@nodedescription @code{@@xref} with two arguments."
msgstr ""

#. type: subsection
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:3866
#, no-wrap
msgid "@code{@@xref} with Two Arguments"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:3867
#, no-wrap
msgid "Two-argument form of cross-references"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:3870
msgid ""
"With two arguments, the second is used as a label for the online output."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:3874
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:3921
msgid "The template is like this:"
msgstr ""

#. type: example
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:3877
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@xref@{@var{node-name}, @var{online-label}@}.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: example
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:3885
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@xref@{Electrical Effects, Lightning@}.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:3889
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:10991
msgid "produces:"
msgstr ""

#. type: example
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:3892
#, no-wrap
msgid "*Note Lightning: Electrical Effects.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: quotation
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:3899
msgid "See Section 5.2 [Electrical Effects], page 57."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:3903
msgid "in a printed manual, where the node name is printed."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:3907
msgid ""
"The second argument to cross-references shares constraints with node names.  "
"The potentially problematic character in this context is the colon.  "
"@xref{Info Node Names Constraints}."
msgstr ""

#. type: node
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:3909
#, no-wrap
msgid "Three Arguments"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:3911
msgid "@nodedescription @code{@@xref} with three arguments."
msgstr ""

#. type: subsection
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:3911
#, no-wrap
msgid "@code{@@xref} with Three Arguments"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:3912
#, no-wrap
msgid "Three-argument form of cross-references"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:3917
msgid ""
"A third argument replaces the node name in the printed output.  The third "
"argument should be the name of the section in the printed output, or else "
"state the topic discussed by that section."
msgstr ""

#. type: group
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:3925
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@xref@{@var{node-name}, @var{online-label}, @var{printed-label}@}.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: group
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:3936
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"@@xref@{Electrical Effects, Lightning, Thunder and Lightning@},\n"
"for details.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: example
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:3944
#, no-wrap
msgid "*Note Lightning: Electrical Effects, for details.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: quotation
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:3951
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:3979
msgid "See Section 5.2 [Thunder and Lightning], page 57, for details."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:3959
msgid ""
"If a third argument is given and the second one is empty, then the third "
"argument serves for both.  (Note how two commas, side by side, mark the "
"empty second argument.)"
msgstr ""

#. type: group
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:3964
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"@@xref@{Electrical Effects, , Thunder and Lightning@},\n"
"for details.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: example
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:3972
#, no-wrap
msgid "*Note Thunder and Lightning: Electrical Effects, for details.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:3987
msgid ""
"The third argument to cross-references shares constraints with node names.  "
"The potentially problematic character in this context is the colon.  "
"@xref{Info Node Names Constraints}."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:3992
msgid ""
"As a practical matter, it is often best to write cross-references with just "
"the first argument if the node name and the section title are the same (or "
"nearly so), and with the first and third arguments only if the node name and "
"title are different."
msgstr ""

#. type: findex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:3993
#, no-wrap
msgid "xrefautomaticsectiontitle"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:3997
msgid ""
"Texinfo offers a setting to use the section title instead of node names by "
"default in cross-references (an explicitly specified third argument still "
"takes precedence):"
msgstr ""

#. type: example
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:4000
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@xrefautomaticsectiontitle on\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:4009
msgid ""
"Typically this line would be given near the beginning of the document and "
"used for the whole manual.  But you can turn it off if you want "
"(@code{@@xrefautomaticsectiontitle off}), for example, if you're including "
"some other sub-document that doesn't have suitable section names.  This "
"setting also applies to node headers in HTML, if "
"@code{@@xrefautomaticsectiontitle} is on, the sections names are used in "
"node headers instead of the node names when possible."
msgstr ""

#. type: node
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:4011
#, no-wrap
msgid "Four and Five Arguments"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:4013
msgid "@nodedescription @code{@@xref} with four and five arguments."
msgstr ""

#. type: subsection
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:4013
#, no-wrap
msgid "@code{@@xref} with Four and Five Arguments"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:4014
#, no-wrap
msgid "Four- and five argument forms of cross-references"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:4019
msgid ""
"In a cross-reference, a fourth argument specifies the name of another "
"manual, different from the file in which the reference appears, and a fifth "
"argument specifies its title as a printed manual."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:4023
msgid "The full template is:"
msgstr ""

#. type: group
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:4028
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"@@xref@{@var{node-name}, @var{online-label}, @var{printed-label},\n"
"@var{manual-name}, @var{printed-manual-title}@}.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: example
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:4038
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"@@xref@{Electrical Effects, Lightning, Thunder and Lightning,\n"
"weather, An Introduction to Meteorology@}.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:4042
msgid "produces this output in Info:"
msgstr ""

#. type: example
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:4045
#, no-wrap
msgid "*Note Lightning: (weather)Electrical Effects.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:4052
msgid ""
"As you can see, the name of the manual is enclosed in parentheses and "
"precedes the name of the node.  In HTML, the manual name and the node name "
"are used to construct the hyperlink URL (@pxref{HTML Xref}), while the link "
"text is based on the label."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:4055
msgid "In a printed manual, the reference looks like this:"
msgstr ""

#. type: quotation
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:4059
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:4091
msgid ""
"See section ``Thunder and Lightning'' in @cite{An Introduction to "
"Meteorology}."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:4065
msgid ""
"The title of the printed manual is typeset like @code{@@cite}; and the "
"reference lacks a page number since the page a reference refers when that "
"reference is to another manual cannot be known."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:4070
msgid ""
"Next case: often, you will leave out the second argument when you use the "
"long version of @code{@@xref}.  In this case, the third argument, the topic "
"description, will be used as the cross-reference name in online formats.  "
"For example,"
msgstr ""

#. type: example
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:4074
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"@@xref@{Electrical Effects, , Thunder and Lightning,\n"
"weather, An Introduction to Meteorology@}.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: group
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:4082
#, no-wrap
msgid "*Note Thunder and Lightning: (weather)Electrical Effects.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:4099
msgid ""
"Next case: If the node name and the section title are the same in the other "
"manual, you may also leave out the section title.  In this case, the node "
"name is used in both instances.  For example,"
msgstr ""

#. type: example
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:4103
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"@@xref@{Electrical Effects,,,\n"
"weather, An Introduction to Meteorology@}.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: group
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:4111
#, no-wrap
msgid "*Note (weather)Electrical Effects::.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: quotation
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:4120
msgid ""
"See section ``Electrical Effects'' in @cite{An Introduction to Meteorology}."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:4133
msgid ""
"In general, there is no reason to have a manual name argument without a "
"printed manual argument, unless no printed manual is generated.  You may "
"also want to refer to another manual file that is within a single printed "
"manual---when multiple Texinfo files are incorporated into the same printed "
"manual but can create separate output files in other output formats.  In "
"this case, you need to specify only the fourth argument, and not the fifth.  "
"If the printed manual title argument is missing, the manual name will be "
"used instead in printed output."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:4139
msgid ""
"A printed manual title argument without an online manual argument is of "
"little use unless only a printed manual is generated from the Texinfo "
"source.  The result in online formats depends on the format, and can be, for "
"example, an empty manual name or a reference to the printed manual formatted "
"in a similar way to the printed output."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:4143
msgid ""
"Finally, it's also allowed to leave out all the arguments @emph{except} the "
"fourth and fifth, to refer to another manual as a whole.  See the next "
"section."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:4145
msgid "@lowersections"
msgstr ""

#. type: section
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:4147
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:4149
#, no-wrap
msgid "Referring to a Manual as a Whole"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:4149
msgid "@nodedescription Refer to an entire manual."
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:4150
#, no-wrap
msgid "Manual, referring to as a whole"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:4151
#, no-wrap
msgid "Referring to an entire manual"
msgstr ""

#.  old name
#. type: anchor{#1}
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:4153
msgid "Top Node Naming"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:4158
msgid ""
"Ordinarily, you must always name a node in a cross-reference.  However, it's "
"not unusual to want to refer to another manual as a whole, rather than a "
"particular section within it.  In this case, giving any section name is an "
"unnecessary distraction."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:4164
msgid ""
"So, with cross-references to other manuals (@pxref{Four and Five "
"Arguments}), if the first argument is either @samp{Top} (capitalized just "
"that way) or omitted entirely, and the third argument is omitted, the "
"printed output includes no node or section name.  (The Info output includes "
"@samp{Top} if it was given.)  For example,"
msgstr ""

#. type: example
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:4167
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@xref@{Top,,, make, The GNU Make Manual@}.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: group
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:4174
#, no-wrap
msgid "*Note (make)Top::.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: quotation
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:4181
msgid "See @cite{The GNU Make Manual}."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:4186
msgid ""
"Info readers will go to the Top node of the manual whether or not the `Top' "
"node is explicitly specified."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:4191
msgid ""
"It's also possible (and is historical practice) to refer to a whole manual "
"by specifying the `Top' node and an appropriate entry for the third argument "
"to the @code{@@xref} command.  Using this idiom, to make a cross-reference "
"to @cite{The GNU Make Manual}, you would write:"
msgstr ""

#. type: example
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:4194
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@xref@{Top,, Overview, make, The GNU Make Manual@}.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:4198
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:4321
msgid "which produces"
msgstr ""

#. type: example
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:4201
#, no-wrap
msgid "*Note Overview: (make)Top.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: quotation
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:4208
msgid "See section ``Overview'' in @cite{The GNU Make Manual}."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:4219
msgid ""
"In this example, @samp{Top} is the name of the first node, and "
"@samp{Overview} is the name of the first section of the manual.  There is no "
"widely-used convention for naming the first section in a printed manual, "
"this is just what the Make manual happens to use.  This arbitrariness of the "
"first name is a principal reason why omitting the third argument in "
"whole-manual cross-references is preferable."
msgstr ""

#. type: node
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:4221
#, no-wrap
msgid "@code{@@xref}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:4223
msgid "@nodedescription Begin a reference with `See' @dots{}"
msgstr ""

#. type: findex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:4226
#, no-wrap
msgid "xref"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:4227
#, no-wrap
msgid "Cross-references using @code{@@xref}"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:4228
#, no-wrap
msgid "References using @code{@@xref}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:4233
msgid ""
"The @code{@@xref} command generates a cross-reference for the beginning of a "
"sentence.  Examples of using @code{@@xref} are in previous sections."
msgstr ""

#. type: node
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:4235
#, no-wrap
msgid "@code{@@ref}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:4237
msgid "@nodedescription A reference for the last part of a sentence."
msgstr ""

#. type: findex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:4240
#, no-wrap
msgid "ref"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:4241
#, no-wrap
msgid "Cross-references using @code{@@ref}"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:4242
#, no-wrap
msgid "References using @code{@@ref}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:4247
msgid ""
"@code{@@ref} is nearly the same as @code{@@xref} except that it does not "
"generate a `See' in the output, just the reference itself.  This makes it "
"useful as the last part of a sentence."
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:4250
#, no-wrap
msgid "Hurricanes"
msgstr ""

#. type: example
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:4253
#, no-wrap
msgid "For more information, @@pxref@{This@}, and @@ref@{That@}.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:4257
msgid "produces in Info:"
msgstr ""

#. type: example
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:4260
#, no-wrap
msgid "For more information, *note This::, and *note That::.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:4264
msgid "and in printed output:"
msgstr ""

#. type: quotation
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:4268
msgid ""
"For more information, see Section 1.1 [This], page 1, and Section 1.2 "
"[That], page 2."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:4274
msgid ""
"The @code{@@ref} command can tempt writers to express themselves in a manner "
"that is suitable for a printed manual but looks awkward in the Info format.  "
"Bear in mind that your audience could be using both the printed and other "
"output formats such as Info.  For example:"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:4275
#, no-wrap
msgid "Sea surges"
msgstr ""

#. type: example
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:4278
#, no-wrap
msgid "Sea surges are described in @@ref@{Hurricanes@}.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:4282
msgid "looks ok in the printed output:"
msgstr ""

#. type: quotation
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:4285
msgid "Sea surges are described in Section 6.7 [Hurricanes], page 72."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:4289
msgid "but is awkward to read in Info, ``note'' being a verb:"
msgstr ""

#. type: example
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:4292
#, no-wrap
msgid "Sea surges are described in *note Hurricanes::.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: node
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:4295
#, no-wrap
msgid "@code{@@pxref}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:4297
msgid "@nodedescription How to write a parenthetical cross-reference."
msgstr ""

#. type: findex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:4300
#, no-wrap
msgid "pxref"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:4301
#, no-wrap
msgid "Cross-references using @code{@@pxref}"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:4302
#, no-wrap
msgid "References using @code{@@pxref}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:4309
msgid ""
"The parenthetical reference command, @code{@@pxref}, is nearly the same as "
"@code{@@xref}, but it is best used within parentheses.  The command differs "
"from @code{@@xref} in that the reference is typeset with a lowercase `see' "
"rather than an uppercase `See'.  In Info, @samp{*note} is output."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:4312
msgid "With one argument, a parenthetical cross-reference looks like this:"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:4313
#, no-wrap
msgid "Flooding"
msgstr ""

#. type: example
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:4316
#, no-wrap
msgid "@dots{} storms cause flooding (@@pxref@{Hurricanes@}) @dots{}\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: group
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:4325
#, no-wrap
msgid "@dots{} storms cause flooding (*note Hurricanes::) @dots{}\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: quotation
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:4333
msgid ""
"@dots{} storms cause flooding (see Section 6.7 [Hurricanes], page 72) @dots{}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:4345
msgid ""
"In past versions of Texinfo, it was not allowed to write punctuation after a "
"@code{@@pxref}, so it could be used @emph{only} before a right parenthesis.  "
"This is no longer the case.  The effect of @samp{@@pxref@{@var{node-name}@}} "
"is similar to that of @samp{see @@ref@{@var{node-name}@}}.  However, in many "
"circumstances the latter is preferable, as this makes it clear in the Info "
"output that the word ``see'' should be present."
msgstr ""

#. type: node
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:4347
#, no-wrap
msgid "@code{@@anchor}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:4349
msgid "@nodedescription Defining arbitrary cross-reference targets"
msgstr ""

#. type: section
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:4349
#, no-wrap
msgid "@code{@@anchor}: Defining Arbitrary Cross-reference Targets"
msgstr ""

#. type: findex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:4352
#, no-wrap
msgid "anchor"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:4353
#, no-wrap
msgid "Anchors"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:4354
#, no-wrap
msgid "Cross-reference targets, arbitrary"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:4355
#, no-wrap
msgid "Targets for cross-references, arbitrary"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:4361
msgid ""
"An @dfn{anchor} is a position in your document, labelled so that "
"cross-references can refer to it, just as they can to nodes.  You create an "
"anchor with the @code{@@anchor} command, and give the label as a normal "
"brace-delimited argument.  For example:"
msgstr ""

#. type: example
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:4366
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This marks the @@anchor@{x-spot@}spot.\n"
"@dots{}\n"
"@@xref@{x-spot,,the spot@}.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: example
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:4374
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This marks the spot.\n"
"@dots{}\n"
"See [the spot], page 1.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:4380
msgid ""
"As you can see, the @code{@@anchor} command itself produces no output.  This "
"example defines an anchor `x-spot' just before the word `spot'.  You can "
"refer to it later with an @code{@@xref} or other cross reference command, as "
"shown (@pxref{Cross References})."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:4386
msgid ""
"It is best to put @code{@@anchor} commands just before the position you wish "
"to refer to; that way, the reader's eye is led on to the correct text when "
"they jump to the anchor.  You can put the @code{@@anchor} command on a line "
"by itself if that helps readability of the source.  Whitespace (including "
"newlines) is ignored after @code{@@anchor}."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:4394
msgid ""
"Anchor names, node names and float labels may not conflict.  Anchors, nodes "
"and float labels are given similar treatment in some ways; for example, the "
"@code{goto-node} command takes either an anchor name or a node name as an "
"argument.  (@xref{Go to node,,, info, Info}.).  Anchors names and float "
"labels could also appear in menus (@pxref{Menus}) and node direction "
"pointers (@pxref{Writing a Node}), although this is not recommended."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:4397
msgid ""
"Anchor names share the same constraints as nodes on the characters that can "
"be included (@pxref{Info Node Names Constraints})."
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:4398
#, no-wrap
msgid "Nodes, deleting or renaming"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:4403
msgid ""
"Because of this duality, when you delete or rename a node, it is usually a "
"good idea to define an @code{@@anchor} with the old name.  That way, any "
"links to the old node, whether from other Texinfo manuals or general web "
"pages, keep working."
msgstr ""

#. type: node
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:4405
#, no-wrap
msgid "@code{@@link}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:4407
msgid "@nodedescription How to make a plain link."
msgstr ""

#. type: section
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:4407
#, no-wrap
msgid "@code{@@link}: Plain, unadorned hyperlink"
msgstr ""

#. type: findex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:4408
#, no-wrap
msgid "link"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:4409
#, no-wrap
msgid "Cross-references using @code{@@link}"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:4410
#, no-wrap
msgid "Plain link"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:4411
#, no-wrap
msgid "Plain hyperlink"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:4416
msgid ""
"@code{@@link} produces a plain hyperlink in output formats that support it, "
"including in HTML, DocBook, @LaTeX{} and online PDF@.  The template is:"
msgstr ""

#. type: example
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:4419
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@link@{@var{node-name}, @var{label}, @var{manual-name}@}\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:4427
msgid ""
"@var{node-name} is the name of the target node or anchor.  Either or both of "
"@var{label} and @var{manual-name} can be omitted.  @var{label}, if given, is "
"the text to use for the link.  @var{manual-name} is the name of the external "
"manual that the target appears within; if not given, the reference is to the "
"current manual."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:4431
msgid ""
"@code{@@link} has similar output to @code{@@ref}, except that it does "
"produce any extra text around the link label in Info or printed output that "
"would mark it as a cross-reference."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:4439
msgid ""
"Be careful about using @code{@@link} to produce links that are necessary for "
"a user to move around a manual, as these links will do nothing in these "
"output formats.  @code{@@link} is best used to add convenience links that "
"are nonetheless not essential for a reader to understand the text of the "
"manual.  For example, you might use @code{@@link} in a code sample to "
"reference documentation of a symbol in a programming library."
msgstr ""

#. type: node
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:4442
#, no-wrap
msgid "@code{@@inforef}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:4444
msgid "@nodedescription How to refer to an Info-only file."
msgstr ""

#. type: section
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:4444
#, no-wrap
msgid "@code{@@inforef}: Cross-references to Info-only Material"
msgstr ""

#. type: findex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:4447
#, no-wrap
msgid "inforef"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:4448
#, no-wrap
msgid "Cross-references using @code{@@inforef}"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:4449
#, no-wrap
msgid "References using @code{@@inforef}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:4458
msgid ""
"@code{@@inforef} is used for making cross-references to Info "
"documents---even from a printed manual.  This was originally used for Info "
"files that were not generated from any Texinfo source.  The command is now "
"obsolete and should not be used.  In addition to having little use, similar "
"output can be obtained with @code{@@xref}, @code{@@ref} or @code{@@pxref} "
"with the Info file name as the fourth argument and no fifth argument."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:4461
msgid ""
"The command takes either two or three arguments, in the following order:"
msgstr ""

#. type: enumerate
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:4465
msgid "The node name."
msgstr ""

#. type: enumerate
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:4468
msgid "The cross-reference name (optional)."
msgstr ""

#. type: enumerate
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:4471
msgid "The Info file name."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:4475
msgid "The template is:"
msgstr ""

#. type: example
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:4478
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"@@inforef@{@var{node-name}, @var{cross-reference-name}, "
"@var{info-file-name}@}\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: node
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:4481
#, no-wrap
msgid "@code{@@url}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:4483
msgid "@nodedescription How to refer to a uniform resource locator."
msgstr ""

#. type: section
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:4483
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"@code{@@url}, @code{@@uref@{@var{url}[, @var{text}][, @var{replacement}]@}}"
msgstr ""

#. type: findex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:4487
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:4498
#, no-wrap
msgid "uref"
msgstr ""

#. type: findex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:4487
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:4489
#, no-wrap
msgid "url"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:4487
#, no-wrap
msgid "URL @subentry referring to"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:4490
#, no-wrap
msgid "@code{href}, producing HTML"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:4497
msgid ""
"@code{@@url} produces a reference to a uniform resource locator (URL@:).  It "
"takes one mandatory argument, the URL@:, and two optional arguments which "
"control the text that is displayed.  In HTML and PDF output, @code{@@url} "
"produces a link you can follow.  (To merely indicate a URL without creating "
"a link people can follow, use @code{@@indicateurl}, "
"@pxref{@code{@@indicateurl}}.)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:4504
msgid ""
"@code{@@uref} is a synonym for @code{@@url}.  (Originally, @code{@@url} had "
"the meaning of @code{@@indicateurl} and @code{@@uref} was required to "
"produce a working link, but in practice @code{@@url} was almost always "
"misused.  So we've changed the meaning.)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:4508
msgid ""
"The second argument, if specified, is the text to display (the default is "
"the URL itself); in output formats other than HTML, the URL is output in "
"addition to this text."
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:4509
#, no-wrap
msgid "Man page, reference to"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:4514
msgid ""
"The third argument, if specified, is the text to display, but in this case "
"the URL is not output in any format.  This is useful when the text is "
"already sufficiently referential, as in a man page.  Also, if the third "
"argument is given, the second argument is ignored."
msgstr ""

#. type: subsection
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:4516
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:4518
#, no-wrap
msgid "@code{@@url} Examples"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:4518
msgid "@nodedescription Examples of using all the forms of @code{@@url}."
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:4520
#, no-wrap
msgid "@code{@@url}, examples of using"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:4521
#, no-wrap
msgid "URL @subentry examples of displaying"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:4526
msgid ""
"First, here is an example of the simplest form of @code{@@url}, with just "
"one argument.  The given URL is both the target and the visible text of the "
"link:"
msgstr ""

#. type: example
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:4529
#, no-wrap
msgid "The official GNU ftp site is @@url@{http://ftp.gnu.org/gnu@}.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: display
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:4534
#, no-wrap
msgid "The official GNU ftp site is @url{http://ftp.gnu.org/gnu}.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: subsubheading
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:4536
#, no-wrap
msgid "Two-argument form of @code{@@url}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:4539
msgid "Here is an example of the two-argument form:"
msgstr ""

#. type: example
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:4542
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The official @@url@{http://ftp.gnu.org/gnu, GNU ftp site@}\n"
"holds programs and texts.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: display
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:4548
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The official @url{http://ftp.gnu.org/gnu, GNU ftp site}\n"
"holds programs and texts.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: example
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:4554
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The official <a href=\"http://ftp.gnu.org/gnu\">GNU ftp site</a>\n"
"holds programs and texts.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: example
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:4560
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The official GNU ftp site (http://ftp.gnu.org/gnu)\n"
"holds programs and texts.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: subsubheading
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:4562
#, no-wrap
msgid "Three-argument form of @code{@@url}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:4565
msgid "Finally, an example of the three-argument form:"
msgstr ""

#. type: example
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:4567
#, no-wrap
msgid "The @@url@{/man.cgi/1/ls,,ls@} program @dots{}\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: display
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:4572
#, no-wrap
msgid "The @url{/man.cgi/1/ls,,ls} program @dots{}\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: example
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:4577
#, no-wrap
msgid "The <a href=\"/man.cgi/1/ls\">ls</a> program @dots{}\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:4582
msgid ""
"By the way, some people prefer to display URLs in the unambiguous format:"
msgstr ""

#. type: display
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:4585
#, no-wrap
msgid "<URL:http://@var{host}/@var{path}>\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:4588
#, no-wrap
msgid "@code{<URL...>} convention, not used"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:4593
msgid ""
"You can use this form in the input file if you wish.  We feel it's not "
"necessary to include the @samp{<URL:} and @samp{>} in the output, since to "
"be useful any software that tries to detect URLs in text already has to "
"detect them without the @samp{<URL:}."
msgstr ""

#. type: subsection
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:4595
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:4597
#, no-wrap
msgid "URL Line Breaking"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:4597
msgid "@nodedescription How lines are broken within @code{@@url} text."
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:4599
#, no-wrap
msgid "Line breaks @subentry URLs"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:4600
#, no-wrap
msgid "Breakpoints within URLs"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:4606
msgid ""
"@TeX{} allows line breaking within URLs at only a few characters (which are "
"special in URLs): @samp{&}, @samp{.}, @samp{#}, @samp{?}, and @samp{/} (but "
"not between two @samp{/} characters).  A tiny amount of stretchable space is "
"also inserted around these characters to help with line breaking."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:4610
msgid ""
"For HTML output, modern browsers will also do line breaking within displayed "
"URLs.  If you need to allow breaks at other characters you can insert "
"@code{@@/} as needed (@pxref{Line Breaks})."
msgstr ""

#. type: findex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:4611
#, no-wrap
msgid "urefbreakstyle"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:4617
msgid ""
"By default, in @TeX{} any such breaks at special characters will occur after "
"the character.  Some people prefer such breaks to happen before the special "
"character.  This can be controlled with the @code{@@urefbreakstyle} command "
"(this command has effect only in @TeX{}):"
msgstr ""

#. type: example
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:4620
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@urefbreakstyle @var{how}\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: vindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:4624
#, no-wrap
msgid "after@r{, value for @code{@@urefbreakstyle}}"
msgstr ""

#. type: vindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:4625
#, no-wrap
msgid "before@r{, value for @code{@@urefbreakstyle}}"
msgstr ""

#. type: vindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:4626
#, no-wrap
msgid "none@r{, value for @code{@@urefbreakstyle}}"
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:4628
#, no-wrap
msgid "after"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:4630
msgid "(the default) Potentially break after the special characters."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:4630
#, no-wrap
msgid "before"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:4632
msgid "Potentially break before the special characters."
msgstr ""

#. type: code{#1}
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:4632
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:22977
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:23022
#, no-wrap
msgid "none"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:4635
msgid ""
"Do not consider breaking at the special characters at all; any potential "
"breaks must be manually inserted."
msgstr ""

#. type: subsection
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:4638
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:4640
#, no-wrap
msgid "@code{@@url} PDF Output Format"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:4640
msgid "@nodedescription A special option to hide links in PDF output."
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:4642
#, no-wrap
msgid "PDF output of URLs"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:4643
#, no-wrap
msgid "URLs, PDF output of"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:4650
msgid ""
"If the ultimate purpose of a PDF is only to be viewed online, perhaps "
"similar to HTML in some inchoate way, you may not want the URLs to be "
"included in the visible text (just as URLs are not visible to readers of web "
"pages).  Texinfo provides a PDF-specific option for this, which must be used "
"inside @code{@@tex}:"
msgstr ""

#. type: findex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:4651
#, no-wrap
msgid "\\urefurlonlylinktrue"
msgstr ""

#. type: example
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:4656
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"@@tex\n"
"\\global\\urefurlonlylinktrue\n"
"@@end tex\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:4662
msgid ""
"The result is that @code{@@url@{http://www.gnu.org, GNU@}} has the visible "
"output of just `GNU', with a link target of @url{http://www.gnu.org}.  "
"Ordinarily, the visible output would include both the label and the url: "
"`GNU (@url{http://www.gnu.org})'."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:4668
msgid ""
"This option only has effect when the PDF output is produced with the "
"pdf@TeX{} program, not with other ways of getting from Texinfo to PDF (e.g., "
"@TeX{} to DVI to PDF)@.  Consequently, it is ok to specify this option "
"unconditionally within @code{@@tex}, as shown above.  It is ignored when DVI "
"is being produced."
msgstr ""

#. type: node
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:4670
#, no-wrap
msgid "@code{@@cite}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:4672
msgid "@nodedescription How to refer to books not in the Info system."
msgstr ""

#. type: section
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:4672
#, no-wrap
msgid "@code{@@cite}@{@var{reference}@}"
msgstr ""

#. type: findex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:4675
#, no-wrap
msgid "cite"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:4681
msgid ""
"Use the @code{@@cite} command for the name of a book that lacks a companion "
"Info file.  For example, we could refer to @cite{A Book}.  The command "
"selects a slanted font in the printed manual, and generates quotation marks "
"in the Info file."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:4685
msgid ""
"If a book is written in Texinfo, it is better to use a cross-reference "
"command since a reader can easily follow such a reference in Info.  "
"@xref{@code{@@xref}}."
msgstr ""

#. type: section
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:4686
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:4688
#, no-wrap
msgid "PDF Colors"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:4688
msgid "@nodedescription Colorizing URLs and other links in PDF output."
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:4690
#, no-wrap
msgid "Colored links, in PDF output"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:4691
#, no-wrap
msgid "Links, coloring in PDF output"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:4692
#, no-wrap
msgid "URLs, coloring in PDF output"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:4699
msgid ""
"By default, URLs and cross-reference links are printed in black in PDF "
"output.  Very occasionally, however, you may want to highlight such ``live'' "
"links with a different color, as is commonly done on web pages.  Texinfo "
"provides a PDF-specific option for specifying these colors, which must be "
"used inside @code{@@tex}:"
msgstr ""

#. type: findex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:4700
#, no-wrap
msgid "\\linkcolor"
msgstr ""

#. type: findex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:4701
#, no-wrap
msgid "\\urlcolor"
msgstr ""

#. type: example
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:4707
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"@@tex\n"
"\\global\\def\\linkcolor@{1 0 0@}  % red\n"
"\\global\\def\\urlcolor@{0 1 0@}   % green\n"
"@@end tex\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:4712
msgid ""
"@code{\\urlcolor} changes the color of @code{@@url} output (both the actual "
"URL and any textual label), while @code{\\linkcolor} changes the color for "
"cross-references to nodes, etc.  They are independent."
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:4713
#, no-wrap
msgid "RGB color specification."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:4716
msgid ""
"The three given values must be numbers between 0 and 1, specifying the "
"amount of red, green, and blue respectively."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:4722
msgid ""
"These definitions only have an effect when the PDF output is produced with "
"the pdf@TeX{} program, not with other ways of getting from Texinfo to PDF "
"(e.g., @TeX{} to DVI to PDF)@.  Consequently, it is ok to specify this "
"option unconditionally within @code{@@tex}, as shown above.  It is ignored "
"when DVI is being produced."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:4725
msgid ""
"We do not recommend colorizing just for fun; unless you have a specific "
"reason to use colors, best to skip it."
msgstr ""

#. type: node
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:4729
#, no-wrap
msgid "Marking Text"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:4733
msgid ""
"@nodedescriptionblock Marking words and phrases as code, keyboard input, "
"meta-syntactic variables, and the like."
msgstr ""

#. type: chapter
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:4734
#, no-wrap
msgid "Marking Text, Words and Phrases"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:4735
#, no-wrap
msgid "Paragraph, marking text within"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:4736
#, no-wrap
msgid "Marking words and phrases"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:4737
#, no-wrap
msgid "Words and phrases, marking them"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:4738
#, no-wrap
msgid "Marking text within a paragraph"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:4739
#, no-wrap
msgid "Text, marking up"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:4747
msgid ""
"In Texinfo, you can mark words and phrases in a variety of ways.  The "
"Texinfo processors use this information to determine how to highlight the "
"text.  You can specify, for example, whether a word or phrase is a defining "
"occurrence, a metasyntactic variable, or a symbol used in a program.  Also, "
"you can emphasize text, in several different ways."
msgstr ""

#. type: node
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:4749
#, no-wrap
msgid "Indicating"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:4751
msgid "@nodedescription How to indicate definitions, files, etc."
msgstr ""

#. type: section
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:4751
#, no-wrap
msgid "Indicating Definitions, Commands, etc."
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:4753
#, no-wrap
msgid "Highlighting text"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:4754
#, no-wrap
msgid "Indicating commands, definitions, etc."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:4761
msgid ""
"Texinfo has commands for indicating just what kind of object a piece of text "
"refers to.  For example, email addresses are marked by @code{@@email}; that "
"way, the result can be a live link to send email when the output format "
"supports it.  If the email address was simply marked as ``print in a "
"typewriter font'', that would not be possible."
msgstr ""

#. type: node
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:4763
#, no-wrap
msgid "Useful Highlighting"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:4765
msgid "@nodedescription Highlighting provides useful information."
msgstr ""

#. type: subsection
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:4765
#, no-wrap
msgid "Highlighting Commands are Useful"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:4768
msgid "The commands serve a variety of purposes:"
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:4770
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:18719
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@code@{@var{sample-code}@}"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:4773
msgid ""
"Indicate text that is a literal example of a piece of a program.  "
"@xref{@code{@@code}}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:4774
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19262
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@kbd@{@var{keyboard-characters}@}"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:4776
msgid "Indicate keyboard input.  @xref{@code{@@kbd}}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:4777
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19270
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@key@{@var{key-name}@}"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:4780
msgid ""
"Indicate the conventional name for a key on a keyboard.  @xref{@code{@@key}}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:4781
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19488
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@samp@{@var{text}@}"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:4784
msgid ""
"Indicate text that is a literal example of a sequence of characters.  "
"@xref{@code{@@samp}}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:4785
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@verb@{@var{text}@}"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:4788
msgid "Write a verbatim sequence of characters.  @xref{@code{@@verb}}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:4789
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19772
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@var@{@var{metasyntactic-variable}@}"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:4791
msgid "Indicate a metasyntactic variable.  @xref{@code{@@var}}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:4792
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:18981
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@env@{@var{environment-variable}@}"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:4794
msgid "Indicate an environment variable.  @xref{@code{@@env}}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:4795
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@file@{@var{file-name}@}"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:4797
msgid "Indicate the name of a file.  @xref{@code{@@file}}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:4798
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:18732
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@command@{@var{command-name}@}"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:4801
msgid "Indicate the name of a command.  @xref{@code{@@command}}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:4802
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@option@{@var{option}@}"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:4805
msgid "Indicate a command-line option.  @xref{@code{@@option}}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:4806
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:18908
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@dfn@{@var{term}@}"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:4809
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:18910
msgid ""
"Indicate the introductory or defining use of a term.  @xref{@code{@@dfn}}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:4810
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:18696
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@cite@{@var{reference}@}"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:4812
msgid "Indicate the name of a book.  @xref{@code{@@cite}}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:4813
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:18583
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@abbr@{@var{abbreviation}@}"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:4815
msgid "Indicate an abbreviation, such as `Comput.'."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:4816
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:18587
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@acronym@{@var{acronym}@}"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:4818
msgid "Indicate an acronym.  @xref{@code{@@acronym}}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:4819
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@indicateurl@{@var{uniform-resource-locator}@}"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:4823
msgid ""
"Indicate an example (that is, nonfunctional) uniform resource locator.  "
"@xref{@code{@@indicateurl}}.  (Use @code{@@url} (@pxref{@code{@@url}}) for "
"live URLs.)"
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:4824
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@email@{@var{email-address}[, @var{displayed-text}]@}"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:4826
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:18964
msgid "Indicate an electronic mail address.  @xref{@code{@@email}}."
msgstr ""

#. type: node
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:4830
#, no-wrap
msgid "@code{@@code}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:4832
msgid "@nodedescription Indicating program code."
msgstr ""

#. type: subsection
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:4832
#, no-wrap
msgid "@code{@@code}@{@var{sample-code}@}"
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:4835
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:4975
#, no-wrap
msgid "code"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:4837
#, no-wrap
msgid "Syntactic tokens, indicating"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:4841
msgid ""
"Use the @code{@@code} command to indicate text that is a piece of a program "
"and which consists of entire syntactic tokens.  Enclose the text in braces."
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:4842
#, no-wrap
msgid "Expressions in a program, indicating"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:4843
#, no-wrap
msgid "Keywords, indicating"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:4844
#, no-wrap
msgid "Reserved words, indicating"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:4848
msgid ""
"Thus, you should use @code{@@code} for an expression in a program, for the "
"name of a variable or function used in a program, or for a keyword in a "
"programming language."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:4853
msgid ""
"Use @code{@@code} for command names in languages that resemble programming "
"languages, such as Texinfo.  For example, @code{@@code} and @code{@@samp} "
"are produced by writing @samp{@@code@{@@@@code@}} and "
"@samp{@@code@{@@@@samp@}} in the Texinfo source, respectively."
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:4854
#, no-wrap
msgid "Case, not altering in @code{@@code}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:4864
msgid ""
"It is incorrect to alter the case of a word inside a @code{@@code} command "
"when it appears at the beginning of a sentence.  Most computer languages are "
"case sensitive.  In C, for example, @code{Printf} is different from the "
"identifier @code{printf}, and most likely is a misspelling of it.  Even in "
"languages which are not case sensitive, it is confusing to a human reader to "
"see identifiers spelled in different ways.  Pick one spelling and always use "
"that.  If you do not want to start a sentence with a command name written "
"all in lowercase, you should rearrange the sentence."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:4867
msgid ""
"The @code{@@code} argument is typeset in a typewriter (monospace) font.  "
"where the output format allows this.  For example,"
msgstr ""

#. type: example
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:4870
#, no-wrap
msgid "The function returns @@code@{nil@}.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:4874
msgid "produces this:"
msgstr ""

#. type: quotation
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:4877
msgid "The function returns @code{nil}."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:4880
msgid ""
"Here are some cases for which it is preferable @emph{not} to use "
"@code{@@code}:"
msgstr ""

#. type: itemize
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:4884
msgid "For shell command names, such as @command{ls} (use @code{@@command})."
msgstr ""

#. type: itemize
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:4887
msgid "For environment variables, such as @env{TEXINPUTS} (use @code{@@env})."
msgstr ""

#. type: itemize
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:4891
msgid ""
"For shell options, such as @samp{-c}, when such options stand alone (use "
"@code{@@option})."
msgstr ""

#. type: itemize
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:4896
msgid ""
"An entire shell command often looks better if written using @code{@@samp} "
"rather than @code{@@code}.  In this case, the rule is to choose the more "
"pleasing format."
msgstr ""

#. type: itemize
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:4902
msgid ""
"For a string of characters shorter than a syntactic token.  For example, if "
"you are writing about @samp{goto-ch}, which is just a part of the name for "
"the @code{goto-char} Emacs Lisp function, you should use @code{@@samp}."
msgstr ""

#. type: itemize
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:4913
msgid ""
"In general, when writing about the characters used in a token; for example, "
"do not use @code{@@code} when you are explaining what letters or printable "
"symbols can be used in the names of functions.  (Use @code{@@samp}.)  Also, "
"you should not use @code{@@code} to mark text that is considered input to "
"programs unless the input is written in a language that is like a "
"programming language.  For example, you should not use @code{@@code} for the "
"keystroke commands of GNU Emacs (use @code{@@kbd} instead) although you may "
"use @code{@@code} for the names of the Emacs Lisp functions that the "
"keystroke commands invoke."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:4922
msgid ""
"By default, @TeX{} will consider breaking lines at @samp{-} and @samp{_} "
"characters within @code{@@code} and related commands.  This can be "
"controlled with @code{@@allowcodebreaks} "
"(@pxref{@code{@@allowcodebreaks}}).  In the HTML output breaking lines is up "
"to the browser's behavior.  For Info, it seems better never to make such "
"breaks."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:4932
msgid ""
"For Info and plaintext, quotation characters are usually output around the "
"output of the @code{@@code} command and related commands (e.g., "
"@code{@@kbd}, @code{@@command}) except in typewriter-like contexts such as "
"the @code{@@example} environment (@pxref{@code{@@example}}) and "
"@code{@@code} itself, etc.  To control which quoting characters are inserted "
"by @command{texi2any} in the output of @samp{@@code}, etc., see the "
"@code{OPEN_QUOTE_SYMBOL} and @code{CLOSE_QUOTE_SYMBOL} customization "
"variables (@pxref{Other Customization Variables})."
msgstr ""

#. type: node
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:4935
#, no-wrap
msgid "@code{@@kbd}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:4937
msgid "@nodedescription Showing keyboard input."
msgstr ""

#. type: subsection
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:4937
#, no-wrap
msgid "@code{@@kbd}@{@var{keyboard-characters}@}"
msgstr ""

#. type: findex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:4940
#, no-wrap
msgid "kbd"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:4941
#, no-wrap
msgid "Keyboard input"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:4945
msgid ""
"Use the @code{@@kbd} command for characters of input to be typed by users.  "
"For example, to refer to the characters @kbd{M-a}, write:"
msgstr ""

#. type: example
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:4948
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@kbd@{M-a@}\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:4952
msgid "and to refer to the characters @kbd{M-x shell}, write:"
msgstr ""

#. type: example
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:4955
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@kbd@{M-x shell@}\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:4957
#, no-wrap
msgid "User input"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:4958
#, no-wrap
msgid "Slanted typewriter font, for @code{@@kbd}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:4963
msgid ""
"By default, the @code{@@kbd} command produces a different font (slanted "
"typewriter instead of normal typewriter, where the output format allows), so "
"users can distinguish the characters that they are supposed to type from "
"those that the computer outputs."
msgstr ""

#. type: findex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:4964
#, no-wrap
msgid "kbdinputstyle"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:4970
msgid ""
"Since the usage of @code{@@kbd} varies from manual to manual, you can "
"control the font switching with the @code{@@kbdinputstyle} command.  This "
"command has no effect on Info output.  Write this command at the beginning "
"of a line with a single word as an argument, one of the following:"
msgstr ""

#. type: vindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:4971
#, no-wrap
msgid "distinct@r{, value for @code{@@kbdinputstyle}}"
msgstr ""

#. type: vindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:4972
#, no-wrap
msgid "example@r{, value for @code{@@kbdinputstyle}}"
msgstr ""

#. type: vindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:4973
#, no-wrap
msgid "code@r{, value for @code{@@kbdinputstyle}}"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:4977
msgid "Always use the same font for @code{@@kbd} as @code{@@code}."
msgstr ""

#. type: findex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:4977
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:6060
#, no-wrap
msgid "example"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:4980
msgid ""
"Use the distinguishing font for @code{@@kbd} only in @code{@@example} and "
"similar environments."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:4980
#, no-wrap
msgid "distinct"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:4982
msgid "(the default) Always use the distinguishing font for @code{@@kbd}."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:4988
msgid ""
"You can embed another @@-command inside the braces of a @code{@@kbd} "
"command.  Here, for example, is the way to describe a command that would be "
"described more verbosely as ``press the @samp{r} key and then press the "
"@key{RETURN} key'':"
msgstr ""

#. type: example
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:4991
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@kbd@{r @@key@{RET@}@}\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:4996
msgid ""
"This produces: @kbd{r @key{RET}}.  (The present manual uses the default for "
"@code{@@kbdinputstyle}.)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:4999
msgid ""
"You also use the @code{@@kbd} command if you are spelling out the letters "
"you type; for example:"
msgstr ""

#. type: example
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:5003
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"To give the @@code@{logout@} command,\n"
"type the characters @@kbd@{l o g o u t @@key@{RET@}@}.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: quotation
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:5011
msgid ""
"To give the @code{logout} command, type the characters @kbd{l o g o u t "
"@key{RET}}."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:5016
msgid ""
"(Also, this example shows that you can add spaces for clarity.  If you "
"explicitly want to mention a space character as one of the characters of "
"input, write @kbd{@@key@{SPC@}} for it.)"
msgstr ""

#. type: node
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:5018
#, no-wrap
msgid "@code{@@key}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:5020
msgid "@nodedescription Specifying keys."
msgstr ""

#. type: subsection
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:5020
#, no-wrap
msgid "@code{@@key}@{@var{key-name}@}"
msgstr ""

#. type: findex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:5023
#, no-wrap
msgid "key"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:5027
msgid ""
"Use the @code{@@key} command for the conventional name for a key on a "
"keyboard, as in:"
msgstr ""

#. type: example
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:5030
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@key@{RET@}\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:5035
msgid ""
"You can use the @code{@@key} command within the argument of an @code{@@kbd} "
"command when the sequence of characters to be typed includes one or more "
"keys that are described by name."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:5038
msgid ""
"For example, to produce @kbd{C-x @key{ESC}} and @kbd{M-@key{TAB}} you would "
"type:"
msgstr ""

#. type: example
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:5042
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"@@kbd@{C-x @@key@{ESC@}@}\n"
"@@kbd@{M-@@key@{TAB@}@}\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:5045
msgid "Here is a list of the recommended names for keys:"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:5045
#, no-wrap
msgid "Recommended names for keys"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:5046
#, no-wrap
msgid "Keys, recommended names"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:5047
#, no-wrap
msgid "Names recommended for keys"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:5048
#, no-wrap
msgid "Abbreviations for keys"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:5049
#, no-wrap
msgid "Control keys, specifying"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:5050
#, no-wrap
msgid "Meta keys, specifying"
msgstr ""

