#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:9292
msgid ""
"Use doubled single-quote characters to begin and end quotations: "
"@w{@t{`@w{}`@dots{}'@w{}'}}.  Two single quotes are converted to left- and "
"right-hand doubled quotation marks, ``like this''."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:9298
msgid ""
"You may occasionally need to produce two consecutive single quotes; for "
"example, in documenting a computer language such as Maxima where @t{'@w{}'} "
"is a valid command.  You can do this with the input @t{'@@w@{@}'}; the empty "
"@code{@@w} command stops the combination into the double-quote characters."
msgstr ""

