#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:14059
msgid ""
"The @command{texi2dvi} program takes care of all the steps for producing a "
"@TeX{} DVI file from a Texinfo document.  Similarly, @command{texi2pdf} "
"produces a PDF file@footnote{@dfn{PDF} stands for `Portable Document "
"Format'.  It was invented by Adobe Systems for document interchange, based "
"on their PostScript language.}."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:14062
msgid ""
"To run @command{texi2dvi} or @command{texi2pdf} on an input file "
"@file{foo.texi}, do this (where @samp{prompt$ } is your shell prompt):"
msgstr ""

#. type: example
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:14066
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"prompt$ @kbd{texi2dvi foo.texi}\n"
"prompt$ @kbd{texi2pdf foo.texi}\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:14070
msgid ""
"As shown in this example, the file names given to @command{texi2dvi} and "
"@command{texi2pdf} must include any extension, such as @samp{.texi}."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:14073
msgid ""
"For a list of all the options, run @samp{texi2dvi --help}.  Some of the "
"options are discussed below."
msgstr ""

#. type: opindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:14074
#, no-wrap
msgid "--pdf@r{, for @command{texi2dvi}}"
msgstr ""

#. type: pindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:14075
#, no-wrap
msgid "pdftexi2dvi"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:14084
msgid ""
"With the @option{--pdf} option, @command{texi2dvi} produces PDF output "
"instead of DVI, by running @command{pdftex} instead of @command{tex}.  "
"Alternatively, the command @command{texi2pdf} is an abbreviation for running "
"@samp{texi2dvi --pdf}.  The command @command{pdftexi2dvi} is also provided "
"as a convenience for AUC-@TeX{} (@pxref{Top,,, auctex, AUC-@TeX{}}), as it "
"prefers to merely prepend @samp{pdf} to DVI producing tools to have PDF "
"producing tools."
msgstr ""

#. type: opindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:14085
#, no-wrap
msgid "--dvipdf@r{, for @command{texi2dvi}}"
msgstr ""

#. type: pindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:14086
#, no-wrap
msgid "dvipdfmx"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:14093
msgid ""
"With the @option{--dvipdf} option, @command{texi2dvi} produces PDF output by "
"running @TeX{} and then a DVI-to-PDF program: if the @env{DVIPDF} "
"environment variable is set, that value is used, else the first program "
"extant among @code{dvipdfmx}, @code{dvipdfm}, @code{dvipdf}, @code{dvi2pdf}, "
"@code{dvitopdf}.  This method generally supports CJK typesetting better than "
"@command{pdftex}."
msgstr ""

#. type: opindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:14094
#, no-wrap
msgid "--ps@r{, for @command{texi2dvi}}"
msgstr ""

#. type: pindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:14095
#, no-wrap
msgid "dvips"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:14100
msgid ""
"With the @option{--ps} option, @command{texi2dvi} produces PostScript "
"instead of DVI, by running @command{tex} and then @command{dvips} "
"(@pxref{Top,,, dvips, Dvips}).  (Or the value of the @env{DVIPS} environment "
"variable, if set.)"
msgstr ""

#. type: opindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:14101
#, no-wrap
msgid "--language@r{, for @command{texi2dvi}}"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:14102
#, no-wrap
msgid "@LaTeX{}, processing with @command{texi2dvi}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:14109
msgid ""
"@command{texi2dvi} can also be used to process @LaTeX{} files.  Normally "
"@command{texi2dvi} is able to guess the input file language by its contents "
"and file name extension; however, if it guesses wrong you can explicitly "
"specify the input language using @option{--language=@var{lang}} command line "
"option, where @var{lang} is either @samp{latex} or @samp{texinfo}."
msgstr ""

#. type: opindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:14110
#, no-wrap
msgid "--command@r{, for @command{texi2dvi}}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:14120
msgid ""
"One useful option to @command{texi2dvi} is @samp{--command=@var{cmd}}.  This "
"inserts @var{cmd} on a line by itself at the start of the file in a "
"temporary copy of the input file, before running @TeX{}.  With this, you can "
"specify different printing formats, such as @code{@@smallbook} "
"(@pxref{@code{@@smallbook}}), @code{@@afourpaper} (@pxref{A4 Paper}), or "
"@code{@@pagesizes} (@pxref{@code{@@pagesizes}}), without actually changing "
"the document source.  (You can also do this on a site-wide basis with "
"@file{texinfo.cnf}; @pxref{Preparing for @TeX{}})."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:14126
msgid ""
"The option @option{-E} (equivalently, @option{-e} and @option{--expand}) "
"does Texinfo macro expansion using @command{texi2any} instead of the @TeX{} "
"implementation (@pxref{Macro Details}).  Each implementation has its own "
"limitations and advantages."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:14132
msgid ""
"@command{texi2dvi} takes the @option{--build=@var{mode}} option to specify "
"where the @TeX{} compilation takes place, and, as a consequence, how "
"auxiliary files are treated.  The build mode can also be set using the "
"environment variable @env{TEXI2DVI_BUILD_MODE}.  The valid values for "
"@var{mode} are:"
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:14134
#, no-wrap
msgid "local"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:14137
msgid ""
"Compile in the current directory, leaving all the auxiliary files around.  "
"This is the traditional TeX use."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:14138
#, no-wrap
msgid "tidy"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:14141
msgid ""
"Compile in a local @code{*.t2d} directory, where the auxiliary files are "
"left.  Output files are copied back to the original file."
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:14158
msgid ""
"Using the @samp{tidy} mode brings several advantages: @itemize - @item the "
"current directory is not cluttered with plethora of temporary files.  @item "
"clutter can be even further reduced using @option{--build-dir=dir}: all the "
"@code{*.t2d} directories are stored there.  @item clutter can be reduced to "
"zero using, e.g., @option{--build-dir=/tmp/\\$USER.t2d} or "
"@option{--build-dir=\\$HOME/.t2d}.  @item the output file is updated after "
"every successful @TeX{} run, for sake of concurrent visualization of the "
"output.  In a @samp{local} build the viewer stops during the whole @TeX{} "
"run.  @item if the compilation fails, the previous state of the output file "
"is preserved.  @item @acronym{PDF} and @acronym{DVI} compilation are kept in "
"separate subdirectories preventing any possibility of auxiliary file "
"incompatibility.  @end itemize"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:14163
msgid ""
"On the other hand, because @samp{tidy} compilation takes place in another "
"directory, occasionally @TeX{} won't be able to find some files (e.g., when "
"using @code{\\graphicspath}): in that case, use @option{-I} to specify the "
"additional directories to consider."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:14164
#, no-wrap
msgid "clean"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:14167
msgid ""
"Same as @samp{tidy}, but remove the auxiliary directory afterwards.  Every "
"compilation therefore requires the full cycle."
msgstr ""

#. type: pindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:14169
#, no-wrap
msgid "etex"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:14175
msgid ""
"@command{texi2dvi} will use @command{etex} if it is available, because it "
"runs faster in some cases, and provides additional tracing information when "
"debugging @file{texinfo.tex}.  Nevertheless, this extended version of @TeX{} "
"is not required, and the DVI output is identical."
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:14176
#, no-wrap
msgid "file recorder for @TeX{}"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:14177
#, no-wrap
msgid "@samp{\\openout} line in log file"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:14183
msgid ""
"@command{texi2dvi} attempts to detect auxiliary files output by @TeX{}, "
"either by using the @option{-recorder} option, or by scanning for "
"@samp{\\openout} in the log file that a run of @TeX{} produces.  You may "
"control how @command{texi2dvi} does this with the "
"@env{TEXI2DVI_USE_RECORDER} environment variable.  Valid values are:"
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:14185
#, no-wrap
msgid "yes"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:14187
msgid "use the @option{-recorder} option, no checks."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:14188
#, no-wrap
msgid "no"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:14190
msgid "scan for @samp{\\openout} in the log file, no checks."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:14191
#, no-wrap
msgid "yesmaybe"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:14195
msgid ""
"check whether @option{-recorder} option is supported, and if yes use it, "
"otherwise check for tracing @samp{\\openout} in the log file is supported, "
"and if yes use it, else it is an error."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:14196
#, no-wrap
msgid "nomaybe"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:14199
msgid ""
"same as @samp{yesmaybe}, except that the @samp{\\openout} trace in log file "
"is checked first."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:14203
msgid ""
"The default is @samp{nomaybe}.  This environment variable is provided for "
"troubleshooting purposes, and may change or disappear in the future."
msgstr ""

#. type: section
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:14205
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:14207
#, no-wrap
msgid "Format with @command{tex}/@command{texindex}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:14207
msgid "@nodedescription Formatting with explicit shell commands."
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:14209
#, no-wrap
msgid "Shell formatting with @command{tex} and @command{texindex}"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:14210
#, no-wrap
msgid "Formatting with @command{tex} and @command{texindex}"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:14211
#, no-wrap
msgid "DVI file"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:14216
msgid ""
"You can do the basic formatting of a Texinfo file with the shell command "
"@command{tex} followed by the name of the Texinfo file.  For example:"
msgstr ""

#. type: example
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:14219
#, no-wrap
msgid "tex foo.texi\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:14226
msgid ""
"files containing information for indices, cross-references, etc.  The DVI "
"file (for @dfn{DeVice Independent} file) can be printed on virtually any "
"device, perhaps after a further conversion (see the previous section)."
msgstr ""

#. type: pindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:14227
#, no-wrap
msgid "texindex"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:14234
msgid ""
"The @command{tex} formatting command itself does not sort the indices; it "
"writes an output file of unsorted index data.  To generate a printed index "
"after running the @command{tex} command, you first need a sorted index to "
"work from.  The @command{texindex} command sorts indices.  "
"(@command{texi2dvi}, described in the previous section, runs @command{tex} "
"and @command{texindex} as necessary.)"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:14236
#, no-wrap
msgid "Names of index files"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:14237
#, no-wrap
msgid "Index file names"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:14245
msgid ""
"@command{tex} outputs unsorted index files under names following a standard "
"convention: the name of your main input file with any @samp{.texi} or "
"similar extension replaced by the two letter index name.  For example, the "
"raw index output files for the input file @file{foo.texi} would be, by "
"default, @file{foo.cp}, @file{foo.vr}, @file{foo.fn}, @file{foo.tp}, "
"@file{foo.pg} and @file{foo.ky}.  Those are exactly the arguments to give to "
"@command{texindex}."
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:14247
#, no-wrap
msgid "Wildcards"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:14248
#, no-wrap
msgid "Globbing"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:14252
msgid ""
"Instead of specifying all the unsorted index file names explicitly, it's "
"typical to use @samp{??} as shell wildcards and give the command in this "
"form:"
msgstr ""

#. type: example
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:14255
#, no-wrap
msgid "texindex foo.??\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:14264
msgid ""
"This command will run @command{texindex} on all the unsorted index files, "
"including any two letter indices that you have defined yourself using "
"@code{@@defindex} or @code{@@defcodeindex}.  You can safely run "
"@samp{texindex foo.??} even if there are files with two letter extensions "
"that are not index files, such as @samp{foo.el}.  The @command{texindex} "
"command reports but otherwise ignores such files."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:14271
msgid ""
"For each file specified, @command{texindex} generates a sorted index file "
"whose name is made by appending @samp{s} to the input file name; for "
"example, @file{foo.cps} is made from @file{foo.cp}.  The @code{@@printindex} "
"command looks for a file with that name (@pxref{Printing Indices & Menus}).  "
"@TeX{} does not read the raw index output file, and @command{texindex} does "
"not alter it."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:14275
msgid ""
"After you have sorted the indices, you need to rerun @command{tex} on the "
"Texinfo file.  This regenerates the output file, this time with up-to-date "
"index entries."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:14278
msgid ""
"Finally, you may need to run @command{tex} one more time, to get the page "
"numbers in the cross-references correct."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:14281
msgid ""
"To summarize, this is a five-step process.  (Alternatively, it's a one-step "
"process: run @command{texi2dvi}; see the previous section.)"
msgstr ""

#. type: enumerate
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:14287
msgid ""
"Run @command{tex} on your Texinfo file.  This generates a DVI file (with "
"undefined cross-references and no indices), and the raw index files (with "
"two letter extensions)."
msgstr ""

#. type: enumerate
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:14291
msgid ""
"Run @command{texindex} on the raw index files.  This creates the "
"corresponding sorted index files (with three letter extensions)."
msgstr ""

#. type: enumerate
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:14297
msgid ""
"Run @command{tex} again on your Texinfo file.  This regenerates the DVI "
"file, this time with indices and defined cross-references, but with page "
"numbers for the cross-references from the previous run, generally incorrect."
msgstr ""

#. type: enumerate
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:14300
msgid "Sort the indices again, with @command{texindex}."
msgstr ""

#. type: enumerate
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:14304
msgid ""
"Run @command{tex} one last time.  This time the correct page numbers are "
"written for the cross-references."
msgstr ""

#. type: pindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:14306
#, no-wrap
msgid "pdftex"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:14310
msgid ""
"To generate PDF, you can run the @command{pdftex} program instead of plain "
"@command{tex}.  That is, run @command{pdftex foo.texi} instead of @samp{tex "
"foo.texi} in the examples above."
msgstr ""

#. type: subsection
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:14312
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:14313
#, no-wrap
msgid "Formatting Partial Documents"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:14315
#, no-wrap
msgid "Formatting partial documents"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:14316
#, no-wrap
msgid "Partial documents, formatting"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:14317
#, no-wrap
msgid "Chapters, formatting one at a time"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:14318
#, no-wrap
msgid "Auxiliary files, omitting"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:14319
#, no-wrap
msgid "Pointer validation @subentry suppressing"
msgstr ""

#. type: vindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:14320
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:15442
#, no-wrap
msgid "novalidate"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:14328
msgid ""
"Sometimes you may wish to print a document while you know it is incomplete, "
"or to print just one chapter of a document.  In such a case, the usual "
"auxiliary files that @TeX{} creates and warnings @TeX{} gives about "
"undefined cross-references are just nuisances.  You can avoid them with the "
"@code{@@novalidate} command, which you must give @emph{before} any "
"sectioning or cross-reference commands."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:14330
msgid "Thus, the beginning of your file would look approximately like this:"
msgstr ""

#. type: example
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:14335
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"@@novalidate\n"
"@dots{}\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:14340
msgid ""
"@command{texi2any}, just like its @code{--no-validate} option "
"(@pxref{Invoking @command{texi2any}})."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:14346
msgid ""
"Furthermore, you need not run @command{texindex} each time after you run "
"@command{tex}.  The @command{tex} formatting command simply uses whatever "
"sorted index files happen to exist from a previous use of "
"@command{texindex}.  If those are out of date, that is usually ok while you "
"are creating or debugging a document."
msgstr ""

#. type: subsection
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:14348
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:14349
#, no-wrap
msgid "Details of @command{texindex}"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:14351
#, no-wrap
msgid "Braces, in index entries"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:14358
msgid ""
"In Texinfo version 6, released in 2015, the @command{texindex} program was "
"completely reimplemented.  The principal functional difference is that index "
"entries beginning with a left brace or right brace (@samp{@{} resp.@: "
"@samp{@}}) can work properly.  For example, these simple index entries are "
"processed correctly, including the ``index initial'' shown in the index:"
msgstr ""

#. type: example
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:14364
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"@@cindex @@@{\n"
"@@cindex @@@}\n"
"...\n"
"@@printindex cp\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:14366
#, no-wrap
msgid "Literate programming, with Texinfo and @command{awk}"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:14367
#, no-wrap
msgid "Texinfo, and literate programming"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:14368
#, no-wrap
msgid "Robbins, Arnold"
msgstr ""

#. type: pindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:14369
#, no-wrap
msgid "texiwebjr"
msgstr ""

#. type: pindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:14370
#, no-wrap
msgid "ti.twjr"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:14377
msgid ""
"Although not a matter of functionality, readers may be interested to know "
"that the new @command{texindex} is a literate program "
"(@url{https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Literate_programming}) using Texinfo for "
"documentation and (portable) @command{awk} for code.  A single source file, "
"@file{texindex/ti.twjr} in this case, produces the runnable program, a "
"printable document, and an online document."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:14383
msgid ""
"The system is called TexiWeb Jr.@: and was created by Arnold Robbins, who "
"also wrote the new @command{texindex}.  Not coincidentally, he is also the "
"long-time maintainer of @command{gawk} (GNU Awk, @pxref{Top,,, gawk, The GNU "
"Awk User's Guide}).  The file @file{texindex/Makefile.am} shows example "
"usage of the system."
msgstr ""

#. type: node
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:14385
#, no-wrap
msgid "Print with @command{lpr}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:14387
msgid "@nodedescription How to print."
msgstr ""

#. type: section
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:14387
#, no-wrap
msgid "Print with @command{lpr} from Shell"
msgstr ""

#. type: pindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:14389
#, no-wrap
msgid "lpr @r{(DVI print command)}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:14395
msgid ""
"The way to print a DVI file depends on your system installation.  Two common "
"ones are @samp{dvips foo.dvi -o} to make a PostScript file first and then "
"print that, and @samp{lpr -d foo.dvi} to print a DVI file directly."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:14399
msgid ""
"For example, the following commands will (probably) suffice to sort the "
"indices, format, and print this manual using the @command{texi2dvi} shell "
"script (@pxref{Format with @command{texi2dvi}})."
msgstr ""

#. type: group
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:14405
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"texi2dvi texinfo.texi\n"
"dvips texinfo.dvi -o\n"
"lpr texinfo.ps\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:14410
msgid ""
"Depending on the @command{lpr} setup on your machine, you might be able to "
"combine the last two steps into @code{lpr -d texinfo.dvi}."
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:14411
#, no-wrap
msgid "PCL file, for printing"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:14416
msgid ""
"You can also generate a PDF file by running @command{texi2dvi} instead of "
"@command{texi2dvi}; a PDF is often directly printable.  Or you can generate "
"a PCL file by using @command{dvilj} instead of @command{dvips}, if you have "
"a printer that prefers that format."
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:14417
#, no-wrap
msgid "Shell printing, on MS-DOS/MS-Windows"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:14418
#, no-wrap
msgid "Printing DVI files, on MS-DOS/MS-Windows"
msgstr ""

#. type: pindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:14419
#, no-wrap
msgid "lpr@r{-d, replacements on MS-DOS/MS-Windows}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:14425
msgid ""
"@command{lpr} is a standard program on Unix systems, but it is usually "
"absent on MS-DOS/MS-Windows.  If so, just create a PostScript or PDF or PCL "
"file, whatever is most convenient, and print that in the usual way for your "
"machine (e.g., by sending to the appropriate port, usually @samp{PRN})."
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:14427
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:14429
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:14430
#, no-wrap
msgid "Preparing for @TeX{}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:14429
msgid "@nodedescription What to do before you use @TeX{}."
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:14431
#, no-wrap
msgid "@TeX{} input initialization"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:14432
#, no-wrap
msgid "@sortas{profile init} @file{.profile} initialization file"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:14433
#, no-wrap
msgid "@sortas{cshrc init} @file{.cshrc} initialization file"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:14434
#, no-wrap
msgid "Initialization file for @TeX{} input"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:14442
msgid ""
"@TeX{} needs to find the @file{texinfo.tex} file that the @samp{\\input "
"texinfo} command on the first line reads.  The @file{texinfo.tex} file tells "
"@TeX{} how to handle @@-commands; it is included in all standard GNU "
"distributions.  The latest version released for general use is available "
"from the usual GNU servers and mirrors:"
msgstr ""

#. type: display
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:14446
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"@uref{http://ftp.gnu.org/gnu/texinfo/texinfo.tex}\n"
"@uref{http://ftpmirror.gnu.org/texinfo/texinfo.tex}\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:14450
msgid ""
"The latest development version is available from the Texinfo source "
"repository:"
msgstr ""

#. type: display
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:14453
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"@uref{http://git.savannah.gnu.org/cgit/texinfo.git/plain/doc/texinfo.tex}\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: pindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:14455
#, no-wrap
msgid "texinfo.tex@r{, installing}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:14462
msgid ""
"@file{texinfo.tex} is essentially a standalone file, so, if you need or want "
"to try a newer version than came with your system, it nearly always suffices "
"to download it and put it anywhere that @TeX{} will find it.  You can "
"replace any existing @file{texinfo.tex} with a newer version (of course "
"saving the original in case of disaster)."
msgstr ""

#. type: pindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:14463
#, no-wrap
msgid "epsf.tex@r{, installing}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:14467
msgid ""
"Also, you should install @file{epsf.tex}, if it is not already installed "
"from another distribution.  More details are at the end of the description "
"of the @code{@@image} command (@pxref{Images})."
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:14468
#, no-wrap
msgid "European Computer Modern fonts @subentry installing"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:14469
#, no-wrap
msgid "EC fonts, installing"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:14470
#, no-wrap
msgid "CM-Super fonts @subentry installing"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:14474
msgid ""
"To use quotation marks other than those used in English, you'll need to have "
"the European Computer Modern fonts (e.g., @file{ecrm1000}) and (for PDF "
"output) CM-Super fonts (@pxref{Inserting Quotation Marks})."
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:14475
#, no-wrap
msgid "@code{feymr10} @subentry installing"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:14476
#, no-wrap
msgid "Euro font, installing"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:14479
msgid ""
"To use the @code{@@euro} command, you'll need the @samp{feym*} fonts (e.g., "
"@file{feymr10}).  @xref{@code{@@euro}}."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:14482
msgid ""
"All of the above files should be installed by default in a reasonable @TeX{} "
"installation."
msgstr ""

#. type: pindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:14483
#, no-wrap
msgid "texinfo.cnf @r{installation}"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:14484
#, no-wrap
msgid "Customizing of @TeX{} for Texinfo"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:14485
#, no-wrap
msgid "Site-wide Texinfo configuration file"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:14495
msgid ""
"Optionally, you may create a file @file{texinfo.cnf} for site "
"configuration.  When processing a Texinfo file, @TeX{} looks for this file "
"in its search path, which includes the current directory and standard "
"installation directories.  You can use this file for local conventions.  For "
"example, if @file{texinfo.cnf} contains the line @samp{@@afourpaper} "
"(@pxref{A4 Paper}), then all Texinfo documents will be processed with that "
"page size in effect.  If you have nothing to put in @file{texinfo.cnf}, you "
"do not need to create it."
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:14496
#, no-wrap
msgid "Environment variable @code{TEXINPUTS}"
msgstr ""

#. type: vindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:14497
#, no-wrap
msgid "TEXINPUTS"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:14504
msgid ""
"You can set the @code{TEXINPUTS} environment variable to allow @TeX{} to "
"find @file{texinfo.cnf}.  (This also works for @file{texinfo.tex} and any "
"other file @TeX{} might read).  For example, if you are using a Bourne "
"shell-compatible shell (@code{sh}, @code{bash}, @code{ksh}, @dots{}), your "
"@file{.profile} file could contain the lines:"
msgstr ""

#. type: example
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:14508
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"TEXINPUTS=.:/home/me/mylib:\n"
"export TEXINPUTS\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:14516
msgid ""
"These settings would cause @TeX{} first to look for an @file{\\input} file "
"in the current directory, indicated by the @samp{.}, then in a hypothetical "
"user @samp{me}'s @file{mylib} directory, and finally in the system "
"directories.  (A leading, trailing, or doubled @samp{:} indicates searching "
"the system directories at that point.)"
msgstr ""

#. type: node
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:14518
#, no-wrap
msgid "Overfull hboxes"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:14520
msgid "@nodedescription What are and what to do with overfull hboxes."
msgstr ""

#. type: section
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:14520
#, no-wrap
msgid "Overfull ``hboxes''"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:14521
#, no-wrap
msgid "Overfull @samp{hboxes}"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:14522
#, no-wrap
msgid "@samp{hbox}, overfull"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:14523
#, no-wrap
msgid "Final output"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:14530
msgid ""
"@TeX{} is sometimes unable to typeset a line within the normal margins.  "
"This most often occurs when @TeX{} comes upon what it interprets as a long "
"word that it cannot hyphenate, such as an electronic mail network address or "
"a very long identifier.  When this happens, @TeX{} prints an error message "
"like this:"
msgstr ""

#. type: example
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:14533
#, no-wrap
msgid "Overfull @@hbox (20.76302pt too wide)\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: findex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:14535
#, no-wrap
msgid "hbox"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:14539
msgid ""
"(In @TeX{}, lines are in ``horizontal boxes'', hence the term, ``hbox''.  "
"@samp{@@hbox} is a @TeX{} primitive not used in the Texinfo language.)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:14544
msgid ""
"@TeX{} also provides the line number in the Texinfo source file and the text "
"of the offending line, which is marked at all the places that @TeX{} "
"considered hyphenation.  @xref{Debugging with @TeX{}}, for more information "
"about typesetting errors."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:14549
msgid ""
"If the Texinfo file has an overfull hbox, you can rewrite the sentence so "
"the overfull hbox does not occur, or you can decide to leave it.  A small "
"excursion into the right margin often does not matter and may not even be "
"noticeable."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:14554
msgid ""
"If you have many overfull boxes and/or an antipathy to rewriting, you can "
"coerce @TeX{} into greatly increasing the allowable interword spacing, thus "
"(if you're lucky) avoiding many of the bad line breaks, like this:"
msgstr ""

#. type: findex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:14555
#, no-wrap
msgid "\\emergencystretch"
msgstr ""

#. type: example
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:14560
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"@@tex\n"
"\\global\\emergencystretch = .9\\hsize\n"
"@@end tex\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:14568
msgid ""
"(You should adjust the fraction as needed.)  This huge value for "
"@code{\\emergencystretch} cannot be the default, since then the typeset "
"output would generally be of noticeably lower quality; its default value is "
"@samp{.15\\hsize}.  @code{\\hsize} is the @TeX{} dimension containing the "
"current line width."
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:14569
#, no-wrap
msgid "Black rectangle in hardcopy"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:14570
#, no-wrap
msgid "Rectangle, black in hardcopy"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:14571
#, no-wrap
msgid "Box, ugly black in hardcopy"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:14572
#, no-wrap
msgid "Ugly black rectangles in hardcopy"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:14577
msgid ""
"For any overfull boxes you do have, @TeX{} will print a large, ugly, black "
"rectangle beside the line that contains the overfull hbox unless told "
"otherwise.  This is so you will notice the location of the problem if you "
"are correcting a draft."
msgstr ""

#. type: findex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:14578
#, no-wrap
msgid "finalout"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:14582
msgid ""
"To prevent such a monstrosity from marring your final printout, write the "
"following in the beginning of the Texinfo file on a line of its own, before "
"the @code{@@titlepage} command:"
msgstr ""

#. type: example
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:14585
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@finalout\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: node
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:14588
#, no-wrap
msgid "Generic Translator @command{texi2any}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:14590
msgid "@nodedescription @command{texi2any}, an all-purpose converter."
msgstr ""

#. type: chapter
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:14590
#, no-wrap
msgid "@command{texi2any}: The Translator for Texinfo"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:14595
msgid ""
"@command{texi2any} is the generic translator for Texinfo that can produce "
"different output formats and is highly customizable.  It supports these "
"formats:"
msgstr ""

#. type: display
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:14604
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Info (by default, or with @option{--info}),\n"
"HTML (with @option{--html}),\n"
"EPUB 3 (with @option{--epub3}),\n"
"plain text (with @option{--plaintext}),\n"
"@LaTeX{} (with @option{--latex}),\n"
"DocBook (with @option{--docbook}),\n"
"Texinfo XML (with @option{--xml}).\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:14609
msgid ""
"@command{makeinfo} is an alias for @command{texi2any}.  By default, both "
"@command{texi2any} and @command{makeinfo} generate Info output; indeed, "
"there are no differences in behavior based on the name."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:14617
msgid ""
"Beside these default formats, command line options to @command{texi2any} can "
"change many aspects of the output.  Beyond that, initialization files "
"provide even more control over the final output---nearly anything not "
"specified in the Texinfo input file.  Initialization files are written in "
"Perl, like the main program, and anything which can be specified on the "
"command line can also be specified within a initialization file."
msgstr ""

#. type: node
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:14619
#, no-wrap
msgid "Invoking @command{texi2any}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:14621
msgid "@nodedescription Running the translator from a shell."
msgstr ""

#. type: section
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:14621
#, no-wrap
msgid "Invoking @command{texi2any} from a Shell"
msgstr ""

#. type: anchor{#1}
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:14624
msgid "Invoking makeinfo"
msgstr ""

#. type: pindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:14624
#, no-wrap
msgid "makeinfo"
msgstr ""

#. type: pindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:14625
#, no-wrap
msgid "texi2any"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:14631
msgid ""
"To process a Texinfo file, invoke @command{texi2any} followed by the name of "
"the Texinfo file.  Also select the format you want to output with the "
"appropriate command line option (default is Info).  Thus, to create the Info "
"file for Bison, type the following to the shell:"
msgstr ""

#. type: example
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:14634
#, no-wrap
msgid "texi2any --info bison.texi\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:14638
msgid ""
"You can specify more than one input file name; each is processed in turn.  "
"If an input file name is @samp{-}, standard input is read."
msgstr ""

#. type: anchor{#1}
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:14641
msgid "@command{makeinfo} Options"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:14641
#, no-wrap
msgid "@command{makeinfo} options"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:14642
#, no-wrap
msgid "Options for @command{makeinfo}"
msgstr ""

#. type: anchor{#1}
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:14644
msgid "@command{texi2any} Options"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:14644
#, no-wrap
msgid "@command{texi2any} options"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:14645
#, no-wrap
msgid "Options for @command{texi2any}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:14650
msgid ""
"The @command{texi2any} program accepts many options.  Perhaps the most basic "
"are those that change the output format.  By default, @command{texi2any} "
"outputs Info."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:14654
msgid ""
"Each command line option is either a long name preceded by @samp{--} or a "
"single letter preceded by @samp{-}.  You can use abbreviations for the long "
"option names as long as they are unique."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:14658
msgid ""
"For example, you could use the following shell command to create an Info "
"file for @file{bison.texi} in which lines are filled to only 68 columns:"
msgstr ""

#. type: example
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:14661
#, no-wrap
msgid "texi2any --fill-column=68 bison.texi\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:14664
msgid "You can write two or more options in sequence, like this:"
msgstr ""

#. type: example
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:14667
#, no-wrap
msgid "texi2any --no-split --fill-column=70 @dots{}\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:14672
msgid ""
"(This would keep the Info file together as one possibly very long file and "
"would also set the fill column to 70.)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:14674
msgid "The options are (approximately in alphabetical order):"
msgstr ""

#. type: opindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:14676
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:14677
#, no-wrap
msgid "--commands-in-node-names"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:14681
msgid ""
"This option now does nothing, but remains for compatibility.  (It used to "
"ensure that @@-commands in node names were expanded throughout the document, "
"especially @code{@@value}.  This is now done by default.)"
msgstr ""

#. type: opindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:14682
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:14683
#, no-wrap
msgid "--conf-dir=@var{dir}"
msgstr ""

#.  @xref{Loading
#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:14690
msgid ""
"Prepend @var{dir} to the directory search list for finding customization "
"files that may be loaded with @option{--init-file} (see below).  The "
"@var{dir} value can be a single directory, or a list of several directories "
"separated by the usual path separator character (@samp{:} on Unix-like "
"systems, @samp{;} on Windows)."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:14691
#, no-wrap
msgid "--css-include=@var{file}"
msgstr ""

#. type: opindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:14692
#, no-wrap
msgid "--css-include"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:14697
msgid ""
"When producing HTML, literally include the contents of @var{file}, which "
"should contain Cascading Style Sheets specifications, in the @samp{<style>} "
"block of the HTML output.  If @var{file} is @samp{-}, read standard input.  "
"@xref{HTML CSS}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:14698
#, no-wrap
msgid "--css-ref=@var{url}"
msgstr ""

#. type: opindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:14699
#, no-wrap
msgid "--css-ref"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:14703
msgid ""
"When producing HTML, add a @samp{<link>} tag to the output which references "
"a cascading style sheet at @var{url}.  This allows using standalone style "
"sheets."
msgstr ""

#. type: opindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:14704
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:14706
#, no-wrap
msgid "-D @var{var}"
msgstr ""

#. type: itemx
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:14705
#, no-wrap
msgid "-D '@var{var} @var{value}'"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:14710
msgid ""
"Cause the Texinfo variable @var{var} to be defined.  This is equivalent to "
"@code{@@set @var{var}} in the Texinfo file (@pxref{@code{@@set @@clear "
"@@value}})."
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:14715
msgid ""
"The argument to the option is always one word to the shell; if it contains "
"internal whitespace, the first word is taken as the variable name and the "
"remainder as the value.  For example, @code{-D 'myvar someval'} is "
"equivalent to @code{@@set myvar someval}."
msgstr ""

#. type: opindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:14716
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:14717
#, no-wrap
msgid "--docbook"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:14719
msgid "Generate DocBook output (rather than Info)."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:14720
#, no-wrap
msgid "--document-language=@var{lang}"
msgstr ""

#. type: option{#1}
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:14721
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:15425
#, no-wrap
msgid "--document-language"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:14726
msgid ""
"Use @var{lang} to translate Texinfo keywords which end up in the output "
"document.  The default is the locale specified by the "
"@code{@@documentlanguage} command if there is one, otherwise English "
"(@pxref{@code{@@documentlanguage}})."
msgstr ""

#. type: opindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:14727
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:14728
#, no-wrap
msgid "--dvi"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:14731
msgid ""
"Generate a TeX DVI file using @command{texi2dvi}, rather than Info "
"(@pxref{@command{texi2any} Printed Output})."
msgstr ""

#. type: opindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:14732
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:14733
#, no-wrap
msgid "--dvipdf"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:14736
msgid ""
"Generate a PDF file using @command{texi2dvi --dvipdf}, rather than Info "
"(@pxref{@command{texi2any} Printed Output})."
msgstr ""

#. type: option{#1}
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:14737
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:14739
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:15423
#, no-wrap
msgid "--enable-encoding"
msgstr ""

#. type: opindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:14738
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:14740
#, no-wrap
msgid "--disable-encoding"
msgstr ""

#. type: vindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:14741
#, no-wrap
msgid "ENABLE_ENCODING"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:14747
msgid ""
"By default, or with @option{--enable-encoding}, output accented and special "
"characters in Info and plain text output based on the document encoding.  "
"With @option{--disable-encoding}, 7-bit ASCII transliterations are output.  "
"Also obeyed in other output formats for index keys sorting and for some "
"plain text output."
msgstr ""

#. type: opindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:14748
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:14749
#, no-wrap
msgid "--epub3"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:14751
msgid "Generate EPUB 3 output."
msgstr ""

#. type: opindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:14752
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:14754
#, no-wrap
msgid "--error-limit=@var{limit}"
msgstr ""

#. type: opindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:14753
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:14755
#, no-wrap
msgid "-e @var{limit}"
msgstr ""

#. type: vindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:14756
#, no-wrap
msgid "ERROR_LIMIT"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:14759
msgid ""
"Report @var{limit} errors before aborting (on the assumption that continuing "
"would be useless); default 100."
msgstr ""

#. type: opindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:14760
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:14762
#, no-wrap
msgid "--fill-column=@var{width}"
msgstr ""

#. type: opindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:14761
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:14763
#, no-wrap
msgid "-f @var{width}"
msgstr ""

#. type: vindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:14764
#, no-wrap
msgid "FILLCOLUMN"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:14771
msgid ""
"Specify the maximum number of columns in a line; this is the right-hand edge "
"of a line.  Paragraphs that are filled will be filled to this width.  "
"(Filling is the process of breaking up and connecting lines so that lines "
"are the same length as or shorter than the number specified as the fill "
"column.  Lines are broken between words.) The default value is 72."
msgstr ""

#. type: opindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:14772
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:14774
#, no-wrap
msgid "--footnote-style=@var{style}"
msgstr ""

#. type: opindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:14773
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:14775
#, no-wrap
msgid "-s @var{style}"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:14782
msgid ""
"Set the footnote style to @var{style}: either @samp{end} for the end node "
"style (the default) or @samp{separate} for the separate node style.  The "
"value set by this option overrides the value set in a Texinfo file by a "
"@code{@@footnotestyle} command (@pxref{Footnote Styles})."
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:14787
msgid ""
"In Info, when the footnote style is @samp{separate}, @command{texi2any} "
"makes a new node containing the footnotes found in the current node.  When "
"the footnote style is @samp{end}, @command{texi2any} places the footnote "
"references at the end of the current node."
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:14792
msgid ""
"In HTML, when the footnote style is @samp{end}, or if the output is not "
"split, footnotes are put at the end of the output.  If set to "
"@samp{separate}, and the output is split, they are placed in a separate file."
msgstr ""

#. type: option{#1}
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:14793
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:14795
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:15433
#, no-wrap
msgid "--force"
msgstr ""

#. type: opindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:14794
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:14796
#, no-wrap
msgid "-F"
msgstr ""

#. type: vindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:14797
#, no-wrap
msgid "FORCE"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:14800
msgid ""
"Ordinarily, if the input file has errors, the output files are not created.  "
"With this option, they are preserved."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:14801
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:17181
#, no-wrap
msgid "--help"
msgstr ""

#. type: opindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:14802
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:14804
#, no-wrap
msgid "-h"
msgstr ""

#. type: opindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:14803
#, no-wrap
msgid "--help@r{, for @command{texi2any}}"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:14807
msgid ""
"Print a message with available options and basic usage, then exit "
"successfully."
msgstr ""

#. type: opindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:14808
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:14809
#, no-wrap
msgid "--html"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:14814
msgid ""
"Generate HTML output (rather than Info).  By default, the HTML output is "
"split into one output file per node, and the split output is written into a "
"subdirectory based on the name of the input file.  @xref{Generating HTML}."
msgstr ""

#. type: opindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:14815
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:14816
#, no-wrap
msgid "-I @var{dir}"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:14824
msgid ""
"Append @var{dir} to the directory search list for finding files that are "
"included using the @code{@@include} command.  By default, @command{texi2any} "
"searches only the current directory.  If @var{dir} is not given, the current "
"directory is appended.  The @var{dir} value can be a single directory or a "
"list of several directories separated by the usual path separator character "
"(@samp{:} on Unix-like systems, @samp{;} on Windows)."
msgstr ""

#. type: opindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:14825
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:14826
#, no-wrap
msgid "--ifdocbook"
msgstr ""

#. type: opindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:14827
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:14828
#, no-wrap
msgid "--ifhtml"
msgstr ""

#. type: opindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:14829
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:14830
#, no-wrap
msgid "--ifinfo"
msgstr ""

#. type: opindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:14831
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:14832
#, no-wrap
msgid "--iflatex"
msgstr ""

#. type: opindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:14833
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:14834
#, no-wrap
msgid "--ifplaintext"
msgstr ""

#. type: opindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:14835
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:14836
#, no-wrap
msgid "--iftex"
msgstr ""

#. type: opindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:14837
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:14838
#, no-wrap
msgid "--ifxml"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:14845
msgid ""
"For the given format, process @samp{@@if@var{format}} and "
"@samp{@@@var{format}} commands, and do not process "
"@samp{@@ifnot@var{format}}, regardless of the format being output.  For "
"instance, if @option{--iftex} is given, then @samp{@@iftex} and @samp{@@tex} "
"blocks will be read, and @samp{@@ifnottex} blocks will be ignored."
msgstr ""

#. type: opindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:14846
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:14847
#, no-wrap
msgid "--no-ifdocbook"
msgstr ""

#. type: opindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:14848
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:14849
#, no-wrap
msgid "--no-ifhtml"
msgstr ""

#. type: opindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:14850
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:14851
#, no-wrap
msgid "--no-ifinfo"
msgstr ""

#. type: opindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:14852
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:14853
#, no-wrap
msgid "--no-iflatex"
msgstr ""

#. type: opindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:14854
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:14855
#, no-wrap
msgid "--no-ifplaintext"
msgstr ""

#. type: opindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:14856
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:14857
#, no-wrap
msgid "--no-iftex"
msgstr ""

#. type: opindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:14858
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:14859
#, no-wrap
msgid "--no-ifxml"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:14866
msgid ""
"For the given format, do not process @samp{@@if@var{format}} and "
"@samp{@@@var{format}} commands, and do process @samp{@@ifnot@var{format}}, "
"regardless of the format being output.  For instance, if "
"@option{--no-ifhtml} is given, then @samp{@@ifhtml} and @samp{@@html} blocks "
"will not be read, and @samp{@@ifnothtml} blocks will be."
msgstr ""

#. type: opindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:14868
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:14869
#, no-wrap
msgid "--info"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:14875
msgid ""
"Generate Info output.  By default, if the output file contains more than "
"about 300,000 bytes, it is split into shorter subfiles of about that size.  "
"The name of the output file and any subfiles is determined by the input file "
"name, or by @code{@@setfilename}, if present (@pxref{Setting the Output File "
"Name}).  @xref{Tag and Split Files}."
msgstr ""

#. type: opindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:14876
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:14877
#, no-wrap
msgid "--init-file=@var{file}"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:14885
msgid ""
"Load @var{file} as code to modify the behavior and output of the generated "
"manual.  It is customary to use the @code{.pm} or the @code{.init} "
"extensions for these customization files, but that is not enforced; the "
"@var{file} name can be anything.  The @option{--conf-dir} option (see above) "
"can be used to add to the list of directories in which these customization "
"files are searched for."
msgstr ""

#. type: opindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:14886
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:14887
#, no-wrap
msgid "--internal-links=@var{file}"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:14888
#, no-wrap
msgid "Internal links, of HTML"
msgstr ""

#. type: vindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:14889
#, no-wrap
msgid "INTERNAL_LINKS"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:14896
msgid ""
"In HTML mode, output a tab-separated file containing three columns: the "
"internal link to an indexed item or item in the table of contents, the name "
"of the index (or table of contents) in which it occurs, and the term which "
"was indexed or entered.  The items are in the natural sorting order for the "
"given element.  This dump can be useful for post-processors."
msgstr ""

#. type: opindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:14897
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:14898
#, no-wrap
msgid "--latex"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:14900
msgid "Generate @LaTeX{} output."
msgstr ""

#. type: opindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:14901
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:14903
#, no-wrap
msgid "--macro-expand=@var{file}"
msgstr ""

#. type: opindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:14902
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:14904
#, no-wrap
msgid "-E @var{file}"
msgstr ""

#. type: vindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:14905
#, no-wrap
msgid "MACRO_EXPAND"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:14909
msgid ""
"Output the Texinfo source, with all Texinfo macros expanded, to @var{file}.  "
"Normally, the result of macro expansion is used internally by "
"@command{texi2any} and then discarded."
msgstr ""

#. type: opindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:14910
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:14911
#, no-wrap
msgid "--no-headers"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:14912
#, no-wrap
msgid "Node separators, omitting with @option{--no-headers}"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:14913
#, no-wrap
msgid "Generating plain text files with @option{--no-headers}"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:14914
#, no-wrap
msgid "Menus, omitting with @option{--no-headers}"
msgstr ""

#. type: vindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:14915
#, no-wrap
msgid "HEADERS"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:14917
msgid "Do not include menus or node separator lines in the output."
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:14922
msgid ""
"When generating Info, this is the same as using @option{--plaintext}, "
"resulting in a simple plain text file.  Furthermore, output is to standard "
"output unless overridden with @option{-o}.  (This behavior is for backward "
"compatibility.)"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:14923
#, no-wrap
msgid "Navigation links, omitting"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:14928
msgid ""
"When generating HTML, and output is split, also output navigation links only "
"at the beginning of each file.  If output is not split, do not include "
"navigation links at the top of each node at all.  @xref{Generating HTML}."
msgstr ""

#. type: option{#1}
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:14929
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:14931
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:15450
#, no-wrap
msgid "--node-files"
msgstr ""

#. type: opindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:14930
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:14932
#, no-wrap
msgid "--no-node-files"
msgstr ""

#. type: vindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:14933
#, no-wrap
msgid "NODE_FILES"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:14939
msgid ""
"With @option{--node-files}, when generating HTML, create redirection files "
"for anchors and any nodes not already output with the file name "
"corresponding to the node name (@pxref{HTML Xref Node Name Expansion}).  "
"This makes it possible for section- and chapter-level cross-manual "
"references to succeed (@pxref{HTML Xref Configuration})."
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:14946
msgid ""
"If the output is split, this is enabled by default.  If the output is not "
"split, @option{--node-files} enables the creation of the redirection files, "
"in addition to the monolithic main output file.  @option{--no-node-files} "
"suppresses the creation of redirection files in any case.  This option has "
"no effect with any output format other than HTML@.  @xref{Generating HTML}."
msgstr ""

#. type: option{#1}
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:14947
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:14949
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:15444
#, no-wrap
msgid "--no-validate"
msgstr ""

#. type: opindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:14948
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:14950
#, no-wrap
msgid "--no-pointer-validate"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:14951
#, no-wrap
msgid "Pointer validation"
msgstr ""

#. type: anchor{#1}
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:14956
msgid "Pointer Validation"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:14956
msgid ""
"Suppress the pointer-validation phase of @command{texi2any}---a dangerous "
"thing to do.  This can also be done with the @code{@@novalidate} command "
"(@pxref{Formatting Partial Documents})."
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:14960
msgid ""
"If you do not suppress pointer validation, @command{texi2any} will check the "
"validity of cross-references and menu entries in the Texinfo file, as well "
"as node pointers if they are given explicitly."
msgstr ""

#. type: enumerate
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:14977
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"If a `Next', `Previous', or `Up' node reference is a reference to a\n"
"node in the current file and is not an external reference such as to\n"
"@file{(dir)}, then the referenced node must exist.\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: enumerate
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:14980
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Every node except the `Top' node must have an `Up' pointer.\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: enumerate
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:14985
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The node referenced by an `Up' pointer must itself reference the\n"
"current node through a menu item, unless the node referenced by `Up'\n"
"has the form @samp{(@var{file})}.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: option{#1}
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:14988
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:14989
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:15441
#, no-wrap
msgid "--no-warn"
msgstr ""

#. type: vindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:14990
#, no-wrap
msgid "NO_WARN"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:14992
msgid "Suppress warning messages (but not error messages)."
msgstr ""

#. type: option{#1}
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:14993
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:15446
#, no-wrap
msgid "--number-footnotes"
msgstr ""

#. type: opindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:14994
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:14995
#, no-wrap
msgid "--no-number-footnotes"
msgstr ""

#. type: vindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:14996
#, no-wrap
msgid "NUMBER_FOOTNOTES"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:15000
msgid ""
"With @option{--no-number-footnotes}, suppress automatic footnote numbering.  "
"By default, footnotes are numbered sequentially within a node, i.e., the "
"current footnote number is reset to 1 at the start of each node."
msgstr ""

#. type: option{#1}
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:15001
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:15003
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:15448
#, no-wrap
msgid "--number-sections"
msgstr ""

#. type: opindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:15002
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:15004
#, no-wrap
msgid "--no-number-sections"
msgstr ""

#. type: vindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:15005
#, no-wrap
msgid "NUMBER_SECTIONS"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:15010
msgid ""
"With @option{--number-sections} (the default), output chapter, section, and "
"appendix numbers as in printed manuals.  This works only with hierarchically "
"structured manuals.  You should specify @code{--no-number-sections} if your "
"manual is not normally structured."
msgstr ""

#. type: opindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:15012
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:15014
#, no-wrap
msgid "--output=@var{file}"
msgstr ""

#. type: opindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:15013
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:15015
#, no-wrap
msgid "-o @var{file}"
msgstr ""

#. type: vindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:15016
#, no-wrap
msgid "OUTFILE"
msgstr ""

#. type: vindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:15017
#, no-wrap
msgid "SUBDIR"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:15023
msgid ""
"Specify that the output should be directed to @var{file}.  This overrides "
"any file name specified in a @code{@@setfilename} command found in the "
"Texinfo source.  If neither @code{@@setfilename} nor this option are "
"specified, the input file name is used to determine the output name.  "
"@xref{Setting the Output File Name}."
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:15026
msgid ""
"If @var{file} is @samp{-}, output goes to standard output and "
"@samp{--no-split} is implied."
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:15033
msgid ""
"If @var{file} is a directory or ends with a @samp{/} the usual rules are "
"used to determine the output file name (namely, use @code{@@setfilename} or "
"the input file name) but the files are written to the @var{file} directory.  "
"For example, @samp{texi2any -o bar/ foo.texi}, with or without "
"@option{--no-split}, will write @file{bar/foo.info}, and possibly other "
"files, under @file{bar/}."
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:15038
msgid ""
"When generating HTML and output is split, @var{file} is used as the name for "
"the directory into which all files are written.  For example, @samp{texi2any "
"-o bar --html foo.texi} will write @file{bar/index.html}, among other files."
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:15044
msgid ""
"When generating EPUB a container directory for the files and directories "
"needed for the EPUB format is created, as well as the EPUB output file.  If "
"@var{file} corresponds to a directory, the container directory is placed "
"within @var{file}.  The EPUB output file is never put in this directory.  If "
"@var{file} corresponds to a file, it is used for the EPUB output file name."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:15045
#, no-wrap
msgid "--output-indent=@var{val}"
msgstr ""

#. type: opindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:15046
#, no-wrap
msgid "--outputindent"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:15049
msgid ""
"This option now does nothing, but remains for compatibility.  (It used to "
"alter indentation in XML/DocBook output.)"
msgstr ""

#. type: opindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:15050
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:15051
#, no-wrap
msgid "-P @var{path}"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:15055
msgid ""
"Prepend @var{path} to the directory search list for @code{@@include}.  If "
"@var{path} is not given, the current directory is prepended.  See @samp{-I} "
"above."
msgstr ""

#. type: opindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:15056
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:15058
#, no-wrap
msgid "--paragraph-indent=@var{indent}"
msgstr ""

#. type: opindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:15057
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:15059
#, no-wrap
msgid "-p @var{indent}"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:15064
msgid ""
"Set the paragraph indentation style to @var{indent}.  The value set by this "
"option overrides the value set in a Texinfo file by an "
"@code{@@paragraphindent} command (@pxref{@code{@@paragraphindent}}).  The "
"value of @var{indent} is interpreted as follows:"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:15069
msgid ""
"Preserve any existing indentation (or lack thereof) at the beginnings of "
"paragraphs."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:15070
#, no-wrap
msgid "@samp{0} or @samp{none}"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:15072
msgid "Delete any existing indentation."
msgstr ""

#. type: var{#1}
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:15073
#, no-wrap
msgid "num"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:15075
msgid "Indent each paragraph by @var{num} spaces."
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:15079
msgid ""
"The default is to indent by two spaces, except for paragraphs following a "
"section heading, which are not indented."
msgstr ""

#. type: opindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:15080
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:15081
#, no-wrap
msgid "--pdf"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:15084
msgid ""
"Generate a PDF file using @command{texi2dvi --pdf}, rather than Info "
"(@pxref{@command{texi2any} Printed Output})."
msgstr ""

#. type: opindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:15085
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:15086
#, no-wrap
msgid "--plaintext"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:15087
#, no-wrap
msgid "Plain text output with @option{--plaintext}"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:15088
#, no-wrap
msgid "ASCII text output with @option{--plaintext}"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:15089
#, no-wrap
msgid "Generating plain text files with @option{--plaintext}"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:15090
#, no-wrap
msgid "Node separators, omitting with @option{--plaintext}"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:15091
#, no-wrap
msgid "Menus, omitting with @option{--plaintext}"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:15092
#, no-wrap
msgid "@file{INSTALL} file, generating"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:15098
msgid ""
"Output a plain text file (rather than Info): do not include menus or node "
"separator lines in the output.  This results in a straightforward plain text "
"file that you can (for example) send in email without complications, or "
"include in a distribution (for example, an @file{INSTALL} file)."
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:15102
msgid ""
"With this option the output goes to standard output by default, instead of "
"to a file with a name based on the input file name or @code{@@setfilename}; "
"this can be overridden with @option{-o}."
msgstr ""

#. type: opindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:15103
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:15104
#, no-wrap
msgid "--ps"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:15107
msgid ""
"Generate a PostScript file using @command{texi2dvi --ps}, rather than Info "
"(@pxref{@command{texi2any} Printed Output})."
msgstr ""

#. type: opindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:15108
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:15110
#, no-wrap
msgid "--set-customization-variable @var{var}=@var{value}"
msgstr ""

#. type: opindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:15109
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:15111
#, no-wrap
msgid "-c @var{var}=@var{value}"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:15119
msgid ""
"Set the customization variable @var{var} to @var{value}.  The @code{=} is "
"optional, but both @var{var} and @var{value} must be quoted to the shell as "
"necessary so the result is a single word.  Many aspects of "
"@command{texi2any} behavior and output may be controlled by customization "
"variables, beyond what can be set in the document by @@-commands and with "
"other command line switches.  @xref{Customization Variables}."
msgstr ""

#. type: opindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:15120
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:15122
#, no-wrap
msgid "--split=@var{how}"
msgstr ""

#. type: opindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:15121
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:15123
#, no-wrap
msgid "--no-split"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:15124
#, no-wrap
msgid "Splitting of output files"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:15125
#, no-wrap
msgid "Output file splitting"
msgstr ""

#. type: anchor{#1}
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:15132
msgid "Splitting Output"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:15132
msgid ""
"When generating Info, by default large output files are split into smaller "
"subfiles, of approximately 300k bytes.  When generating HTML, by default "
"each output file contains one node (@pxref{Generating HTML}).  "
"@option{--no-split} suppresses this splitting of the output."
msgstr ""

#. type: vindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:15133
#, no-wrap
msgid "SPLIT"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:15137
msgid ""
"Alternatively, @option{--split=@var{how}} may be used to specify at which "
"level the HTML output should be split.  The possible values for @var{how} "
"are:"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:15142
msgid ""
"The output is split at @code{@@chapter} and other sectioning @@-commands at "
"this level (@code{@@appendix}, etc.)."
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:15145
msgid "The output is split at @code{@@section} and similar."
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:15148
msgid "The output is split at every node.  This is the default."
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:15153
msgid ""
"Plain text output can be split similarly to HTML@.  This may be useful for "
"extracting sections from a Texinfo document and making them available as "
"separate files."
msgstr ""

#. type: opindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:15154
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:15155
#, no-wrap
msgid "--split-size=@var{num}"
msgstr ""

#. type: vindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:15156
#, no-wrap
msgid "SPLIT_SIZE"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:15160
msgid ""
"Keep Info files to at most @var{num} characters if possible; default is "
"300,000.  (However, a single node will never be split across Info files.)"
msgstr ""

#. type: option{#1}
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:15161
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:15162
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:15463
#, no-wrap
msgid "--transliterate-file-names"
msgstr ""

#. type: vindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:15163
#, no-wrap
msgid "TRANSLITERATE_FILE_NAMES"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:15166
msgid ""
"Enable transliteration of non-ASCII characters in node names for the purpose "
"of file name creation.  @xref{HTML Xref 8-bit Character Expansion}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:15167
#, no-wrap
msgid "-U @var{var}"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:15170
msgid ""
"Cause @var{var} to be undefined.  This is equivalent to @code{@@clear "
"@var{var}} in the Texinfo file (@pxref{@code{@@set @@clear @@value}})."
msgstr ""

#. type: option{#1}
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:15171
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:15172
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:15465
#, no-wrap
msgid "--verbose"
msgstr ""

#. type: vindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:15173
#, no-wrap
msgid "VERBOSE"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:15177
msgid ""
"Cause @command{texi2any} to display messages saying what it is doing.  "
"Normally, @command{texi2any} only outputs messages if there are errors or "
"warnings."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:15178
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:17299
#, no-wrap
msgid "--version"
msgstr ""

#. type: opindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:15179
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:15181
#, no-wrap
msgid "-V"
msgstr ""

#. type: opindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:15180
#, no-wrap
msgid "--version@r{, for @command{texi2any}}"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:15183
msgid "Print the version number, then exit successfully."
msgstr ""

#. type: opindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:15184
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:15185
#, no-wrap
msgid "--Xopt @var{str}"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:15188
msgid ""
"Pass @var{str} (a single shell word) to @command{texi2dvi}; may be repeated "
"(@pxref{@command{texi2any} Printed Output})."
msgstr ""

#. type: opindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:15189
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:15190
#, no-wrap
msgid "--xml"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:15192
msgid "Generate Texinfo XML output (rather than Info)."
msgstr ""

#. type: node
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:15196
#, no-wrap
msgid "@command{texi2any} Environment Variables"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:15198
msgid "@nodedescription Control over output format and XS use."
msgstr ""

#. type: section
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:15198
#, no-wrap
msgid "Environment Variables Recognized by @command{texi2any}"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:15200
#, no-wrap
msgid "Environment variable @code{TEXINFO_OUTPUT_FORMAT}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:15204
msgid ""
"@command{texi2any} also reads the environment variable "
"@env{TEXINFO_OUTPUT_FORMAT} to determine the output format, if not "
"overridden by a command line option.  The value should be one of:"
msgstr ""

#. type: example
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:15207
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"docbook  dvi  dvipdf  epub3  html  info  latex  pdf  plaintext  ps  xml\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:15210
msgid "If not set or otherwise specified, Info output is the default."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:15214
msgid ""
"@code{TEXINFO_OUTPUT_FORMAT} may take some other special values, which do "
"not correspond to any command-line settable output format "
"(@pxref{Customization Variables and Options})."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:15218
msgid ""
"The customization variable of the same name is also read; if set, that "
"overrides an environment variable setting, but not a command-line option.  "
"@xref{Customization Variables and Options}."
msgstr ""

#. type: vindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:15219
#, no-wrap
msgid "TEXINFO_XS"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:15220
#, no-wrap
msgid "Perl extension modules (XS)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:15230
msgid ""
"You can control @command{texi2any}'s use of Perl extension modules by "
"setting the @env{TEXINFO_XS} environment variable.  These modules are "
"compiled native code that the interpreted Perl code can use.  Ideally, these "
"extension modules should just work, and the only noticeable difference they "
"should make is that @command{texi2any} finishes running sooner.  However, "
"you can use this environment variable for the purposes of troubleshooting: "
"for example, if you have problems with the output of @command{texi2any} "
"varying depending on whether the extension modules are in use."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:15233
msgid ""
"The following values of @env{TEXINFO_XS} are recognized by "
"@command{texi2any}:"
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:15235
#, no-wrap
msgid "default"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:15238
msgid ""
"The default behavior.  Try to load extension modules, and silently fall back "
"to the interpreted Perl implementations if this fails."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:15239
#, no-wrap
msgid "warn"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:15242
msgid ""
"Try to load extension modules, and if this fails, give a warning message "
"before falling back to the interpreted Perl implementations."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:15243
#, no-wrap
msgid "debug"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:15245
msgid "Try to load extension modules, printing many messages while doing so."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:15246
#, no-wrap
msgid "omit"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:15248
msgid "Do not use extension modules."
msgstr ""

#. type: vindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:15251
#, no-wrap
msgid "TEXINFO_XS_PARSER"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:15258
msgid ""
"Set @env{TEXINFO_XS_PARSER} to @samp{0} to disable the use of the native "
"code implementation of the parser module.  This is the part of "
"@command{texi2any} that converts Texinfo input into an internal tree format "
"used for further processing into output formats.  This may be useful for "
"working around bugs or incompatibilities between the native code "
"implementation and the implementation in pure Perl code."
msgstr ""

#. type: section
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:15260
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:15262
#, no-wrap
msgid "@command{texi2any} Printed Output"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:15262
msgid "@nodedescription Calling @command{texi2dvi}."
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:15264
#, no-wrap
msgid "Printed output, through @command{texi2any}"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:15265
#, no-wrap
msgid "Output, printed through @command{texi2any}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:15276
msgid ""
"To justify the name Texinfo-to-@emph{any}, @command{texi2any} has basic "
"support for creating printed output in the various formats: @TeX{} DVI, PDF, "
"and PostScript.  This is done via the simple method of executing the "
"@command{texi2dvi} program when those output formats are requested, after "
"checking the validity of the input to give users the benefit of "
"@command{texi2any}'s error checking.  If you don't want such error checking, "
"perhaps because your manual plays advanced @TeX{} tricks together with "
"@file{texinfo.tex}, just invoke @command{texi2dvi} directly."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:15284
msgid ""
"The output format options for this are @option{--dvi}, @option{--dvipdf}, "
"@option{--pdf}, and @option{--ps}.  @xref{Format with @command{texi2dvi}}, "
"for more details on these options and general @command{texi2dvi} operation.  "
"In addition, the @option{--verbose}, @option{--silent}, and @option{--quiet} "
"options are passed on if specified; the @option{-I} and @option{-o} options "
"are likewise passed on with their arguments, and @option{--debug} without "
"its argument."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:15290
msgid ""
"The only option remaining that is related to the @command{texi2dvi} "
"invocation is @option{--Xopt}.  Here, just the argument is passed on and "
"multiple @option{--Xopt} options accumulate.  This provides a way to "
"construct an arbitrary command line for @command{texi2dvi}.  For example, "
"running"
msgstr ""

#. type: example
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:15293
#, no-wrap
msgid "texi2any --Xopt -t --Xopt @@a4paper --pdf foo.texi\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: example
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:15299
#, no-wrap
msgid "texi2dvi -t @@a4paper --pdf foo.texi\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:15308
msgid ""
"Although one might wish that other options to @command{texi2any} would take "
"effect, they don't.  For example, running @samp{texi2any "
"--no-number-sections --dvi foo.texi} still results in a DVI file with "
"numbered sections.  (Perhaps this could be improved in the future, if "
"requests are received.)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:15312
msgid ""
"The actual name of the command that is invoked is specified by the "
"@code{TEXI2DVI} customization variable (@pxref{Other Customization "
"Variables}).  As you might guess, the default is @samp{texi2dvi}."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:15315
msgid ""
"@command{texi2any} itself does not generate any normal output when it "
"invokes @command{texi2dvi}, only diagnostic messages."
msgstr ""

#. type: section
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:15317
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:15319
#, no-wrap
msgid "Customization Variables"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:15319
msgid "@nodedescription Configuring @command{texi2any}."
msgstr ""

#. type: quotation
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:15321
#, no-wrap
msgid "Warning"
msgstr ""

#. type: quotation
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:15325
msgid ""
"These customization variable names and meanings may change in any Texinfo "
"release.  We always try to avoid incompatible changes, but we cannot "
"absolutely promise, since needs change over time."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:15330
msgid ""
"Many aspects of the behavior and output of @command{texi2any} may be "
"modified by modifying so-called @dfn{customization variables}.  These fall "
"into a few general categories:"
msgstr ""

#. type: itemize
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:15335
msgid ""
"Those associated with @@-commands; for example, @code{@@documentlanguage}."
msgstr ""

#. type: itemize
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:15341
msgid ""
"Those associated with command-line options; for example, the customization "
"variable @code{SPLIT} is associated with the @option{--split} command-line "
"option, and @code{TEXINFO_OUTPUT_FORMAT} allows specifying the output format."
msgstr ""

#. type: itemize
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:15344
msgid "Those associated with customizing the HTML output."
msgstr ""

#. type: itemize
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:15347
msgid "Other ad hoc variables."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:15355
msgid ""
"Customization variables may set on the command line using "
"@code{--set-customization-variable '@var{var} @var{value}'} (quoting the "
"variable/value pair to the shell) or @code{--set-customization-variable "
"@var{var}=@var{value}} (using @code{=}).  A special @var{value} is "
"@samp{undef}, which sets the variable to this special ``undefined'' Perl "
"value."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:15357
msgid "The sections below give the details for each of these."
msgstr ""

#. type: menuentry
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:15367
msgid "Commands: Customization Variables for @@-Commands."
msgstr ""

#. type: menuentry
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:15367
msgid "Options: Customization Variables and Options."
msgstr ""

#. type: menuentry
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:15367
msgid "HTML: HTML Customization Variables."
msgstr ""

#. type: menuentry
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:15367
msgid "MathJax: MathJax Customization Variables."
msgstr ""

#. type: menuentry
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:15367
msgid "latex2html: @command{latex2html} Customization Variables."
msgstr ""

#. type: menuentry
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:15367
msgid "tex4ht: @command{tex4ht} Customization Variables."
msgstr ""

#. type: menuentry
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:15367
msgid "LaTeX: @LaTeX{} Customization Variables."
msgstr ""

#. type: menuentry
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:15367
msgid "Other: Other Customization Variables"
msgstr ""

#. type: subsection
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:15370
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:15371
#, no-wrap
msgid "Customization Variables for @@-Commands"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:15373
#, no-wrap
msgid "Customization variables for @@-commands"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:15374
#, no-wrap
msgid "@sortas{at} @@-commands @subentry customization variables for"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:15378
msgid ""
"Each of the following @@-commands has an associated customization variable "
"with the same name (minus the leading @code{@@}):"
msgstr ""

#. type: example
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:15395
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"@@afivepaper            @@afourpaper        @@afourlatex\n"
"@@afourwide             @@allowcodebreaks   @@bsixpaper\n"
"@@contents              @@clickstyle        @@codequotebacktick\n"
"@@codequoteundirected   @@deftypefnnewline  @@documentdescription\n"
"@@documentencoding      @@documentlanguage  @@evenfooting\n"
"@@evenfootingmarks      @@evenheading       @@evenheadingmarks\n"
"@@everyfooting          @@everyfootingmarks @@everyheading\n"
"@@everyheadingmarks     @@exampleindent     @@firstparagraphindent\n"
"@@fonttextsize          @@footnotestyle     @@frenchspacing\n"
"@@headings              @@kbdinputstyle     @@microtype\n"
"@@novalidate            @@oddfooting        @@oddfootingmarks\n"
"@@oddheading            @@oddheadingmarks   @@pagesizes\n"
"@@paragraphindent       @@setfilename       @@setchapternewpage\n"
"@@shortcontents         @@smallbook         @@summarycontents\n"
"@@urefbreakstyle        @@xrefautomaticsectiontitle\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:15403
msgid ""
"Setting such a customization variable to a value @samp{foo} is similar to "
"executing @code{@@@var{cmd} foo}.  It is not exactly the same, though, since "
"any side effects of parsing the Texinfo source are not redone.  Also, some "
"variables do not take Texinfo code when generating particular formats, but "
"an argument that is already formatted.  This is the case, for example, for "
"HTML for @code{documentdescription}."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:15407
msgid ""
"Note that if @command{texi2any} is invoked to process the file with @TeX{} "
"(e.g., with the @option{--pdf} option), then these customization variables "
"may not be passed on to @TeX{}."
msgstr ""

#. type: subsection
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:15409
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:15410
#, no-wrap
msgid "Customization Variables and Options"
msgstr ""

