"Setting such a customization variable to a value @samp{foo} is essentially "
"the same as specifying the @code{--@var{opt}=foo} if the option takes an "
"argument, or @code{--@var{opt}} if not."
msgstr ""

#. type: vindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:15471
#, no-wrap
msgid "TEXINFO_OUTPUT_FORMAT"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:15476
msgid ""
"In addition, the customization variable @code{TEXINFO_OUTPUT_FORMAT} allows "
"specifying what @command{texi2any} outputs, either one of the usual output "
"formats that can be specified with options, or various other forms:"
msgstr ""

#. type: itemx
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:15479
#, no-wrap
msgid "dvi"
msgstr ""

#. type: itemx
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:15480
#, no-wrap
msgid "dvipdf"
msgstr ""

#. type: itemx
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:15481
#, no-wrap
msgid "epub3"
msgstr ""

#. type: itemx
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:15483
#, no-wrap
msgid "info"
msgstr ""

#. type: itemx
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:15484
#, no-wrap
msgid "pdf"
msgstr ""

#. type: itemx
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:15485
#, no-wrap
msgid "plaintext"
msgstr ""

#. type: itemx
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:15486
#, no-wrap
msgid "ps"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:15491
msgid ""
"These correspond to the command-line options (and "
"@code{TEXINFO_OUTPUT_FORMAT} environment variable values) of the same name.  "
"@xref{Invoking @command{texi2any}}."
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:15492
#, no-wrap
msgid "tree representation, for debugging"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:15493
#, no-wrap
msgid "debugging document, with tree representation"
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:15494
#, no-wrap
msgid "debugtree"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:15497
msgid ""
"Instead of generating a regular output format, output a text representation "
"of the tree obtained by parsing the input texinfo document."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:15498
#, no-wrap
msgid "parse"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:15500
msgid "Do only Texinfo source parsing; there is no output."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:15501
#, no-wrap
msgid "plaintexinfo"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:15506
msgid ""
"Output the Texinfo source with all the macros, @code{@@include} and "
"@code{@@value@{@}} expanded.  This is similar to setting "
"@option{--macro-expand}, but instead of being output in addition to the "
"normal conversion, output of Texinfo is the main output."
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:15507
#, no-wrap
msgid "raw text output"
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:15508
#, no-wrap
msgid "rawtext"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:15512
msgid ""
"Output raw text, with minimal formatting.  For example, footnotes are "
"ignored and there is no paragraph filling.  This is used by the parser for "
"file names and copyright text in HTML comments, for example."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:15513
#, no-wrap
msgid "structure"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:15516
msgid ""
"Do only Texinfo source parsing and determination of the document structure; "
"there is no output."
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:15517
#, no-wrap
msgid "SXML output"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:15518
#, no-wrap
msgid "S-expressions, output format"
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:15519
#, no-wrap
msgid "texinfosxml"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:15522
msgid ""
"Output the document in TexinfoSXML representation, a syntax for writing XML "
"data using Lisp S-expressions."
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:15523
#, no-wrap
msgid "spell checking"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:15524
#, no-wrap
msgid "word counting"
msgstr ""

#. type: pindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:15525
#, no-wrap
msgid "detexinfo"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:15526
#, no-wrap
msgid "stripping Texinfo commands"
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:15527
#, no-wrap
msgid "textcontent"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:15532
msgid ""
"Output the text content only, stripped of commands; this is useful for spell "
"checking or word counting, for example.  The trivial @code{detexinfo} script "
"setting this is in the @file{util} directory of the Texinfo source as an "
"example.  It's one line:"
msgstr ""

#. type: example
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:15535
#, no-wrap
msgid "exec texi2any -c TEXINPUT_OUTPUT_FORMAT=textcontent \"$@@\"\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: subsection
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:15539
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:15540
#, no-wrap
msgid "HTML Customization Variables"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:15545
msgid ""
"This table gives the customization variables which apply to HTML output "
"only.  A few other customization variables apply to both HTML and other "
"output formats; see @ref{Other Customization Variables}."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:15547
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:15949
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:15985
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:16027
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:16058
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:16110
msgid "@vtable @code"
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:15547
#, no-wrap
msgid "AVOID_MENU_REDUNDANCY"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:15550
msgid ""
"If set, and the menu entry and menu description are the same, then do not "
"print the menu description; default false."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:15551
#, no-wrap
msgid "AFTER_BODY_OPEN"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:15554
msgid ""
"If set, the corresponding text will appear at the beginning of each HTML "
"file; default unset."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:15555
#, no-wrap
msgid "AFTER_SHORT_TOC_LINES"
msgstr ""

#. type: itemx
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:15556
#, no-wrap
msgid "AFTER_TOC_LINES"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:15561
msgid ""
"If set, the corresponding text is output after the short table of contents "
"for @code{AFTER_SHORT_TOC_LINES} and after the table of contents for "
"@code{AFTER_TOC_LINES}; otherwise, a default string is used.  At the time of "
"writing, a @code{</div>} element is closed."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:15565
msgid ""
"In general, you should set @code{BEFORE_SHORT_TOC_LINES} if "
"@code{AFTER_SHORT_TOC_LINES} is set, and you should set "
"@code{BEFORE_TOC_LINES} if @code{AFTER_TOC_LINES} is set."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:15566
#, no-wrap
msgid "BASEFILENAME_LENGTH"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:15570
msgid ""
"The maximum length of a base file name; default 245.  Changing this would "
"make cross-manual references to such long node names invalid (@pxref{HTML "
"Xref Link Basics})."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:15571
#, no-wrap
msgid "BEFORE_SHORT_TOC_LINES"
msgstr ""

#. type: itemx
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:15572
#, no-wrap
msgid "BEFORE_TOC_LINES"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:15577
msgid ""
"If set, the corresponding text is output before the short table of contents "
"for @code{BEFORE_SHORT_TOC_LINES} and before the table of contents for "
"@code{BEFORE_TOC_LINES}, otherwise a default string is used.  At the time of "
"writing, a @code{<div ...>} element is opened."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:15581
msgid ""
"In general you should set @code{AFTER_SHORT_TOC_LINES} if "
"@code{BEFORE_SHORT_TOC_LINES} is set, and you should set "
"@code{AFTER_TOC_LINES} if @code{BEFORE_TOC_LINES} is set."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:15583
#, no-wrap
msgid "BIG_RULE"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:15587
msgid ""
"Rule used after and before the top element and before special elements, but "
"not for footers and headers; default @code{<hr>}."
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:15588
#, no-wrap
msgid "@code{<body>} text, customizing"
msgstr ""

#. type: opindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:15589
#, no-wrap
msgid "lang@r{, HTML attribute}"
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:15590
#, no-wrap
msgid "BODYTEXT"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:15594
msgid ""
"The text appearing in @code{<body>}.  By default, sets the HTML @code{lang} "
"attribute to the document language (@pxref{@code{@@documentlanguage}})."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:15595
#, no-wrap
msgid "CASE_INSENSITIVE_FILENAMES"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:15598
msgid ""
"Construct output file names as if the filesystem were case insensitive "
"(@pxref{HTML Splitting}); default false."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:15599
#, no-wrap
msgid "CHAPTER_HEADER_LEVEL"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:15602
msgid ""
"Header formatting level used for chapter level sectioning commands; default "
"@samp{2}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:15603
#, no-wrap
msgid "CHECK_HTMLXREF"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:15607
msgid ""
"Check that manuals which are the target of external cross-references "
"(@pxref{Four and Five Arguments}) are present in @file{htmlxref.cnf} "
"(@pxref{HTML Xref Configuration}); default false."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:15608
#, no-wrap
msgid "COMPLEX_FORMAT_IN_TABLE"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:15611
msgid "If set, use tables for indentation of complex formats; default false."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:15612
#, no-wrap
msgid "CONTENTS_OUTPUT_LOCATION"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:15620
msgid ""
"If set to @samp{after_top}, output the contents at the end of the "
"@code{@@top} section.  If set to @samp{inline}, output the contents where "
"the @code{@@contents} and similar @@-commands are located.  If set to "
"@samp{separate_element} output the contents in separate elements, either at "
"the end of the document if not split, or in a separate file.  If set to "
"@samp{after_title} the tables of contents are output after the title; "
"default @samp{after_top}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:15621
#, no-wrap
msgid "CONVERT_TO_LATEX_IN_MATH"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:15626
msgid ""
"If set, try to convert any Texinfo @@-commands inside @code{@@math} and "
"@code{@@displaymath} to @LaTeX{}, before converting the @code{@@math} or "
"@code{@@displaymath} to HTML.  Default @code{undef}.  If undefined, set if "
"@code{HTML_MATH} is set."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:15627
#, no-wrap
msgid "COPIABLE_LINKS"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:15633
msgid ""
"If set, output copiable links for the definition commands (@pxref{Definition "
"Commands}) and table commands (@pxref{Two-column Tables}) where an index "
"entry is defined.  A link appears as a `@U{00B6}' sign that appears when you "
"hover the mouse pointer over the heading text."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:15634
#, no-wrap
msgid "DATE_IN_HEADER"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:15636
msgid "Put the document generation date in the header; off by default."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:15637
#, no-wrap
msgid "DEF_TABLE"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:15641
msgid ""
"If set, a @code{<table>} construction for @code{@@deffn} and similar "
"@@-commands is used (looking more like the @TeX{} output), instead of "
"definition lists; default false."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:15642
#, no-wrap
msgid "DEFAULT_RULE"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:15646
msgid ""
"Rule used between element, except before and after the top element, and "
"before special elements, and for footers and headers; default @code{<hr>}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:15647
#, no-wrap
msgid "DO_ABOUT"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:15652
msgid ""
"If set to 0 never do an About special element; if set to 1 always do an "
"About special element; default 0."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:15653
#, no-wrap
msgid "EXTERNAL_CROSSREF_SPLIT"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:15658
msgid ""
"For cross-references to other manuals, this determines if the other manual "
"is considered to be split or monolithic.  By default, it is set based on the "
"value of @code{SPLIT}.  @xref{HTML Xref}, and @pxref{HTML Xref "
"Configuration}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:15659
#, no-wrap
msgid "EXTERNAL_DIR"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:15663
msgid ""
"Base directory for external manuals; default none.  It is better to use the "
"general external cross-reference mechanism (@pxref{HTML Xref Configuration}) "
"than this variable."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:15664
#, no-wrap
msgid "EXTERNAL_CROSSREF_EXTENSION"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:15667
msgid ""
"File extension for cross-references to other manuals.  If unset, based on "
"@code{EXTENSION}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:15668
#, no-wrap
msgid "EXTRA_HEAD"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:15670
msgid "Additional text appearing within @code{<head>}; default unset."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:15671
#, no-wrap
msgid "FOOTNOTE_END_HEADER_LEVEL"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:15674
msgid ""
"Header formatting level used for the footnotes header with the `end' "
"footnotestyle; default @samp{4}.  @xref{Footnote Styles}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:15675
#, no-wrap
msgid "FOOTNOTE_SEPARATE_HEADER_LEVEL"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:15679
msgid ""
"Header formatting level used for the footnotes header with the `separate' "
"footnotestyle; default @samp{4}.  @xref{Footnote Styles}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:15680
#, no-wrap
msgid "FRAMES"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:15683
msgid ""
"If set, a file describing the frame layout is generated, together with a "
"file with the short table of contents; default false."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:15684
#, no-wrap
msgid "FRAMESET_DOCTYPE"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:15687
msgid "Same as DOCTYPE, but for the file containing the frame description."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:15688
#, no-wrap
msgid "HEADER_IN_TABLE"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:15691
msgid ""
"Use tables for header formatting rather than a simple @code{<div>} element; "
"default false."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:15692
#, no-wrap
msgid "HTML_MATH"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:15700
msgid ""
"Method to use to render @code{@@math}.  This can be unset, set to "
"@samp{mathjax} (@pxref{MathJax Customization Variables}), set to @samp{l2h}, "
"which uses @command{latex2html} (@pxref{@command{latex2html} Customization "
"Variables}), or set to @samp{t4h}, which uses @command{tex4ht} "
"(@pxref{@command{tex4ht} Customization Variables}).  In the default case, "
"setting @code{HTML_MATH} also sets @code{CONVERT_TO_LATEX_IN_MATH}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:15701
#, no-wrap
msgid "HTML_ROOT_ELEMENT_ATTRIBUTES"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:15704
msgid ""
"Use that string for the @code{<html>} HTML document root element.  Default "
"undefined."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:15705
#, no-wrap
msgid "HTMLXREF_FILE"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:15711
msgid ""
"Set the file name used for cross-references to other manuals.  If not "
"defined, @file{htmlxref.cnf} is used (@pxref{HTML Xref Configuration}).  Not "
"defined in the default case.  If @code{TEST} is set, @code{HTMLXREF_MODE} is "
"set to the default and @code{HTMLXREF_FILE} is not defined, information on "
"cross-references to other manuals is not used."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:15716
msgid ""
"If @code{HTMLXREF_MODE} is set to @samp{file} the file name is directly used "
"as the source of information, otherwise the file name is searched for in "
"directories, and all the files found are used (@pxref{HTML Xref "
"Configuration})."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:15717
#, no-wrap
msgid "HTMLXREF_MODE"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:15724
msgid ""
"How cross-references to other manuals information is determined.  If set to "
"@samp{none}, no information is used.  If set to @samp{file}, the information "
"is determined from a file path, @file{htmlxref.cnf} in the default case, or "
"the value of @code{HTMLXREF_FILE}.  If not defined (the default) or set to "
"any other value, search in directories and use all the files (@pxref{HTML "
"Xref Configuration})."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:15725
#, no-wrap
msgid "ICONS"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:15727
msgid "Use icons for the navigation panel; default false."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:15728
#, no-wrap
msgid "IMAGE_LINK_PREFIX"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:15731
msgid ""
"If set, the associated value is prepended to the image file links; default "
"unset."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:15732
#, no-wrap
msgid "INDEX_ENTRY_COLON"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:15735
msgid ""
"Symbol used between the index entry and the associated node or section; "
"default @samp{:}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:15736
#, no-wrap
msgid "INFO_JS_DIR"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:15744
msgid ""
"(Experimental.)  Add a JavaScript browsing interface to the manual.  The "
"value of the variable is the directory to place the code for this interface, "
"so you would run the program as e.g.@: @samp{texi2any --html -c "
"INFO_JS_DIR=js @var{manual}.texi} to place files in a @samp{js} directory "
"under the output.  This provides some of the functionality of the Info "
"browsers in a web browser, such as keyboard navigation and index lookup.  "
"This only works with non-split HTML output."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:15749
msgid ""
"The interface should provide an acceptable fallback in functionality if "
"JavaScript or web browser features are not available.  However, please be "
"cautious when using this option, in case you do make your documentation "
"harder to access for some of your users."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:15750
#, no-wrap
msgid "IGNORE_REF_TO_TOP_NODE_UP"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:15752
msgid "Ignore references to @code{TOP_NODE_UP}, the up node for the Top node."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:15753
#, no-wrap
msgid "INLINE_CSS_STYLE"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:15756
msgid ""
"Put CSS directly in HTML elements rather than at the beginning of the "
"output; default false."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:15757
#, no-wrap
msgid "JS_WEBLABELS"
msgstr ""

#. type: itemx
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:15758
#, no-wrap
msgid "JS_WEBLABELS_FILE"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:15763
msgid ""
"Specify how to use a @dfn{JavaScript license web labels} page to give "
"licensing information and source code for any JavaScript used in the HTML "
"files for the manual.  (See "
"@uref{https://www.gnu.org/licenses/javascript-labels.html})."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:15770
msgid ""
"With the value @samp{generate} (the default), generate a labels page at "
"@code{JS_WEBLABELS_FILE}, and link to it in the HTML output files.  Only do "
"this if actually referencing JavaScript files (either with @code{HTML_MATH} "
"set to @samp{mathjax}, or when using the experimental JS browsing interface "
"when @code{INFO_JS_DIR} is set).  With this setting, "
"@code{JS_WEBLABELS_FILE} must be a relative file name."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:15776
msgid ""
"With the value @samp{reference}, link to the labels file given by "
"@code{JS_WEBLABELS_FILE} in the output, and do not generate a labels file.  "
"This setting is useful if you separately maintain a single labels file for a "
"larger website that includes your manual."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:15778
msgid "With @samp{omit}, neither generate nor link to a labels file."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:15779
#, no-wrap
msgid "MAX_HEADER_LEVEL"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:15783
msgid ""
"Maximum header formatting level used (higher header formatting level numbers "
"correspond to lower sectioning levels); default @samp{4}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:15784
#, no-wrap
msgid "MENU_ENTRY_COLON"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:15787
msgid ""
"Symbol used between the menu entry and the description; default @samp{:}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:15788
#, no-wrap
msgid "MENU_SYMBOL"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:15793
msgid ""
"Symbol used in front of menu entries when node names are used for menu "
"entries formatting; default is undefined and set to @code{&bull;} if "
"@code{USE_NUMERIC_ENTITY} is not set, and to @code{&#8217;} if set."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:15794
#, no-wrap
msgid "MONOLITHIC"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:15797
msgid ""
"Output only one file including the table of contents.  Set by default, but "
"only relevant when the output is not split."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:15798
#, no-wrap
msgid "NO_CSS"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:15800
msgid "Do not use CSS; default false.  @xref{HTML CSS}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:15801
#, no-wrap
msgid "NO_CUSTOM_HTML_ATTRIBUTE"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:15803
msgid "Do not output HTML with custom attributes in elements; default false."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:15804
#, no-wrap
msgid "NO_NUMBER_FOOTNOTE_SYMBOL"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:15807
msgid ""
"Symbol used for footnotes if @code{NUMBER_FOOTNOTES} is false.  Default is "
"@code{*}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:15808
#, no-wrap
msgid "NODE_NAME_IN_INDEX"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:15811
msgid ""
"If true, use node names in index entries, otherwise prefer section names.  "
"If undefined, use @code{USE_NODES} value in HTML.  Default is undefined."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:15812
#, no-wrap
msgid "PRE_BODY_CLOSE"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:15815
msgid ""
"If set, the given text will appear at the footer of each HTML file; default "
"unset."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:15816
#, no-wrap
msgid "PROGRAM_NAME_IN_ABOUT"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:15820
msgid ""
"Used when an About element is output.  If set, output the program name and "
"miscellaneous related information in About special element; default false."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:15821
#, no-wrap
msgid "PROGRAM_NAME_IN_FOOTER"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:15824
msgid ""
"If set, output the program name and miscellaneous related information in the "
"page footers; default false."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:15825
#, no-wrap
msgid "SECTION_NAME_IN_TITLE"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:15829
msgid ""
"If set, when output is split, use the argument of the chapter structuring "
"command (e.g., @code{@@chapter} or @code{@@section})  in the @code{<title>} "
"instead of the argument to @code{@@node}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:15830
#, no-wrap
msgid "SHORT_TOC_LINK_TO_TOC"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:15834
msgid ""
"If set, the cross-references in the Short table of contents links to the "
"corresponding Table of Contents entries, if a Table of Contents is output; "
"default true."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:15835
#, no-wrap
msgid "SHOW_BUILTIN_CSS_RULES"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:15837
msgid "Output the built-in default CSS rules on the standard output and exit."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:15838
#, no-wrap
msgid "SHOW_TITLE"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:15842
msgid ""
"If set, output the title at the beginning of the document; default "
"@samp{undef}.  If set to @samp{undef}, setting @code{NO_TOP_NODE_OUTPUT} "
"also sets @code{SHOW_TITLE} for HTML."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:15843
#, no-wrap
msgid "SIMPLE_MENU"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:15847
msgid ""
"If set, use a simple preformatted style for the menu, instead of breaking "
"down the different parts of the menu; default false.  @xref{Menu Parts}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:15848
#, no-wrap
msgid "TOC_LINKS"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:15851
msgid "If set, links from headings to toc entries are created; default false."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:15852
#, no-wrap
msgid "TOP_FILE"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:15857
msgid ""
"This file name may be used for the top-level file.  The extension is set "
"appropriately, if necessary.  This is used to override the default, and is, "
"in general, only taken into account when output is split, and for HTML@."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:15858
#, no-wrap
msgid "TOP_NODE_FILE_TARGET"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:15861
msgid ""
"File name used for the Top node in cross-references; default is "
"@code{index.html}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:15862
#, no-wrap
msgid "TOP_NODE_UP_URL"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:15869
msgid ""
"A URL used for Top node up references; the default is @code{undef}, in that "
"case no Top node Up reference is generated.  For more about the Top node "
"pointers, @pxref{First Node}.  For overriding the Up pointer name in case "
"@code{TOP_NODE_UP_URL} is set and for other formats, see @code{TOP_NODE_UP} "
"in @ref{Other Customization Variables}."
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:15870
#, no-wrap
msgid "@code{accesskey} @subentry customization variable for"
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:15871
#, no-wrap
msgid "USE_ACCESSKEY"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:15873
msgid "Use @code{accesskey} in cross-references; default true."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:15874
#, no-wrap
msgid "USE_ISO"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:15878
msgid ""
"Use entities for doubled single-quote characters (@pxref{Inserting Quotation "
"Marks}), and @samp{---} and @samp{--} (@pxref{Conventions}); default true."
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:15879
#, no-wrap
msgid "@code{<link>} HTML tag, in @code{<head>}"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:15880
#, no-wrap
msgid "@code{<head>} HTML tag, and @code{<link>}"
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:15881
#, no-wrap
msgid "USE_LINKS"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:15884
msgid ""
"Generate @code{<link>} elements in the HTML @code{<head>} output; default "
"true."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:15885
#, no-wrap
msgid "USE_NEXT_HEADING_FOR_LONE_NODE"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:15891
msgid ""
"If set, a node not associated to a sectioning command but followed by a "
"heading command not usually associated to node such as @code{@@heading} "
"before other formatted contents do not have its name output as a heading, "
"under the assumption that the command found provides the heading.  Default "
"true."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:15892
#, no-wrap
msgid "USE_NODE_DIRECTIONS"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:15900
msgid ""
"If true, use nodes to determine where next, up and prev link to in node "
"headers.  If false, use sections.  If undefined, use @code{USE_NODES} "
"value.  Default is undefined.  Note that this setting does not determine the "
"link string only where the links points to, see @ref{Three Arguments, , "
"xrefautomaticsectiontitle} for the link string customization.  If nodes and "
"sections are systematically associated, this customization has no practical "
"effect."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:15901
#, no-wrap
msgid "USE_REL_REV"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:15903
msgid "Use @code{rel} in cross-references; default true."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:15904
#, no-wrap
msgid "USE_TITLEPAGE_FOR_TITLE"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:15907
msgid ""
"Use the full @code{@@titlepage} as the title, not a simple title string; "
"default true.  Only relevant if @code{SHOW_TITLE} is set."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:15908
#, no-wrap
msgid "USE_XML_SYNTAX"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:15910
msgid "Use XML/XHTML compatible syntax."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:15911
#, no-wrap
msgid "VERTICAL_HEAD_NAVIGATION"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:15913
msgid "If set, a vertical navigation panel is used; default false."
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:15914
#, no-wrap
msgid "Navigation panel, bottom of page"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:15915
#, no-wrap
msgid "Navigation footer"
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:15916
#, no-wrap
msgid "WORDS_IN_PAGE"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:15922
msgid ""
"When output is split by nodes, specifies the approximate minimum page length "
"at which a navigation panel is placed at the bottom of a page.  To avoid "
"ever having the navigation buttons at the bottom of a page, set this to a "
"sufficiently large number.  The default is 300."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:15923
#, no-wrap
msgid "XREF_USE_FLOAT_LABEL"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:15927
msgid ""
"If set, for the float name in cross-references, use the float label instead "
"of the type followed by the float number (@pxref{@code{@@float}}).  The "
"default is off."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:15928
#, no-wrap
msgid "XREF_USE_NODE_NAME_ARG"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:15937
msgid ""
"Only relevant for cross-reference commands with no cross reference name "
"(second argument).  If set to@tie{}1, use the node name (first) argument in "
"cross-reference @@-commands for the text displayed as the hyperlink.  If set "
"to@tie{}0, use the node name if @code{USE_NODES} is set, otherwise the "
"section name.  If set to @samp{undef}, use the first argument in "
"preformatted environments, otherwise use the node name or section name "
"depending on @code{USE_NODES}.  The default is @samp{undef}."
msgstr ""

#. type: subsection
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:15941
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:15942
#, no-wrap
msgid "MathJax Customization Variables"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:15947
msgid ""
"This table lists the customization variables which can be used when MathJax "
"is being used, which will be the case when @code{HTML_MATH} is set to "
"@samp{mathjax}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:15949
#, no-wrap
msgid "MATHJAX_SCRIPT"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:15954
msgid ""
"URL of the MathJax component file (e.g.@: @file{tex-svg.js}) you are using.  "
"@command{texi2any} provides a default value for this variable, but you are "
"encouraged to host this file yourself on your website so that you are not "
"dependent on others' hosting."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:15955
#, no-wrap
msgid "MATHJAX_SOURCE"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:15962
msgid ""
"A URL of the full source code in its preferred form for modification, or "
"instructions for obtaining such source code, for the component file named by "
"@code{MATHJAX_SCRIPT}.  `Preferred form for modification' means that this "
"should not be in a `minified' form.  Used in the license labels page "
"(@pxref{HTML Customization Variables}, under @code{JS_WEBLABELS})."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:15968
msgid ""
"Again, @command{texi2any} provides a default value for this variable, but "
"you are encouraged to host the source code for MathJax and its dependencies "
"yourself.  This is in order to make the source code available reliably, and "
"to reduce you and your users' dependence on others' distribution systems."
msgstr ""

#. type: subsection
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:15971
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:15972
#, no-wrap
msgid "@command{latex2html} Customization Variables"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:15979
msgid ""
"This table lists the customization variables which can be used when "
"@command{latex2html} is being used to convert @code{@@math}, "
"@code{@@displaymath}, @code{@@latex} and @code{@@tex} sections for HTML@.  "
"These customization variables are relevant only if @code{HTML_MATH} is set "
"to @samp{l2h}."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:15983
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:16025
msgid ""
"To actually convert @code{@@tex} sections, @option{--iftex} should be used, "
"and to actually convert @code{@@latex} sections, @option{--iflatex} should "
"be used."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:15985
#, no-wrap
msgid "L2H_CLEAN"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:15988
msgid ""
"If set, the intermediate files generated in relation with "
"@command{latex2html} are removed; default true."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:15989
#, no-wrap
msgid "L2H_FILE"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:15992
msgid ""
"If set, the given file is used as @command{latex2html}'s init file; default "
"unset."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:15993
#, no-wrap
msgid "L2H_HTML_VERSION"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:15995
msgid "The HTML version used in the @command{latex2html} call; default unset."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:15996
#, no-wrap
msgid "L2H_L2H"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:15998
msgid ""
"The program invoked as @command{latex2html}; default is @code{latex2html}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:15999
#, no-wrap
msgid "L2H_SKIP"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:16005
msgid ""
"If set to a true value, the actual call to @command{latex2html} is skipped; "
"previously generated content is reused instead.  If set to 0, the cache is "
"not used at all.  If set to @samp{undef}, the cache is used for as many "
"@TeX{} fragments as possible and for any remaining the command is run.  The "
"default is @samp{undef}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:16006
#, no-wrap
msgid "L2H_TMP"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:16011
msgid ""
"Set the directory used for temporary files.  None of the file name "
"components in this directory name may start with @samp{.}; otherwise, "
"@command{latex2html} will fail (because of @command{dvips}).  The default is "
"the empty string, which means the current directory."
msgstr ""

#. type: subsection
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:16014
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:16015
#, no-wrap
msgid "@command{tex4ht} Customization Variables"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:16021
msgid ""
"This table lists the customization variables which can be used when "
"@command{tex4ht} is being used to convert @code{@@math}, "
"@code{@@displaymath}, @code{@@tex} and @code{@@latex} sections for HTML@.  "
"These customization variables are relevant only if @code{HTML_MATH} is set "
"to @samp{t4h}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:16027
#, no-wrap
msgid "T4H_LATEX_CONVERSION"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:16031
msgid ""
"If set, the conversion type used for @code{@@latex} sections.  Possibilities "
"are @samp{latex}, @samp{tex} and @samp{texi}.  Set to @samp{latex} if not "
"defined."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:16032
#, no-wrap
msgid "T4H_MATH_CONVERSION"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:16036
msgid ""
"If set, the conversion type used for @code{@@math} and @code{@@displymath}.  "
"Possibilities are @samp{latex}, @samp{tex} and @samp{texi}.  Set to "
"@samp{tex} if not defined."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:16037
#, no-wrap
msgid "T4H_TEX_CONVERSION"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:16041
msgid ""
"If set, the conversion type used for @code{@@tex} sections.  Possibilities "
"are @samp{latex}, @samp{tex} and @samp{texi}.  Set to @samp{tex} if not "
"defined."
msgstr ""

#. type: subsection
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:16044
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:16045
#, no-wrap
msgid "@LaTeX{} Customization Variables"
msgstr ""

#. type: quotation
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:16048
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:17866
#, no-wrap
msgid "warning"
msgstr ""

#. type: quotation
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:16051
msgid ""
"@LaTeX{} output customization is experimental.  Nothing is decided, "
"everything can change, and we would welcome any feedback."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:16056
msgid ""
"This table gives the customization variables which apply to @LaTeX{} output "
"only."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:16058
#, no-wrap
msgid "CLASS_BEGIN_USEPACKAGE"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:16063
msgid ""
"If set, the corresponding text will replace the @LaTeX{} "
"@code{\\documentclass}, package imports that are always output and are "
"output right after @code{\\documentclass}, and package imports that depend "
"on the document encoding setting the input and font encoding "
"(@code{inputenc} and @code{fontenc})."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:16065
msgid "The text replaced is along:"
msgstr ""

#. type: example
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:16076
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"\\documentclass@{book@}\n"
"\\usepackage@{amsfonts@}\n"
"\\usepackage@{amsmath@}\n"
"\\usepackage[gen]@{eurosym@}\n"
"\\usepackage@{textcomp@}\n"
"\\usepackage@{graphicx@}\n"
"\\usepackage@{etoolbox@}\n"
"\\usepackage@{titleps@}\n"
"\\usepackage[utf8]@{inputenc@}\n"
"\\usepackage[T1]@{fontenc@}\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:16078
#, no-wrap
msgid "END_USEPACKAGE"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:16083
msgid ""
"If set, the corresponding text will replace the package imports that depend "
"on the Texinfo commands used, and the last packages imports that are always "
"output and output after all the other packages imports.  The last package "
"imports corresponds to @samp{\\usepackage[hidelinks]@{hyperref@}}."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:16087
msgid ""
"Here is an example of the corresponding text for a document with indices, "
"@code{@@need}, @code{@@multitable}, definition commands, @code{@@cartouche}, "
"lists, and @code{@@float}:"
msgstr ""

#. type: example
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:16098
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"\\usepackage@{imakeidx@}\n"
"\\usepackage@{needspace@}\n"
"\\usepackage@{array@}\n"
"\\usepackage@{embrac@}\n"
"\\usepackage@{expl3@}\n"
"\\usepackage@{tabularx@}\n"
"\\usepackage[framemethod=tikz]@{mdframed@}\n"
"\\usepackage@{enumitem@}\n"
"\\usepackage@{float@}\n"
"\\usepackage[hidelinks]@{hyperref@}\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: subsection
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:16102
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:16103
#, no-wrap
msgid "Other Customization Variables"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:16108
msgid ""
"This table gives the remaining customization variables, which apply to "
"multiple formats, or affect global behavior, or otherwise don't fit into the "
"categories of the previous sections."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:16110
#, no-wrap
msgid "ASCII_DASHES_AND_QUOTES"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:16116
msgid ""
"For Info output, when set, use plain ASCII characters to represent quotation "
"marks, hyphens and dashes when these are given in the Texinfo source as "
"@samp{-}, @samp{--}, @samp{---}, @samp{`}, @samp{``}, @samp{'}, and "
"@samp{''}, rather than UTF-8 directional quotation marks, en dashes, vel "
"sim.  On by default."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:16117
#, no-wrap
msgid "ASCII_GLYPH"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:16122
msgid ""
"For Info output, use ASCII output for glyph commands such as the copyright "
"sign (@command{@@copyright@{@}}, becoming @samp{(C)}), and the bullet symbol "
"(@command{@@bullet@{@}}, becoming @samp{*}), rather than other Unicode "
"sequences.  Off by default."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:16123
#, no-wrap
msgid "ASCII_PUNCTUATION"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:16128
msgid ""
"Avoid any unncessary or gratuitious non-ASCII, UTF-8 sequences in the "
"output.  Implies both @code{ASCII_DASHES_AND_QUOTES} and @code{ASCII_GLYPH} "
"and additionally affects the output of commands such as @code{@@samp} which "
"output quotation marks."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:16129
#, no-wrap
msgid "AUTO_MENU_DESCRIPTION_ALIGN_COLUMN"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:16134
msgid ""
"For Info output, column at which to start a menu entry description provided "
"by @code{@@nodedescription} or @code{@@nodedescriptionblock}.  Undefined by "
"default, in which case 45% of the fill column value is used (@pxref{Invoking "
"@command{texi2any}})."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:16135
#, no-wrap
msgid "AUTO_MENU_MAX_WIDTH"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:16140
msgid ""
"Maximum number of columns in a menu entry line in Info when adding a "
"description from @code{@@nodedescription} or @code{@@nodedescriptionblock}.  "
"Undefined by default, in which case 10% more than the fill column value is "
"used (@pxref{Invoking @command{texi2any}})."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:16141
#, no-wrap
msgid "CHECK_MISSING_MENU_ENTRY"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:16145
msgid ""
"When a @code{@@menu} block occurs in a node, check if there is a menu entry "
"for all subordinate nodes in the document sectioning structure.  On by "
"default."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:16146
#, no-wrap
msgid "CHECK_NORMAL_MENU_STRUCTURE"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:16151
msgid ""
"Warn if the node pointers (either explicitly or automatically set)  are not "
"consistent with the order of node menu entries.  This is a more thorough "
"structure check than that provided by @code{CHECK_MISSING_MENU_ENTRY}.  Off "
"by default."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:16152
#, no-wrap
msgid "CLOSE_QUOTE_SYMBOL"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:16159
msgid ""
"When a closing quote is needed, e.g. for @code{@@samp} output, use this "
"character; default @code{&#8217;} in DocBook.  Undefined in the default case "
"in HTML and set to @code{&rsquo;} if @code{USE_NUMERIC_ENTITY} is not set, "
"to @code{&#8217;} if set, and to a quote character if "
"@code{OUTPUT_CHARACTERS} is set and the output encoding includes that "
"character."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:16162
msgid ""
"The default for Info is set the same as for @code{OPEN_QUOTE_SYMBOL}, except "
"that the Unicode code is a closing quote (see below)."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:16163
#, no-wrap
msgid "CLOSE_DOUBLE_QUOTE_SYMBOL"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:16168
msgid ""
"When a closing double quote is needed, for @samp{@@dfn} in Info, use this "
"character.  The default for Info is set the same as for "
"@code{OPEN_DOUBLE_QUOTE_SYMBOL}, except that the Unicode code is a closing "
"double quote (see below)."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:16169
#, no-wrap
msgid "COMMAND_LINE_ENCODING"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:16173
msgid ""
"Encoding used to decode command-line arguments.  Default is based on the "
"locale encoding.  This may affect file names inserted into output files or "
"error messages printed by the program."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:16176
msgid ""
"Note that some file and directory names from the command line may not be "
"decoded immediately, and may not be decoded at all."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:16177
#, no-wrap
msgid "CPP_LINE_DIRECTIVES"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:16180
msgid ""
"Recognize @code{#line} directives in a ``preprocessing'' pass "
"(@pxref{External Macro Processors}); on by default."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:16181
#, no-wrap
msgid "DEBUG"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:16186
msgid "If set, debugging output is generated; default is off (zero)."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:16187
#, no-wrap
msgid "DOC_ENCODING_FOR_INPUT_FILE_NAME"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:16193
msgid ""
"If set, use the input Texinfo document encoding information for the encoding "
"of input file names, such as file names specified as @code{@@include} or "
"@code{@@verbatiminclude} arguments.  If unset, use the locale encoding "
"instead.  Default is set, except on MS-Windows where the locale encoding is "
"used by default."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:16197
msgid ""
"Note that this is for file names only; the default encoding or "
"@code{@@documentencoding} is always used for the encoding of file content "
"(@pxref{@code{@@documentencoding}})."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:16199
msgid "The @code{INPUT_FILE_NAME_ENCODING} variable overrides this variable."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:16200
#, no-wrap
msgid "DOC_ENCODING_FOR_OUTPUT_FILE_NAME"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:16205
msgid ""
"If set, use the input Texinfo document encoding information for the encoding "
"of output file names, such as files specified with @option{--output}.  If "
"unset, use the locale encoding instead.  Default is unset, so files names "
"are encoded using the current locale."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:16208
msgid ""
"Note that this is for file names only; @code{OUTPUT_ENCODING_NAME} is used "
"for the encoding of file content."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:16210
msgid "The @code{OUTPUT_FILE_NAME_ENCODING} variable overrides this variable."
msgstr ""

#. type: vindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:16211
#, no-wrap
msgid "SystemLiteral"
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:16212
#, no-wrap
msgid "DOCTYPE"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:16218
msgid ""
"For DocBook, HTML, XML@.  Specifies the @code{SystemLiteral}, the entity's "
"system identifier.  This is a URI which may be used to retrieve the entity, "
"and identifies the canonical DTD for the document.  The default value is "
"different for each of HTML, DocBook and XML."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:16219
#, no-wrap
msgid "DUMP_TEXI"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:16223
msgid ""
"For debugging.  If set, no conversion is done, only parsing and macro "
"expansion.  If the option @option{--macro-expand} is set, the Texinfo source "
"is also expanded to the corresponding file.  Default false."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:16224
#, no-wrap
msgid "DUMP_TREE"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:16227
msgid ""
"For debugging.  If set, the tree constructed upon parsing a Texinfo document "
"is output to standard error; default false."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:16228
#, no-wrap
msgid "EPUB_CREATE_CONTAINER_FILE"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:16231
msgid ""
"If set to 0, do not generate the EPUB output file.  Default is set to 1."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:16232
#, no-wrap
msgid "EPUB_KEEP_CONTAINER_FOLDER"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:16237
msgid ""
"If set, keep the directory containing the directories and files needed for "
"EPUB.  The EPUB output file is a ZIP archive of this directory.  Default is "
"not defined.  Set if not defined and @code{TEST} or @code{DEBUG} is set. "
"@xref{EPUB Output File and Directory}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:16238
#, no-wrap
msgid "EXTENSION"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:16241
msgid ""
"The extension added to the output file name.  The default is different for "
"each output format."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:16242
#, no-wrap
msgid "FORMAT_MENU"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:16248
msgid ""
"If set to @samp{menu}, output Texinfo menus.  This is the default for Info.  "
"@samp{sectiontoc} is the default setting for HTML, where instead of the "
"contents of @code{@@menu} blocks being output, a list of subordinate "
"sections is output in each node.  If set to @samp{nomenu}, do not output "
"menus."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:16251
msgid ""
"This variable is set to @samp{nomenu} when generating DocBook, or when "
"@option{--no-headers} is specified."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:16254
#, no-wrap
msgid "HANDLER_FATAL_ERROR_LEVEL"
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:16261
#, no-wrap
msgid "HIGHLIGHT_SYNTAX"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:16269
msgid ""
"If set, @code{@@example} blocks with language information as first argument "
"are highlighted in the HTML output.  It is also possible to specify a "
"default for the language with @code{HIGHLIGHT_SYNTAX_DEFAULT_LANGUAGE}.  "
"Syntax highlighting requires an external program to generate the highlighted "
"HTML.  The @code{HIGHLIGHT_SYNTAX} value allows to select a specific "
"program.  The possibilities are @code{highlight}, @code{pygments}, any other "
"value standing for @code{source-highlight} (@pxref{Syntax Highlighting})."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:16270
#, no-wrap
msgid "HIGHLIGHT_SYNTAX_DEFAULT_LANGUAGE"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:16273
msgid ""
"The default language used for syntax highlighting when there is no language "
"information."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:16274
#, no-wrap
msgid "IGNORE_SPACE_AFTER_BRACED_COMMAND_NAME"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:16277
msgid ""
"If set, spaces are ignored after an @@-command that takes braces.  Default "
"true, matching the @TeX{} behavior."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:16278
#, no-wrap
msgid "INDEX_SPECIAL_CHARS_WARNING"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:16283
msgid ""
"If set, warn about @samp{:} in index entry, as not all Info readers may be "
"able to process these.  For Info and plaintext only.  Default false, because "
"parsing problems there don't prevent navigation; readers can still "
"relatively easily find their way to the node in question."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:16284
#, no-wrap
msgid "INFO_SPECIAL_CHARS_QUOTE"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:16290
msgid ""
"If set, whenever there are problematic characters for Info output in places "
"such as node names or menu items, surround the part of the construct where "
"they appear with quoting characters, as described in @ref{Info Format "
"Specification}.  Default is set for Info and unset for plaintext.  "
"@xref{Node Line Requirements}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:16291
#, no-wrap
msgid "INFO_SPECIAL_CHARS_WARNING"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:16297
msgid ""
"If set, warn about problematic constructs for Info output (such as the "
"string @samp{::}) in node names, menu items, and cross-references.  If not "
"defined, set unless @code{INFO_SPECIAL_CHARS_QUOTE} is set.  Default is set "
"for Info and not defined for plaintext. Similar warnings in index entries "
"are covered by @code{INDEX_SPECIAL_CHARS_WARNING}."
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:16298
#, no-wrap
msgid "Encoding @subentry input file names"
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:16299
#, no-wrap
msgid "INPUT_FILE_NAME_ENCODING"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:16306
msgid ""
"Encoding used for input file names.  This variable overrides any encoding "
"from the document or current locale.  Normally, you do not need to set this "
"variable, but it can be used if file names are in a certain character "
"encoding on a filesystem.  An alternative is to set "
"@code{DOC_ENCODING_FOR_INPUT_FILE_NAME} to @samp{0} to use the locale "
"encoding.  See also @code{OUTPUT_FILE_NAME_ENCODING}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:16307
#, no-wrap
msgid "LOCALE_ENCODING"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:16310
msgid ""
"Locale encoding obtained from the system.  You should not need to explicitly "
"set this variable."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:16311
#, no-wrap
msgid "MAX_MACRO_CALL_NESTING"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:16315
msgid ""
"The maximal number of recursive calls of @@-commands defined through "
"@code{@@rmacro}; default 100000.  The purpose of this variable is to avoid "
"infinite recursions."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:16316
#, no-wrap
msgid "MESSAGE_ENCODING"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:16319
msgid ""
"Encoding used to encode messages output by @command{texi2any}.  Default is "
"based on the locale encoding."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:16323
msgid ""
"It is also used for command-line argument passed to commands called from "
"@command{texi2any}.  For example, @command{latex2html} will be called from "
"@command{texi2any} if @code{HTML_MATH} is set to @samp{l2h}."
msgstr ""

#. type: code{#1}
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:16324
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:16331
#, no-wrap
msgid "NO_TOP_NODE_OUTPUT"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:16331
msgid ""
"If set do not output the Top node content.  The Top node is still parsed, "
"but the content is discarded.  Not set in the default case for HTML@.  Set "
"in the default case for EPUB@.  If @code{SHOW_TITLE} is @samp{undef}, "
"setting @code{NO_TOP_NODE_OUTPUT} also sets @code{SHOW_TITLE} for HTML."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:16337
msgid ""
"Setting @code{NO_TOP_NODE_OUTPUT}, which removes the Top node and adds a "
"title page corresponds more to the formatting of a book.  Setting "
"@code{NO_TOP_NODE_OUTPUT} to false, with @code{SHOW_TITLE} remaining "
"@samp{undef}, and false, corresponds more to a document setup for browsing, "
"with a direct access to the information at the Top node."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:16344
msgid ""
"For DocBook, @code{NO_TOP_NODE_OUTPUT} is set to true.  Setting "
"@code{NO_TOP_NODE_OUTPUT} to false causes the Top node content to be "
"output.  It is not recommended to output the Top node in DocBook as the "
"title and copying informations are always output.  This option is kept for "
"DocBook for compatibility, as before 2022 the Top node was output in "
"DocBook.  It could be removed in the future."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:16345
#, no-wrap
msgid "NO_USE_SETFILENAME"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:16349
msgid ""
"If set, do not use @code{@@setfilename} to set the document name; instead, "
"base the output document name only on the input file name.  The default is "
"false."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:16350
#, no-wrap
msgid "NODE_NAME_IN_MENU"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:16353
msgid ""
"If set, use node names in menu entries, otherwise prefer section names; "
"default true."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:16354
#, no-wrap
msgid "OPEN_QUOTE_SYMBOL"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:16361
msgid ""
"When an opening quote is needed, e.g., for @samp{@@samp} output, use the "
"specified character; default @code{&#8216;} for DocBook.  Undefined in the "
"default case in HTML and set to @code{&lsquo;} if @code{USE_NUMERIC_ENTITY} "
"is not set, to @code{&#8217;} if set, and to a quote character if "
"@code{OUTPUT_CHARACTERS} is set and the output encoding includes that "
"character."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:16367
msgid ""
"For Info, the default depends on the enabled document encoding.  If "
"@option{--disable-encoding} is set or the document encoding is not UTF-8, "
"@samp{'} is used.  This character usually appears as an undirected single "
"quote on modern systems.  Otherwise, the Info output uses a Unicode left "
"quote."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:16368
#, no-wrap
msgid "OPEN_DOUBLE_QUOTE_SYMBOL"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:16373
msgid ""
"When an opening double quote is needed, for @samp{@@dfn} output in Info, use "
"the specified character.  If @option{--disable-encoding} is set or the "
"document encoding is not UTF-8, @samp{\"} is used.  Otherwise, the Info "
"output uses a Unicode left double quote."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:16374
#, no-wrap
msgid "OUTPUT_CHARACTERS"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:16380
msgid ""
"If not set, the default, output accented and special characters in HTML, XML "
"and DocBook using XML entities, and in @LaTeX{} using macros.  If set, "
"output accented characters in HTML, XML, DocBook and @LaTeX{} output and "
"special characters in HTML and @LaTeX{} output based on the document "
"encoding.  @xref{@code{@@documentencoding}}, and @ref{Inserting Accents}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:16381
#, no-wrap
msgid "OUTPUT_ENCODING_NAME"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:16388
msgid ""
"Normalized encoding name used for output files.  Should be a usable charset "
"name in HTML, typically one of the preferred IANA encoding names.  By "
"default, if an input encoding is set (typically through "
"@code{@@documentencoding}), this information is used to set the output "
"encoding name, otherwise the output encoding is based on the default "
"encoding.  @xref{@code{@@documentencoding}}."
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:16389
#, no-wrap
msgid "Encoding @subentry output file names"
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:16390
#, no-wrap
msgid "OUTPUT_FILE_NAME_ENCODING"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:16393
msgid ""
"Encoding used for output file names.  This variable overrides any encoding "
"from the document or current locale."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:16397
msgid ""
"Normally, you do not need to set this variable, but it can be used if file "
"names should be created in a certain character encoding on a filesystem.  "
"See also @code{INPUT_FILE_NAME_ENCODING}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:16398
#, no-wrap
msgid "PACKAGE"
msgstr ""

#. type: itemx
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:16399
#, no-wrap
msgid "PACKAGE_VERSION"
msgstr ""

#. type: itemx
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:16400
#, no-wrap
msgid "PACKAGE_AND_VERSION"
msgstr ""

#. type: itemx
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:16401
#, no-wrap
msgid "PACKAGE_URL"
msgstr ""

#. type: itemx
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:16402
#, no-wrap
msgid "PACKAGE_NAME"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:16407
msgid ""
"The implementation's short package name, package version, package name and "
"version concatenated, package URL@:, and full package name, respectively.  "
"By default, these variables are all set through Autoconf, Automake, and "
"@code{configure}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:16408
#, no-wrap
msgid "PREFIX"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:16414
msgid ""
"The output file prefix, which is prepended to some output file names.  By "
"default it is set by @code{@@setfilename} or from the input file "
"(@pxref{Setting the Output File Name}).  How this value is used depends on "
"the value of other customization variables or command line options, such as "
"whether the output is split.  The default is unset."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:16415
#, no-wrap
msgid "PROGRAM"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:16418
msgid ""
"Name of the program used.  By default, it is set to the name of the program "
"launched, with a trailing @samp{.pl} removed."
msgstr ""

#. type: anchor{#1}
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:16419
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:20267
#, no-wrap
msgid "texi-elements-by-size"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:16420
#, no-wrap
msgid "Longest nodes, finding"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:16421
#, no-wrap
msgid "Sorting nodes by size"
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:16422
#, no-wrap
msgid "SORT_ELEMENT_COUNT"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:16429
msgid ""
"If set, the name of a file to which a list of elements (nodes or sections, "
"depending on the output format) is dumped, sorted by the number of lines "
"they contain after removal of @@-commands; default unset.  This is used by "
"the program @code{texi-elements-by-size} in the @file{util/} directory of "
"the Texinfo source distribution (@pxref{texi-elements-by-size})."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:16430
#, no-wrap
msgid "SORT_ELEMENT_COUNT_WORDS"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:16433
msgid ""
"When dumping the elements-by-size file (see preceding item), use word counts "
"instead of line counts; default false."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:16434
#, no-wrap
msgid "TEST"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:16439
msgid ""
"If set to true, some variables which are normally dynamically generated anew "
"for each run (date, program name, version) are set to fixed and given "
"values.  This is useful to compare the output to a reference file, as is "
"done for the tests.  The default is false."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:16440
#, no-wrap
msgid "TEXI2DVI"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:16443
msgid ""
"Name of the command used to produce PostScript, PDF, and DVI; default "
"@samp{texi2dvi}.  @xref{@command{texi2any} Printed Output}."
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:16444
#, no-wrap
msgid "compatibility, with @command{texi2html}"
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:16445
#, no-wrap
msgid "TEXI2HTML"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:16448
msgid ""
"Generate HTML and try to be as compatible as possible with "
"@command{texi2html}; default false."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:16449
#, no-wrap
msgid "TEXINFO_DTD_VERSION"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:16452
msgid ""
"For XML@.  Version of the DTD used in the XML output preamble.  The default "
"is set based on a variable in @file{configure.ac}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:16453
#, no-wrap
msgid "TEXTCONTENT_COMMENT"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:16457
msgid ""
"For stripped text content output (i.e., when @code{TEXINFO_OUTPUT_FORMAT} is "
"set to @code{textcontent}).  If set, also output comments.  Default false."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:16458
#, no-wrap
msgid "TOP_NODE_UP"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:16464
msgid ""
"Up node for the Top node; default @samp{(dir)}.  This node name is supposed "
"to be already formatted for the output format.  In HTML can be used in "
"attribute, so should not contain any element.  Used for HTML output only if "
"@code{TOP_NODE_UP_URL} is set to override the URL@:, see "
"@code{TOP_NODE_UP_URL} in @ref{HTML Customization Variables}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:16465
#, no-wrap
msgid "TREE_TRANSFORMATIONS"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:16470
msgid ""
"The associated value is a comma separated list of transformations that can "
"be applied to the Texinfo tree prior to outputting the result.  If more than "
"one is specified, the ordering is irrelevant; each is always applied at the "
"necessary point during processing."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:16475
msgid ""
"By default, the tree transformations @samp{move_index_entries_after_items} "
"and @samp{relate_index_entries_to_table_entries} are executed for HTML and "
"DocBook output.  Here's an example of updating the master menu in a document:"
msgstr ""

#. type: example
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:16482
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"texi2any \\\n"
"  -c TREE_TRANSFORMATIONS=regenerate_master_menu \\\n"
"  -c TEXINFO_OUTPUT_FORMAT=plaintexinfo \\\n"
"  mydoc.texi \\\n"
"  -o /tmp/out\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:16488
msgid ""
"Texinfo macros and conditionals, it's necessary to remove any such "
"differences before installing the updates in the original document.  This "
"may be remedied in a future release.)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:16492
msgid ""
"The following transformations are currently supported (many are used in the "
"@code{pod2texi} utility distributed with Texinfo; @pxref{Invoking "
"@command{pod2texi}}):"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:16494
msgid "@ftable @samp"
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:16494
#, no-wrap
msgid "complete_tree_nodes_menus"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:16497
msgid ""
"Add menu entries or whole menus for nodes associated with sections of any "
"level, based on the sectioning tree."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:16498
#, no-wrap
msgid "complete_tree_nodes_missing_menu"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:16501
msgid ""
"Add whole menus for nodes associated with sections without menu.  The menus "
"are based on the sectioning tree."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:16502
#, no-wrap
msgid "fill_gaps_in_sectioning"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:16506
msgid ""
"Adds empty @code{@@unnumbered...} sections in a tree to fill gaps in "
"sectioning.  For example, an @code{@@unnumberedsec} will be inserted if a "
"@code{@@chapter} is followed by a @code{@@subsection}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:16507
#, no-wrap
msgid "insert_nodes_for_sectioning_commands"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:16509
msgid "Insert nodes for sectioning commands lacking a corresponding node."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:16510
#, no-wrap
msgid "move_index_entries_after_items"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:16515
msgid ""
"In @code{@@enumerate} and @code{@@itemize}, move index entries appearing "
"just before an @code{@@item} to just after the @code{@@item}.  Comment lines "
"between index entries are moved too.  As mentioned, this is always done for "
"HTML and DocBook output."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:16516
#, no-wrap
msgid "regenerate_master_menu"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:16520
msgid ""
"Update the Top node master menu, either replacing the (first)  "
"@code{@@detailmenu} in the Top node menu, or creating it at the end of the "
"Top node menu."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:16521
#, no-wrap
msgid "relate_index_entries_to_table_entries"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:16526
msgid ""
"In @code{@@table}, @code{@@vtable} and @code{@@ftable}, reassociate the "
"index entry information from an index @@-command appearing right after an "
"@code{@@item} line with the first element of the @code{@@item}.  Remove the "
"index @@-command from the tree."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:16527
#, no-wrap
msgid "simple_menu"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:16531
msgid ""
"Mostly the same as @code{SIMPLE_MENU}: use a simple preformatted style for "
"the menu.  It differs from setting @code{SIMPLE_MENU} in that "
"@code{SIMPLE_MENU} only has an effect in HTML output."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:16534
#, no-wrap
msgid "USE_NODES"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:16538
msgid ""
"Preferentially use nodes to decide where elements are separated.  If set to "
"false, preferentially use sectioning to decide where elements are "
"separated.  The default is true."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:16539
#, no-wrap
msgid "USE_NUMERIC_ENTITY"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:16542
msgid ""
"For HTML, XML and DocBook@.  If set, use numeric entities instead of named "
"entities.  By default, set to true for DocBook output."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:16543
#, no-wrap
msgid "USE_UP_NODE_FOR_ELEMENT_UP"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:16547
msgid ""
"Fill in up sectioning direction with node direction when there is no "
"sectioning up direction.  In practice this can only happen when there is no "
"@@top section.  Not set by default."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:16548
#, no-wrap
msgid "USE_SETFILENAME_EXTENSION"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:16552
msgid ""
"Default is on for Info, off for other output.  If set, use exactly what "
"@code{@@setfilename} gives for the output file name, including the "
"extension.  You should not need to explicitly set this variable."
msgstr ""

#. type: pindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:16553
#, no-wrap
msgid "Text::Unidecode"
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:16554
#, no-wrap
msgid "USE_UNIDECODE"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:16557
msgid ""
"If set to false, do not use the @code{Text::Unidecode} Perl module to "
"transliterate more characters; default true."
msgstr ""

#. type: section
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:16561
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:16563
#, no-wrap
msgid "Internationalization of Document Strings"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:16563
msgid "@nodedescription Translating program-inserted text."
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:16565
#, no-wrap
msgid "I18n, of document strings"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:16566
#, no-wrap
msgid "Internationalization of document strings"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:16567
#, no-wrap
msgid "Document strings, internationalization of"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:16568
#, no-wrap
msgid "Output document strings, internationalization of"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:16569
#, no-wrap
msgid "Translating strings in output documents"
msgstr ""

#. type: vindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:16571
#, no-wrap
msgid "documentlanguage @r{customization variable}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:16578
msgid ""
"@command{texi2any} writes fixed strings into the output document at various "
"places: cross-references, page footers, the help page, alternate text for "
"images, and so on.  The string chosen depends on the value of the "
"@code{documentlanguage} at the time of the string being output "
"(@pxref{@code{@@documentlanguage}}, for the Texinfo command interface)."
msgstr ""

#. type: pindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:16579
#, no-wrap
msgid "libintl-perl @r{Gettext implementation}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:16589
msgid ""
"The Gettext framework is used for those strings (@pxref{Top,,, gettext, "
"Gettext}).  The @code{libintl-perl} package is used as the @code{gettext} "
"implementation; more specifically, the pure Perl implementation is used, so "
"Texinfo can support consistent behavior across all platforms and "
"installations, which would not otherwise be possible.  @code{libintl-perl} "
"is included in the Texinfo distribution and always installed, to ensure that "
"it is available if needed.  It is also possible to use the system "
"@code{gettext} (the choice can be made at build-time)."
msgstr ""

#. type: vindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:16590
#, no-wrap
msgid "texinfo_document @r{Gettext domain}"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:16591
#, no-wrap
msgid "Perl format strings for translation"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:16600
msgid ""
"The Gettext domain @samp{texinfo_document} is used for the strings.  "
"Translated strings are written as Texinfo, and may include @@-commands.  In "
"translated strings, the varying parts of the string are not usually denoted "
"by @code{%s} and the like, but by @samp{@{arg_name@}}.  (This convention is "
"common for @code{gettext} in Perl and is fully supported in GNU Gettext; "
"@pxref{perl-format,, Perl Format Strings, gettext, GNU Gettext}.)  For "
"example, in the following, @samp{@{section@}} will be replaced by the "
"section name:"
msgstr ""

#. type: example
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:16603
#, no-wrap
msgid "see @{section@}\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:16610
msgid ""
"These Perl-style brace format strings are used for two reasons: first, "
"changing the order of @code{printf} arguments is only available since "
"Perl@tie{}5.8.0; second, and more importantly, the order of arguments is "
"unpredictable, since @@-command expansion may lead to different orders "
"depending on the output format."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:16612
msgid "The expansion of a translation string is done like this:"
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:16614
#, no-wrap
msgid "First, the string is translated.  The locale"
msgstr ""

#. type: enumerate
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:16616
msgid "is @var{documentlanguage}@code{.}@var{documentencoding}."
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:16617
#, no-wrap
msgid "@code{us-ascii} encoding, and translations"
msgstr ""

#. type: enumerate
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:16620
msgid ""
"If the @var{documentlanguage} has the form @samp{ll_CC}, that is tried "
"first, and then just @samp{ll}."
msgstr ""

#. type: enumerate
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:16625
msgid ""
"To cope with the possibility of having multiple encodings, a special use of "
"the @code{us-ascii} locale encoding is also possible.  If the @samp{ll} "
"locale in the current encoding does not exist, and the encoding is not "
"@code{us-ascii}, then @code{us-ascii} is tried."
msgstr ""

#. type: enumerate
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:16633
msgid ""
"The idea is that if there is a @code{us-ascii} encoding, it means that all "
"the characters in the charset may be expressed as @@-commands.  For example, "
"there is a @code{fr.us-ascii} locale that can accommodate any encoding, "
"since all the Latin@tie{}1 characters have associated @@-commands.  On the "
"other hand, Japanese has only a translation @code{ja.utf-8}, since there are "
"no @@-commands for Japanese characters."
msgstr ""

#. type: enumerate
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:16638
msgid ""
"The @code{us-ascii} locales are not needed much now that UTF-8 is used for "
"most documents.  Note that accented characters are required to be expressed "
"as @@-commands in the @code{us-ascii} locales, which may be inconvenient for "
"translators."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:16639
#, no-wrap
msgid "Next, the string is expanded as Texinfo, and converted."
msgstr ""

#. type: enumerate
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:16642
msgid ""
"The arguments are substituted; for example, @samp{@{arg_name@}} is replaced "
"by the corresponding actual argument."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:16650
msgid ""
"In the following example, @samp{@{date@}}, @samp{@{program_homepage@}} and "
"@samp{@{program@}} are the arguments of the string.  Since they are used in "
"@code{@@uref}, their order is not predictable.  @samp{@{date@}}, "
"@samp{@{program_homepage@}} and @samp{@{program@}} are substituted after the "
"expansion:"
msgstr ""

#. type: example
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:16654
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Generated on @@emph@{@{date@}@} using\n"
"@@uref@{@{program_homepage@}, @@emph@{@{program@}@}@}.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:16662
msgid ""
"This approach is admittedly a bit complicated.  Its usefulness is that it "
"supports having translations available in different encodings for encodings "
"which can be covered by @@-commands, and also specifying how the formatting "
"for some commands is done, independently of the output format---yet still be "
"language-dependent.  For example, the @samp{@@pxref} translation string can "
"be like this:"
msgstr ""

#. type: example
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:16665
#, no-wrap
msgid "see @{node_file_href@} section `@{section@}' in @@cite@{@{book@}@}\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:16671
msgid ""
"which allows for specifying a string independently of the output format, "
"while nevertheless with rich formatting it may be translated appropriately "
"in many languages."
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:16673
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:16678
#, no-wrap
msgid "Invoking @command{pod2texi}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:16675
msgid "@nodedescription Translating Perl Pod to Texinfo."
msgstr ""

#. type: section
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:16675
#, no-wrap
msgid "Invoking @command{pod2texi}: Convert Pod to Texinfo"
msgstr ""

#. type: pindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:16677
#, no-wrap
msgid "pod2texi"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:16679
#, no-wrap
msgid "Pod, converting to Texinfo"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:16680
#, no-wrap
msgid "Perl Pod, converting to Texinfo"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:16687
msgid ""
"The @command{pod2texi} program translates Perl Pod documentation file(s)  to "
"Texinfo.  There are two basic modes of operation: generating a standalone "
"manual from each input Pod, or (if @code{--base-level=1} or higher is given) "
"generating Texinfo subfiles suitable for use with @code{@@include}."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:16702
msgid ""
"The @command{pod2texi} program may be useful outside of the rest of Texinfo; "
"thus, the invocation of @command{pod2texi} is documented in the Pod language "
"using the man page format to follow the convention used in Perl standalone "
"programs, with a version on the web "
"@url{http://www.gnu.org/software/texinfo/manual/pod2texi.html} and a version "
"included below.  The version included in the manual is also an example of "
"@command{pod2texi} use, as it is converted from Pod using @command{pod2texi}."
msgstr ""

#. type: node
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:16711
#, no-wrap
msgid "pod2texi manual page"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:16713
msgid "@nodedescription @command{pod2texi} invocation in a manual page format."
msgstr ""

#. type: include
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:16713
#, no-wrap
msgid "pod2texi.texi"
msgstr ""

#. type: node
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:16716
#, no-wrap
msgid "@command{texi2html}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:16718
msgid "@nodedescription An ancestor of @command{texi2any}."
msgstr ""

#. type: section
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:16718
#, no-wrap
msgid "@command{texi2html}: Ancestor of @command{texi2any}"
msgstr ""

#. type: pindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:16720
#, no-wrap
msgid "texi2html"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:16728
msgid ""
"Conceptually, the @command{texi2html} program is the parent of today's "
"@command{texi2any} program.  @command{texi2html} was developed "
"independently, originally by Lionel Cons in 1998; at the time, "
"@command{makeinfo} could not generate HTML@.  Many other people contributed "
"to @command{texi2html} over the years."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:16733
msgid ""
"The present @command{texi2any} uses little of the actual code of "
"@command{texi2html}, and has quite a different basic approach to the "
"implementation (namely, parsing the Texinfo document into a tree), but "
"still, there is a family resemblance."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:16739
msgid ""
"By design, @command{texi2any} supports nearly all the features of "
"@command{texi2html} in some way.  However, we did not attempt to maintain "
"strict compatibility, so no @command{texi2html} executable is installed by "
"the Texinfo package.  An approximation can be run with an invocation like "
"this:"
msgstr ""

#. type: example
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:16742
#, no-wrap
msgid "texi2any --set-customization-variable TEXI2HTML=1 ...\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:16746
msgid ""
"for the previous @command{texi2html}.  Here are the biggest differences:"
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:16748
#, no-wrap
msgid "Most blatantly, the command line options of @command{texi2html}"
msgstr ""

#. type: itemize
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:16751
msgid ""
"are now customization variables, for the most part.  A table of approximate "
"equivalents is given below."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:16752
#, no-wrap
msgid "The program-level customization API is very different in"
msgstr ""

#. type: itemize
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:16754
msgid "@command{texi2any}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:16755
#, no-wrap
msgid "Indices cannot be split."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:16765
msgid ""
"We do not intend to reimplement these differences.  Therefore, the route "
"forward for authors is alter manuals and build processes as necessary to use "
"the new features and methods of @command{texi2any}.  The @command{texi2html} "
"maintainers (one of whom is the principal author of @command{texi2any}) do "
"not intend to make further releases."
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:16766
#, no-wrap
msgid "Options of @command{texi2html}"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:16767
#, no-wrap
msgid "Command-line options of @command{texi2html}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:16772
