#. type: chapter
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:16803
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:16805
#, no-wrap
msgid "Creating and Installing Info Files"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:16805
msgid "@nodedescription Details on Info output."
msgstr ""

#.  removed, merged to this node and Emacs Info mode
#. type: anchor{#1}
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:16808
msgid "Creating an Info File"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:16815
msgid ""
"This chapter gives some information on the Info output and describes how to "
"install Info files.  For the creation of Info files with @command{texi2any}, "
"see @ref{Generic Translator @command{texi2any}}, and with Emacs, @ref{Info "
"Formatting}.  @xref{Info Files}, for general information about the file "
"format.  @xref{Info Format Specification}, for a detailed technical "
"specification of the Info format."
msgstr ""

#. type: section
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:16817
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:16818
#, no-wrap
msgid "Installing an Info File"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:16819
#, no-wrap
msgid "Installing an Info file"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:16820
#, no-wrap
msgid "Info files @subentry installation"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:16821
#, no-wrap
msgid "@file{dir} directory for Info installation"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:16827
msgid ""
"Info files are usually kept in the @file{info} directory.  You can read Info "
"files using the standalone Info program or the Info reader built into "
"Emacs.  (@xref{Top,,, info, Info}, for an introduction to Info.)"
msgstr ""

#. type: node
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:16829
#, no-wrap
msgid "Directory File"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:16831
msgid "@nodedescription The top-level menu for all Info files."
msgstr ""

#. type: subsection
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:16831
#, no-wrap
msgid "The Directory File @file{dir}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:16838
msgid ""
"For Info to work, the @file{info} directory must contain a file that serves "
"as a top-level directory for the Info system.  By convention, this file is "
"called @file{dir}.  (You can find the location of this file within Emacs by "
"typing @kbd{C-h i} to enter Info and then typing @kbd{C-x C-f} to see the "
"location of the @file{info} directory.)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:16842
msgid ""
"The @file{dir} file is itself an Info file.  It contains the top-level menu "
"for all the Info files in the system.  The menu looks like this:"
msgstr ""

#. type: group
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:16853
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"* Menu:\n"
"* Info:    (info).     Documentation browsing system.\n"
"* Emacs:   (emacs).    The extensible, self-documenting\n"
"                      text editor.\n"
"* Texinfo: (texinfo).  With one source file, make\n"
"                      either a printed manual using\n"
"                      @@TeX@{@} or an Info file.\n"
"@dots{}\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:16861
msgid ""
"Each of these menu entries points to the `Top' node of the Info file that is "
"named in parentheses.  (The menu entry does not need to specify the `Top' "
"node, since Info goes to the `Top' node if no node name is mentioned.  "
"@xref{Other Info Files, , Nodes in Other Info Files}.)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:16865
msgid ""
"Thus, the @samp{Info} entry points to the `Top' node of the @file{info} file "
"and the @samp{Emacs} entry points to the `Top' node of the @file{emacs} file."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:16869
msgid ""
"In each of the Info files, the `Up' pointer of the `Top' node refers back to "
"the @code{dir} file.  For example, the line for the `Top' node of the Emacs "
"manual looks like this in Info:"
msgstr ""

#. type: example
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:16872
#, no-wrap
msgid "File: emacs  Node: Top, Up: (DIR), Next: Distrib\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:16878
msgid ""
"In this case, the @file{dir} file name is written in uppercase letters---it "
"can be written in either upper- or lowercase.  This is not true in general, "
"it is a special case for @file{dir}."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:16881
msgid ""
"See the @file{util/dir-example} file in the Texinfo distribution for a large "
"sample @code{dir} file."
msgstr ""

#. type: node
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:16883
#, no-wrap
msgid "New Info File"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:16885
msgid "@nodedescription Listing a new Info file."
msgstr ""

#. type: subsection
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:16885
#, no-wrap
msgid "Listing a New Info File"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:16886
#, no-wrap
msgid "Adding a new Info file"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:16887
#, no-wrap
msgid "Listing a new Info file"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:16888
#, no-wrap
msgid "New Info file, listing it in @file{dir} file"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:16889
#, no-wrap
msgid "Info files @subentry listing a new"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:16890
#, no-wrap
msgid "@file{dir} file listing"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:16896
msgid ""
"To add a new Info file to your system, you must write a menu entry to add to "
"the menu in the @file{dir} file in the @file{info} directory.  For example, "
"if you were adding documentation for GDB, you would write the following new "
"entry:"
msgstr ""

#. type: example
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:16899
#, no-wrap
msgid "* GDB: (gdb).           The source-level C debugger.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:16905
msgid ""
"The first part of the menu entry is the menu entry name, followed by a "
"colon.  The second part is the name of the Info file, in parentheses, "
"followed by a period.  The third part is the description."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:16914
msgid ""
"The name of an Info file often has a @file{.info} extension.  Thus, the Info "
"file for GDB might be called either @file{gdb} or @file{gdb.info}.  The Info "
"reader programs automatically try the file name both with and without "
"@file{.info}@footnote{On MS-DOS/MS-Windows systems, Info will try the "
"@file{.inf} extension as well.}; so it is better to avoid clutter and not to "
"write @samp{.info} explicitly in the menu entry.  For example, the GDB menu "
"entry should use just @samp{gdb} for the file name, not @samp{gdb.info}."
msgstr ""

#. type: node
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:16916
#, no-wrap
msgid "Other Info Directories"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:16918
msgid ""
"@nodedescription How to specify Info files that are located in other "
"directories."
msgstr ""

#. type: subsection
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:16918
#, no-wrap
msgid "Info Files in Other Directories"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:16919
#, no-wrap
msgid "Installing Info in another directory"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:16920
#, no-wrap
msgid "Info installed in another directory"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:16921
#, no-wrap
msgid "Another Info directory"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:16922
#, no-wrap
msgid "@file{dir} files and Info directories"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:16926
msgid ""
"If an Info file is not in the @file{info} directory, there are three ways to "
"specify its location:"
msgstr ""

#. type: enumerate
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:16930
msgid ""
"Write the file name in the @file{dir} file as the second part of the menu."
msgstr ""

#. type: enumerate
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:16936
msgid ""
"Specify the Info directory name in the @code{INFOPATH} environment variable "
"in your @file{.profile} or @file{.cshrc} initialization file.  (Only you and "
"others who set this environment variable will be able to find Info files "
"whose location is specified this way.)"
msgstr ""

#. type: enumerate
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:16942
msgid ""
"If you are using Emacs, list the name of the file in a second @file{dir} "
"file, in its directory; and then add the name of that directory to the "
"@code{Info-directory-list} variable in your personal or site initialization "
"file."
msgstr ""

#. type: enumerate
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:16948
msgid ""
"This variable tells Emacs where to look for @file{dir} files (the files must "
"be named @file{dir}).  Emacs merges the files named @file{dir} from each of "
"the listed directories.  (In Emacs version 18, you can set the "
"@code{Info-directory} variable to the name of only one directory.)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:16953
msgid ""
"For example, to reach a test file in the @file{/home/bob/info} directory, "
"you could add an entry like this to the menu in the standard @file{dir} file:"
msgstr ""

#. type: example
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:16956
#, no-wrap
msgid "* Test: (/home/bob/info/info-test).  Bob's own test file.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:16961
msgid ""
"In this case, the absolute file name of the @file{info-test} file is written "
"as the second part of the menu entry."
msgstr ""

#. type: vindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:16962
#, no-wrap
msgid "INFOPATH"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:16963
#, no-wrap
msgid "Environment variable @code{INFOPATH}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:16968
msgid ""
"If you don't want to edit the system @file{dir} file, you can tell Info "
"where to look by setting the @code{INFOPATH} environment variable in your "
"shell startup file.  This works with both the Emacs and standalone Info "
"readers."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:16974
msgid ""
"Emacs uses the @code{INFOPATH} environment variable to initialize the value "
"of Emacs's own @code{Info-directory-list} variable.  The standalone Info "
"reader merges any files named @file{dir} in any directory listed in the "
"@env{INFOPATH} variable into a single menu presented to you in the node "
"called @samp{(dir)Top}."
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:16975
#, no-wrap
msgid "Colon, last in @env{INFOPATH}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:16981
msgid ""
"However you set @env{INFOPATH}, if its last character is a colon (on "
"MS-DOS/MS-Windows systems, use a semicolon instead), this is replaced by the "
"default (compiled-in) path.  This gives you a way to augment the default "
"path with new directories without having to list all the standard places.  "
"For example (using @code{sh} syntax):"
msgstr ""

#. type: example
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:16985
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"INFOPATH=/home/bob/info:\n"
"export INFOPATH\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:16990
msgid ""
"will search @file{/home/bob/info} first, then the standard directories.  "
"Leading or doubled colons are not treated specially."
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:16991
#, no-wrap
msgid "@file{dir} file, creating your own"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:16997
msgid ""
"When you create your own @file{dir} file for use with "
"@code{Info-directory-list} or @env{INFOPATH}, it's easiest to start by "
"copying an existing @file{dir} file and replace all the text after the "
"@samp{* Menu:} with your desired entries.  That way, the punctuation and "
"special @kbd{CTRL-_} characters that Info needs will be present."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:17000
msgid ""
"As one final alternative, which works only with Emacs Info, you can change "
"the @code{Info-directory-list} variable.  For example:"
msgstr ""

#. type: example
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:17005
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"(add-hook 'Info-mode-hook '(lambda ()\n"
"\t     (add-to-list 'Info-directory-list\n"
"\t\t\t  (expand-file-name \"~/info\"))))\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: node
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:17008
#, no-wrap
msgid "Installing Dir Entries"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:17010
msgid ""
"@nodedescription How to specify what menu entry to add to the Info directory."
msgstr ""

#. type: subsection
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:17010
#, no-wrap
msgid "Installing Info Directory Files"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:17016
msgid ""
"When you install an Info file onto your system, you can use the program "
"@code{install-info} to update the Info directory file @file{dir}.  Normally "
"the makefile for the package runs @code{install-info}, just after copying "
"the Info file into its proper installed location."
msgstr ""

#. type: findex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:17018
#, no-wrap
msgid "direntry"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:17026
msgid ""
"In order for the Info file to work with @code{install-info}, you include the "
"commands @code{@@dircategory} and @code{@@direntry}@dots{}@code{@@end "
"direntry} in the Texinfo source file.  Use @code{@@direntry} to specify the "
"menu entries to add to the Info directory file.  Use @code{@@dircategory} to "
"specify a category for the manual, which determines which part of the Info "
"directory to put it in.  @xref{Directory Category}."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:17028
msgid "Here is how these commands are used in this manual:"
msgstr ""

#. type: example
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:17036
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"@@dircategory Texinfo documentation system\n"
"@@direntry\n"
"* Texinfo: (texinfo).           The GNU documentation format.\n"
"* install-info: (texinfo)Invoking install-info. @dots{}\n"
"@dots{}\n"
"@@end direntry\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:17039
msgid "Here's what this produces in the Info file:"
msgstr ""

#. type: example
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:17047
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"INFO-DIR-SECTION Texinfo documentation system\n"
"START-INFO-DIR-ENTRY\n"
"* Texinfo: (texinfo).           The GNU documentation format.\n"
"* install-info: (texinfo)Invoking install-info. @dots{}\n"
"@dots{}\n"
"END-INFO-DIR-ENTRY\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:17052
msgid ""
"The @code{install-info} program sees these lines in the Info file, and that "
"is how it knows what to do."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:17057
msgid ""
"Always use the @code{@@direntry} and @code{@@dircategory} commands near the "
"beginning of the Texinfo input, before the first @code{@@node} command.  If "
"you use them later on in the input, @code{install-info} will not notice them."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:17067
msgid ""
"@code{install-info} will automatically reformat the description of the menu "
"entries it is adding.  As a matter of convention, the description of the "
"main entry (above, @samp{The GNU documentation format}) should start at "
"column 32, starting at zero (as in @code{what-cursor-position} in Emacs).  "
"This will make it align with most others.  Description for individual "
"utilities best start in column 48, where possible.  For more information "
"about formatting see the @samp{--calign}, @samp{--align}, and "
"@samp{--max-width} options in @ref{Invoking @command{install-info}}."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:17071
msgid ""
"If you use @code{@@dircategory} more than once in the Texinfo source, each "
"usage specifies the `current' category; any subsequent @code{@@direntry} "
"commands will add to that category."
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:17072
#, no-wrap
msgid "Invoking nodes, including in dir file"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:17077
msgid ""
"Each `Invoking' node for every program installed should have a corresponding "
"@code{@@direntry}.  This lets users easily find the documentation for the "
"different programs they can run, as with the traditional @command{man} "
"system."
msgstr ""

#. type: subsection
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:17079
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:17081
#, no-wrap
msgid "Invoking @command{install-info}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:17081
msgid "@nodedescription @code{install-info} options."
msgstr ""

#. type: pindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:17083
#, no-wrap
msgid "install-info"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:17091
msgid ""
"@code{install-info} inserts menu entries from an Info file into the "
"top-level @file{dir} file in the Info system (see the previous sections for "
"an explanation of how the @file{dir} file works).  @code{install-info} also "
"removes menu entries from the @file{dir} file.  It's most often run as part "
"of software installation, or when constructing a @file{dir} file for all "
"manuals on a system.  Synopsis:"
msgstr ""

#. type: example
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:17094
#, no-wrap
msgid "install-info [@var{option}@dots{}] [@var{info-file} [@var{dir-file}]]\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:17100
msgid ""
"If @var{info-file} or @var{dir-file} are not specified, the options "
"(described below) that define them must be.  There are no compile-time "
"defaults, and standard input is never used.  @code{install-info} can read "
"only one Info file and write only one @file{dir} file per invocation."
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:17101
#, no-wrap
msgid "@file{dir}, created by @code{install-info}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:17104
msgid ""
"If @var{dir-file} (however specified) does not exist, @code{install-info} "
"creates it if possible (with no entries)."
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:17105
#, no-wrap
msgid "Compressed dir files, reading"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:17106
#, no-wrap
msgid "XZ-compressed dir files, reading"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:17107
#, no-wrap
msgid "Bzipped dir files, reading"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:17108
#, no-wrap
msgid "Lzip-compressed dir files, reading"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:17109
#, no-wrap
msgid "LZMA-compressed dir files, reading"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:17110
#, no-wrap
msgid "Dir files, compressed"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:17119
msgid ""
"If any input file is compressed with @code{gzip} (@pxref{Top,,, gzip, "
"Gzip}), @code{install-info} automatically uncompresses it for reading.  And "
"if @var{dir-file} is compressed, @code{install-info} also automatically "
"leaves it compressed after writing any changes.  If @var{dir-file} itself "
"does not exist, @code{install-info} tries to open @file{@var{dir-file}.gz}, "
"@file{@var{dir-file}.xz}, @file{@var{dir-file}.bz2}, "
"@file{@var{dir-file}.lz}, and @file{@var{dir-file}.lzma}, in that order."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:17121
msgid "Options:"
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:17123
#, no-wrap
msgid "--add-once"
msgstr ""

#. type: opindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:17124
#, no-wrap
msgid "--add-once@r{, for @command{install-info}}"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:17126
msgid ""
"Specifies that the entry or entries will only be put into a single section."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:17127
#, no-wrap
msgid "--align=@var{column}"
msgstr ""

#. type: opindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:17128
#, no-wrap
msgid "--align=@var{column}@r{, for @command{install-info}}"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:17133
msgid ""
"Specifies the column that the second and subsequent lines of menu entry's "
"description will be formatted to begin at.  The default for this option is "
"@samp{35}.  It is used in conjunction with the @samp{--max-width} option.  "
"@var{column} starts counting at 1."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:17134
#, no-wrap
msgid "--append-new-sections"
msgstr ""

#. type: opindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:17135
#, no-wrap
msgid "--append-new-sections@r{, for @command{install-info}}"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:17137
msgid ""
"Instead of alphabetizing new sections, place them at the end of the DIR file."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
