#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:18174
msgid ""
"Quotation mark @@-commands (@code{@@quotedblright@{@}} and the like), are "
"likewise replaced by their Unicode values.  Normal quotation "
"@emph{characters} (e.g., ASCII ` and ') are not altered.  @xref{Inserting "
"Quotation Marks}."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:18179
msgid ""
"Any @code{@@acronym}, @code{@@abbr}, @code{@@email}, and @code{@@image} "
"commands are replaced by their first argument.  (For these commands, all "
"subsequent arguments are optional, and ignored here.)  "
"@xref{@code{@@acronym}}, and @ref{@code{@@email}}, and @ref{Images}."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:18181
msgid "Accents are handled according to the next section."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:18183
msgid "Any other command is an error, and the result is unspecified."
msgstr ""

#. type: node
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:18185
#, no-wrap
msgid "HTML Xref 8-bit Character Expansion"
msgstr ""

#. type: subsection
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:18186
#, no-wrap
msgid "HTML Cross-reference 8-bit Character Expansion"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:18187
#, no-wrap
msgid "HTML cross-references @subentry 8-bit character expansion"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:18188
#, no-wrap
msgid "8-bit characters, in HTML cross-references"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:18189
#, no-wrap
msgid "Expansion of 8-bit characters in HTML cross-references"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:18190
#, no-wrap
msgid "Transliteration of 8-bit characters in HTML cross-references"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:18198
msgid ""
"Usually, characters other than plain 7-bit ASCII are transformed into the "
"corresponding Unicode code point(s) in Normalization Form@tie{}C, which uses "
"precomposed characters where available.  (This is the normalization form "
"recommended by the W3C and other bodies.)  This holds when that code point "
"is @code{0xffff} or less, as it almost always is."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:18201
msgid ""
"These will then be further transformed by the rules above into the string "
"@samp{_@var{hhhh}}, where @var{hhhh} is the code point in hex."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:18203
msgid "For example, combining this rule and the previous section:"
msgstr ""

#. type: example
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:18207
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"@@node @@b@{A@} @@TeX@{@} @@u@{B@} @@point@{@}@@enddots@{@}\n"
"@result{} A-TeX-B_0306-_22C6_002e_002e_002e\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:18214
msgid ""
"Notice: 1)@tie{}@code{@@enddots} expands to three periods which in turn "
"expands to three @samp{_002e}'s; 2)@tie{}@code{@@u@{B@}} is a `B' with a "
"breve accent, which does not exist as a pre-accented Unicode character, "
"therefore expands to @samp{B_0306} (B with combining breve)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:18221
msgid ""
"When the Unicode code point is above @code{0xffff}, the transformation is "
"@samp{__@var{xxxxxx}}, that is, two leading underscores followed by six hex "
"digits.  Since Unicode has declared that their highest code point is "
"@code{0x10ffff}, this is sufficient.  (We felt it was better to define this "
"extra escape than to always use six hex digits, since the first two would "
"nearly always be zeros.)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:18233
msgid ""
"This method works fine if the node name consists mostly of ASCII characters "
"and contains only few 8-bit ones.  But if the document is written in a "
"language whose script is not based on the Latin alphabet (for example, "
"Ukrainian), it will create file names consisting almost entirely of "
"@samp{_@var{xxxx}} notations, which is inconvenient and all but unreadable.  "
"To handle such cases, @command{texi2any} offers the "
"@option{--transliterate-file-names} command line option.  This option "
"enables @dfn{transliteration} of node names into ASCII characters for the "
"purposes of file name creation and referencing.  The transliteration is "
"based on phonetic principles, which makes the generated file names more "
"easily understandable."
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:18234
#, no-wrap
msgid "Normalization Form C, Unicode"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:18239
msgid ""
"For the definition of Unicode Normalization Form@tie{}C, see Unicode report "
"UAX#15, @uref{http://www.unicode.org/reports/tr15/}.  Many related documents "
"and implementations are available elsewhere on the web."
msgstr ""

#. type: node
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:18241
#, no-wrap
msgid "HTML Xref Mismatch"
msgstr ""

#. type: subsection
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:18242
#, no-wrap
msgid "HTML Cross-reference Mismatch"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:18243
#, no-wrap
msgid "HTML cross-references @subentry mismatch"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:18244
#, no-wrap
msgid "Mismatched HTML cross-reference source and target"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:18250
msgid ""
"As mentioned earlier (@pxref{HTML Xref Link Basics}), the generating "
"software may need to guess whether a given manual being cross-referenced is "
"available in split or monolithic form---and, inevitably, it might guess "
"wrong.  However, when the @emph{referent} manual is generated, it is "
"possible to handle at least some mismatches."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:18256
msgid ""
"In the case where we assume the referent is split, but it is actually "
"available in mono, the only recourse would be to generate a "
"@file{manual_html/} subdirectory full of HTML files which redirect back to "
"the monolithic @file{manual.html}.  Since this is essentially the same as a "
"split manual in the first place, it's not very appealing."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:18262
msgid ""
"On the other hand, in the case where we assume the referent is mono, but it "
"is actually available in split, it is possible to use JavaScript to redirect "
"from the putatively monolithic @file{manual.html} to the different "
"@file{manual_html/node.html} files.  Here's an example:"
msgstr ""

#. type: example
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:18274
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"function redirect() @{\n"
"  switch (location.hash) @{\n"
"    case \"#Node1\":\n"
"      location.replace(\"manual_html/Node1.html#Node1\"); break;\n"
"    case \"#Node2\" :\n"
"      location.replace(\"manual_html/Node2.html#Node2\"); break;\n"
"    @dots{}\n"
"    default:;\n"
"  @}\n"
"@}\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:18277
msgid "Then, in the @code{<body>} tag of @file{manual.html}:"
msgstr ""

#. type: example
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:18280
#, no-wrap
msgid "<body onLoad=\"redirect();\">\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:18286
msgid ""
"Once again, this is something the software which generated the "
"@emph{referent} manual has to do in advance, it's not something the software "
"generating the cross-reference in the present manual can control."
msgstr ""

#. type: node
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:18288
#, no-wrap
msgid "HTML Xref Configuration"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:18290
msgid "@nodedescription @file{htmlxref.cnf}."
msgstr ""

#. type: subsection
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:18290
#, no-wrap
msgid "HTML Cross-reference Configuration: @file{htmlxref.cnf}"
msgstr ""

#. type: pindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:18292
#, no-wrap
msgid "htmlxref.cnf"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:18293
#, no-wrap
msgid "HTML cross-references @subentry configuration"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:18294
#, no-wrap
msgid "Cross-reference configuration, for HTML"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:18295
#, no-wrap
msgid "Configuration, for HTML cross-manual references"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:18300
msgid ""
"@command{texi2any} reads a file named @file{htmlxref.cnf} to gather "
"information for cross-references to other manuals in HTML output.  It is "
"looked for in the following directories:"
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:18302
#, no-wrap
msgid "./"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:18304
msgid "(the current directory)"
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:18305
#, no-wrap
msgid "./.texinfo/"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:18307
msgid "(under the current directory)"
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:18308
#, no-wrap
msgid "~/.texinfo/"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:18310
msgid "(where @code{~} is the current user's home directory)"
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:18311
#, no-wrap
msgid "@var{sysconfdir}/texinfo/"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:18314
msgid ""
"(where @var{sysconfdir} is the system configuration directory specified at "
"compile-time, e.g., @file{/usr/local/etc})"
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:18315
#, no-wrap
msgid "@var{datadir}/texinfo/"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:18317
msgid "(likewise specified at compile time, e.g., @file{/usr/local/share})"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:18323
msgid ""
"All files found are used, with earlier entries overriding later ones.  The "
"Texinfo distribution includes a default file which handles many GNU manuals; "
"it is installed in the last of the above directories, i.e., "
"@file{@var{datadir}/texinfo/htmlxref.cnf}."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:18328
msgid ""
"The @code{HTMLXREF_MODE} customization variable can be set to modify how the "
"files are found.  For instance, if set to @samp{none}, no external "
"information is used.  @code{HTMLXREF_FILE} sets the file name to something "
"else than @file{htmlxref.cnf}.  @pxref{HTML Customization Variables}."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:18334
msgid ""
"The file is line-oriented.  Lines consisting only of whitespace are "
"ignored.  Comments are indicated with a @samp{#} at the beginning of a line, "
"optionally preceded by whitespace.  Since @samp{#} can occur in URLs (like "
"almost any character), it does not otherwise start a comment."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:18337
msgid ""
"Each non-blank non-comment line must be either a @dfn{variable assignment} "
"or @dfn{manual information}."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:18339
msgid "A variable assignment line looks like this:"
msgstr ""

#. type: example
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:18342
#, no-wrap
msgid "@var{varname} = @var{varvalue}\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:18349
msgid ""
"Whitespace around the @samp{=} is optional and ignored.  The @var{varname} "
"should consist of letters; case is significant.  The @var{varvalue} is an "
"arbitrary string, continuing to the end of the line.  Variables are then "
"referenced with @samp{$@{@var{varname}@}}; variable references can occur in "
"the @var{varvalue}."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:18351
msgid "A manual information line looks like this:"
msgstr ""

#. type: example
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:18354
#, no-wrap
msgid "@var{manual} @var{keyword} @var{urlprefix}\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:18362
msgid ""
"with @var{manual} the short identifier for a manual, @var{keyword} being one "
"of: @code{mono}, @code{node}, @code{section}, @code{chapter}, and "
"@var{urlprefix} described below.  Variable references can occur only in the "
"@var{urlprefix}.  For example (used in the canonical @file{htmlxref.cnf}):"
msgstr ""

#. type: example
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:18370
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"G = http://www.gnu.org\n"
"GS = $@{G@}/software\n"
"hello mono    $@{GS@}/hello/manual/hello.html\n"
"hello chapter $@{GS@}/hello/manual/html_chapter/\n"
"hello section $@{GS@}/hello/manual/html_section/\n"
"hello node    $@{GS@}/hello/manual/html_node/\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:18372
#, no-wrap
msgid "monolithic manuals, for HTML cross-references"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:18375
msgid ""
"If the keyword is @code{mono}, @var{urlprefix} gives the host, directory, "
"and file name for @var{manual} as one monolithic file."
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:18376
#, no-wrap
msgid "split manuals, for HTML cross-references"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:18380
msgid ""
"If the keyword is @code{node}, @code{section}, or @code{chapter}, "
"@var{urlprefix} gives the host and directory for @var{manual} split into "
"nodes, sections, or chapters, respectively."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:18388
msgid ""
"When available, @command{texi2any} will use the ``corresponding'' value for "
"cross-references between manuals.  That is, when generating monolithic "
"output (@option{--no-split}), the @code{mono} URL will be used, when "
"generating output that is split by node, the @code{node} URL will be used, "
"etc.  However, if a manual is not available in that form, anything that is "
"available can be used.  Here is the search order for each style:"
msgstr ""

#. type: example
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:18394
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"node    @result{} node,    section, chapter, mono\n"
"section @result{} section, chapter, node,    mono\n"
"chapter @result{} chapter, section, node,    mono\n"
"mono    @result{} mono,    chapter, section, node\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: opindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:18396
#, no-wrap
msgid "--node-files@r{, and HTML cross-references}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:18400
msgid ""
"These section- and chapter-level cross-manual references can succeed only "
"when the target manual was created using @option{--node-files}; this is the "
"default for split output."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:18405
msgid ""
"If you have additions or corrections to the @file{htmlxref.cnf} distributed "
"with Texinfo, please email @email{bug-texinfo@@gnu.org} as usual.  You can "
"get the latest version from "
"@url{http://ftpmirror.gnu.org/@/texinfo/@/htmlxref.cnf}."
msgstr ""

#. type: appendix
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:18407
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:18409
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@-Command Details"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:18409
msgid "@nodedescription Details of the Texinfo @@-commands."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:18413
msgid ""
"Here are the details of @@-commands: information about their syntax, a list "
"of commands, and information about where commands can appear."
msgstr ""

#. type: node
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:18415
#, no-wrap
msgid "Command Syntax"
msgstr ""

#. type: section
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:18416
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@-Command Syntax"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:18417
#, no-wrap
msgid "@sortas{at} @@-commands @subentry syntax"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:18418
#, no-wrap
msgid "Syntax, of @@-commands"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:18419
#, no-wrap
msgid "Command syntax"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:18422
msgid "Texinfo has the following types of @@-command:"
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:18424
#, no-wrap
msgid "1. Brace commands"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:18429
msgid ""
"These commands start with @@ followed by a letter or a word, followed by an "
"argument within braces.  For example, the command @code{@@dfn} indicates the "
"introductory or defining use of a term; it is used as follows: @samp{In "
"Texinfo, @@@@-commands are @@dfn@{mark-up@} commands.}"
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:18430
#, no-wrap
msgid "2. Line commands"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:18436
msgid ""
"These commands occupy an entire line.  The line starts with @@, followed by "
"the name of the command (a word); for example, @code{@@center} or "
"@code{@@cindex}.  If no argument is needed, the word is followed by the end "
"of the line.  If there is an argument, it is separated from the command name "
"by a space.  Braces are not used."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:18438
#, no-wrap
msgid "3. Block commands"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:18446
msgid ""
"These commands are written at the start of a line, with general text on "
"following lines, terminated by a matching @code{@@end} command on a line of "
"its own.  For example, @code{@@example}, then the lines of a coding example, "
"then @code{@@end example}.  Some of these block commands take arguments as "
"line commands do; for example, @code{@@enumerate A} opening an environment "
"terminated by @code{@@end enumerate}.  Here @samp{A} is the argument."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:18447
#, no-wrap
msgid "4. Symbol insertion commands with no arguments"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:18454
msgid ""
"These commands start with @@ followed by a word followed by a left and "
"right- brace.  These commands insert special symbols in the document; they "
"do not take arguments.  Some examples: @code{@@dots@{@}} @result{} "
"@samp{@dots{}}, @code{@@equiv@{@}} @result{} @samp{@equiv{}}, "
"@code{@@TeX@{@}} @result{} `@TeX{}', and @code{@@bullet@{@}} @result{} "
"@samp{@bullet{}}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:18455
#, no-wrap
msgid "5. Non-alphabetic commands"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:18464
msgid ""
"The names of commands in all of the above categories consist of alphabetic "
"characters, almost entirely in lower-case.  Unlike those, the non-alphabetic "
"commands consist of an @@ followed by a punctuation mark or other character "
"that is not part of the Latin alphabet.  Non-alphabetic commands are almost "
"always part of text within a paragraph.  The non-alphabetic commands include "
"@code{@@@@}, @code{@@@{}, @code{@@@}}, @code{@@.}, @code{@@@kbd{SPACE}}, and "
"most of the accent commands."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:18465
#, no-wrap
msgid "6. Miscellaneous commands"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:18473
msgid ""
"There are a handful of commands that don't fit into any of the above "
"categories; for example, the obsolete command @code{@@refill}, which is "
"always used at the end of a paragraph immediately following the final period "
"or other punctuation character.  @code{@@refill} takes no argument and does "
"not require braces.  Likewise, @code{@@tab} used in a @code{@@multitable} "
"block does not take arguments, and is not followed by braces."
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:18475
#, no-wrap
msgid "Braces and argument syntax"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:18485
msgid ""
"Thus, the alphabetic commands fall into classes that have different argument "
"syntaxes.  You cannot tell to which class a command belongs by the "
"appearance of its name, but you can tell by the command's meaning: if the "
"command stands for a glyph, it is in class 4 and does not require an "
"argument; if it makes sense to use the command among other text as part of a "
"paragraph, the command is in class 1 and must be followed by an argument in "
"braces.  The non-alphabetic commands, such as @code{@@:}, are exceptions to "
"the rule; they do not need braces."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:18489
msgid ""
"The purpose of having different syntax for commands is to make Texinfo files "
"easier to read, and also to help the GNU Emacs paragraph and filling "
"commands work properly."
msgstr ""

#. type: node
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:18491
#, no-wrap
msgid "Command List"
msgstr ""

#. type: section
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:18492
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@-Command List"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:18493
#, no-wrap
msgid "Alphabetical @@-command list"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:18494
#, no-wrap
msgid "List of @@-commands"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:18495
#, no-wrap
msgid "@sortas{at} @@-commands @subentry list of"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:18496
#, no-wrap
msgid "Reference to @@-commands"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:18501
msgid ""
"Here is an alphabetical list of the @@-commands in Texinfo.  Square "
"brackets, @t{[}@w{ }@t{]}, indicate optional arguments; an ellipsis, "
"@samp{@dots{}}, indicates repeated text."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:18503
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@@var{whitespace}"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:18506
msgid ""
"An @code{@@} followed by a space, tab, or newline produces a normal, "
"stretchable, interword space.  @xref{Multiple Spaces}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:18507
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@!"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:18510
msgid ""
"Produce an exclamation point that ends a sentence (usually after an "
"end-of-sentence capital letter).  @xref{Ending a Sentence}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:18511
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@\""
msgstr ""

#. type: itemx
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:18512
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@'"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:18515
msgid ""
"Generate an umlaut or acute accent, respectively, over the next character, "
"as in @\"o and @'o.  @xref{Inserting Accents}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:18516
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@&"
msgstr ""

#. type: itemx
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:18517
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@ampchar@{@}"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:18519
msgid "Generate an ampersand.  @xref{Inserting an Ampersand}."
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:18522
msgid "Force a line break.  @xref{Line Breaks}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:18523
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@,@{@var{c}@}"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:18526
msgid ""
"Generate a cedilla accent under @var{c}, as in @,{c}.  @xref{Inserting "
"Accents}."
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:18529
msgid ""
"Insert a discretionary hyphenation point.  @xref{@code{@@- @@hyphenation}}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:18530
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@."
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:18533
msgid ""
"Produce a period that ends a sentence (usually after an end-of-sentence "
"capital letter).  @xref{Ending a Sentence}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:18534
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@/"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:18536
msgid "Produces no output, but allows a line break.  @xref{Line Breaks}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:18537
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@:"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:18541
msgid ""
"Tell printed output processors to refrain from inserting extra whitespace "
"after an immediately preceding period, question mark, exclamation mark, or "
"colon.  @xref{Not Ending a Sentence}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:18542
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@="
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:18545
msgid ""
"Generate a macron (bar) accent over the next character, as in @=o.  "
"@xref{Inserting Accents}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:18546
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@?"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:18549
msgid ""
"Produce a question mark that ends a sentence (usually after an "
"end-of-sentence capital letter).  @xref{Ending a Sentence}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:18550
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@@@"
msgstr ""

#. type: itemx
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:18551
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@atchar@{@}"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:18553
msgid "Insert an at sign, @samp{@@}.  @xref{Inserting an Atsign}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:18554
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@\\"
msgstr ""

#. type: itemx
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:18555
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@backslashchar@{@}"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:18559
msgid ""
"Insert a backslash, @samp{\\}; @code{@@backslashchar@{@}} works anywhere, "
"while @code{@@\\} works only inside @code{@@math}.  @xref{Inserting a "
"Backslash}, and @ref{Inserting Math}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:18560
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@^"
msgstr ""

#. type: itemx
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:18561
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@`"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:18565
msgid ""
"Generate a circumflex (hat) or grave accent, respectively, over the next "
"character, as in @^o and @`e.  @xref{Inserting Accents}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:18566
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@@{"
msgstr ""

#. type: itemx
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:18567
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@lbracechar@{@}"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:18569
msgid "Insert a left brace, @samp{@{}.  @xref{Inserting Braces}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:18570
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@@}"
msgstr ""

#. type: itemx
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:18571
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@rbracechar@{@}"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:18573
msgid "Insert a right brace, @samp{@}}.  @xref{Inserting Braces}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:18574
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@~"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:18577
msgid ""
"Generate a tilde accent over the next character, as in @~N.  @xref{Inserting "
"Accents}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:18578
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@AA@{@}"
msgstr ""

#. type: itemx
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:18579
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@aa@{@}"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:18582
msgid ""
"Generate the uppercase and lowercase Scandinavian A-ring letters, "
"respectively: @AA{}, @aa{}.  @xref{Inserting Accents}."
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:18586
msgid ""
"Indicate a general abbreviation, such as `Comput.'.  @xref{@code{@@abbr}}."
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:18590
msgid ""
"Indicate an acronym in all capital letters, such as `NASA'.  "
"@xref{@code{@@acronym}}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:18591
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@AE@{@}"
msgstr ""

#. type: itemx
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:18592
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@ae@{@}"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:18595
msgid ""
"Generate the uppercase and lowercase AE ligatures, respectively: @AE{}, "
"@ae{}.  @xref{Inserting Accents}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:18596
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@afivepaper"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:18598
msgid "Change page dimensions for the A5 paper size.  @xref{A4 Paper}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:18599
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@afourlatex"
msgstr ""

#. type: itemx
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:18600
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@afourpaper"
msgstr ""

#. type: itemx
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:18601
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@afourwide"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:18603
msgid "Change page dimensions for the A4 paper size.  @xref{A4 Paper}."
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:18607
msgid ""
"Make the command @samp{@@@var{new}} a synonym for the existing command "
"@samp{@@@var{existing}}.  @xref{@code{@@alias}}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:18608
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@allowcodebreaks @var{true-false}"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:18611
msgid ""
"Control breaking at @samp{-} and @samp{_} in printed output.  "
"@xref{@code{@@allowcodebreaks}}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:18612
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@anchor@{@var{name}@}"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:18615
msgid ""
"Define @var{name} as the current location for use as a cross-reference "
"target.  @xref{@code{@@anchor}}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:18616
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@appendix @var{title}"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:18619
msgid ""
"Begin an appendix.  The title appears in the table of contents.  "
"@xref{@code{@@unnumbered @@appendix}}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:18620
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@appendixsec @var{title}"
msgstr ""

#. type: itemx
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:18621
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@appendixsection @var{title}"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:18626
msgid ""
"Begin an appendix section within an appendix.  The section title appears in "
"the table of contents.  @code{@@appendixsection} is a longer spelling of the "
"@code{@@appendixsec} command.  @xref{@code{@@unnumberedsec @@appendixsec "
"@@heading}}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:18627
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@appendixsubsec @var{title}"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:18630
msgid ""
"Begin an appendix subsection.  The title appears in the table of contents.  "
"@xref{@code{@@unnumberedsubsec @@appendixsubsec @@subheading}}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:18631
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@appendixsubsubsec @var{title}"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:18634
msgid ""
"Begin an appendix subsubsection.  The title appears in the table of "
"contents.  @xref{@code{@@subsubsection}}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:18635
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@arrow@{@}"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:18638
msgid ""
"Generate a right arrow glyph: @samp{@arrow{}}.  Used by default for "
"@code{@@click}.  @xref{Click Sequences}."
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:18644
msgid ""
"Keep the argument as is.  Used following @code{@@table}, @code{@@ftable}, "
"and @code{@@vtable} to print the table's first column without highlighting "
"(``as is'').  @xref{@code{@@asis}}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:18645
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@author @var{author}"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:18648
msgid ""
"Set a manual author in the title page.  @xref{@code{@@title @@subtitle "
"@@author}}.  Set a quotation author in @code{@@quotation}.  "
"@xref{@code{@@quotation}}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:18649
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@b@{@var{text}@}"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:18651
msgid "Set @var{text} in a @b{bold} font, if possible.  @xref{Fonts}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:18652
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@bullet@{@}"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:18655
msgid ""
"Generate a large round dot, @bullet{}, or the closest possible thing to "
"one.  Often used with @code{@@table}.  @xref{@code{@@bullet}}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:18656
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@bsixpaper"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:18658
msgid "Change page dimensions for the B6 paper size.  @xref{A4 Paper}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:18659
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@bye"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:18662
msgid ""
"Stop processing a file.  The processors do not see anything in the input "
"file following @code{@@bye}.  @xref{Ending a File}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:18663
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@c @var{comment}"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:18667
msgid ""
"Begin a comment in Texinfo.  The rest of the line does not appear in any "
"output.  A synonym for @code{@@comment}.  @kbd{DEL} also starts a comment.  "
"@xref{Comments}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:18668
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@caption"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:18671
msgid ""
"Define the full caption for a @code{@@float}.  @xref{@code{@@caption "
"@@shortcaption}}."
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:18676
msgid ""
"Highlight an example or quotation by drawing a box with rounded corners "
"around it, if possible.  Pair with @code{@@end cartouche}.  "
"@xref{@code{@@cartouche}}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:18677
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@center @var{line-of-text}"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:18680
msgid ""
"Center the line of text following the command.  @xref{@code{@@titlefont "
"@@center @@sp}}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:18681
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@centerchap @var{line-of-text}"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:18683
msgid ""
"Like @code{@@chapter}, but centers the chapter title.  "
"@xref{@code{@@chapter}}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:18684
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@chapheading @var{title}"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:18687
msgid ""
"Print an unnumbered chapter-like heading, but omit from the table of "
"contents.  @xref{@code{@@majorheading @@chapheading}}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:18688
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@chapter @var{title}"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:18691
msgid ""
"Begin a numbered chapter.  The chapter title appears in the table of "
"contents.  @xref{@code{@@chapter}}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:18692
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@cindex @var{entry}"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:18695
msgid ""
"Add @var{entry} to the index of concepts.  @xref{Index Entries, , Defining "
"the Entries of an Index}."
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:18699
msgid ""
"Highlight the name of a book or other reference that has no companion Info "
"file.  @xref{@code{@@cite}}."
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:18706
msgid ""
"Unset @var{flag}, preventing the Texinfo formatting commands from formatting "
"text between subsequent pairs of @code{@@ifset @var{flag}} and @code{@@end "
"ifset} commands, and preventing @code{@@value@{@var{flag}@}} from expanding "
"to the value to which @var{flag} is set.  @xref{@code{@@set @@clear "
"@@value}}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:18707
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@click@{@}"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:18710
msgid ""
"Represent a single ``click'' in a GUI@.  Used within "
"@code{@@clicksequence}.  @xref{Click Sequences}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:18711
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@clicksequence@{@var{action} @@click@{@} @var{action}@}"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:18713
msgid "Represent a sequence of clicks in a GUI@.  @xref{Click Sequences}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:18714
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@clickstyle @@@var{cmd}"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:18718
msgid ""
"Execute @@@var{cmd} for each @code{@@click}; the default is @code{@@arrow}.  "
"The usual following empty braces on @@@var{cmd} are omitted.  @xref{Click "
"Sequences}."
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:18722
msgid ""
"Indicate an expression, a syntactically complete token of a program, or a "
"program name.  @xref{@code{@@code}}."
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:18727
msgid ""
"Control output of @code{`} and @code{'} in code examples.  @xref{Inserting "
"Quote Characters}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:18728
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@comma@{@}"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:18731
msgid ""
"Insert a comma `,' character; only needed when a literal comma would be "
"taken as an argument separator.  @xref{Inserting a Comma}."
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:18734
msgid ""
"Indicate a command name, such as @command{ls}.  @xref{@code{@@command}}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:18735
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@comment @var{comment}"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:18739
msgid ""
"Begin a comment in Texinfo.  The rest of the line does not appear in any "
"output.  A synonym for @code{@@c}.  @xref{Comments}."
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:18744
msgid ""
"Print a complete table of contents or specify that a table of content should "
"be output, for formats that may output a table of contents.  @xref{Contents, "
", Generating a Table of Contents}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:18745
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@copying"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:18748
msgid ""
"Specify copyright holders and copying conditions for the document.  Pair "
"with @code{@@end copying}.  @xref{@code{@@copying}}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:18749
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@copyright@{@}"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:18752
msgid "Generate the copyright symbol @copyright{}.  @xref{@code{@@copyright}}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:18753
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@defblock"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:18756
msgid ""
"Start a block containing definitions.  Pair with @samp{@@end defblock}.  "
"@xref{Generic Definition Commands}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:18757
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@defcodeindex @var{index-name}"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:18760
msgid ""
"Define a new index and its indexing command.  Print entries in an "
"@code{@@code} font.  @xref{New Indices, , Defining New Indices}."
msgstr ""

#. type: itemx
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:18762
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@defcvx @var{category} @var{class} @var{name}"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:18767
msgid ""
"Format a description for a variable associated with a class in "
"object-oriented programming.  Takes three arguments: the category of thing "
"being defined, the class to which it belongs, and its name.  "
"@xref{Definition Commands}."
msgstr ""

#. type: itemx
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:18769
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@deffnx @var{category} @var{name} @var{arguments}@dots{}"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:18774
msgid ""
"Format a description for a function, interactive command, or similar entity "
"that may take arguments.  @code{@@deffn} takes as arguments the category of "
"entity being described, the name of this particular entity, and its "
"arguments, if any.  @xref{Definition Commands}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:18775
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@defindex @var{index-name}"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:18778
msgid ""
"Define a new index and its indexing command.  Print entries in a roman "
"font.  @xref{New Indices, , Defining New Indices}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:18779
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@definfoenclose @var{newcmd}, @var{before}, @var{after}"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:18784
msgid ""
"Create a new command @code{@@@var{newcmd}} for online formats that marks "
"text by enclosing it in strings that precede and follow the text.  "
"@xref{@code{@@definfoenclose}}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:18785
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@defivar @var{class} @var{instance-variable-name}"
msgstr ""

#. type: itemx
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:18786
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@defivarx @var{class} @var{instance-variable-name}"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:18790
msgid ""
"Format a description for an instance variable in object-oriented "
"programming.  The command is equivalent to @samp{@@defcv @{Instance "
"Variable@} @dots{}}.  @xref{Definition Commands}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:18791
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@defline @var{category} @var{name} @var{arguments}@dots{}"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:18795
msgid ""
"Use within a @code{@@defblock} environment to give the heading prototype "
"line for a symbol being defined.  This command does not create any index "
"entries.  @xref{Generic Definition Commands}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:18796
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@defmac @var{macroname} @var{arguments}@dots{}"
msgstr ""

#. type: itemx
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:18797
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@defmacx @var{macroname} @var{arguments}@dots{}"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:18800
msgid ""
"Format a description for a macro; equivalent to @samp{@@deffn Macro "
"@dots{}}.  @xref{Definition Commands}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:18801
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@defmethod @var{class} @var{method-name} @var{arguments}@dots{}"
msgstr ""

#. type: itemx
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:18802
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@defmethodx @var{class} @var{method-name} @var{arguments}@dots{}"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:18806
msgid ""
"Format a description for a method in object-oriented programming; equivalent "
"to @samp{@@defop Method @dots{}}.  @xref{Definition Commands}."
msgstr ""

#. type: itemx
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:18808
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@defopx @var{category} @var{class} @var{name} @var{arguments}@dots{}"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:18814
msgid ""
"Format a description for an operation in object-oriented programming.  "
"@code{@@defop} takes as arguments the name of the category of operation, the "
"name of the operation's class, the name of the operation, and its arguments, "
"if any.  @xref{Definition Commands}, and @ref{Abstract Objects}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:18815
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@defopt @var{option-name}"
msgstr ""

#. type: itemx
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:18816
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@defoptx @var{option-name}"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:18819
msgid ""
"Format a description for a user option; equivalent to @samp{@@defvr @{User "
"Option@} @dots{}}.  @xref{Definition Commands}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:18820
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@defspec @var{special-form-name} @var{arguments}@dots{}"
msgstr ""

#. type: itemx
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:18821
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@defspecx @var{special-form-name} @var{arguments}@dots{}"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:18824
msgid ""
"Format a description for a special form; equivalent to @samp{@@deffn "
"@{Special Form@} @dots{}}.  @xref{Definition Commands}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:18825
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@deftp @var{category} @var{name-of-type} @var{attributes}@dots{}"
msgstr ""

#. type: itemx
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:18826
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@deftpx @var{category} @var{name-of-type} @var{attributes}@dots{}"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:18831
msgid ""
"Format a description for a data type; its arguments are the category, the "
"name of the type (e.g., @samp{int}) , and then the names of attributes of "
"objects of that type.  @xref{Definition Commands}, and @ref{Data Types}."
msgstr ""

#. type: itemx
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:18833
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@deftypecvx @var{category} @var{class} @var{data-type} @var{name}"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:18836
msgid ""
"Format a description for a typed class variable in object-oriented "
"programming.  @xref{Definition Commands}, and @ref{Abstract Objects}."
msgstr ""

#. type: itemx
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:18838
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"@@deftypefnx @var{category} @var{data-type} @var{name} @var{arguments}@dots{}"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:18843
msgid ""
"Format a description for a function or similar entity that may take "
"arguments and that is typed.  @code{@@deftypefn} takes as arguments the "
"category of entity being described, the type, the name of the entity, and "
"its arguments, if any.  @xref{Definition Commands}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:18844
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@deftypefnnewline @var{on-off}"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:18848
msgid ""
"Specifies whether return types for @code{@@deftypefn} and similar are "
"printed on lines by themselves; default is off.  @xref{Typed Functions,, "
"Functions in Typed Languages}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:18849
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@deftypefun @var{data-type} @var{function-name} @var{arguments}@dots{}"
msgstr ""

#. type: itemx
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:18850
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"@@deftypefunx @var{data-type} @var{function-name} @var{arguments}@dots{}"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:18854
msgid ""
"Format a description for a function in a typed language.  The command is "
"equivalent to @samp{@@deftypefn Function @dots{}}.  @xref{Definition "
"Commands}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:18855
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@deftypeivar @var{class} @var{data-type} @var{variable-name}"
msgstr ""

#. type: itemx
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:18856
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@deftypeivarx @var{class} @var{data-type} @var{variable-name}"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:18859
msgid ""
"Format a description for a typed instance variable in object-oriented "
"programming. @xref{Definition Commands}, and @ref{Abstract Objects}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:18860
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"@@deftypeline @var{category} @var{data-type} @var{name} "
"@var{arguments}@dots{}"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:18864
msgid ""
"Use within a @code{@@defblock} environment to give the heading prototype "
"line for a symbol being defined, with data types.  This command does not "
"create any index entries.  @xref{Generic Definition Commands}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:18865
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"@@deftypemethod @var{class} @var{data-type} @var{method-name} "
"@var{arguments}@dots{}"
msgstr ""

#. type: itemx
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:18866
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"@@deftypemethodx @var{class} @var{data-type} @var{method-name} "
"@var{arguments}@dots{}"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:18869
msgid ""
"Format a description for a typed method in object-oriented programming.  "
"@xref{Definition Commands}."
msgstr ""

#. type: itemx
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:18871
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"@@deftypeopx @var{category} @var{class} @var{data-type} @var{name} "
"@var{arguments}@dots{}"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:18874
msgid ""
"Format a description for a typed operation in object-oriented programming.  "
"@xref{Definition Commands}, and @ref{Abstract Objects}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:18875
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@deftypevar @var{data-type} @var{variable-name}"
msgstr ""

#. type: itemx
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:18876
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@deftypevarx @var{data-type} @var{variable-name}"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:18880
msgid ""
"Format a description for a variable in a typed language.  The command is "
"equivalent to @samp{@@deftypevr Variable @dots{}}.  @xref{Definition "
"Commands}."
msgstr ""

#. type: itemx
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:18882
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@deftypevrx @var{category} @var{data-type} @var{name}"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:18887
msgid ""
"Format a description for something like a variable in a typed language---an "
"entity that records a value.  Takes as arguments the category of entity "
"being described, the type, and the name of the entity.  @xref{Definition "
"Commands}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:18888
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@defun @var{function-name} @var{arguments}@dots{}"
msgstr ""

#. type: itemx
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:18889
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@defunx @var{function-name} @var{arguments}@dots{}"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:18892
msgid ""
"Format a description for a function; equivalent to @samp{@@deffn Function "
"@dots{}}.  @xref{Definition Commands}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:18893
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@defvar @var{variable-name}"
msgstr ""

#. type: itemx
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:18894
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@defvarx @var{variable-name}"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:18897
msgid ""
"Format a description for a variable; equivalent to @samp{@@defvr Variable "
"@dots{}}.  @xref{Definition Commands}."
msgstr ""

#. type: itemx
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:18899
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@defvrx @var{category} @var{name}"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:18903
msgid ""
"Format a description for any kind of variable.  @code{@@defvr} takes as "
"arguments the category of the entity and the name of the entity.  "
"@xref{Definition Commands}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:18904
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@detailmenu"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:18907
msgid ""
"Mark the (optional) detailed node listing in a master menu.  @xref{Master "
"Menu Parts}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:18911
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@DH@{@}"
msgstr ""

#. type: itemx
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:18912
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@dh@{@}"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:18915
msgid ""
"Generate the uppercase and lowercase Icelandic letter eth, respectively: "
"@DH{}, @dh{}.  @xref{Inserting Accents}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:18916
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@dircategory @var{dirpart}"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:18918
msgid "Specify a category for the manual.  @xref{Directory Category}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:18919
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@direntry"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:18922
msgid ""
"Begin the Info directory menu entry for this file.  Pair with @code{@@end "
"direntry}.  @xref{Installing Dir Entries}."
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:18927
msgid ""
"Begin a kind of example.  Like @code{@@example} (indent text, do not fill), "
"but do not select a new font.  Pair with @code{@@end display}.  "
"@xref{@code{@@display}}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:18928
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@displaymath"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:18930
msgid "Format a block of math in ``display'' format.  @xref{Inserting Math}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:18931
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@dmn@{@var{dimension}@}"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:18933
msgid "Format a unit of measure, as in 12@dmn{pt}.  @xref{@code{@@dmn}}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:18934
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@docbook"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:18937
msgid ""
"Enter DocBook completely.  Pair with @code{@@end docbook}.  @xref{Raw "
"Formatter Commands}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:18938
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@documentdescription"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:18941
msgid ""
"Set the document description text, included in the HTML output.  Pair with "
"@code{@@end documentdescription}.  @xref{@code{@@documentdescription}}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:18942
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@documentencoding @var{enc}"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:18945
msgid ""
"Declare the input encoding to be @var{enc}.  "
"@xref{@code{@@documentencoding}}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:18946
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@documentlanguage @var{CC}"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:18949
msgid ""
"Declare the document language as the two-character ISO-639 abbreviation "
"@var{CC}.  @xref{@code{@@documentlanguage}}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:18950
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@dotaccent@{@var{c}@}"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:18953
msgid ""
"Generate a dot accent over the character @var{c}, as in @dotaccent{o}.  "
"@xref{Inserting Accents}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:18954
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@dotless@{@var{i-or-j}@}"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:18957
msgid ""
"Generate dotless i (`@dotless{i}') and dotless j (`@dotless{j}').  "
"@xref{Inserting Accents}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:18958
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@dots@{@}"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:18961
msgid "Generate an ellipsis, @samp{@dots{}}.  @xref{@code{@@dots}}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:18962
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@email@{@var{address}[, @var{displayed-text}]@}"
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:18965
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@emph@{@var{text}@}"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:18967
msgid "Emphasize @var{text}.  @xref{Emphasis, , Emphasizing Text}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:18968
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@end @var{environment}"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:18971
msgid ""
"Ends @var{environment}, as in @samp{@@end example}.  @xref{Formatting "
"Commands,,@@-commands}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:18972
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@enddots@{@}"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:18975
msgid ""
"Generate an end-of-sentence ellipsis, like this: @enddots{} "
"@xref{@code{@@dots}}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:18976
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@enumerate [@var{number-or-letter}]"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:18980
msgid ""
"Begin a numbered list, using @code{@@item} for each entry.  Optionally, "
"start list with @var{number-or-letter}.  Pair with @code{@@end enumerate}.  "
"@xref{@code{@@enumerate}}."
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:18984
msgid ""
"Indicate an environment variable name, such as @env{PATH}.  "
"@xref{@code{@@env}}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:18985
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@equiv@{@}"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:18988
msgid ""
"Indicate to the reader the exact equivalence of two forms with a glyph: "
"@samp{@equiv{}}.  @xref{@code{@@equiv}}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:18989
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@error@{@}"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:18992
msgid ""
"Indicate to the reader with a glyph that the following text is an error "
"message: @samp{@error{}}.  @xref{@code{@@error}}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:18993
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@errormsg@{@var{msg}@}"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:18997
msgid ""
"Report @var{msg} as an error to standard error, and exit unsuccessfully.  "
"Texinfo commands within @var{msg} are expanded to plain text.  "
"@xref{Conditionals}, and @ref{External Macro Processors}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:18998
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@euro@{@}"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19000
msgid "Generate the Euro currency sign.  @xref{@code{@@euro}}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19001
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@evenfooting [@var{left}] @@| [@var{center}] @@| [@var{right}]"
msgstr ""

#. type: itemx
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19002
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@evenheading [@var{left}] @@| [@var{center}] @@| [@var{right}]"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19006
msgid ""
"Specify page footings resp.@: headings for even-numbered (left-hand)  "
"pages.  @xref{Custom Headings, , How to Make Your Own Headings}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19007
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@everyfooting [@var{left}] @@| [@var{center}] @@| [@var{right}]"
msgstr ""

#. type: itemx
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19008
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@everyheading [@var{left}] @@| [@var{center}] @@| [@var{right}]"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19011
msgid ""
"Specify page footings resp.@: headings for every page.  Not relevant to "
"Info.  @xref{Custom Headings, , How to Make Your Own Headings}."
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19017
msgid ""
"Begin an example.  Indent text, do not fill, and select fixed-width font.  "
"Pair with @code{@@end example}.  @code{@@example} accepts optional "
"arguments, separated by commas.  It is recommended to set the first argument "
"to the language of the example code.  @xref{@code{@@example}}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19018
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@exampleindent @var{indent}"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19021
msgid ""
"Indent example-like environments by @var{indent} number of spaces (perhaps "
"0).  @xref{@code{@@exampleindent}}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19022
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@exclamdown@{@}"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19024
msgid "Generate an upside-down exclamation point.  @xref{Inserting Accents}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19025
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@exdent @var{line-of-text}"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19027
msgid "Remove any indentation a line might have.  @xref{@code{@@exdent}}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19028
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@expansion@{@}"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19031
msgid ""
"Indicate the result of a macro expansion to the reader with a special glyph: "
"@samp{@expansion{}}.  @xref{@code{@@expansion}}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19032
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@file@{@var{filename}@}"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19035
msgid ""
"Highlight the name of a file, buffer, node, directory, etc.  "
"@xref{@code{@@file}}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19036
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@finalout"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19039
msgid ""
"Prevent @TeX{} from printing large black warning rectangles beside over-wide "
"lines.  @xref{Overfull hboxes}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19040
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@findex @var{entry}"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19043
msgid ""
"Add @var{entry} to the index of functions.  @xref{Index Entries, , Defining "
"the Entries of an Index}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19044
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@firstparagraphindent @var{word}"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19048
msgid ""
"Control indentation of the first paragraph after section headers according "
"to @var{word}, one of `none' or `insert'.  "
"@xref{@code{@@firstparagraphindent}}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19049
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@float"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19052
msgid ""
"Environment to define floating material.  Pair with @code{@@end float}.  "
"@xref{Floats}."
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19059
msgid ""
"Do not fill text; left (right) justify every line while leaving the right "
"(left) end ragged.  Leave font as is.  Pair with @code{@@end flushleft} "
"(@code{@@end flushright}).  @xref{@code{@@flushleft @@flushright}}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19060
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@fonttextsize @var{10-11}"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19063
msgid ""
"Change the size of the main body font in the printed output.  @xref{Fonts}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19064
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@footnote@{@var{text-of-footnote}@}"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19070
msgid ""
"Enter a footnote, for a reference that documents or elucidates the primary "
"text.  Footnote text is printed at the bottom of the page in printed "
"output.  In other formats, footnote text can be output in the same node, in "
"a separate node, or simply be marked as being footnote text.  "
"@xref{Footnotes}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19071
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@footnotestyle @var{style}"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19076
msgid ""
"Specify a footnote style, either @samp{end} for the end node style or "
"@samp{separate} for the separate style.  In the separate style, footnotes "
"are put in a separate node or file.  @xref{Footnote Styles}."
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19080
msgid ""
"Begin a kind of example.  Like @code{@@display}, but do not indent.  Pair "
"with @code{@@end format}.  @xref{@code{@@example}}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19081
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@frenchspacing @var{on-off}"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19083
msgid "Control spacing after punctuation.  @xref{@code{@@frenchspacing}}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19084
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@ftable @var{formatting-command}"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19089
msgid ""
"Begin a two-column table, using @code{@@item} for each entry.  Automatically "
"enter each of the items in the first column into the index of functions.  "
"Pair with @code{@@end ftable}.  The same as @code{@@table}, except for "
"indexing.  @xref{@code{@@ftable @@vtable}}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19090
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@geq@{@}"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19092
msgid ""
"Generate a greater-than-or-equal sign, `@geq{}'.  @xref{@code{@@geq @@leq}}."
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19096
msgid ""
"Disallow page breaks within following text.  Pair with @code{@@end group}.  "
"Ignored in Info.  @xref{@code{@@group}}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19097
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@guillemetleft@{@}"
msgstr ""

#. type: itemx
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19098
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@guillemetright@{@}"
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19099
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@guillemotleft@{@}"
msgstr ""

#. type: itemx
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19100
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@guillemotright@{@}"
msgstr ""

#. type: itemx
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19101
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@guilsinglleft@{@}"
msgstr ""

#. type: itemx
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19102
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@guilsinglright@{@}"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19108
msgid ""
"Double and single angle quotation marks: @guillemetleft{} @guillemetright{} "
"@guilsinglleft{} @guilsinglright{}.  @code{@@guillemotleft} and "
"@code{@@guillemotright} are synonyms for @code{@@guillemetleft} and "
"@code{@@guillemetright}.  @xref{Inserting Quotation Marks}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19109
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@H@{@var{c}@}"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19111
msgid "Generate the long Hungarian umlaut accent over @var{c}, as in @H{o}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19112
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@hashchar@{@}"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19116
msgid ""
"Insert a hash `#' character; only needed when a literal hash would introduce "
"@code{#line} directive.  @xref{Inserting a Hashsign}, and @ref{External "
"Macro Processors}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19117
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@heading @var{title}"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19120
msgid ""
"Print an unnumbered section-like heading, but omit from the table of "
"contents.  @xref{@code{@@unnumberedsec @@appendixsec @@heading}}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19121
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@headings @var{on-off-single-double}"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19124
msgid ""
"Turn page headings on or off, and/or specify single-sided or double-sided "
"page headings for printing.  @xref{@code{@@headings}}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19125
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@headitem"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19127
msgid "Begin a heading row in a multitable.  @xref{Multitable Rows}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19128
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@headitemfont@{@var{text}@}"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19131
msgid ""
"Set @var{text} in the font used for multitable heading rows; mostly useful "
"in multitable templates.  @xref{Multitable Rows}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19132
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@html"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19135
msgid ""
"Enter HTML completely.  Pair with @code{@@end html}.  @xref{Raw Formatter "
"Commands}."
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19138
msgid "Explicitly define hyphenation points.  @xref{@code{@@- @@hyphenation}}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19139
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@i@{@var{text}@}"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19141
msgid "Set @var{text} in an @i{italic} font, when possible.  @xref{Fonts}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19142
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@ifclear @var{txivar}"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19146
msgid ""
"If the Texinfo variable @var{txivar} is not set, format the following text.  "
"Pair with @code{@@end ifclear}.  @xref{@code{@@set @@clear @@value}}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19147
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@ifcommanddefined @var{txicmd}"
msgstr ""

#. type: itemx
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19148
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@ifcommandnotdefined @var{txicmd}"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19152
msgid ""
"If the Texinfo code @samp{@@@var{txicmd}} is (not) defined, format the "
"follow text.  Pair with the corresponding @code{@@end ifcommand...}.  "
"@xref{Testing for Texinfo Commands}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19153
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@ifdocbook"
msgstr ""

#. type: itemx
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19154
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@ifhtml"
msgstr ""

#. type: itemx
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19155
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@ifinfo"
msgstr ""

#. type: itemx
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19156
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@iflatex"
msgstr ""

#. type: itemx
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19157
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@ifplaintext"
msgstr ""

#. type: itemx
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19158
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@ifxml"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19164
msgid ""
"Begin text that will appear only in the given output format.  "
"@code{@@ifinfo} output appears in both Info and (for historical "
"compatibility) plain text output.  Pair with @code{@@end ifdocbook} resp.@: "
"@code{@@end ifhtml}@enddots{} @xref{Conditionals}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19165
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@ifnotdocbook"
msgstr ""

#. type: itemx
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19166
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@ifnothtml"
msgstr ""

#. type: itemx
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19167
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@ifnotlatex"
msgstr ""

#. type: itemx
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19168
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@ifnotplaintext"
msgstr ""

#. type: itemx
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19169
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@ifnottex"
msgstr ""

#. type: itemx
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19170
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@ifnotxml"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19175
msgid ""
"Begin text to be ignored in one output format but not the others.  "
"@code{@@ifnothtml} text is omitted from HTML output, etc.  Pair with the "
"corresponding @code{@@end ifnot@var{format}}.  @xref{Conditionals}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19176
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@ifnotinfo"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19180
msgid ""
"Begin text to appear in output other than Info and (for historical "
"compatibility) plain text.  Pair with @code{@@end ifnotinfo}.  "
"@xref{Conditionals}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19181
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@ifset @var{txivar}"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19185
msgid ""
"If the Texinfo variable @var{txivar} is set, format the following text.  "
"Pair with @code{@@end ifset}.  @xref{@code{@@set @@clear @@value}}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19186
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@iftex"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19189
msgid ""
"Begin text to appear only in the @TeX{} output.  Pair with @code{@@end "
"iftex}.  @xref{Conditionals}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19190
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@ignore"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19193
msgid ""
"Begin text that will not appear in any output.  Pair with @code{@@end "
"ignore}.  @xref{Comments, , Comments and Ignored Text}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19194
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"@@image@{@var{filename}, [@var{width}], [@var{height}], [@var{alt}], "
"[@var{ext}]@}"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19198
msgid ""
"Include graphics image in external @var{filename} scaled to the given "
"@var{width} and/or @var{height}, using @var{alt} text and looking for "
"@samp{@var{filename}.@var{ext}} in HTML@.  @xref{Images}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19199
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@include @var{filename}"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19201
msgid ""
"Read the contents of Texinfo source file @var{filename}.  @xref{Include "
"Files}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19202
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@indent"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19204
msgid "Insert paragraph indentation.  @xref{@code{@@indent}}."
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19208
msgid ""
"Indent a block of arbitrary text on the left.  Pair with @code{@@end "
"indentedblock}.  @xref{@code{@@indentedblock}}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19209
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@indicateurl@{@var{indicateurl}@}"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19212
msgid ""
"Indicate text that is a uniform resource locator for the World Wide Web.  "
"@xref{@code{@@indicateurl}}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19213
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@inforef@{@var{node-name}, [@var{entry-name}], @var{info-file-name}@}"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19216
msgid ""
"Make a cross-reference to an Info file for which there is no printed "
"manual.  @xref{@code{@@inforef}}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19217
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@inlinefmt@{@var{fmt}, @var{text}@}"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19220
msgid ""
"Insert @var{text} only if the output format is @var{fmt}.  @xref{Inline "
"Conditionals}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19221
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@inlinefmtifelse@{@var{fmt}, @var{text}, @var{else-text}@}"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19223
msgid ""
"Insert @var{text} if the output format is @var{fmt}, else @var{else-text}."
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19227
msgid "Insert @var{text} only if the Texinfo variable @var{var} is (not) set."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19228
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@inlineraw@{@var{fmt}, @var{raw-text}@}"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19231
msgid ""
"Insert @var{text} as in a raw conditional, only if the output format is "
"@var{fmt}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19232
#, no-wrap
msgid "\\input @var{macro-definitions-file}"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19239
msgid ""
"Use the specified macro definitions file.  This command is used only in the "
"first line of a Texinfo file to cause @TeX{} to make use of the "
"@file{texinfo} macro definitions file.  The @code{\\} in @code{\\input} is "
"used instead of an @code{@@} because @TeX{} does not recognize @code{@@} "
"until after it has read the definitions file.  @xref{Texinfo File Header}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19240
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@insertcopying"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19243
msgid ""
"Insert the text previously defined with the @code{@@copying} environment.  "
"@xref{@code{@@insertcopying}}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19244
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@item"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19249
msgid ""
"Indicate the beginning of a marked paragraph for @code{@@itemize} and "
"@code{@@enumerate}; indicate the beginning of the text of a first column "
"entry for @code{@@table}, @code{@@ftable}, and @code{@@vtable}.  @xref{Lists "
"and Tables}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19250
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@itemize @var{mark-generating-character-or-command}"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19254
msgid ""
"Begin an unordered list: indented paragraphs with a mark, such as "
"@code{@@bullet}, inside the left margin at the beginning of each item.  Pair "
"with @code{@@end itemize}.  @xref{@code{@@itemize}}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19255
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@itemx"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19261
msgid ""
"Like @code{@@item} in @code{@@table}, @code{@@ftable}, and @code{@@vtable}, "
"but do not generate extra vertical space above the item text.  Thus, when "
"several items have the same description, use @code{@@item} for the first and "
"@code{@@itemx} for the others.  @xref{@code{@@itemx}}."
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19264
msgid ""
"Indicate characters of input to be typed by users.  @xref{@code{@@kbd}}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19265
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@kbdinputstyle @var{style}"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19269
msgid ""
"Specify when @code{@@kbd} should use a font distinct from @code{@@code} "
"according to @var{style}: @code{code}, @code{distinct}, @code{example}.  "
"@xref{@code{@@kbd}}."
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19272
msgid "Indicate the name of a key on a keyboard.  @xref{@code{@@key}}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19273
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@kindex @var{entry}"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19276
msgid ""
"Add @var{entry} to the index of keys.  @xref{Index Entries, , Defining the "
"Entries of an Index}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19277
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@L@{@}"
msgstr ""

#. type: itemx
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19278
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@l@{@}"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19281
msgid ""
"Generate the uppercase and lowercase Polish suppressed-L letters, "
"respectively: @L{}, @l{}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19282
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@LaTeX@{@}"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19284
msgid "Generate the @LaTeX{} logo.  @xref{@code{@@TeX @@LaTeX}}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19285
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@latex"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19288
msgid ""
"Enter @LaTeX{} completely.  Pair with @code{@@end latex}.  @xref{Raw "
"Formatter Commands}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19289
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@leq@{@}"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19291
msgid ""
"Generate a less-than-or-equal sign, `@leq{}'.  @xref{@code{@@geq @@leq}}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19292
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@linemacro @var{macroname} @{@var{params}@}"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19295
msgid ""
"Define a new macro which takes rest of the line as an argument, and expands "
"to a whole number of complete lines.  @xref{Line Macros}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19296
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@link@{@var{nodename}, @var{label}, @var{manual-name}@}"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19299
msgid ""
"Create a plain link with no visible markup or page reference.  "
"@xref{@code{@@link}}."
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19303
msgid ""
"Begin an example of Lisp code.  Indent text, do not fill, and select "
"fixed-width font.  Pair with @code{@@end lisp}.  @xref{@code{@@lisp}}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19304
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@listoffloats"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19307
msgid ""
"Produce a table-of-contents-like listing of @code{@@float}s.  "
"@xref{@code{@@listoffloats}}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19308
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@lowersections"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19312
msgid ""
"Change subsequent chapters to sections, sections to subsections, and so on. "
"@xref{Raise/lower sections, , @code{@@raisesections} and "
"@code{@@lowersections}}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19313
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@macro @var{macroname} @{@var{params}@}"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19316
msgid ""
"Define a new Texinfo command @code{@@@var{macroname}@{@var{params}@}}.  Pair "
"with @code{@@end macro}.  @xref{Defining Macros}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19317
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@majorheading @var{title}"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19322
msgid ""
"Print an unnumbered chapter-like heading, but omit from the table of "
"contents.  This generates more vertical whitespace before the heading than "
"the @code{@@chapheading} command.  @xref{@code{@@majorheading "
"@@chapheading}}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19323
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@math@{@var{mathematical-expression}@}"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19325
msgid "Format a mathematical expression.  @xref{Inserting Math}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19326
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@menu"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19329
msgid ""
"Mark the beginning of a menu of nodes.  No effect in a printed manual.  Pair "
"with @code{@@end menu}.  @xref{Menus}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19330
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@microtype @var{on-off}"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19332
msgid "Turn microtype on or off.  @xref{Microtypography}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19333
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@minus@{@}"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19335
msgid "Generate a minus sign, `@minus{}'.  @xref{@code{@@minus}}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19336
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@multitable @var{column-width-spec}"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19340
msgid ""
"Begin a multi-column table.  Begin each row with @code{@@item} or "
"@code{@@headitem}, and separate columns with @code{@@tab}.  Pair with "
"@code{@@end multitable}.  @xref{Multitable Column Widths}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19341
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@need @var{n}"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19345
msgid ""
"Start a new page in a printed manual if fewer than @var{n} mils (thousandths "
"of an inch) remain on the current page.  @xref{@code{@@need}}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19346
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@node @var{name}, [@var{next}], [@var{previous}], [@var{up}]"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19349
msgid ""
"Begin a new node.  Only the first argument is mandatory.  @xref{Writing a "
"Node}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19350
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@nodedescription @var{node-description}"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19353
msgid ""
"Provide a short elaboration of the purpose of a node.  @xref{Node "
"Descriptions}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19354
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@nodedescriptionblock"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19357
msgid ""
"Used to start a longer node description.  Pair with @samp{@@end "
"nodedescriptionblock}.  @xref{Node Descriptions}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19358
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@noindent"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19361
msgid ""
"Prevent text from being indented as if it were a new paragraph.  "
"@xref{@code{@@noindent}}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19362
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@novalidate"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19366
msgid ""
"Suppress validation of node references and omit creation of auxiliary files "
"with @TeX{}.  Use before any sectioning or cross-reference commands.  "
"@xref{Pointer Validation}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19367
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@O@{@}"
msgstr ""

#. type: itemx
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19368
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@o@{@}"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19371
msgid ""
"Generate the uppercase and lowercase O-with-slash letters, respectively: "
"@O{}, @o{}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19372
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@oddfooting [@var{left}] @@| [@var{center}] @@| [@var{right}]"
msgstr ""

#. type: itemx
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19373
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@oddheading [@var{left}] @@| [@var{center}] @@| [@var{right}]"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19377
msgid ""
"Specify page footings resp.@: headings for odd-numbered (right-hand)  "
"pages.  @xref{Custom Headings, , How to Make Your Own Headings}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19378
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@OE@{@}"
msgstr ""

#. type: itemx
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19379
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@oe@{@}"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19382
msgid ""
"Generate the uppercase and lowercase OE ligatures, respectively: @OE{}, "
"@oe{}.  @xref{Inserting Accents}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19383
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@ogonek@{@var{c}@}"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19386
msgid ""
"Generate an ogonek diacritic under the next character, as in @ogonek{a}.  "
"@xref{Inserting Accents}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19387
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@option@{@var{option-name}@}"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19390
msgid ""
"Indicate a command-line option, such as @option{-l} or @option{--help}.  "
"@xref{@code{@@option}}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19391
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@ordf@{@}"
msgstr ""

#. type: itemx
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19392
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@ordm@{@}"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19395
msgid ""
"Generate the feminine and masculine Spanish ordinals, respectively: @ordf{}, "
"@ordm{}.  @xref{Inserting Accents}."
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19398
msgid "Start a new page in a printed manual.  @xref{@code{@@page}}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19399
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@pagesizes [@var{width}][, @var{height}]"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19401
msgid "Change page dimensions.  @xref{pagesizes}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19402
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@paragraphindent @var{indent}"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19406
msgid ""
"Indent paragraphs by @var{indent} number of spaces (perhaps 0); preserve "
"source file indentation if @var{indent} is @code{asis}.  "
"@xref{@code{@@paragraphindent}}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19407
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@part @var{title}"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19411
msgid ""
"Begin a group of chapters or appendixes; included in the tables of "
"contents.  @xref{@code{@@part}}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19412
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@pindex @var{entry}"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19415
msgid ""
"Add @var{entry} to the index of programs.  @xref{Index Entries, , Defining "
"the Entries of an Index}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19416
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@point@{@}"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19419
msgid ""
"Indicate the position of point in a buffer to the reader with a glyph: "
"@samp{@point{}}.  @xref{@code{@@point}}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19420
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@pounds@{@}"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19423
msgid ""
"Generate the pounds sterling currency sign, @samp{@pounds{}}.  "
"@xref{@code{@@pounds}}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19424
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@print@{@}"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19427
msgid ""
"Indicate printed output to the reader with a glyph: @samp{@print{}}.  "
"@xref{@code{@@print}}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19428
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@printindex @var{index-name}"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19430
msgid ""
"Generate the index for @var{index-name}.  @xref{Printing Indices & Menus}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19431
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"@@pxref@{@var{node}, [@var{entry}], [@var{node-title}], [@var{info-file}], "
"[@var{printed-manual}]@}"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19437
msgid ""
"Make a reference to be used within parentheses.  Starts with a lowercase "
"`see' in a printed manual.  The first argument is mandatory, except for "
"references to whole manuals.  To refer to another manual as a whole, the "
"@var{printed-manual} and/or the @var{info-file} are the only required "
"arguments.  @xref{@code{@@pxref}}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19438
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@questiondown@{@}"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19440
msgid "Generate an upside-down question mark.  @xref{Inserting Accents}."
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19445
msgid ""
"Narrow the margins to indicate text that is quoted from another work.  Takes "
"optional argument specifying prefix text.  Pair with @code{@@end "
"quotation}.  @xref{@code{@@quotation}}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19446
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@quotedblleft@{@}"
msgstr ""

#. type: itemx
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19447
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@quotedblright@{@}"
msgstr ""

#. type: itemx
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19448
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@quoteleft@{@}"
msgstr ""

#. type: itemx
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19449
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@quoteright@{@}"
msgstr ""

#. type: itemx
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19450
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@quotedblbase@{@}"
msgstr ""

#. type: itemx
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19451
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@quotesinglbase@{@}"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19455
msgid ""
"Produce various quotation marks: @quotedblleft{} @quotedblright{} "
"@quoteleft{} @quoteright{} @quotedblbase{} @quotesinglbase{}.  "
"@xref{Inserting Quotation Marks}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19456
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@r@{@var{text}@}"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19459
msgid ""
"Set @var{text} in the regular @r{roman} font, if possible.  @xref{Fonts}."
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19464
msgid ""
"Fill text; left justify every line while leaving the right end ragged.  "
"Leave font as is.  Pair with @code{@@end raggedright}.  "
"@xref{@code{@@raggedright}}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19465
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@raisesections"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19468
msgid ""
"Change subsequent sections to chapters, subsections to sections, and so on.  "
"@xref{Raise/lower sections}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19469
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"@@ref@{@var{node}, [@var{entry}], [@var{node-title}], [@var{info-file}], "
"[@var{printed-manual}]@}"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19475
msgid ""
"Make a plain reference that does not start with any special text.  Follow "
"command with a punctuation mark.  The first argument is mandatory, except "
"for references to whole manuals.  To refer to another manual as a whole, the "
"@var{printed-manual} and/or the @var{info-file} are the only required "
"arguments.  @xref{@code{@@ref}}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19476
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@registeredsymbol@{@}"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19479
msgid ""
"Generate the legal symbol @registeredsymbol{}.  "
"@xref{@code{@@registeredsymbol}}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19480
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@result@{@}"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19483
msgid ""
"Indicate the result of an expression to the reader with a special glyph: "
"@samp{@result{}}.  @xref{@code{@@result}}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19484
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@ringaccent@{@var{c}@}"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19487
msgid ""
"Generate a ring accent over the next character, as in @ringaccent{o}.  "
"@xref{Inserting Accents}."
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19491
msgid ""
"Indicate a literal example of a sequence of characters, in general.  "
"@xref{@code{@@samp}}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19492
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@sansserif@{@var{text}@}"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19495
msgid ""
"Set @var{text} in a @sansserif{sans serif} font if possible.  @xref{Fonts}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19496
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@sc@{@var{text}@}"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19499
msgid ""
"Set @var{text} in a small caps font if possible, and uppercase in Info.  "
"@xref{Smallcaps}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19500
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@section @var{title}"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19505
msgid ""
"Begin a section within a chapter.  The section title appears in the table of "
"contents.  Within @code{@@chapter} and @code{@@appendix}, the section title "
"is numbered; within @code{@@unnumbered}, the section is unnumbered.  "
"@xref{@code{@@section}}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19506
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@seealso@{@var{index-text}@}"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19509
msgid ""
"Use in an index entry to refer the reader to another relevant index entry.  "
"@xref{Advanced Indexing}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19510
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@seeentry@{@var{index-text}@}"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19513
msgid ""
"Use in an index entry to redirect the reader to another index entry.  "
"@xref{Advanced Indexing}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19514
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@set @var{txivar} [@var{string}]"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19517
msgid ""
"Define the Texinfo variable @var{txivar}, optionally to the value "
"@var{string}.  @xref{@code{@@set @@clear @@value}}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19518
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@setchapternewpage @var{on-off-odd}"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19521
msgid ""
"Specify whether chapters start on new pages, and if so, whether on "
"odd-numbered (right-hand) new pages.  @xref{@code{@@setchapternewpage}}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19522
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@setfilename @var{info-file-name}"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19525
msgid ""
"Provide a name to be used for the output files.  This command is ignored for "
"@TeX{} formatting.  @xref{@code{@@setfilename}}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19526
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@settitle @var{title}"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19530
msgid ""
"Specify the title for page headers in a printed manual, and the default "
"document title for HTML.  @xref{@code{@@settitle}}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19531
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@shortcaption"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19534
msgid ""
"Define the short caption for a @code{@@float}.  @xref{@code{@@caption "
"@@shortcaption}}."
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19540
msgid ""
"Print a short table of contents, with chapter-level entries only, or specify "
"that a short table of contents should be output.  For formats that may "
"output a short table of contents.  @xref{Contents, , Generating a Table of "
"Contents}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19541
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@shorttitlepage @var{title}"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19543
msgid "Generate a minimal title page.  @xref{@code{@@titlepage}}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19544
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@slanted@{@var{text}@}"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19546
msgid "Set @var{text} in a @slanted{slanted} font if possible.  @xref{Fonts}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19547
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@smallbook"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19550
msgid ""
"In printed output, use a 7 by 9.25 inch format rather than the regular 8.5 "
"by 11 inch format.  @xref{@code{@@smallbook}}."
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19555
msgid ""
"Begin a kind of example.  Like @code{@@display}, but use a smaller font size "
"where possible.  Pair with @code{@@end smalldisplay}.  @xref{small}."
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19560
msgid ""
"Begin an example.  Like @code{@@example}, but use a smaller font size where "
"possible.  Pair with @code{@@end smallexample}.  @xref{small}."
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19565
msgid ""
"Begin a kind of example.  Like @code{@@format}, but use a smaller font size "
"where possible.  Pair with @code{@@end smallformat}.  @xref{small}."
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19570
msgid ""
"Like @code{@@indentedblock}, but use a smaller font size where possible.  "
"Pair with @code{@@end smallindentedblock}.  @xref{small}."
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19574
msgid ""
"Begin an example of Lisp code.  Same as @code{@@smallexample}.  Pair with "
"@code{@@end smalllisp}.  @xref{small}."
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19578
msgid ""
"Like @code{@@quotation}, but use a smaller font size where possible.  Pair "
"with @code{@@end smallquotation}.  @xref{small}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19579
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@sortas @{@var{key}@}"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19582
msgid ""
"Used in the arguments to index commands to give a string by which the index "
"entry should be sorted.  @xref{Indexing Commands}."
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19585
msgid "Skip @var{n} blank lines.  @xref{@code{@@sp}}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19586
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@ss@{@}"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19588
msgid ""
"Generate the German sharp-S es-zet letter, @ss{}.  @xref{Inserting Accents}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19589
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@strong @{@var{text}@}"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19592
msgid ""
"Emphasize @var{text} more strongly than @code{@@emph}.  @xref{emph & strong, "
", Emphasizing Text}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19593
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@sub @{@var{text}@}"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19595
msgid ""
"Set @var{text} as a subscript.  @xref{Inserting Subscripts and Superscripts}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19596
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@subentry"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19599
msgid ""
"Use in an index entry to separate parts of a multi-level entry.  "
"@xref{Advanced Indexing}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19600
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@subheading @var{title}"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19604
msgid ""
"Print an unnumbered subsection-like heading, but omit from the table of "
"contents of a printed manual.  @xref{@code{@@unnumberedsubsec "
"@@appendixsubsec @@subheading}}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19605
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@subsection @var{title}"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19610
msgid ""
"Begin a subsection within a section.  The subsection title appears in the "
"table of contents.  Same context-dependent numbering as @code{@@section}.  "
"@xref{@code{@@subsection}}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19611
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@subsubheading @var{title}"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19614
msgid ""
"Print an unnumbered subsubsection-like heading, but omit from the table of "
"contents of a printed manual.  @xref{@code{@@subsubsection}}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19615
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@subsubsection @var{title}"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19619
msgid ""
"Begin a subsubsection within a subsection.  The subsubsection title appears "
"in the table of contents.  Same context-dependent numbering as "
"@code{@@section}.  @xref{@code{@@subsubsection}}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19620
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@subtitle @var{title}"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19622
msgid ""
"Set a subtitle for the title page.  @xref{@code{@@title @@subtitle "
"@@author}}."
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19626
msgid ""
"Print or specify a short table of contents.  Synonym for "
"@code{@@shortcontents}.  @xref{Contents, , Generating a Table of Contents}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19627
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@sup @{@var{text}@}"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19629
msgid ""
"Set @var{text} as a superscript.  @xref{Inserting Subscripts and "
"Superscripts}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19630
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@syncodeindex @var{from-index} @var{to-index}"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19634
msgid ""
"Merge the index named in the first argument into the index named in the "
"second argument, formatting the entries from the first index with "
"@code{@@code}.  @xref{Combining Indices}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19635
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@synindex @var{from-index} @var{to-index}"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19639
msgid ""
"Merge the index named in the first argument into the index named in the "
"second argument.  Do not change the font of @var{from-index} entries.  "
"@xref{Combining Indices}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19640
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@t@{@var{text}@}"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19643
msgid ""
"Set @var{text} in a @t{fixed-width}, typewriter-like font, if possible.  "
"@xref{Fonts}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19644
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@tab"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19646
msgid "Separate columns in a row of a multitable.  @xref{Multitable Rows}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19647
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@table @var{formatting-command}"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19654
msgid ""
"Begin a two-column table (description list), using @code{@@item} for each "
"entry.  Write each first column entry on the same line as @code{@@item}.  "
"First column entries are printed in the font resulting from "
"@var{formatting-command}.  Pair with @code{@@end table}.  @xref{Two-column "
"Tables, , Making a Two-column Table}.  Also see @ref{@code{@@ftable "
"@@vtable}}, and @ref{@code{@@itemx}}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19655
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@TeX@{@}"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19657
msgid "Generate the @TeX{} logo.  @xref{@code{@@TeX @@LaTeX}}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19658
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@tex"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19661
msgid ""
"Enter @TeX{} completely.  Pair with @code{@@end tex}.  @xref{Raw Formatter "
"Commands}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19662
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@textdegree@{@}"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19664
msgid "Generate the degree symbol.  @xref{@code{@@textdegree}}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19665
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:22874
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@thischapter"
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19666
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:22865
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@thischaptername"
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19667
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:22869
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@thischapternum"
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19668
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:22860
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@thissection"
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19669
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:22852
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@thissectionname"
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19670
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:22856
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@thissectionnum"
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19671
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:22884
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@thisfile"
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19672
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:22848
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@thispage"
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19673
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:22879
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@thistitle"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19681
msgid ""
"Only allowed in a heading or footing.  Stands for, respectively, the number "
"and name of the current chapter (in the format `Chapter 1: Title'), the "
"current chapter name only, the current chapter number only, the number and "
"name of the current section, the current section name only, the current "
"section number only, the file name, the current page number, and the title "
"of the document.  @xref{Custom Headings,, How to Make Your Own Headings}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19682
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@TH@{@}"
msgstr ""

#. type: itemx
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19683
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@th@{@}"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19686
msgid ""
"Generate the uppercase and lowercase Icelandic letter thorn, respectively: "
"@TH{}, @th{}.  @xref{Inserting Accents}."
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19690
msgid ""
"Generate a normal interword space at which a line break is not allowed.  "
"@xref{@code{@@tie}}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19691
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@tieaccent@{@var{cc}@}"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19694
msgid ""
"Generate a tie-after accent over the next two characters @var{cc}, as in "
"`@tieaccent{oo}'.  @xref{Inserting Accents}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19695
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@tindex @var{entry}"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19698
msgid ""
"Add @var{entry} to the index of data types.  @xref{Index Entries, , Defining "
"the Entries of an Index}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19699
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@title @var{title}"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19701
msgid ""
"Set the title for the title page.  @xref{@code{@@title @@subtitle @@author}}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19702
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@titlefont@{@var{text}@}"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19705
msgid ""
"Print @var{text} in a larger than normal font, if possible.  "
"@xref{@code{@@titlefont @@center @@sp}}."
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19710
msgid ""
"Begin the title page.  Write the command on a line of its own, paired with "
"@code{@@end titlepage}.  The title page is not output, in the default case, "
"in online formats.  @xref{@code{@@titlepage}}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19711
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@today@{@}"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19714
msgid ""
"Insert the current date, in `1 Jan 1900' style.  @xref{Custom Headings, , "
"How to Make Your Own Headings}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19715
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@top @var{title}"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19720
msgid ""
"Mark the topmost @code{@@node} in the file, which must be defined on the "
"line immediately preceding the @code{@@top} command.  The title is formatted "
"as a chapter-level heading.  In @TeX{} the @code{@@top} command is merely a "
"synonym for @code{@@unnumbered}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19721
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@U@{@var{hex}@}"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19724
msgid ""
"Output a representation of Unicode character U+@var{hex}.  @xref{Inserting "
"Unicode}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19725
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@u@{@var{c}@}"
msgstr ""

#. type: itemx
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19726
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@ubaraccent@{@var{c}@}"
msgstr ""

#. type: itemx
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19727
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@udotaccent@{@var{c}@}"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19731
msgid ""
"Generate a breve, underbar, or underdot accent, respectively, over or under "
"the character @var{c}, as in @u{o}, @ubaraccent{o}, @udotaccent{o}.  "
"@xref{Inserting Accents}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19732
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@unmacro @var{macroname}"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19735
msgid ""
"Undefine the macro @code{@@@var{macroname}} if it has been defined.  "
"@xref{Defining Macros}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19736
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@unnumbered @var{title}"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19739
msgid ""
"Begin a chapter that appears without chapter numbers of any kind.  The title "
"appears in the table of contents.  @xref{@code{@@unnumbered @@appendix}}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19740
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@unnumberedsec @var{title}"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19744
msgid ""
"Begin a section that appears without section numbers of any kind.  The title "
"appears in the table of contents.  @xref{@code{@@unnumberedsec @@appendixsec "
"@@heading}}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19745
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@unnumberedsubsec @var{title}"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19748
msgid ""
"Begin an unnumbered subsection.  The title appears in the table of "
"contents.  @xref{@code{@@unnumberedsubsec @@appendixsubsec @@subheading}}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19749
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@unnumberedsubsubsec @var{title}"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19752
msgid ""
"Begin an unnumbered subsubsection.  The title appears in the table of "
"contents.  @xref{@code{@@subsubsection}}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19753
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@uref@{@var{url}[, @var{displayed-text}][, @var{replacement}@}"
msgstr ""

#. type: itemx
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19754
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@url@{@var{url}[, @var{displayed-text}][, @var{replacement}@}"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19757
msgid ""
"Define a cross-reference to an external uniform resource locator, e.g., for "
"the World Wide Web.  @xref{@code{@@url}}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19758
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@urefbreakstyle @var{style}"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19762
msgid ""
"Specify how @code{@@uref}/@code{@@url} should break at special characters: "
"@code{after}, @code{before}, @code{none}.  @xref{@code{@@url}}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19763
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@v@{@var{c}@}"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19766
msgid ""
"Generate check accent over the character @var{c}, as in @v{o}.  "
"@xref{Inserting Accents}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19767
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@value@{@var{txivar}@}"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19771
msgid ""
"Insert the value, if any, of the Texinfo variable @var{txivar}, previously "
"defined by @code{@@set}.  @xref{@code{@@set @@clear @@value}}."
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19775
msgid ""
"Highlight a metasyntactic variable, which is something that stands for "
"another piece of text.  @xref{@code{@@var}}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19776
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@verb@{@var{delim} @var{literal} @var{delim}@}"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19780
msgid ""
"Output @var{literal}, delimited by the single character @var{delim}, exactly "
"as is (in the fixed-width font), including any whitespace or Texinfo special "
"characters.  @xref{@code{@@verb}}."
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19784
msgid ""
"Output the text of the environment exactly as is (in the fixed-width font).  "
"Pair with @code{@@end verbatim}.  @xref{@code{@@verbatim}}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19785
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@verbatiminclude @var{filename}"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19788
msgid ""
"Output the contents of @var{filename} exactly as is (in the fixed-width "
"font).  @xref{@code{@@verbatiminclude}}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19789
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@vindex @var{entry}"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19792
msgid ""
"Add @var{entry} to the index of variables.  @xref{Index Entries, , Defining "
"the Entries of an Index}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19793
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@vskip @var{amount}"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19798
msgid ""
"In a printed manual, insert whitespace so as to push text on the remainder "
"of the page towards the bottom of the page.  Used in formatting the "
"copyright page with the argument @samp{0pt plus 1filll}.  (Note spelling of "
"@samp{filll}.)  @xref{Copyright}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19799
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@vtable @var{formatting-command}"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19804
msgid ""
"Begin a two-column table, using @code{@@item} for each entry.  Automatically "
"enter each of the items in the first column into the index of variables.  "
"Pair with @code{@@end vtable}.  The same as @code{@@table}, except for "
"indexing.  @xref{@code{@@ftable @@vtable}}."
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19807
msgid "Disallow line breaks within @var{text}.  @xref{@code{@@w}}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19808
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@xml"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19811
msgid ""
"Enter XML completely.  Pair with @code{@@end xml}.  @xref{Raw Formatter "
"Commands}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19812
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"@@xref@{@var{node}, [@var{entry}], [@var{node-title}], [@var{info-file}], "
"[@var{printed-manual}]@}"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19818
msgid ""
"Make a reference that starts with `See' in a printed manual.  Follow command "
"with a punctuation mark.  The first argument is mandatory, except for "
"references to whole manuals.  To refer to another manual as a whole, the "
"@var{printed-manual} and/or the @var{info-file} are the only required "
"arguments.  @xref{@code{@@xref}}."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19819
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@xrefautomaticsectiontitle @var{on-off}"
msgstr ""

#. type: table
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19822
msgid ""
"By default, use the section title instead of the node name in cross "
"references, including in node headers in HTML.  @xref{Three Arguments}."
msgstr ""

#. type: node
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19826
#, no-wrap
msgid "Command Contexts"
msgstr ""

#. type: section
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19827
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@-Command Contexts"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19829
#, no-wrap
msgid "Contexts, of @@-commands"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19836
msgid ""
"Here we describe approximately which @@-commands can be used in which "
"contexts.  It is not exhaustive or meant to be a complete reference.  "
"Discrepancies between the information here and the Texinfo processors "
"implementations are most likely to be resolved in favor of the "
"implementations."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19840
msgid ""
"By @dfn{general text} below, we mean anything except sectioning and other "
"such outer-level document commands, such as @code{@@section}, @code{@@node}, "
"and @code{@@setfilename}."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19846
msgid ""
"@code{@@c}, @code{@@comment} and @code{@@if ... @@end if} conditional "
"commands may appear anywhere (except the conditionals must still be on lines "
"by themselves).  @code{@@caption} and @code{@@shortcaption} may only appear "
"in @code{@@float} but may contain general text.  @code{@@footnote} content "
"likewise."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19852
msgid ""
"@@-commands with braces marking text (such as @code{@@strong}, @code{@@sc}, "
"@code{@@asis}) may contain raw formatter commands such as @code{@@html} but "
"no other block commands (other commands terminated by @code{@@end}) and may "
"not be split across paragraphs, but may otherwise contain general text."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19857
msgid ""
"In addition to the block command restriction, on @code{@@center}, "
"@code{@@exdent} and @code{@@item} in @code{@@table} lines, @@-commands that "
"makes only sense in a paragraph are not accepted, such as @code{@@indent}."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19860
msgid ""
"In addition to the above, sectioning commands cannot contain "
"@code{@@anchor}, @code{@@footnote} or @code{@@verb}."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19866
msgid ""
"In addition to the above, remaining commands (@code{@@node}, "
"@code{@@anchor}, @code{@@printindex}, @code{@@ref}, @code{@@math}, "
"@code{@@cindex}, @code{@@url}, @code{@@image}, and so on) cannot contain "
"cross-reference commands (@code{@@ref}, @code{@@xref}, @code{@@pxref} and "
"@code{@@inforef})."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19869
msgid ""
"For precise and complete information, we suggest looking into the test suite "
"in the sources, which exhaustively tries combinations."
msgstr ""

#. type: section
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19871
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19872
#, no-wrap
msgid "Obsolete @@-Commands"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19876
msgid ""
"Here are Texinfo @@-commands which are obsolete or have been removed "
"completely.  This section is for historical purposes."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19878
msgid "@ftable @code"
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19878
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@refill"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19883
msgid ""
"This command used to refill and indent the paragraph after all the other "
"processing has been done.  It is no longer needed, since all formatters now "
"automatically refill as needed, but you may still see it in the source to "
"some manuals, as it does no harm."
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19884
#, no-wrap
msgid "Contents, after title page"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19885
#, no-wrap
msgid "Table of contents, after title page"
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19886
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@setcontentsaftertitlepage"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19894
msgid ""
"In the past, the contents commands were sometimes placed at the end of the "
"file, after any indices and just before the @code{@@bye}, but we no longer "
"recommend this.  This command could be used by a user printing a manual, to "
"force the contents to be printed after the title page (after the @samp{@@end "
"titlepage} line)  even if the @code{@@contents} command was at the end of "
"the manual."
msgstr ""

#. type: item
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19895
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@setshortcontentsaftertitlepage"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19898
msgid ""
"This placed the short table of contents after the @samp{@@end titlepage} "
"command even if the @code{@@shortcontents} command was at the end."
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19901
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19907
#, no-wrap
msgid "Tips"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19903
msgid "@nodedescription Hints on how to write a Texinfo document."
msgstr ""

#. type: appendix
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19903
#, no-wrap
msgid "Tips and Hints"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19906
msgid "Here are some tips for writing Texinfo documentation:"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19908
#, no-wrap
msgid "Usage tips"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19909
#, no-wrap
msgid "Hints"
msgstr ""

#. type: itemize
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19913
msgid "Write in the present tense, not in the past or the future."
msgstr ""

#. type: itemize
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19917
msgid ""
"Write actively! For example, write ``We recommend that @dots{}'' rather than "
"``It is recommended that @dots{}''."
msgstr ""

#. type: itemize
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19920
msgid "Use 70 or 72 as your fill column.  Longer lines are hard to read."
msgstr ""

#. type: itemize
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19923
msgid "Include a copyright notice and copying permissions."
msgstr ""

#. type: itemize
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19928
msgid ""
"Design your manual so that it can be read sequentially, as far as possible.  "
"People tire of flipping back and forth to find information that should be "
"presented to them as they need it."
msgstr ""

#. type: subsubheading
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19932
#, no-wrap
msgid "Index, Index, Index!"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19936
msgid ""
"Write many index entries, in different ways.  Readers like indices; they are "
"helpful and convenient."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19942
msgid ""
"Although it is easiest to write index entries as you write the body of the "
"text, some people prefer to write entries afterwards.  In either case, write "
"an entry before the paragraph to which it applies.  This way, an index entry "
"points to the first page of a paragraph that is split across pages."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19944
msgid "Here are more index-related hints we have found valuable:"
msgstr ""

#. type: itemize
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19949
msgid ""
"Write each index entry differently, so each entry refers to a different "
"place in the document."
msgstr ""

#. type: itemize
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19955
msgid ""
"Write index entries only where a topic is discussed significantly.  For "
"example, it is not useful to index ``debugging information'' in a chapter on "
"reporting bugs.  Someone who wants to know about debugging information will "
"certainly not find it in that chapter."
msgstr ""

#. type: itemize
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19962
msgid ""
"Consistently capitalize the first word of every concept index entry, or else "
"consistently use lowercase.  Terse entries often call for lowercase; longer "
"entries for capitalization.  Whichever case convention you use, please use "
"one or the other consistently! Mixing the two styles looks bad."
msgstr ""

#. type: itemize
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19968
msgid ""
"Always capitalize or use uppercase for those words in an index for which "
"this is proper, such as names of countries or acronyms.  Always use the "
"appropriate case for case-sensitive names, such as those in C or Lisp."
msgstr ""

#. type: itemize
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19973
msgid ""
"Write the indexing commands that refer to a whole section immediately after "
"the section command, and write the indexing commands that refer to a "
"paragraph before that paragraph."
msgstr ""

#. type: itemize
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19976
msgid ""
"In the example that follows, a blank line comes after the index entry for "
"``Leaping'':"
msgstr ""

#. type: group
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19982
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"@@section The Dog and the Fox\n"
"@@cindex Jumping, in general\n"
"@@cindex Leaping\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: group
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19988
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"@@cindex Dog, lazy, jumped over\n"
"@@cindex Lazy dog jumped over\n"
"@@cindex Fox, jumps over dog\n"
"@@cindex Quick fox jumps over dog\n"
"The quick brown fox jumps over the lazy dog.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: itemize
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19995
msgid ""
"(Note that the example shows entries for the same concept that are written "
"in different ways---@samp{Lazy dog}, and @samp{Dog, lazy}---so readers can "
"look up the concept in different ways.)"
msgstr ""

#. type: subsubheading
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:19998
#, no-wrap
msgid "Blank Lines"
msgstr ""

#. type: itemize
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:20006
msgid ""
"Insert a blank line between a sectioning command and the first following "
"sentence or paragraph, or between the indexing commands associated with the "
"sectioning command and the first following sentence or paragraph, as shown "
"in the tip on indexing.  It makes the source easier to read."
msgstr ""

#. type: itemize
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:20011
msgid ""
"Always insert a blank line before a @code{@@table} command and after an "
"@code{@@end table} command; but never insert a blank line after an "
"@code{@@table} command."
msgstr ""

#. type: group
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:20018
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Types of fox:\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: group
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:20022
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"@@table @@samp\n"
"@@item Quick\n"
"Jump over lazy dogs.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: group
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:20028
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"@@item Brown\n"
"Also jump over lazy dogs.\n"
"@@end table\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: group
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:20033
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"@@noindent\n"
"On the other hand, @dots{}\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: itemize
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:20039
msgid ""
"Insert blank lines before and after @code{@@itemize} @dots{} @code{@@end "
"itemize} and @code{@@enumerate} @dots{} @code{@@end enumerate} in the same "
"way."
msgstr ""

#. type: subsubheading
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:20042
#, no-wrap
msgid "Complete Phrases"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:20045
msgid "Complete phrases are easier to read than @dots{}"
msgstr ""

#. type: itemize
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:20051
msgid ""
"Write entries in an itemized list as complete sentences; or at least, as "
"complete phrases.  Incomplete expressions @dots{} awkward @dots{} like this."
msgstr ""

#. type: itemize
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:20056
msgid ""
"Write the prefatory sentence or phrase for a multi-item list or table as a "
"complete expression.  Do not write ``You can set:''; instead, write ``You "
"can set these variables:''.  The former expression sounds cut off."
msgstr ""

#. type: subsubheading
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:20059
#, no-wrap
msgid "Editions, Dates and Versions"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:20066
msgid ""
"Include edition numbers, version numbers, and dates in the @code{@@copying} "
"text (for people reading the Texinfo file, and for the legal copyright in "
"the output files).  Then use @code{@@insertcopying} in the "
"@code{@@titlepage} section for people reading the printed output "
"(@pxref{Short Sample})."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:20070
msgid ""
"It is easiest to handle such version information using @code{@@set} and "
"@code{@@value}.  @xref{@code{@@value} Example}, and @ref{GNU Sample Texts}."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:20077
msgid ""
"Definition commands are @code{@@deffn}, @code{@@defun}, @code{@@defmac}, and "
"the like, and enable you to write descriptions in a uniform format."
msgstr ""

#. type: itemize
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:20083
msgid ""
"Write just one definition command for each entity you define with a "
"definition command.  The automatic indexing feature creates an index entry "
"that leads the reader to the definition."
msgstr ""

#. type: itemize
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:20088
msgid ""
"Use @code{@@table} @dots{} @code{@@end table} in an appendix that contains a "
"summary of functions, not @code{@@deffn} or other definition commands."
msgstr ""

#. type: subsubheading
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:20091
#, no-wrap
msgid "Capitalization"
msgstr ""

#. type: itemize
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:20097
msgid ""
"Capitalize ``Texinfo''; it is a name.  Do not write the @samp{x} or @samp{i} "
"in uppercase."
msgstr ""

#. type: itemize
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:20100
msgid "Capitalize ``Info''; it is a name."
msgstr ""

#. type: itemize
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:20106
msgid ""
"Write @TeX{} using the @code{@@TeX@{@}} command.  Note the uppercase "
"@samp{T} and @samp{X}.  This command causes the formatters to typeset the "
"name according to the wishes of Donald Knuth, who wrote @TeX{}.  (Likewise "
"@code{@@LaTeX@{@}} for @LaTeX{}.)"
msgstr ""

#. type: subsubheading
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:20109
#, no-wrap
msgid "Spaces"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:20114
msgid ""
"Do not use spaces to format a Texinfo file, except inside of "
"@code{@@example} @dots{} @code{@@end example} and other literal environments "
"and commands."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:20117
msgid "For example, @TeX{} fills the following:"
msgstr ""

#. type: group
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:20125
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   @@kbd@{C-x v@}\n"
"   @@kbd@{M-x vc-next-action@}\n"
"      Perform the next logical operation\n"
"      on the version-controlled file\n"
"      corresponding to the current buffer.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:20131
msgid "so it looks like this:"
msgstr ""

#. type: quotation
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:20138
msgid ""
"@kbd{C-x v} @kbd{M-x vc-next-action} Perform the next logical operation on "
"the version-controlled file corresponding to the current buffer."
msgstr ""

#. type: quotation
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:20144
msgid ""
"`C-x v' `M-x vc-next-action' Perform the next logical operation on the "
"version-controlled file corresponding to the current buffer."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:20150
msgid ""
"In this case, the text should be formatted with @code{@@table}, "
"@code{@@item}, and @code{@@itemx}, to create a table."
msgstr ""

#. type: subsubheading
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:20152
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@code, @@samp, @@var, and @samp{---}"
msgstr ""

#. type: itemize
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:20158
msgid ""
"Use @code{@@code} around Lisp symbols, including command names.  For example,"
msgstr ""

#. type: example
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:20161
#, no-wrap
msgid "The main function is @@code@{vc-next-action@}, @dots{}\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: itemize
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:20166
msgid ""
"Avoid putting letters such as @samp{s} immediately after an @samp{@@code}.  "
"Such letters look bad."
msgstr ""

#. type: itemize
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:20170
msgid ""
"Use @code{@@var} around meta-variables.  Do not write angle brackets around "
"them."
msgstr ""

#. type: itemize
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:20175
msgid ""
"Use three hyphens in a row, @samp{---}, to indicate a long dash.  The Info "
"formatter reduces three hyphens to two; a long dash is typeset in other "
"output formats."
msgstr ""

#. type: subsubheading
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:20178
#, no-wrap
msgid "Periods Outside of Quotes"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:20185
msgid ""
"Place periods and other punctuation marks @emph{outside} of quotations, "
"unless the punctuation is part of the quotation.  This practice goes against "
"some publishing conventions in the United States, but enables the reader to "
"distinguish between the contents of the quotation and the whole passage."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:20188
msgid ""
"For example, you should write the following sentence with the period outside "
"the end quotation marks:"
msgstr ""

#. type: example
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:20191
#, no-wrap
msgid "Evidently, @samp{au} is an abbreviation for ``author''.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:20196
msgid ""
"since @samp{au} does @emph{not} serve as an abbreviation for @samp{author.} "
"(with a period following the word)."
msgstr ""

#. type: subsubheading
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:20198
#, no-wrap
msgid "Introducing New Terms"
msgstr ""

#. type: itemize
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:20204
msgid ""
"Introduce new terms so that a reader who does not know them can understand "
"them from context; or write a definition for the term."
msgstr ""

#. type: itemize
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:20208
msgid ""
"For example, in the following, the terms ``check in'', ``register'' and "
"``delta'' are all appearing for the first time; the example sentence should "
"be rewritten so they are understandable."
msgstr ""

#. type: quotation
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:20213
msgid ""
"The major function assists you in checking in a file to your version control "
"system and registering successive sets of changes to it as deltas."
msgstr ""

#. type: itemize
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:20219
msgid ""
"Use the @code{@@dfn} command around a word being introduced, to indicate "
"that the reader should not expect to know the meaning already, and should "
"expect to learn the meaning from this passage."
msgstr ""

#. type: subsubheading
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:20222
#, no-wrap
msgid "Program Invocation Nodes"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:20228
msgid ""
"You can invoke programs such as Emacs, GCC, and @code{gawk} from a shell.  "
"The documentation for each program should contain a section that describes "
"this.  Unfortunately, if the node names and titles for these sections are "
"all different, they are difficult for users to find."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:20232
msgid ""
"So, there is a convention to name such sections with a phrase beginning with "
"the word `Invoking', as in `Invoking Emacs'; this way, users can find the "
"section easily."
msgstr ""

#. type: subsubheading
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:20234
#, no-wrap
msgid "ANSI C Syntax"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:20238
msgid ""
"When you use @code{@@example} to describe a C function's calling "
"conventions, use the ANSI C syntax, like this:"
msgstr ""

#. type: example
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:20241
#, no-wrap
msgid "void dld_init (char *@@var@{path@});\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:20247
msgid ""
"And in the subsequent discussion, refer to the argument values by writing "
"the same argument names, again highlighted with @code{@@var}."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:20250
msgid "Avoid the obsolete style that looks like this:"
msgstr ""

#. type: example
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:20253
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"#include <dld.h>\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: example
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:20256
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"dld_init (path)\n"
"  char *path;\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:20265
msgid ""
"Also, it is best to avoid writing @code{#include} above the declaration just "
"to indicate that the function is declared in a header file.  The practice "
"may give the misimpression that the @code{#include} belongs near the "
"declaration of the function.  Either state explicitly which header file "
"holds the declaration or, better yet, name the header file used for a group "
"of functions at the beginning of the section that describes the functions."
msgstr ""

#. type: subsubheading
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:20267
#, no-wrap
msgid "Node Length"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:20275
msgid ""
"Keep nodes (sections) to a reasonable length, whatever reasonable might be "
"in the given context.  Don't hesitate to break up long nodes into subnodes "
"and have an extensive tree structure; that's what it's there for.  Many "
"times, readers will probably try to find a single specific point in the "
"manual, using search, indexing, or just plain guessing, rather than reading "
"the whole thing from beginning to end."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:20280
msgid ""
"You can use the @command{texi-elements-by-size} utility to see a list of all "
"nodes (or sections) in the document, sorted by size (either lines or words), "
"to find candidates for splitting.  It's in the @file{util/} subdirectory of "
"the Texinfo sources."
msgstr ""

#. type: subsubheading
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:20282
#, no-wrap
msgid "Bad Examples"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:20285
msgid "Here are several examples of bad writing to avoid:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:20288
msgid ""
"In this example, say, `` @dots{} you must @code{@@dfn}@{check in@} the new "
"version.'' That flows better."
msgstr ""

#. type: quotation
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:20292
msgid ""
"When you are done editing the file, you must perform a @code{@@dfn}@{check "
"in@}."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:20296
msgid ""
"In the following example, say, ``@dots{} makes a unified interface such as "
"VC mode possible.''"
msgstr ""

#. type: quotation
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:20301
msgid ""
"SCCS, RCS and other version-control systems all perform similar functions in "
"broadly similar ways (it is this resemblance which makes a unified control "
"mode like this possible)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:20304
msgid "And in this example, you should specify what `it' refers to:"
msgstr ""

#. type: quotation
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:20308
msgid ""
"If you are working with other people, it assists in coordinating everyone's "
"changes so they do not step on each other."
msgstr ""

#. type: subsubheading
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:20311
#, no-wrap
msgid "And Finally @dots{}"
msgstr ""

#. type: itemize
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:20318
msgid ""
"Pronounce @TeX{} as if the @samp{X} were a Greek `chi', as the last sound in "
"the name `Bach'.  But pronounce Texinfo as in `speck': ``teckinfo''."
msgstr ""

#. type: itemize
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:20324
msgid ""
"Write notes for yourself at the very end of a Texinfo file after the "
"@code{@@bye}.  None of the processors process text after the @code{@@bye}; "
"it is as if the text were within @code{@@ignore} @dots{} @code{@@end ignore}."
msgstr ""

#. type: appendix
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:20327
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:20329
#, no-wrap
msgid "Sample Texinfo Files"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:20329
msgid "@nodedescription Complete examples, including full texts."
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:20330
#, no-wrap
msgid "Sample Texinfo files"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:20333
msgid "This appendix includes texts to be used in GNU manuals."
msgstr ""

#. type: section
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:20335
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:20336
#, no-wrap
msgid "GNU Sample Texts"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:20338
#, no-wrap
msgid "GNU sample texts"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:20339
#, no-wrap
msgid "Sample texts, GNU"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:20340
#, no-wrap
msgid "Full texts, GNU"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:20344
msgid ""
"Following is a sample Texinfo document with the full texts that should be "
"used (adapted as necessary) in GNU manuals."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:20351
msgid ""
"As well as the legal texts, it also serves as a practical example of how "
"many elements in a GNU system can affect the manual.  If you're not familiar "
"with all these different elements, don't worry.  They're not required and a "
"perfectly good manual can be written without them.  They're included here "
"nonetheless because many manuals do (or could)  benefit from them."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:20353
msgid "@xref{Short Sample}, for a minimal example of a Texinfo file."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:20355
msgid "Here are some notes on the example:"
msgstr ""

#. type: pindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:20358
#, no-wrap
msgid "automake@r{, and version info}"
msgstr ""

#. type: vindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:20359
#, no-wrap
msgid "UPDATED @r{Automake variable}"
msgstr ""

#. type: vindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:20360
#, no-wrap
msgid "UPDATED-MONTH @r{Automake variable}"
msgstr ""

#. type: vindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:20361
#, no-wrap
msgid "VERSION @r{Automake variable}"
msgstr ""

#. type: pindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:20362
#, no-wrap
msgid "time-stamp.el"
msgstr ""

#. type: itemize
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:20369
msgid ""
"The @file{version.texi} in the @code{@@include} command is maintained "
"automatically by Automake (@pxref{Texinfo,,, automake, GNU Automake}).  It "
"sets the @samp{VERSION}, @samp{UPDATED} and @samp{UPDATED-MONTH} values used "
"elsewhere.  If your distribution doesn't use Automake, but you do use Emacs, "
"you may find the @code{time-stamp.el} package helpful (@pxref{Time Stamps,,, "
"emacs, The GNU Emacs Manual})."
msgstr ""

#. type: itemize
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:20374
msgid ""
"The @code{@@syncodeindex} command reflects the recommendation to use only "
"one index where possible, to make it easier for readers to look up index "
"entries."
msgstr ""

#. type: itemize
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:20380
msgid ""
"The @code{@@dircategory} specify a category for the manual.  It is used for "
"constructing the Info directory.  @xref{Directory Category}, which includes "
"a variety of recommended category names.  @xref{Installing Dir Entries}."
msgstr ""

#. type: itemize
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:20385
msgid ""
"The `Invoking' node is a GNU standard to help users find the basic "
"information about command-line usage of a given program.  @xref{Manual "
"Structure Details,,, standards, GNU Coding Standards}."
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:20387
#, no-wrap
msgid "GNU Free Documentation License, including entire"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:20388
#, no-wrap
msgid "Free Documentation License, including entire"
msgstr ""

#. type: itemize
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:20395
msgid ""
"This sample shows how to includes the FDL in a manual using the "
"@command{@@include} command.  The @file{fdl.texi} file is available in the "
"Texinfo and other GNU source distributions.  It is also available on the GNU "
"website (at @uref{https://www.gnu.org/licenses/fdl-1.3.html}) along with "
"guidance for using it."
msgstr ""

#. type: itemize
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:20398
msgid "If the FSF is not the copyright holder, then use the appropriate name."
msgstr ""

#. type: itemize
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:20404
msgid ""
"For documents that express your personal views, feelings or experiences, it "
"is more appropriate to use a license permitting only verbatim copying, "
"rather than the FDL@.  @xref{Verbatim Copying License}."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:20408
msgid "Here is the sample document:"
msgstr ""

#. type: settitle
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:20413
#, no-wrap
msgid "GNU Sample @value{VERSION}"
msgstr ""

#. type: copying
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:20419
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This manual is for GNU Sample (version @value{VERSION}, @value{UPDATED}),\n"
"which is an example in the Texinfo documentation.\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: copying
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:20421
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:20506
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Copyright @copyright{} 2016 Free Software Foundation, Inc.\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: quotation
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:20429
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Permission is granted to copy, distribute and/or modify this document\n"
"under the terms of the GNU Free Documentation License, Version 1.3 or\n"
"any later version published by the Free Software Foundation; with no\n"
"Invariant Sections, with no Front-Cover Texts, and with no Back-Cover\n"
"Texts.  A copy of the license is included in the section entitled\n"
"``GNU Free Documentation License''.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: menuentry
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:20435
#, no-wrap
msgid "sample: (sample)Invoking sample"
msgstr ""

#. type: top
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:20438
