msgstr ""

#. type: section
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:20483
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:20484
#, no-wrap
msgid "Verbatim Copying License"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:20486
#, no-wrap
msgid "Verbatim copying license"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:20487
#, no-wrap
msgid "License for verbatim copying"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:20492
msgid ""
"For software manuals and other documentation, it is critical to use a "
"license permitting free redistribution and updating, so that when a free "
"program is changed, the documentation can be updated as well."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:20496
msgid ""
"On the other hand, for documents that express your personal views, feelings "
"or experiences, it is more appropriate to use a license permitting only "
"verbatim copying."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:20500
msgid ""
"Here is a sample text for such a license permitting verbatim copying only.  "
"This is just the license text itself.  For a complete sample document, see "
"the previous sections."
msgstr ""

#. type: copying
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:20504
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This document is a sample for allowing verbatim copying only.\n"
"\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: quotation
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:20511
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Permission is granted to make and distribute verbatim copies\n"
"of this entire document without royalty provided the\n"
"copyright notice and this permission notice are preserved.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: section
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:20516
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:20517
#, no-wrap
msgid "All-permissive Copying License"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:20519
#, no-wrap
msgid "All-permissive copying license"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:20520
#, no-wrap
msgid "License for all-permissive copying"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:20525
msgid ""
"For software manuals and other documentation, it is important to use a "
"license permitting free redistribution and updating, so that when a free "
"program is changed, the documentation can be updated as well."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:20530
msgid ""
"On the other hand, for small supporting files, short manuals (under 300 "
"lines long) and rough documentation (README files, INSTALL files, etc.), the "
"full FDL would be overkill.  They can use a simple all-permissive license."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:20534
msgid ""
"Here is a sample text for such an all-permissive license.  This is just the "
"license text itself.  For a complete sample document, see the previous "
"sections."
msgstr ""

#. type: example
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:20537
#, no-wrap
