#, no-wrap
msgid "@code{@@smallbook}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:23088
msgid "@nodedescription How to print small format books and manuals."
msgstr ""

#. type: section
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:23088
#, no-wrap
msgid "@code{@@smallbook}: Printing ``Small'' Books"
msgstr ""

#. type: findex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:23091
#, no-wrap
msgid "smallbook"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:23092
#, no-wrap
msgid "Small book size"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:23093
#, no-wrap
msgid "Book, printing small"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:23094
#, no-wrap
msgid "Page sizes for books"
msgstr ""

#. type: cindex
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:23095
#, no-wrap
msgid "Size of printed book"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:23103
msgid ""
"By default, @TeX{} typesets pages for printing in an 8.5 by 11 inch format, "
"which is the ``letter'' size commonly used in the United States.  However, "
"you can direct @TeX{} or @LaTeX{} to typeset a document in a 7 by 9.25 inch "
"format that is suitable for bound books by inserting the following command "
"on a line by itself at the beginning of the Texinfo file, before the title "
"page:"
msgstr ""

#. type: example
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:23106
#, no-wrap
msgid "@@smallbook\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:23113
msgid ""
"(Since many books are about 7 by 9.25 inches, this command might better have "
"been called the @code{@@regularbooksize} command, but it came to be called "
"the @code{@@smallbook} command by comparison to the 8.5 by 11 inch format.)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: texinfo/texinfo-ed.7.1-en_US.texi:23117
msgid ""
"@xref{Format with @command{texi2dvi} or @command{texi2pdf}}, and "
"@ref{Preparing for @TeX{}}, for other ways to format with @code{@@smallbook} "
"with @TeX{} that do not require changing the source file."
msgstr ""

#. type: node
